window.CULTIVATION_CHAPTERS=(window.CULTIVATION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2001,"title":"Chapter 2001: Yu Rou’s True Feelings","paragraphs":["Chapter 2001: Yu Rou’s True Feelings","“Brother!”","Unable to contain herself, Yu Rou subconsciously threw herself into his arms, wrapping him in a tight embrace, years of longing and emotion pouring into that single, desperate gesture.","“Y-Yuan?!” Bai Lianhua exclaimed in a shocked tone, her eyes wide with surprise.","Xia Jingyi swallowed nervously, her face slightly red after seeing Yuan’s handsome face.","“I’m sorry it took this long to see you guys again,” Yuan said as he caressed Yu Rou’s back, who was only a head shorter than him now.","“...”","Yu Rou didn’t respond—she simply held him tighter, burying her face into his robes as if afraid he might vanish if she let go.","“You were unable to log off Cultivation Online for several years, right? How is your body right now?” Bai Lianhua asked since it seemed like Yu Rou wasn’t going to speak.","“My body is fine. If I weren’t a cultivator, it would’ve been dangerous.”","“So that is your real body, correct?”","“Correct,” he confirmed.","“Does this mean we won’t be able to see you on Earth again?” Bai Lianhua continued to ask.","“For now, but it’s not like I cannot return to Earth ever again. Unfortunately, I don’t know when that will happen. It could take years if not decades before I get to return safely.”","Yu Rou’s body trembled at such words.","Yuan noticed this and looked down, but he wasn’t sure what to say.","Yu Rou suddenly lifted her face from his chest and looked at him with tears flowing down her face.","“Brother... What if I want to come to the Nine Heavens?” she asked.","“That’s...” Yuan became speechless.","While he was certain the Celestial Emperor would do everything in his power to prevent him from returning to the Nine Heavens if he visited Earth, he wasn’t sure how the Celestial Emperor would respond to others attempting to enter the Nine Heavens.","After a moment of silence, Yuan finally spoke. “That’s not a decision you make on a whim. Choosing this path means giving up the life you’ve known—it’s not something to take lightly.”","“I know that!” she shouted.","“...”","After a brief pause, she continued softly,","“When you first left home with Meixiu, I realized just how much I hated being apart from you. Every day felt like a small ache. But I endured it, because, back then, I could still see you often enough.”","“But after you moved to Dragon Spiral Mountain and I joined the Eternal Lotuses... we’ve barely seen each other at all. Then you couldn’t log out of Cultivation Online... and now it’s been over half a decade since we last saw each other.”","Her voice trembled as she continued, “I can’t do this anymore, Brother. It’s become too much for me to bear. You’re the only family member I have left...”","“Yu Rou...” Yuan didn’t know what to say.","He shifted his gaze to the others, who shook their heads in silence.","After a moment of silence, Yuan sighed and said, “If that’s what you really want, I won’t stop you. However, it’s going to take some time to open the gateway between our worlds again, so you’ll have to wait until then. In the meantime, I’ll try to visit you as much as possible.”","Yu Rou nodded.","“Okay...” she mumbled.","Once Yu Rou had calmed down, they gathered around a table, and Yuan began recounting his experiences over the past few years, sharing the long and winding journey that had kept them apart.","However, aside from Yu Rou, the others struggled to focus, still caught up in the weight of her earlier outburst. None of them had noticed her pain before since she had always carried herself with quiet strength, acting composed and independent.","Even Meixiu, who had always been the closest to Yu Rou, had failed to see the loneliness hiding behind her calm demeanor. It wasn’t until recently, when Yu Rou had finally stopped pretending, that Meixiu began to see her pain.","Once Yuan finished recounting his journey, Yu Rou and the others began recalling theirs.","Bai Lianhua would spend most of her time and effort growing her faction both on Earth and in the Nine Heavens, while Xia Jingyi focused on improving her zither techniques, even joining a music sect for three years.","As for Yu Rou, cultivation had become her only escape from the loneliness she carried. She immersed herself in it for most of her days, using it as a shield against the emptiness, hence why her cultivation had surpassed even Bai Lianhua, being at the 7th level of Spirit Lord. On occasion, she took on monster extermination quests—not for merit or recognition, but simply to vent the emotions she kept buried inside.","“Brother, it’s been a while since you last saw Snowy, right? Do you even remember her?”","“Oh, that tiger cub from back then? I remember.” He nodded.","“She’s grown a lot since then, and she even saved my life many times.”","“Come out, Snowy.”","Yu Rou suddenly called.","In the next moment, a towering figure emerged from Yu Rou’s dantian and appeared at her side. No longer the small, adorable cub from years past, Snowy had grown into a majestic white tiger—massive in size, and with a fierce and commanding presence.","“Wow, you’ve really grown.”","Surprisingly, Snowy’s cultivation was at the peak of Spirit King, an entire realm stronger than her own master.","“...”","However, the moment Snowy laid eyes on Yuan, she instinctively shrank back, her massive form trembling ever so slightly—an involuntary reaction born of instinctual reverence.","“Snowy? There’s no need to be afraid. This is my brother. Don’t you remember?” Yu Rou was quite surprised by Snowy’s reaction. In fact, she’d never seen Snowy acting nervous before, much less afraid.","Seeing this, Yuan smiled and said, “She must be reacting to my bloodline.”","He suddenly retrieved a glass vial that contained his blood and offered it to Yu Rou.","“Feed her this. It’ll help her grow.”","“This... is blood?” Yu Rou looked at the vial with interest and confusion, wondering why Yuan wanted her to feed Snowy blood.","Join Privilege for 50 Adv Chapters! Only Available in the App!"]},{"number":2002,"title":"Chapter 2002: Snowy’s Transformation","paragraphs":["\"Is this blood from a magical beast or something?\" Yu Rou asked as she uncorked the vial.","A distinct scent immediately filled the air, one perceptible only to beasts. Snowy’s ears perked up, and her eyes widened with excitement, her instincts awakened by the unmistakable aroma.","Like a beast in heat, Snowy pounced onto Yu Rou, who quickly shouted, \"Ah! You’re going to make me drop it!\"","However, Snowy didn’t move away. Instead, she leaned in even closer, her tongue poking out eagerly as she pressed her head toward the vial—like someone desperately trying to catch a single drop of water in the desert.","\"Okay! Okay! I get it! Here!\" Yu Rou said in a flustered tone as she quickly poured the blood onto Snowy’s outstretched tongue.","The moment the blood touched her taste buds, Snowy’s entire body quivered with delight, her pupils dilating as a surge of satisfaction rushed through her.","In the very next moment, Snowy let out a thunderous roar as her aura exploded outward, wild and untamed, shaking the air around her.","Meanwhile, notifications began appearing before Yu Rou.","<Snowy has consumed ??? blood>","<Snowy’s bloodline has started to transform!>","<Progress: 5%>","\"Snowy’s bloodline is transforming!\" Yu Rou exclaimed after seeing these notifications.","\"What?! Really?!\" Bai Lianhua and Xia Jingyi were just as surprised to hear this.","\"What was that blood you fed her?\" Yu Rou turned to look at Yuan for answers.","Yuan smiled and said, \"It’s my blood.\"","\"Huh?\" Yu Rou and the others stared at him with wide eyes, seemingly unable to comprehend it.","\"My bloodline is quite unique and has the ability to evolve a beast’s bloodline. It’s not guaranteed, but it has a higher chance of working on those with a weaker bloodline.\"","\"What an incredible ability... as expected of my brother,\" Yu Rou murmured with quiet admiration.","She then glanced at Snowy, who had suddenly crouched down, her massive form curling slightly as if she had suddenly drifted off to sleep.","\"She’ll be fine. Just give her some time to evolve her bloodline,\" Yuan explained.","Yu Rou nodded.","Some time later, Yu Rou spoke in a faint, dispirited voice, \"Brother... are you going to leave again soon?\"","\"No, I’ll be staying at the Super Perfect Physique Tempering Sect for some time to let my body finish merging some more.\"","Yu Rou’s expression immediately brightened, and she asked, \"Then, can I spend more time with you?\"","\"Of course,\" he nodded.","They continued chatting for almost an entire day until Bai Lianhua said, \"It was very nice seeing you again, Yuan. I’d like to stay here for longer, but I have a lot of work to do at the faction. Let’s meet again soon.\"","\"S-See you later...\" Xia Jingyi spoke in a timid voice.","\"Before you go, let me give you something...\"","Yuan transferred several techniques to them, bestowing cultivation and martial arts methods to Bai Lianhua, while entrusting Xia Jingyi with a collection of profound zither techniques.","\"T-These are Ancient and Mythic-rank techniques!\" Bai Lianhua exclaimed in shock after realizing what Yuan had given her.","Xia Jingyi was too shocked to even say anything.","\"No need to thank me. Just consider it a gift for taking care of my sister when I couldn’t,\" Yuan said.","\"You can leave without me. I’ll stay here for a little longer,\" Yu Rou said.","\"Okay...\"","Once Bai Lianhua and Xia Jingyi left, Meixiu and Chu Liuxiang also left a little bit later, leaving Yuan and Yu Rou alone.","\"How long are you going to stay?\" Yu Rou asked him.","\"I’ll stay here until you want to leave,\" he said.","\"Are you sure? Don’t you have a lot of things to do?\"","\"Yes, but they can wait for now.\"","\"In that case, I’ll stay here as long as possible!\"","Over the next several days, Yu Rou and Yuan spent their time reminiscing about their childhood. Yuan would often play the zither for her, guide her through her cultivation, and pass down several techniques to help her grow stronger.","Time passed quickly, and before they realized, they’d spent almost an entire month inside Senior Bai’s world.","\"I’ll leave tomorrow,\" Yu Rou said.","Although she wanted to spend more time with Yuan, she knew that she couldn’t keep him there forever.","\"Okay.\"","Later that night.","\"Brother, can I sleep with you tonight?\" Yu Rou knocked on his door and asked.","\"You’re not a child anymore, you know.\"","\"So what? I still want to snuggle with you like we used to. I’m coming in!\"","Inside his room, Yuan was seated on the floor.","\"You’re cultivating?\"","\"Now that I’ve reached Immortal Ascension, I don’t need to sleep anymore,\" Yuan explained. \"In fact, I feel far more rested through cultivation than I would from sleeping.\"","\"Since this is going to be my last day with you, sleep with me!\"","She pulled him off the floor and dragged him to the bed.","\"You may have grown up, but you’re still a bit spoiled, aren’t you?\" Yuan said with a warm smile.","Yu Rou didn’t reply, but a quiet smile spread across her face.","A few quiet minutes passed as they lay side by side on the bed.","Then, in a soft voice, Yu Rou whispered, \"Brother...\"","\"What is it?\"","\"When do you think I’ll be able to travel to the Nine Heavens?\"","\"Hard to say. After all, we need someone who can activate the teleportation device on Earth, but the Lord has already sacrificed his cultivation to open it.\"","He continued, \"Even if you make it to the Nine Heavens, what will you do then?\"","\"I want to go where you go,\" she immediately said.","\"That’s too dangerous. There’s no way I can bring you to the places I’ll be going.\"","\"I don’t need to be exactly by your side. I just want to be near enough so you can visit more conveniently.\"","\"But you can do that already through the Myriad of Techniques.\"","\"It doesn’t feel the same...\" she sighed. \"I want to be with you physically... not in this avatar...\"","Eventually, Yu Rou drifted into a deep, peaceful sleep—the kind she hadn’t experienced in years."]},{"number":2003,"title":"Chapter 2003: Meeting Li Jinxi","paragraphs":["Chapter 2003: Meeting Li Jinxi","The following morning, Yu Rou slowly opened her eyes.","“Brother...” she whispered, a warm smile blossoming on her face as she gazed at Yuan, peacefully asleep beside her.","A sudden impulse stirred within her, and after a brief moment of hesitation, she leaned in and pressed a soft, gentle kiss on his lips.","Yuan opened his eyes a few moments later.","“Good morning, brother.” Yu Rou acted normally, but her face was flushed with redness.","“Morning.”","Yuan sat up, pretending like he didn’t notice the kiss.","“I’ll make breakfast.” Yu Rou said as she got off the bed and left the room.","After she left, Yuan released a deep sigh. With his experience, there was no way he hadn’t noticed it—Yu Rou’s feelings for him went beyond simple sibling affection. While it might appear as familial love on the surface, he could clearly sense the deeper emotions she tried to hide.","Even if they weren’t blood-related, they had grown up together as siblings, and that bond carried weight. Yuan wasn’t sure how he would respond if Yu Rou ever chose to confess her feelings.","Would he be able to accept her... or would that line between them remain one he couldn’t cross?","Some time later, after eating breakfast, they made their way to the exit.","“Brother... do you think I’ll be able to see you again soon?” she asked.","He nodded and said, “I’ll try to meet you again before I return to my journey.”","“Okay. It’s a promise.”","Yu Rou suddenly embraced him tightly.","“Take this before you go.” Yuan retrieved a spatial ring and offered it to her.","“What’s this?” she asked.","“There are a few treasures inside that will help you if you ever get yourself into trouble that you cannot handle.”","“Thank you...”","Once Yu Rou left, Yuan also left the Myriad of Techniques and returned to the Super Perfect Physique Tempering Sect.","“Wow, I didn’t think you’d spend an entire month with Yu Rou.” Chu Liuxiang remarked when he returned.","“A month is nothing if you consider how long we’ve been apart,” he said.","“That’s true.”","“What are you going to do now?” Meixiu asked.","“I’ll stay at this sect for a little longer. Also, there’s still someone I need to talk to...”","“Oh, you mean Jinxi?” Chu Liuxiang said.","He nodded and said, “She’s definitely waiting for me.”","“Good luck,” Meixiu said.","Yuan left to find Li Jinxi shortly afterward.","After asking around, he made his way to the training grounds, but not the one reserved exclusively for the Sect Leader. Instead, he headed to the grounds designated for sect elders, where Li Jinxi was known to train. She often sparred with the elders, as none of the regular disciples were strong enough to challenge her.","When he arrived, Li Jinxi was in the middle of a sparring match with a sect elder who was at the Bronze Immortal stage while only being at the peak of Divine Ancestor herself. Moreover, though faint, Li Jinxi was unmistakably using Immortal Qi.","“No matter how many times I witness it, it still amazes me how she can wield Immortal Qi at her current cultivation level. She’s a true prodigy.”","“I heard she had just stepped into the Divine Realm when she joined the sect around five years ago. If she’d arrived a few years earlier, she might already be an Immortal by now.”","“Her combat experience is frighteningly high for someone her age. I heard she’s not even a hundred years old, yet she fights like someone who’s lived through millennia of battle.”","Yuan could hear the murmurs of the sect elders watching from the sidelines, their voices laced with awe and deep respect for Li Jinxi’s talent and rapid rise.","Eventually, the sparring ended in a draw.","“As amazing as always, Lady Ji.” The sect elder clasped his hands together and gave her a polite bow.","“Thank you for your time.” Ji Linxi returned the bow.","“No, the pleasure is mine. It’s an honor to exchange swords with a genius like you. By the way, my grandson, who’s a Core Disciple here, asked me to—”","The sect elder abruptly stopped mid-sentence, his gaze shifting as he noticed Li Jinxi had turned her head, her attention clearly fixed elsewhere.","Everyone quickly noticed her sudden distraction and turned to see what had caught her attention, only to find an unfamiliar, strikingly handsome man standing there, someone none of them recognized.","“I didn’t think you’d actually come see me,” Li Jinxi suddenly said.","“Why wouldn’t I?”","“You visited everyone but me, and that was a month ago.”","“That’s... I was going to visit you sooner, but I ended up staying with Yu Rou for longer than anticipated...”","“Relax, I’m aware. I was just joking with you.”","Yuan was speechless. Li Jinxi wasn’t the type to joke around.","‘How much has she changed since we last met?’ he wondered inwardly.","“Do you remember our arrangements?” Li Jinxi suddenly asked.","“Of course. I’ll take you on anytime.”","“Then meet me at the place you sparred with Senior Kelan a month ago tomorrow,” she said before flying away.","“...”","Yuan could only stand there with a dazed look on his face.","“Excuse me, but who are you?” One of the sect elders suddenly asked, snapping him out of his daze.","“I’m just a guest.”","After saying that, Yuan activated Shadow Veil and disappeared before them like a ghost.","The following day, Yuan made his way to the white space training ground. Not seeing Li Jinxi outside, he decided to head inside to check if she was already there.","Sure enough, once inside, he could see Li Jinxi standing not far away with the Golden Empress already in her grasp.","“Before we begin, I want to make one thing clear—fight me with everything you have from the very start,” Li Jinxi said calmly, her gaze locked with Yuan’s. “If you hold back or look down on me... I won’t forgive you.”","Yuan gave a silent nod in response, his expression unreadable.","Join Privilege for 50 Adv Chapters! Only Available in the App!"]},{"number":2004,"title":"Chapter 2004: Li Jinxi’s True Feelings","paragraphs":["\"Come at me whenever you’re ready.\" Li Jinxi said as she unleashed her full cultivation and as much Immortal Qi as she could muster without going out of control.","However, despite her seemingly confident expression, Li Jinxi already knew that she wouldn’t be able to defeat Yuan, who could fight on par with God Ascension cultivators.","In response, Yuan retrieved Number One Under Heaven and activated God of War’s Astral Arts from the get-go.","\"Here I come,\" Yuan warned her before speeding toward her.","Li Jinxi raised her sword high and swung with all her might, unleashing a powerful technique that made the very air around them tremble with its force.","Yet with a single, effortless motion, Yuan swung his sword, shattering her technique completely, as though it were no more than a breeze before a storm.","Li Jinxi gritted her teeth and unleashed one technique after another in rapid succession, each strike fueled by relentless determination.","But Yuan didn’t even bother to defend. He continued to approach her, allowing every attack to land directly on his body, unflinching, as if her efforts couldn’t even reach him.","\"Damn it!\"","Li Jinxi roared as she unleashed her strongest technique.","[Golden Empress’ Absolute Decree!]","Suddenly, a golden energy surged around the Golden Empress in Li Jinxi’s grasp, radiating a powerful pressure that rippled through the air.","Had she unleashed this technique during her spar with the sect elder the day before, there was no doubt she would have claimed victory with ease.","However, Li Jinxi didn’t stop there and infused the energy with Immortal Qi and Enhanced Sword Aura.","Seeing this, Yuan tightened his grip on his sword, his eyes narrowing as he prepared to meet her strike head-on.","In the next moment, Yuan swung his sword, channeling Immortal Qi through the blade and layering it with Enhanced Sword Aura.","A split second later, their swords collided, unleashing a shockwave so powerful it sent ripples through the air and carved fractures into the very fabric of space around them.","Li Jinxi had expected to hold her ground for at least a few seconds, but the instant their swords collided, the overwhelming force behind Yuan’s strike shattered her balance. Before she could react, her body was hurled through the air, utterly powerless to resist.","Li Jinxi coughed up a mouthful of blood, her body trembling as she struggled to rise to her feet.","’So I couldn’t even withstand a single strike from him, huh?’","Li Jinxi let out a quiet breath and stopped trying to stand. Instead, she remained on the ground, her gaze drifting upward as she stared into the endless white space, her expression dazed.","Seeing this, Yuan withdrew his sword and approached her.","\"Are you okay?\" he asked gently.","\"No, I’m not,\" she replied without hesitation. \"No matter how hard I try, no matter how much effort I put in... I still can’t seem to catch up to you.\"","\"Why are you so hung up on catching up? It’s not like I will leave you behind or anything,\" Yuan said. \"In fact, you’re soaring when compared to the others.\"","She glared at him and said, \"How else am I supposed to get you to accept me?\"","\"What?\" Yuan raised his eyebrows, puzzled by her words.","\"If it isn’t obvious by now, I have regained my memories as Jin Xi,\" she said. \"And with them came everything she carried, such as her experiences... and her feelings for you.\"","\"I’m well aware of that... but those memories belong to your previous life.\"","\"So what?\" she snapped, her voice trembling with frustration. \"Are you saying I should just cast aside everything I felt and experienced back then? Even if that life ended and we’ve been reborn, we’re still the same soul—still the same people.\"","She took a breath, her eyes locked onto his.","\"What about Meixiu and Chu Liuxiang? You accepted them in this life. So why can’t you accept me?\"","Yuan let out a quiet sigh and said, \"While it’s true that my feelings for them have strengthened after regaining my memories, I’ve known and loved them long before my memories returned. Their feelings for me... they were already there, even before they began recalling anything from their past lives.\"","He paused for a moment, his gaze steady as he continued.","\"But you...\"","He stopped there—not because he didn’t want to continue, but because he couldn’t. Yuan didn’t know Li Jinxi’s feelings well enough to say more.","When they had first met, she had seemed like nothing more than a battle fanatic. Their relationship had never felt like anything deeper than companionship, similar to how he viewed the other members of the Demon Sealing Faction, though perhaps... just slightly more.","If Li Jinxi’s feelings for him had only awakened after regaining Jin Xi’s memories, then to Yuan, it felt less like love born naturally, and more like something inherited, even forced, and he wasn’t sure how to respond to it.","Li Jinxi quickly understood what he was trying to say.","\"So you think I only feel this way because of my past life?\" she asked, her voice tight with emotion.","She clenched her fists before shouting, \"That’s not true! I’ve had these feelings for you long before my memories as Jin Xi returned! I just... I’ve never been good with words—or expressing my feelings.\"","Her voice softened, and her face flushed with redness as she continued.","\"Yes, Jin Xi’s memories helped me understand my emotions better, and they strengthened what I already felt—but don’t think for a second that I didn’t already love you before then...\"","Li Jinxi’s mind drifted back to their first encounter on the stage at the Jaded Garden.","At the time, she hadn’t recognized it for what it was, but she eventually realized that she had started falling for him in he middle of that very battle, and that feeling would only continue to grow as they continued to spar and spend more time with each other.","Unfortunately, fighting was the only thing she excelled at. To others, it may have seemed like she viewed Yuan as nothing more than a rival, someone to challenge and chase. But in truth, it had always been more than that, and she just never knew how to show it."]},{"number":2005,"title":"Chapter 2005: A New Addition to the Family","paragraphs":["After listening to Li Jinxi’s confession, Yuan smiled and said, \"I’m flattered you feel that way about me, but I wasn’t doubting your feelings.\"","He continued, \"After all, even though I have reincarnated many times, the feelings my incarnations experienced and their emotions are still mine, but not everyone will think like me. I just wanted to make sure that was what you really wanted.\"","\"I am certain that’s what I want,\" she responded with a serious face.","\"I see...\"","\"So...\" Li Jinxi sat up and stared at him intently, clearly waiting for his response.","Yuan extended his hands toward her and smiled, \"I was unable to answer Jin Xi’s feelings because I lacked the courage before, and I lost her before I could. This time, however, I will not make the same mistake.\"","Li Jinxi gently took his hand, her voice barely above a whisper.","\"Does that mean—\"","Before she could finish, Yuan pulled her to her feet—and straight into his arms. Without a word, he leaned in and pressed a soft, tender kiss to her lips.","Li Jinxi’s eyes widened with surprise, but she quickly closed her eyes to enjoy the moment.","’Ah... so this is what it feels like to be finally accepted...’","Jin Xi had spent thousands of years chasing after Tian Xin, only to meet a lonely, unfulfilled end, so one could only imagine the fulfillment Li Jinxi, who had her experience and emotions, was feeling at this moment.","\"Let’s go back to my place...\" Li Jinxi said afterward.","She wanted to embrace him on the spot, but she was afraid that someone else might enter the training ground and witness it.","Yuan nodded, and the two of them left the training ground the next moment.","Once they arrived at her living quarters, Li Jinxi brought Yuan directly to the bedroom, where she immediately removed her robes, revealing her defined and flawlessly toned body.","\"W-What do you think...?\" she asked, her face flushed with redness.","\"It’s beautiful.\" Yuan smiled before kissing her all over her body.","Once Yuan was finished, Li Jinxi swapped roles and began licking all of his body.","Many moments later, Yuan inserted his sword into her scabbard, connecting their bodies together.","The room soon echoed with Li Jinxi’s blissful cries, a sound so pure and unrestrained, unlike anything she had ever made before.","Time slipped by unnoticed as they lost themselves in waves of pleasure, the outside world forgotten. Before they realized it, days had passed.","Though it was her first experience, Li Jinxi’s monstrous endurance allowed her to cultivate with him for days without rest.","\"It’s a pity that my first experience is through my avatar...\" Li Jinxi sighed.","\"Does it really matter? It feels no different from your real body,\" Yuan commented.","\"No, there is a difference.\"","\"...\"","Yuan couldn’t refute her words. Once a cultivator reached a certain level, the subtle flaws in an avatar became apparent. Though it might feel identical to a real body at first, there were nuanced differences.","After all, no matter how powerful a formation might be, it was impossible to perfectly replicate one’s physical body using only the soul.","\"What are you going to do now?\" Li Jinxi asked him.","\"I’ll continue to stay here until I have a solid plan.\"","\"I see... By the way...\" Li Jinxi paused, a hint of nervousness creeping into her voice. \"Which of us is going to tell Meixiu and Liuxiang about this...?\"","Caught up in the moment, she had completely forgotten that Yuan already had two official partners. And now, she had crossed that line with him... without ever speaking to them first.","Yuan smiled and said, \"We can do it together.\"","\"Do you think they’ll be angry...?\" she asked.","\"It’s not impossible, but it’s unlikely, since they’re just like you.\"","Li Jinxi felt slightly better and silently nodded, but she wasn’t completely relieved.","Some time later, Yuan and Li Jinxi met up with Meixiu and Chu Liuxiang.","\"Um... this might be sudden, but I’ve decided to accept Li Jinxi into the family,\" Yuan said, getting straight to the point without hesitation.","\"...\"","Chu Liuxiang and Meixiu didn’t respond immediately. Instead, they turned to face each other and exchanged silent glances, their expressions unreadable.","\"Sorry, I know I should’ve come to you two first for permission, but I—\"","Just as Li Jinxi opened her mouth to speak, Chu Liuxiang smiled and said, \"Why do you need our permission? It’s not like we own him. If he accepted you, then that’s that.\"","Meixiu nodded and added, \"We have long accepted the fact that he’ll add more people into the family. Honestly, I’m a little surprised it took this long.\"","Chu Liuxiang chuckled and continued, \"Right? I was expecting you to join the family long ago.\"","Li Jinxi was speechless. She never thought they’d be so calm and accepting. However, now that she thought about it, the two of them wouldn’t have been able to co-exist with each other if they couldn’t accept Yuan having multiple partners.","\"Anyway, welcome to the family, Jinxi,\" Meixiu said.","\"Thank you...\"Li Jinxi didn’t know what else to say.","\"So, who else do you plan on adding to the family?\" Chu Liuxiang turned to look at Yuan.","He responded with a weird smile, \"Don’t make it sound like I have a list of potential partners. I don’t have anything planned.\"","\"Considering how many lives you’ve lived, I wouldn’t be surprised if we have a few more additions to the family soon,\" she chuckled.","After chatting for a while, Li Jinxi and Chu Liuxiang eventually returned to their own living quarters, leaving Yuan to spend the week with Meixiu.","The following week, he devoted his time to Chu Liuxiang, and then to Li Jinxi the week after.","In the blink of an eye, two months had passed, and it was once again time to visit Yu Rou and the others at the Myriad of Techniques.","However, upon their arrival, an unexpected figure appeared.","\"Yuan? You’re back?\"","It was none other than Senior Bai."]},{"number":2006,"title":"Chapter 2006: Faceless Sword Emperor","paragraphs":["\"It’s been a while, Senior Bai.\" Yuan greeted him with a warm smile.","\"Indeed, it has been a while. Last I heard from you, you were still in the Sixth Heaven. Where are you right now?\" Senior Bai asked.","\"I’m currently in the Seventh Heaven, and I’ve been staying at Kelan’s sect for the last several months,\" he said.","\"What?\" Senior Bai frowned after hearing this. \"You’ve been at Kelan’s place for several months already? How come I didn’t hear anything about this from him?\"","\"Oh, he went into seclusion shortly after I showed up.\"","Senior Bai rubbed his eyes and sighed, \"That meathead... he should’ve at least notified me about your return before he went into seclusion.\"","Yuan chuckled before asking, \"How have you been?\"","\"Same as usual, but I’ve been spending more time at my sect,\" he said.","\"Your sect... that would be the Gates of Heaven, correct?\" Yuan recalled participating in a trial that required him to fight a disciple from this sect.","\"Yes, that’s correct. Whenever you have the time, you should visit. There’s one within the Seventh Heaven, as well.\"","\"As well? There’s more than one Gates of Heaven?\" Chu Liuxiang asked.","Senior Bai nodded and explained, \"I have three sects, one in the Fifth Heaven, the Seventh Heaven, and the Ninth Heaven. Of course, they all share the same name and are essentially the same sect.\"","\"What is the purpose of having three sects?\" Bai Lianhua asked out of curiosity.","\"It’s quite pointless to have multiple sects if you place them all in the same realm. However, if you spread them apart, you’ll be able to gain many more disciples. Also, it gives those in the lower heavens another method of ascending.\"","\"I see...\" Bai Lianhua muttered, as she’d been contemplating branching out her faction recently.","Senior Bai turned to look at Yuan and continued, \"The next Sword Emperor Qualifications will be happening soon, and it’ll take place within the Gates of Heaven. You use the sword, right? You might learn a thing or two if you go.\"","\"Sword Emperor Qualifications? What is that?\" Li Jinxi asked, her curiosity piqued.","Senior Bai then explained, \"In the world of swordmasters, the highest attainable title is the Sword Emperor, much like how blacksmiths have the title God of Creation, and alchemists have the God of Alchemy. The Sword Emperor is, in essence, the God of Swords. However, there can be multiple Sword Emperors.\"","\"The Sword Emperor Qualification is exactly what it sounds like—an event where swordmasters compete for the chance to earn the title of Sword Emperor.\"","\"Sword Emperor...\" Yuan muttered.","Li Jinxi glanced over at Yuan. In Jin Xi’s memories, Tian Xin also acquired the title of Sword Emperor. In fact, he was the strongest Sword Emperor in history.","\"How does one join this event?\" Yuan suddenly asked.","Senior Bai smiled and said, \"Are you looking to join? Unfortunately, even with your talents, it’d be impossible for you to join in your current state. Only those who have achieved Supreme Sword Aura may join, after all.\"","\"Supreme Sword Aura, huh? Indeed, I can’t use that right now. However, if I have enough time...\" Yuan showed a confident smile. \"When is the event happening?\"","\"It’s going to happen in seven years.\"","\"Seven years?\" Yuan raised his eyebrows. \"I thought you said it’d be soon. That’s quite far away.\"","\"Seven years is nothing for Immortals like me.\"","\"I guess that’s true. Anyway, seven years should be more than enough for me to master Supreme Sword Aura,\" Yuan said casually.","Senior Bai stared at him, utterly dumbfounded. He couldn’t believe what he was hearing. Most cultivators spent their entire lives unable to even grasp Enhanced Sword Aura, let alone Supreme Sword Aura. And the participants in the Sword Emperor Qualification? Nearly all of them would be God Ascension realm experts who had lived for tens of thousands of years.","\"Well, if you’re truly serious about mastering Supreme Sword Aura,\" Senior Bai said thoughtfully, \"then you should visit the Holy Sword Temple. It’s a unique place that exists beyond the bounds of the Nine Heavens, and nearly every Sword Emperor throughout history has gone there to learn their Supreme Sword Aura. In fact, the strongest Sword Emperor in history, the Faceless Sword Emperor, also trained there.\"","\"Faceless Sword Emperor...\" Yuan raised his eyebrows at this title.","Senior Bai mistook Yuan’s reaction as intrigue and explained, \"The Faceless Sword Emperor earned his title because he always wore a mask and almost nobody knew his true identity. He had other titles such as the Undefeated Sword Emperor and the Mystical Sword Emperor. He’s one of the most revered figures in the world of swordmasters.\"","Li Jinxi couldn’t help but smile after hearing this. The Faceless Sword Emperor was, without doubt, Tian Xin.","Senior Bai continued, \"No one knows where the Faceless Sword Emperor came from—only that from the very beginning of his recorded history, he lived as an undefeated prodigy. However, just as mysterious as his rise was his disappearance. After attaining the title of Sword Emperor, he vanished without a trace, almost as if he had never existed at all.\"","He lifted his head to look at the clear blue sky and sighed, \"To tell you the truth, I’ve encountered him once. However, he was just passing by, and I was only a snooty little brat back then. Though I was a mortal, I could tell how formidable he was at a glance. He was a true monster—one that might rival even you, Yuan.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"Alright, I’ve decided. I’ll visit the Holy Sword Temple next.\"","Of course, it wasn’t solely because he wanted to participate in the Sword Emperor Qualifications. If he wanted to fight and kill God Ascension realm cultivators, he’d need to learn Supreme Sword Aura eventually.","\"I should’ve mentioned this first, but not just anyone can enter the Holy Sword Temple. You’ll need a referral and then pass a test before you can train there,\" Senior Bai suddenly said."]},{"number":2007,"title":"Chapter 2007: The Great One’s Appearance","paragraphs":["\"Referral? From whom?\" Yuan asked.","\"Only Sword Emperors and reputable swordmasters are allowed to give out referrals. Fortunately, we have someone in the faction who can give you a referral. I’ll contact them after this.\"","\"Okay. What about the test?\"","\"Oh, it’s quite simple. Your Enhanced Sword Aura just needs to be powerful enough to damage the Sword Wall at the Holy Sword Temple.\"","\"I see. Should be doable.\"","\"By the way, what is your cultivation at right—\" Senior Bai stopped his sentence midway when Yuan exuded some of his cultivation, as he’d been suppressing it.","\"Peak of Immortal Ascension?!\" Senior Bai almost couldn’t believe his eyes. The last time they met, Yuan was still in the Spirit Realm.","’His cultivation increased by an entire Major Realm in less than a decade?! At this rate, he’ll become an Immortal by our next meeting!’","\"Is my cultivation not enough?\" Yuan asked.","\"No, there shouldn’t be any problems as long as you can use Enhanced Sword Aura.\"","Yuan nodded.","\"Then there’s no problem.\"","He showed off his Enhanced Sword Aura, which had reached its maximum mastery long ago.","\"Even in the Ninth Heaven, only a handful of prodigies have ever managed to attain Enhanced Sword Aura before reaching the Immortal Realm,\" Senior Bai said, swallowing nervously. \"But none of them could hold a candle to your level.\"","\"That’s only natural,\" Chu Liuxiang remarked in a prideful tone, acting like she was the one being praised.","\"By the way... about what happened at the Dragon Spiral Mountain...\" Senior Bai suddenly brought up the topic, his tone more serious now. It was an incident witnessed by the Celestial Overlords, after all.","\"Are you okay? Do you know why the Heaven’s Mandate and the Celestial Emperor showed up, even causing such a major scene?\"","Though Yuan trusted Senior Bai deeply enough to entrust his life to him, he chose not to reveal everything. He didn’t want to drag him into such a dangerous matter, especially with the Celestial Overlord’s situation.","\"I don’t know why, but I think the Celestial Emperor doesn’t want me in the Nine Heavens,\" he said while shaking his head.","Senior Bai became silent. He was aware of the Celestial Emperor’s Curse, and while he never figured out why the Celestial Emperor would target Yuan, he knew there was something between them.","\"If you ever find yourself in a situation that you cannot handle alone, don’t hesitate to rely on us—on the Celestial Overlords. Regardless of your rank, you’re still one of us, so as long as you didn’t commit any crimes, we’ll back you with our full power.\"","Senior Bai could tell that Yuan wasn’t revealing everything, but he didn’t press. He trusted Yuan—and believed that, when the time was right, he would share the truth on his own terms.","Yuan offered a grateful smile and said, \"I’ll keep that in mind. Thank you.\"","\"Anyway, I won’t intrude on your time any longer. I’ll leave now to speak with that individual who will give you a referral.\"","With that, Senior Bai left shortly after.","\"Looks like you’ll be busy again soon, brother.\" Yu Rou sighed.","\"Senior Bai didn’t mention how long it’ll take for him to get that referral, so I might still have some time left to spend with you,\" he said.","Not wanting to waste any time, they began chatting with each other, talking about their recent experiences and future plans.","Eventually, everyone but Yu Rou and Yuan left. The siblings spent the next week with each other like their last meeting.","\"If I don’t show up for the next meeting, that means I have already left.\"","\"Don’t worry, I’ll be okay... even if I’ll be a little lonely,\" Yu Rou said softly as she embraced him. \"Now that you’ve regained your body, the thing I worried about most is finally behind us.\"","Meanwhile, after he left, Senior Bai reported to Xu Jiaqi about Yuan’s return and Kelan’s blunder.","\"I see... so he’s regained his true body and traveled to the Nine Heavens with it...\" Xu Jiaqi muttered to herself after hearing the report, a sense of relief washing over her.","\"By the way, did you ask him about what happened at the Dragon Spiral Mountain?\" she suddenly asked.","\"Yes, but he didn’t say much. However, he’s definitely hiding something, though.\"","Xu Jiaqi sighed, \"It’s fine. He probably doesn’t want to cause us any trouble. My father was also like that. He’d always try to solve everything on his own.\"","\"Now then, about the Holy Sword Temple... I’ll contact that person myself,\" she continued.","Senior Bai smiled and said, \"That’s relieving to hear. I don’t want to deal with that eccentric person.\"","\"I know,\" she calmly remarked.","Some time later, after finishing her current work, Xu Jiaqi left to find this eccentric person to give Yuan the referral.","Meanwhile, at the Azure Dragon Clan, just as peace had become the norm, an unfathomable presence suddenly descended out of nowhere, blanketing their entire territory in a suffocating pressure.","Upon sensing the overwhelming presence, everyone in the city froze in terror. Not a single soul dared to move, let alone glance around in search of the source, as immense fear gripped their hearts.","Jiao Zhenhai and the others immediately stopped their cultivation and rushed out of their residences, moving toward the source of the presence, which was rapidly closing in on them.","However, despite the audacity with which this individual had unleashed their presence across the Azure Dragon Clan’s territory, not a single member felt offended, nor did they approach with anger. Instead, they felt a deep sense of humility, as if standing in the presence of something far beyond themselves.","Moments later, Jiao Zhenhai and the other clan members came face to face with the individual. He stood half-naked, his upper torso exposed, revealing a physique so flawless it was as though heaven itself had craved it. His long, golden hair flowed behind him with unnatural grace, swaying gently as if caught in a soft breeze, even though they were all submerged in water.","\"The Azure Dragon Clan humbly greets the Great One!\" Jiao Zhenhai and the others called out in unison, their heads lowered in deep submission and reverence, their voices echoing with solemn respect."]},{"number":2008,"title":"Chapter 2008: The Great One’s Appearance(2)","paragraphs":["Despite the Great One’s seemingly sudden appearance, the Azure Dragon Clan was not surprised at all. In fact, they’d anticipated his appearance when they learned that it was Dragon Goddess Yeyou who had stopped the Mystic Sea Dragon Clan’s invasion from Yuan.","The Great One narrowed his golden eyes, his naturally arrogant gaze sweeping over the Azure Dragon Clan like he had absolute authority over them.","\"So, you’ve anticipated my arrival, have you?\" he said, his voice calm yet imposing. \"Then you must also know why I’m here. Let’s not waste time and tell me what I want to know. Is it true that Dragon Goddess Yeyou appeared here recently?\"","\"Yes, that is correct.\" Jiao Zhenhai didn’t dare to lie before the Great One since he could see through everything.","\"Tell me everything, and do it from the very beginning. If you dare try to mislead me or leave even the slightest details out, I’ll completely wipe your bloodline from existence. Do I make myself clear?\"","The Great One’s aura surged in a threatening manner.","Jiao Zhenhai and the others trembled beneath the weight of the Great One’s overwhelming presence. Knowing full well that this being did not bluff or tolerate deceit, Zhenhai quickly recalled everything—from the moment their family had been poisoned by the Mystic Sea Dragon Clan, to their fateful encounter with Yuan, and ultimately, the appearance of Dragon Goddess Yeyou herself, which ended up driving the Mystic Sea Dragon Clan away.","\"Yuan...\" The Great One narrowed his eyes after hearing this familiar name.","However, no matter how vast his experience or knowledge, there was simply no way he could have linked Yuan’s existence to the Immortal Monarch—even with all the information he had been given.","Even with the information that Yuan possessed the Immortal Monarch’s blood, he assumed it had been bestowed upon him by Dragon Goddess Yeyou.","’I need more information.’","The Great One set his sights on the Holy Dragon Clan next.","Before leaving the Azure Dragon Clan, the Great One said, \"Since you’ve experienced Dragon Goddess Yeyou’s prowess first-hand, I want you to do some quick comparison.\"","Without warning, he suddenly unleashed a surge of his aura, so immense that it didn’t just engulf the Azure Dragon Clan’s territory, but swept across the entire Sea of Dragons like a tidal wave.","The sudden eruption of aura startled every living entity within the sea, sending beasts and cultivators alike fleeing from his direction as if their very lives depended on it.","Within the Azure Dragon Clan, the pressure was unbearable and so overwhelming that even the strongest among them coughed up mouthfuls of blood. Not even a God Ascension realm cultivator like Jiao Zhenhai was spared.","Fortunately, the Great One quickly retracted his aura a second later, or everyone around him would’ve died from the pressure alone.","\"If you were to compare my aura to that of Dragon Goddess Yeyou,\" the Great One asked, his voice devoid of guilt or apology, \"how did I measure up? Would you say I’m stronger?\"","After taking a moment to catch his breath, Jiao Zhenahi responded, \"Your aura was definitely stronger than what I felt from Dragon Goddess Yeyou.\"","A satisfied smile tugged at the corners of the Great One’s handsome face. Without another word, he turned and soared away—his figure cutting through the water like it didn’t exist as he headed straight toward the Holy Dragon Clan.","\"...\"","A heavy silence lingered over the Azure Dragon Clan and the Underwater City, persisting long after the Great One had departed.","Eventually, Jiao Zhenhai let out a deep, weary sigh. \"I have the feeling that even if we had succeeded in claiming the Dragon Spiral Mountain, the Great One still wouldn’t have offered us his help.\"","The others silently nodded, agreeing with him.","A few days later, the Great One arrogantly announced his arrival by engulfing the entire Dragon Spiral Mountain in his overwhelming presence, just as he did to the Azure Dragon Clan.","Immediately, the Holy Dragon Emperor approached him and greeted, \"The Holy Dragon Clan greets the Great One.\"","The Great One narrowed his eyes and remarked, \"Just like the Azure Dragon Clan, you anticipated my appearance. Did Dragon Goddess Yeyou warn you that I’d show up?\"","\"No, but knowing your history with her, anyone would make this assumption,\" he said.","\"Then you must also know why I am here.\"","\"Yes. It’s true that Dragon Goddess Yeyou has returned.\" The Holy Dragon Emperor admitted.","Based on the Great One’s earlier comment, the Holy Dragon Emperor knew that he had visited the Azure Dragon Clan prior to showing up at the Holy Dragon Clan, so there was no reason to hide it, and it’d only enrage him.","\"Tell me everything you know,\" said the Great One, his overbearing tone leaving no room for discussion.","However, the Holy Dragon Emperor shook his head and said, \"Unfortunately, that is not possible.\"","The Great One narrowed his eyes ever so slightly, fixing the Holy Dragon Emperor with a gaze that radiated silent menace.","\"Since I am in a good mood, I’ll pretend I didn’t hear your last sentence. You better choose your next words wisely, or I might sink the Dragon Spiral Mountain by accident,\" said the Great One as his aura began to surge violently.","\"Who knows? It might even summon Dragon Goddess Yeyou once she learns of it.\"","\"Why are you still chasing after Dragon Goddess Yeyou? I heard she wants nothing to do with you. Aren’t you afraid of incurring her wrath?\"","\"I might have feared her in the past, but things are different now. I don’t know where she has been this entire time, but I am quite certain that I have surpassed her during her absence. Once I find her, I am going to battle and defeat her.\"","In the past, when the Great One pursued Dragon Goddess Yeyou, she would always say that she’d only accept someone stronger than herself, hence why he’d started collecting treasures and using them to strengthen himself."]},{"number":2009,"title":"Chapter 2009: The Great One’s Appearance(3)","paragraphs":["The Holy Dragon Emperor could only sigh inwardly after hearing the Great One’s declaration—that he’d defeat Dragon Goddess Yeyou.","While it was true that Dragon Goddess Yeyou may not have been improving her strength since her disappearance because she’d lost her body, and her soul had split into several parts, nobody could say for certain that the Great One had surpassed her, but it was definitely a possibility.","\"Once I defeat her, I’ll finally obtain the one thing I’ve yearned but failed to claim in this life,\" the Great One declared, his eyes burning with fervent determination.","The Holy Dragon Emperor narrowed his eyes at the Great One’s words, which carried an unsettling undertone, as if he saw Dragon Goddess Yeyou not as a person, but as something to be claimed.","\"In any case, I cannot help you. They didn’t mention where they’d go after leaving the Dragon Spiral Mountain.\"","The smile on the Great One’s face slowly disappeared, and he responded, \"Maybe, but I won’t know for sure until I force it out of you. How many do I have to kill to make you talk? Half?\"","The Holy Dragon Emperor sneered in disdain, \"You may have gotten stronger over the years, but your character has fallen quite lowly, Great One. Even if you kill everyone, my answer will remain the same. I don’t know where Dragon Goddess Yeyou went.\"","The Great One said nothing in return, but his aura surged violently, speaking louder than any words ever could.","The Holy Dragon Emperor wasted no time, instantly transforming into his dragon form. Though he knew full well that the Great One stood as an even greater threat than the Celestial Emperor had been, he refused to retreat. Defeat was likely, but cowering was never an option.","\"It’s been a while since a dragon has dared to defy me, so I’ll enjoy this for a while.\"","Moments later, the Great One and the Holy Dragon Emperor collided in a thunderous clash, their fierce exchanges unleashing shockwaves in every direction, each impact chipping away at the Dragon Spiral Mountain, piece by piece.","\"Heavens! The Great One is attacking us!\"","\"W-What should we do?!\"","The Holy Dragon Clan was thrown into momentary panic, but their hesitation didn’t last. Just like when the Celestial Emperor attacked, they surged forward to assist him, even if their efforts barely made a dent in the overwhelming power of the Great One.","Though the Great One’s individual power surpassed even that of the Celestial Emperor, the Holy Dragon Clan managed to hold out against him far longer than expected. Of course, this endurance was only possible because the Great One was clearly holding back.","If the Great One had gone all out from the beginning, the Holy Dragon Clan would’ve perished almost instantly.","Eventually, the Great One hovered alone above the Dragon Spiral Mountain, his presence dominating the skies. Below him, the Holy Dragon Emperor and the rest of the clan lay scattered across the battered landscape, defeated and motionless, unable to lift even a finger after their overwhelming defeat.","Their fight had attracted many spectators again, though not as many as when the Celestial Emperor attacked.","\"What the hell? Isn’t that the Great One? Why is he attacking the Holy Dragon Clan, too?\"","\"I don’t know what the Holy Dragon Clan did, but to offend both the Celestial Emperor and the Great One... they’re fated to be erased from existence soon.\"","\"And since it’s the Great One, the other Royal Dragon Clans wouldn’t be able to do anything about it.\"","Some time later, the Great One’s voice echoed across the battered peaks, loud and clear, rippling through the mountain like thunder, \"Though I do not wish to do this because of my respect for Dragon Goddess Yeyou, your defiance cannot go unpunished. As retribution, I shall destroy the final Dragon Spiral Mountain in the Nine Heavens.\"","The Great One raised a single finger, and in an instant, an overwhelming aura surged from his body. At the tip of his finger, a small orb of condensed energy began to form, glowing intensely. It rapidly expanded, growing larger and brighter until it blazed in the sky like a miniature sun, radiating power that shook the heavens.","Moments later, the Great One gave a casual flick of his finger, and the blazing miniature sun shot through the air toward the mountain. As it descended, the heat radiating from it was so intense that it caused the surrounding sea to boil violently, sending waves of steam rising into the heavens.","The Holy Dragon Clan could do nothing but watch in helpless silence as the blazing sun descended upon them. One by one, they began to close their eyes—not out of fear, but in solemn acceptance of the death they could no longer escape.","However, amid the chaos and impending doom, a lone figure silently appeared between the descending sun and the Dragon Spiral Mountain like a ghost.","He was small in stature, appearing no older than a young teenager, yet his eyes gleamed with ancient knowledge and unfathomable experience. Strangely, he emitted no presence whatsoever, and his body was semi-transparent, as if he didn’t exist within the fabric of reality itself.","Though the Holy Dragon Clan failed to notice him because of his lack of presence, the Great One did not.","The moment his eyes fell upon the small figure, his body tensed, and a flicker of something rare flashed in his eyes: hesitation. Without a word, he clenched his fists, and in an instant, the blazing sun above dissipated, abruptly canceling his attack.","\"What is the meaning of this?\" The Great One spoke with a frown on his face.","\"It’d be problematic if you were to destroy the Dragon Spiral Mountain,\" said the young teenager.","\"I wasn’t talking about the Dragon Spiral Mountain. Why are you here?\"","\"Isn’t it obvious? I’m here to stop you.\"","\"With an avatar that doesn’t even have an ounce of power?\" The Great One sneered. \"Are you looking down on me?\"","\"You’re right. I don’t have any power in this state, so I cannot physically stop your actions. However, I can offer you a word of advice. If you were to destroy the Dragon Spiral Mountain, Senior Sister Yeyou will not forgive you,\" said the young teenager.","\"You speak as if it’s a certainty. Both you and Yeyou vanished without a trace after that bastard’s era came to an end—only to reappear now, at the exact same time?\" The Great One’s eyes narrowed, voice edged with suspicion and frustration.","\"What is the meaning of this... Dragon Ancestor?\"","The Great One’s last words shocked all of the spectators. Nobody there could’ve anticipated the reappearance of the Dragon Ancestor.","\"That teenager is the Dragon Ancestor?! The third Dragon of Origin?!\"","\"I thought he died long ago!\"","\"No, he simply disappeared, just like Dragon Goddess Yeyou. For both of them to show up now... something big will happen in the Nine Heavens very soon...\"","As murmurs of concern spread among the spectators, the Dragon Ancestor finally spoke, his tone calm but laced with biting sarcasm, \"Are you upset we didn’t include you? Feeling left out?\"","He paused, his gaze unflinching.","\"Well, maybe that wouldn’t have happened if you hadn’t spent those days hounding Senior Sister Yeyou like some lovesick, perverted maniac.\"","The Great One trembled, his eyes flaring with rage.","\"Do not mock my feelings for her!\" he roared.","\"I am not mocking you. I am merely reminding you why Senior Sister Yeyou despised you and why she ultimately chose to keep you out of our group. And if you continue to chase after her like you did in the past... I doubt she’ll be able to resist killing you.\"","\"Hahaha! Kill me?! Maybe she had that power in the past, but things are different now! I am stronger than her!\" The Great One laughed.","The Dragon Ancestor merely shook his head with a pitiful smile, \"Oh, you ignorant one. Senior Sister Yeyou’s power is far more than you can fathom, and what you witnessed in the past was merely a fraction of her true power since neither you nor I was strong enough to make her fight seriously.\"","\"...\"","The Great One was left speechless, his eyes widening in disbelief.","’What she showed me... was only a fraction of her true strength?’","Even for someone like him, such a thought was difficult to accept—nearly unfathomable.","The Dragon Ancestor suddenly glanced down at his body, watching as it began to fade, his form slowly unraveling into fragments of light.","\"Looks like my time is running out,\" he muttered, then lifted his gaze to meet the Great One’s.","\"If you truly intend to destroy the Dragon Spiral Mountain, there’s nothing I can do to stop you. However, bear this in mind—that Senior Sister Yeyou would skin you alive if you did. And instead of chasing after her, why don’t you come find me? I’ll share with you one of Senior Sister Yeyou’s greatest secrets.\"","Before the Great One could respond, the Dragon Ancestor’s body vanished as if he had never existed in the first place.","\"...\"","The Great One continued to hover above the Dragon Spiral Mountain long after the Dragon Ancestor had faded, his expression unreadable as he lingered in silence, lost in deep thought.","Eventually, the Great One clicked his tongue in annoyance, and without saying a word, he vanished from the skies above the Dragon Spiral Mountain, leaving behind only the weight of his presence and the silence that followed.","The Holy Dragon Emperor could only stare at the sky in disbelief.","\"Looks like we’re fated to continue serving Dragon Goddess Yeyou...\" he mumbled."]},{"number":2010,"title":"Chapter 2010: The Dragon Ancestor’s Unexpected Appearance","paragraphs":["Shortly after the second incident, news of the events at the Dragon Spiral Mountain spread through the Nine Heavens like wildfire.","\"You will not believe what just happened at the Dragon Spiral Mountain!\"","\"Aren’t you a little late to the party? I heard about that literally a day after it happened several months ago.\"","\"No! This is a new incident that just happened recently! This time, it was the Great One who attacked the Holy Dragon Clan at the Dragon Spiral Mountain!\"","\"Heavens! The Great One? You’re lying! For dragons like them, that’s even worse than offending the Celestial Emperor! After all, not even the Royal Dragon Clans could do anything about it!\"","\"I’m serious! Not only that, but the Dragon Ancestor, who was thought to have died long ago, also made an appearance! Though, he was in the form of an avatar, so something might’ve happened to his physical body.\"","\"The Dragon Ancestor is back?! We’d just received news of Dragon Goddess Yeyou’s return! What in heaven’s name is happening in the Nine Heavens?!\"","News of the Dragon Ancestor’s appearance sent unprecedented shockwaves throughout the Nine Heavens—far greater than those caused by the mention of Dragon Goddess Yeyou—primarily because his name carried even greater fame and influence.","Unlike the Great One, who lived a selfish life, and Dragon Goddess Yeyou, who lived a secluded one, the Dragon Ancestor was the only one who communicated with and offered assistance to the other dragon clans.","To many dragon clans, he was regarded as their forefather—the true Dragon of Origin. Beyond that, the Dragon Ancestor had established his own lineage, one that continues to reign as the foremost dragon clan in all of the Nine Heavens. His influence was nothing short of unfathomable.","Upon hearing of the Dragon Ancestor’s return and his words to ’find him’—even though they were meant for the Great One—the Ten Royal Dragon Clans wasted no time, dispatching their armies across the Nine Heavens in a relentless search for his whereabouts.","Naturally, the Celestial Emperor became even more cautious when he received this news.","Meanwhile, while the entire world was in an uproar, Yuan continued to spend his time with his own people, especially his partners, spending most of his time in the bedroom with them.","A month passed since his meeting with Senior Bai, a familiar figure appeared at the Super Perfect Physique Tempering Sect.","It was none other than Xi Meili.","\"Sister Meili!\" Feng Yuxiang was very happy to see her.","\"Hello, everyone. I’m sorry it took this long for me to come here. I had to travel the Seventh Heaven without using any teleportation formations, which took a while,\" she apologized.","\"Are you okay? I hear you were in the fight with Heaven’s Mandate,\" Yuan asked her.","She nodded, \"Thankfully. If it weren’t for Yin and Yang, I would’ve definitely died that day,\" she sighed.","\"What about Dong Ye? Do you know where he’s at?\" he then asked.","\"We went our separate ways once I was close enough to you guys. Unfortunately, he didn’t tell me anything before leaving.\"","\"That’s fine. He’s a crafty and cautious person. He’ll return to us soon.\"","With Xi Meili’s return, the others began catching up with her.","\"By the way, did you hear? The Great One attacked the Dragon Spiral Mountain after the Celestial Emperor, and the Dragon Ancestor showed up to stop him,\" Xi Meili revealed what she heard during her journey.","\"What? The Dragon Ancestor?\" Yuan’s eyes widened at this information.","\"Yes, but from what I heard, it was just his avatar, so he didn’t appear in the flesh.\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes and said, \"Either he was too far away, so he sent his avatar, or something happened to his physical body.\"","Xi Meili nodded and added, \"He also told the Great One to find him. However, it could just be a stalling tactic.\"","\"Maybe Yeyou knows something. I will ask her later,\" said Yuan.","\"Okay.\"","And shortly after Xi Meili’s appearance, Kelan emerged from his seclusion. Though his cultivation remained the same, his aura had changed drastically since his seclusion.","\"Yuan! Let’s fight again!\"","The first thing he did after coming out of seclusion was ask for a fight.","\"Sure.\" Yuan immediately accepted since he was also itching for a fight after spending so much time in the bedroom.","Yuan and Kelan met up at the white training ground the following day. The others also showed up to spectate.","\"Although I lost to you last time, I have a good feeling the results will be different this time,\" Kelan proudly declared as they stood a dozen meters away from each other.","Yuan smiled and said, \"You’d better have improved drastically after learning such a precious technique.\"","Kelan fell silent for a moment.","Then, with a solemn expression, he said, \"I know I shouldn’t pry, but my curiosity won’t let me stay quiet. Where in heaven’s name did you obtain this technique, which was believed to be lost to time itself?\"","He quickly added, \"Of course, you don’t have to answer it. I just wanted to get the question off my chest.\"","Yuan then said, \"I acquired it from the Nameless Emperor’s Tomb.\"","\"The Nameless Emperor’s Tomb! To think such a precious treasure has been hiding there for this long. It really makes one wonder what else is hidden in that death trap.\"","Kelan had visited the Nameless Emperor’s Tomb more than once, but each venture yielded nothing of true value. After barely escaping with his life during his last expedition, he swore never to return, as the risks simply outweighed the rewards.","However, upon learning that Yuan had acquired such a priceless technique from that very place, doubt crept into his conviction, and he began to reconsider.","\"Alright, enough yapping from me. Let me show you how far I’ve come with the Great Mammoth Body Refinement Technique!\" Kelan’s aura erupted as his body began to swell, muscles bulging and bones creaking, growing taller and bigger until he resembled that of a true giant."]},{"number":2011,"title":"Chapter 2011: Referral","paragraphs":["Though his size paled in comparison to Kulas during his reign as the Giant Emperor, Kelan had reached a level of mastery that allowed him to amplify both his size and strength in just a few short months, something that required geniuses decades to achieve during the Primordial Era.","\"Come.\"","When Yuan beckoned him, Kelan charged like a sumo wrestler, each thunderous step shaking the ground beneath him. Just like before, Yuan met him head-on, unarmed and relying solely on his body.","Wanting to test the limit of his new technique, Kelan only used his physique and nothing else. He figured he would be able to rival Yuan with his new technique somehow.","Unfortunately for him, it didn’t take long for Kelan to return to reality.","’Fuck! It’s only been a few months, but his physique has gotten even stronger!’","Kelan quickly realized that he wasn’t the only one who had grown stronger during the last few months. Of course, Yuan didn’t do any real training, and the only exercise he did was in the bedroom with his partners and a few light spars with the others. However, his soul and body were still in the process of merging, so he was constantly getting stronger without needing to do anything, much like Feng Yuxiang’s situation.","Yuan smiled and said, \"You may have learned a new technique, but you still haven’t learned your lesson.\"","\"What? What lesson?\" Kelan frowned.","\"To never underestimate me!\" Yuan laughed out loud as he began pushing Kelan back despite the difference in their size.","\"Also, have you already forgotten how you acquired the technique?\"","A profound smile appeared on Yuan’s face as his body suddenly began growing, quickly reaching Kelan’s size.","\"Y-You!\"","Though he knew he shouldn’t be surprised—after all, he had learned the technique from Yuan—Kelan still couldn’t help but be flabbergasted after seeing Yuan use the Great Mammoth Body Refinement Technique.","However, Yuan didn’t remain in his giant form for long and said, \"Though I can use the technique, I don’t like increasing my size to make myself an easier target, and it hinders my mobility, too.\"","Of course, the biggest reason why Yuan stopped using the Great Mammoth Body Refinement Technique was simply because he didn’t need it.","\"What’s wrong? Are you done already?\" Yuan asked when Kelan stopped moving and stood still like an iron statue.","\"A-As you wish!\" Kelan shouted before he resumed his assault.","Since he couldn’t defeat Yuan with the Great Mammoth Body Refinement Technique alone, he began using his martial techniques.","Eventually, he started using his cultivation and Immortal Qi. Yet, the results remained the same, and Yuan continued to push him back.","However, despite how badly he was still losing to Yuan, Kelan refused to use Celestial Qi. It was the one thing he swore he wouldn’t use unless Yuan could use Celestial Qi, as it would be too unfair.","Their sparring lasted for nearly an entire week until Kelan was forced to stop because he received a certain message.","\"Okay, let’s stop here,\" Kelan suddenly said. \"Senior Bai has contacted me, saying that your referral is ready, whatever that means. I was also summoned by Celestial Overlord Xu.\"","\"Oh, I’m going to train at the Holy Sword Temple,\" Yuan explained.","\"D-Did you just say the Holy Sword Temple?! But you’re still a mortal!\"","\"So what? One’s sword understanding has nothing to do with their cultivation. Theoretically, a mortal can use Supreme Sword Aura.\"","\"Yeah, there’s no way...\" Kelan shook his head. \"You may be a monster, but even you cannot learn Supreme Sword Aura at your age.\"","\"Wanna bet?\" Yuan said with a smile.","\"Uhh...\" Kelan instantly hesitated despite his earlier confidence.","\"No... I’m fine.\"","\"What a pity. I was going to bet another lost technique compatible with your giant bloodline.\" Yuan shrugged.","\"WHAT?!\" Kelan exclaimed. \"IS THAT TRUE?!\"","\"It doesn’t matter anymore since you don’t want to bet.\"","\"I’ll bet!\" Kelan hastily changed his mind.","He continued, \"What do you want? If that technique is as valuable as the Great Mammoth Body Refinement Technique, I don’t think I have anything I can use to bet.\"","\"If I win, you’ll let me take a look at your treasury and pick any one treasure I want. How about it?\"","\"Are you sure? I may own a sect, but my treasury is quite lackluster. You will definitely be disappointed,\" he said.","\"That’s up for me to decide.\"","\"Alright. If that’s what you want, don’t complain afterward—not that you’ll win. Also, I’ll give you a hundred years to train at the Holy Sword Temple.\"","Yuan raised his eyebrows.","\"A hundred years? You’re being too generous. You might as well give me the treasure now.\"","Kelan frowned and said, \"Then ten years. You have ten years to learn Supreme Sword Aura.\"","\"Sure.\" Yuan nodded.","Kelan extended his hand and said, \"Let’s shake on it.\"","After shaking on it, they left the training grounds and made their way to the Myriad of Techniques.","The others stayed back so they wouldn’t end up crowding the place.","When they arrived at the Myriad of Techniques, it wasn’t just Senior Bai present, but Xu Jiaqi as well.","\"It’s been a while, Sister Xu.\"","\"...\"","However, Xu Jiaqi didn’t respond. She simply stared at him with wide eyes, frozen in place. Although she had long believed Yuan to be the reincarnation of the Celestial Overlord’s founder, seeing him fully grown left her breathless, and her memories of the founder were forcefully resurfaced.","However, she quickly snapped out of it and said, \"Sorry, but you look just like the Celestial Overlord’s founder. If I had seen you outside, I would have definitely mistaken you for him.\"","She swiftly reached into her spatial ring and retrieved a crimson, sword-shaped badge, its surface etched with ancient symbols. Holding it with both hands, she offered it to him.","\"This is your referral,\" she said. \"Present it to the masters of the Holy Sword Temple, and they will allow you to enter.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Yuan accepted the badge and inspected it with interest."]},{"number":2012,"title":"Chapter 2012: Grand Sword Crater","paragraphs":["\"When will you head to the Holy Sword Temple?\" Xu Jiaqi asked Yuan shortly after giving him the sword-shaped badge.","\"I’ll have to figure out how to get there first,\" he said.","Though he’d been to the Holy Sword Temple before as Tian Xin, he couldn’t recall how to get there.","\"Only the Holy Sword Clan, who owns the place, can bring you to the Holy Sword Temple,\" Xu Jiaqi explained.","\"So I have to contact the Holy Sword Clan, huh? Where do I find them?\"","\"While their main headquarters is in the Ninth Heaven, they also have a branch in the Seventh and Eighth Heaven. You can find them at the Grand Sword Crater.\"","\"The Grand Sword Crater, right? I’ll go find them as soon as possible.\"","\"Good luck. The Holy Sword Clan is known for being eccentric, so try not to cause any trouble. They’re also a top 20 faction with the most swordmasters in the world,\" said Senior Bai.","\"No promises,\" Yuan said with a playful smile.","Yuan left shortly after, leaving Kelan behind.","Once Yuan was gone, Xu Jiaqi turned her attention to Kelan.","\"Now then... Commander Kelan.\"","\"Y-Yes!\"","Kelan subconsciously straightened his back after being called.","\"I’m pretty sure I instructed you to notify me immediately when Yuan returns. Yet, you ignored my order and went straight to seclusion after his return. What do you have to say about that?\" she narrowed her gaze at him.","Kelan lowered his head and apologized, \"I’m sorry. I got too excited when he gave me a technique.\"","\"A technique?\" Senior Bai and Xu Jiaqi raised their eyebrows.","Kelan was extremely picky when it came to learning new techniques, so it was pretty surprising to hear that he’d gotten so excited about a technique that he forgot about his mission.","Though they were intrigued by the technique, they didn’t force Kelan to reveal it since that was his private business with Yuan.","\"I’ll let you go with a warning this time,\" Xu Jiaqi said.","\"Thank you, Celestial Overlord!\"","After returning to the sect, Yuan explained the situation to the others.","\"So you’ll be leaving again soon, huh?\" Chu Liuxiang sighed. Though she knew he would eventually leave again, it didn’t make her feel better when that time finally arrived.","\"I won’t be leaving immediately. I promised Yu Rou that I’d let her know before I leave, so I’ll stay here until our next meeting,\" said Yuan.","Thus, Yuan spent his remaining time in the sect with them until it was time for his meeting with Yu Rou.","At the Myriad of Techniques, Yuan announced his next destination to Yu Rou and the others at the end of their meeting.","\"How long do you think you’ll be gone this time?\" Yu Rou asked.","\"It’s hard to say, but it’ll definitely be at least a few years.\"","\"I see...\" Yu Rou lowered her head for a moment, but she quickly raised her head again and spoke with a calm smile, \"Be safe, brother.\"","\"The same goes for you.\"","Yu Rou went to embrace him the next moment.","\"See you later.\"","After leaving the Myriad of Techniques, Yuan immediately began preparing to head to the Holy Sword Temple.","\"Since I cannot enter your dantian like the others, I’ll stay here and train with the others,\" Xi Meili said to Yuan before he left.","Yuan nodded.","After saying his goodbyes with the others, Yuan left the Super Perfect Physique Tempering Sect and made his way toward the Grand Sword Crater. Unfortunately, there was no teleportation device near his destination, so he could only teleport to the nearest place and travel from there.","After emerging from the teleportation device, Yuan wasted no time and used Feng Yuxiang’s flying treasure to travel.","Three months later, Yuan arrived at his destination.","\"This is the Grand Sword Crater...?\" Feng Yuxiang murmured, her voice filled with awe as her gaze swept across the horizon.","True to its name, the Grand Sword Crater was a monumental sight—a single, flawless gash carved into the land, stretching thousands of miles in length and plunging deep into the earth like a wound left by a heavenly blade.","Though the landscape resembled the aftermath of a cataclysmic battle, the vast fissure was far from abandoned, with countless swordmasters moving busily around and within its depths.","Legend has it that this colossal fissure was carved by a Sword Emperor with a single strike. Now, swordmasters from across the world gather here, hoping to glean insight from the remnants of his might and deepen their own understanding of the sword.","Of course, not every swordmaster came here in pursuit of insight. In truth, the majority sought to attract the attention of the Holy Sword Clan, who frequented the crater in search of talented swordmasters to recruit for their faction.","To draw the attention of the Holy Sword Clan, many swordmasters would periodically release their Sword Aura, feigning moments of insight, while others openly practiced their sword techniques in hopes of being noticed.","\"What a bunch of weirdos,\" Feng Yuxiang remarked when she saw the odd scene before her.","Some time later, Yuan began wandering the Grand Sword Crater in search of the Holy Sword Clan.","\"White and golden robes...\" Yuan occasionally muttered to himself as he used divine sense to quickly scout the area without stopping.","Several days later, Yuan came to a stop when he finally found someone who looked to be from the Holy Sword Clan.","He focused his divine sense on a bald old man clad in elegant white and gold robes adorned with intricate sword engravings.","The old man was surrounded by swordmasters, yet his gaze was fixed on a lone youth quietly cultivating before him, exuding a decent amount of Enhanced Sword Aura.","\"Not bad... not bad at all...\" The old man nodded in acknowledgement.","Seeing this, envy flickered in the eyes of the surrounding swordmasters, each secretly wishing it was their Sword Aura that had captured the old man’s attention."]},{"number":2013,"title":"Chapter 2013: Holy Sword Clan","paragraphs":["When Yuan saw the situation, he decided not to interrupt but to spectate instead.","A few minutes later, the young man who’d caught the attention of the old man from the Holy Sword Clan opened his eyes and stood up, seemingly unaware of the elder’s presence.","The old man cleared his throat loudly to announce his presence before speaking, \"Young man, what’s your name?\"","The young man was startled momentarily, but he quickly recovered when he saw the old man’s white and golden robes.","Then, he hastily lowered his body and bowed, \"This junior is called Chu Ling. I apologize for not noticing you earlier, Senior.\"","The old man smiled and said, \"It’s my fault for sneaking up on you. Anyway, if you don’t mind me asking, how old are you?\"","\"This junior is currently 3,291 years old,\" the young man responded.","The surrounding swordmasters expressed surprise after hearing the young man’s response.","\"So you’ve achieved Enhanced Sword Aura in under 5,000 years. Very impressive indeed. Do you currently have a teacher?\" the old man continued to ask, almost like he was giving a job interview.","\"No, I do not, but I did spend a thousand years at the Gleaming Sword Sect.\"","The old man nodded before retrieving what looked like a slab of metal and said, \"If you can leave even the slightest scratch on this plate using your Enhanced Sword Aura, I’ll recruit you into the Holy Sword Clan.\"","Chu Ling swallowed nervously at the opportunity before him. The Holy Sword Clan was home to three Sword Emperors. Joining them was a dream pursued by countless swordmasters.","\"Are you willing to accept this challenge?\" the old man asked.","\"I am willing!\" Chu Ling immediately responded.","The old man nodded and placed the metal on the ground.","\"Whenever you are ready,\" he said.","Chu Ling retrieved his sword and took a moment to prepare himself.","Then, everyone watched as Chu Ling’s body surged with Enhanced Sword Aura, and he struck the metal plate with a resounding clang that echoed through the crater.","The spectators anticipated Chu Ling to leave a mark on the metal plate, but to their shock, he was suddenly hurled backward like a ragdoll.","Before anyone could make sense of what had just happened, a cold, mocking laughter echoed through the air. All eyes turned toward the old man, who was now laughing hysterically, as though he’d just witnessed the most absurd joke in the world.","\"W-What is going on...?\" Chu Ling muttered in a daze as he slowly got back to his feet.","The old man responded, \"That was the best you could do with that level of Enhanced Sword Aura? What a waste of talents!\"","\"What’s happening, Young Master?\" Feng Yuxiang asked, as she was just as confused as the others.","Yuan calmly explained, \"While his Enhanced Sword Aura is indeed commendable, he has no idea how to wield it. It’s like handing a divine blade to a child—powerful, yet utterly wasted.\"","\"I didn’t know you needed to know how to use Sword Aura,\" Feng Yuxiang remarked.","\"While Weapon Aura is inherently powerful and can be used as is, you still need to learn to control it to utilize its full potential. It’s like comparing a sharp knife with a dull knife.\"","The old man approached Chu Ling and shook his head, \"Sorry, but it looks like you didn’t pass the test.\"","\"P-Please give me one more chance! I will do it properly this time!\" Chu Ling fell to his knees and begged.","The old man narrowed his eyes and sneered in disdain, \"Another chance? Do you know how many people here would kill for a first chance? You were given a chance, but you squandered it.\"","Without giving Chu Ling another look, the old man turned around and walked away, leaving him devastated.","However, before the old man could get too far, Yuan descended right before him, blocking his path.","\"...\"","The old man halted his movements and stared at Yuan with a somewhat surprised face. He’d been wandering the Grand Sword Crater for many years, but nobody had so boldly stood in his path before.","\"Do you think I can give it a go?\" Yuan asked.","\"What?\" The old man frowned.","\"That metal slab. I want to try striking it with my Sword Aura,\" he clarified.","\"I don’t know if you’re acting on boldness or pure stupidity, but I will give you a chance to walk away with your life.\"","Yuan didn’t say anything, but he exuded some of his Sword Aura. It wasn’t his Enhanced Sword Aura, but just his ordinary Sword Aura.","The old man’s eyes widened after sensing Yuan’s ordinary Sword Aura, even doubting his own eyes for a second.","’His ordinary Sword Aura feels as powerful as the last guy’s Enhanced Sword Aura! But how is that possible?!’ he cried inwardly, not daring to believe what he was sensing.","In order to confirm the phenomenon before him, the old man retrieved the metal slab and tossed it on the ground.","\"Go ahead.\"","Without saying a word, Yuan retrieved a random sword from his spatial ring and swung it at the metal slab.","The people around them expected to hear a loud clanging sound like usual, but to their puzzlement, Yuan’s strike didn’t make even the slightest sound.","\"Did he miss?\" They wondered out loud as their eyes shifted to the metal slab on the ground.","\"No way...\"","Despite staring at the object with their own eyes, nobody there dared to believe what they were witnessing.","\"Th-This is...\" The old man’s voice trembled as he stared at the metal slab lying on the ground, now cleanly split in two.","\"Hm? It’s not as durable as I thought it would be...\" Yuan muttered.","The old man’s body shook. Then, without warning, he lunged forward and grabbed both of Yuan’s arms.","\"You must join our Holy Sword Clan!\" he declared.","However, Yuan remained calm and said, \"I think there’s been a misunderstanding. I’m not trying to join the Holy Sword Clan.\"","\"What?\"","It wasn’t just the old man—everyone present wore the same stunned expression after hearing Yuan’s words, their minds struggling to grasp such nonsense."]},{"number":2014,"title":"Chapter 2014: Holy Sword Clan(2)","paragraphs":["After a moment of silence, the old man cleared his throat and spoke in a forceful tone, \"I must have misheard you just now. Can you repeat what you said?\"","\"I said that I am not interested in joining the Holy Sword Clan,\" Yuan calmly repeated, shocking everyone there for a second time.","\"Blasphemy! If you’re not interested in joining the Holy Sword Clan, why did you even bother with the metal plate?! Are you messing with me?!\"","The old man exclaimed, his face flushed in redness. However, he didn’t give up and continued trying to recruit Yuan.","\"The Holy Sword Clan is the number one faction for swordmasters in the Nine Heavens! If you wish to become a Sword Emperor, your best chance lies with us. We not only house three Sword Emperors, but the majority of Sword Emperors in history have hailed from our clan!\" the old man proclaimed, his tone filled with pride as he tried to sway Yuan’s decision.","\"I’ll think about it after I finish training at the Holy Sword Temple,\" Yuan calmly responded.","\"What? The Holy Sword Temple?\"","The old man wore a dumbfounded expression on his face, but before he could speak further, Yuan retrieved the sword-shaped badge from his spatial ring and showed it off.","\"This is my actual reason for approaching you,\" he said.","\"That’s the Holy Sword Emblem! Where did you get that from?!\" The old man exclaimed.","\"Does it matter where?\"","\"Of course, it does! How do I know that you didn’t steal it or find it by chance?\"","Yuan didn’t argue further and showed the old man his faction symbol.","\"I got it from someone in my faction.\"","\"Celestial Overlords!\" The old man and those around him sucked in a breath of cold breath after seeing his faction symbol.","\"Alright, come with me. I’ll take you to our headquarters to speak with the elders.\"","Yuan nodded and silently followed the old man into the depths of the Grand Sword Crater. After descending to the bottom of the massive fissure, they proceeded northward without pause.","Though the number of swordmasters within the Grand Sword Crater wasn’t as overwhelming as outside, their presence was still significant, and Yuan couldn’t go more than a few minutes without witnessing one practicing their sword techniques.","After several days of travel and passing by numerous members of the Holy Sword Clan, they finally arrived at the clan’s headquarters, located in the widest expanse of the Grand Sword Crater.","Sandwiched between two colossal walls of earth stood several sword-shaped buildings, each varying in height but radiating the same grand presence.","The old man brought Yuan to the tallest building and then had him wait inside one of the guest rooms.","\"Wait here while I bring one of our elders here,\" said the old man before walking out and closing the door.","However, Yuan could tell that the old man didn’t leave and remained outside for some reason.","A few moments later, the door opened, and the old man walked back inside.","\"My name is Li Bowen, the 4th elder of the Holy Sword Clan,\" he introduced himself.","The old man’s unusual actions left Yuan speechless.","Li Bowen smiled and said, \"There’s no need for the suspicious looks. I really am an elder.\"","He then took a seat right in front of Yuan and continued, \"Alright, let’s get straight to the topic. The Holy Sword Temple.\"","Yuan quietly nodded.","\"Although you have the Holy Sword Emblem, that is only one of the requirements to enter the Holy Sword Temple. Is that your true cultivation?\" Li Bowen asked.","\"Yes, it is.\"","\"In all my years at the Holy Sword Clan, I have never heard of a mortal asking to enter the Holy Sword Temple, much less stand before one myself. Do you even know what you’re getting yourself into?\"","\"As long as I can learn Supreme Sword Aura, I don’t care.\"","Li Bowen narrowed his eyes and said, \"The Holy Sword Temple may serve as a training ground, but it is a perilous place where even Immortals can easily lose their life, much less a mortal like you. I’m sure you already know that, so I won’t waste my breath trying to change your mind. However, I still have to test your qualifications.\"","\"How will you do that?\" Yuan asked.","\"It’s very simple and straightforward. I just need to test your Enhanced Sword Aura.\"","\"Sounds good.\"","\"Then follow me.\"","The next moment, they left the room, and Li Bowen led Yuan to another building. Within it lay a vast training ground, where several swordmasters were striking a towering wall with their Enhanced Sword Aura. Naturally, the wall was forged from a special material, similar to the metal slab Yuan had effortlessly split in two, but also vastly different at the same time.","The swordmasters in the room struck the wall with meticulously controlled Enhanced Sword Aura and had been doing so for several hours now, yet not a single one of them managed to leave even the faintest scratch.","\"This wall is forged from a unique material with unparalleled resistance to slashing attacks. Don’t even think about comparing it to the metal slab you cut through a few days ago—this is at least a thousand times more durable,\" Li Bowen explained with a somewhat proud look on his face.","\"So, how deep does the cut need to be for me to qualify?\" Yuan asked.","Li Bowen smiled and replied, \"One inch. If you can somehow manage to leave a cut that deep on this wall, I’ll personally take you to the Holy Sword Temple. But there’s a condition—you can only use a Spirit-grade sword and rely solely on your Enhanced Sword Aura. No martial techniques, no powerful treasures.\"","\"Fair enough.\"","Li Bowen retrieved an ordinary Spirit-grade sword that one could purchase from anywhere and handed it to Yuan.","\"Whenever you’re—\"","Li Bowen abruptly paused mid-sentence, his expression tightening.","Sensing several unfamiliar auras entering the building, he turned toward the entrance, and his eyes widened in disbelief after seeing their faces.","\"W-What are they doing here?!\" he muttered under his breath, his voice tinged with shock and unease.","Meanwhile, those training at the wall halted their training and quietly bowed to the group.","Yuan followed Li Bowen’s gaze toward the group that had just stepped into the building.","There were six individuals in total, but all eyes were naturally drawn to the two at the front—a strikingly beautiful young woman and a handsome young man, both adorned in the distinguished robes of the Holy Sword Clan.","\"I’ll be back. Don’t do anything until then.\" Li Bowen said to Yuan before approaching the group.","\"Greetings, Holy Sword Maiden, Holy Sword King, and everyone else.\"","\"Elder Li, it’s been a while,\" said the handsome man, who was known as the Holy Sword King within the Holy Sword Clan.","\"Yes, it’s been around 150 years. What brought you guys to the Seventh Heaven?\"","\"The Sword Emperor Qualifications, of course. I know there are still a few years before it begins, but we decided to come down earlier,\" he explained.","\"I see...\"","\"Do you mind if we use the training grounds for a bit?\" The Holy Sword Maiden suddenly said.","\"Of course not... but at your level...\"","\"We won’t be the ones to use it,\" she elaborated, looking at the other four behind her.","\"Oh, I see. In any case, feel free to use it. If you need anything, don’t hesitate to call me.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Li Bowen returned to Yuan shortly after and said to him, \"Sorry, but we’ll have to do your qualifications another time.\"","\"But it won’t even take a minute... I just need to hit the wall once,\" Yuan said.","Li Bowen responded with voice transmission, \"I know, but this isn’t about that. Do you see that beautiful woman with silver hair and that young man with the short red hair? They’re the Holy Sword Maiden and the Holy Sword King. Their status within the Holy Sword Clan is only below the Sword Emperors. While the Holy Sword Maiden might not mind your presence, the Holy Sword King is known for being easily irritable. I am doing this for your own good. If you offend them, you can kiss your chance to enter the Holy Sword Temple, even with a referral. Don’t worry, I doubt they’ll stay for too long.\"","Yuan found it a pain in the ass, but he’d rather wait a few days, even weeks, if it meant not causing any unnecessary trouble.","\"I don’t mind waiting a little,\" he said.","\"Thank you for your understanding. You can stay in one of our guest rooms for now,\" Li Bowen said.","The next moment, Yuan followed Li Bowen to the exit.","\"Who’s that?\" The Holy Sword Maiden asked one of the swordmasters who had been training there before their arrival.","\"I’m not sure. He arrived only a few moments earlier than you guys, but I think he was trying to qualify for the Holy Sword Temple.\"","The Holy Sword King laughed and said, \"There’s no way. That guy was a mortal.\"","\"Oh... then I don’t know... Sorry.\"","\"It’s fine.\" The Holy Sword Maiden shook her head.","After leaving the training ground, Li Bowen brought Yuan to his guest room.","\"You can stay here for now. I’ll contact you when they are finished with the place, which shouldn’t take too long.\"","Once Li Bowen left and he was alone, Yuan sat on the ground and closed his eyes.","’I might as well use this time to perfect my Enhanced Sword Aura,’ he thought inwardly before immersing himself in Tian Xin’s memories."]},{"number":2015,"title":"Chapter 2015: Holy Sword Clan(3)","paragraphs":["Unlike his predecessors, Tian Xin was unique in the sense that he was born with all of his previous life’s memories intact. This gave him an unfathomable advantage, allowing him to train with all of his previous knowledge since the day he was born.","Because of this, Tian Xin was always considered a prodigy no matter where he went. Moreover, not only was Tian Xin born with all of his memories, but he also came from a renowned background, one that was known for creating many powerful swordmasters.","One could consider Tian Xin being born with a diamond spoon in his mouth. Yet, despite this, he did not rely on his family even in the slightest and left home at a young age to travel the Nine Heavens.","During his journey, Tian Xin quickly gained fame as an undefeated and mysterious warrior, his identity shrouded in mystery beneath the mask he always wore.","He encountered Jin Xi early in his journey. After being defeated by him, she chose to follow him to get stronger, whether he liked it or not.","Although he ignored her in the beginning, they eventually became something akin to master and disciple. Of course, Tian Xin never admitted that he was teaching her, only giving her cryptic advice.","It didn’t take long for Jin Xi to develop feelings for Tian Xin, and in time, he began to feel the same. Yet, neither of them ever voiced their hearts. Though Jin Xi’s affection often showed in her actions, quite obvious at times, she never found the courage to confess.","As for Tian Xin, while he was aware of Jin Xi’s feelings, he chose to feign ignorance.","Together, they honed their swordsmanship. While Jin Xi struggled to achieve Enhanced Sword Aura, Tian Xin had long mastered Enhanced Sword Aura and was already looking to reach the next realm—the level of Supreme Sword Aura.","As Yuan recalled his experiences as Tian Xin, Enhanced Sword Aura naturally emanated from his body. Since the strength of one’s Weapon Aura stems primarily from comprehension, his Enhanced Sword Aura became sharper and toward perfection at an unfathomable rate.","In the blink of an eye, a whole month has passed since Yuan arrived at the Holy Sword Clan.","*Knock* *Knock*","Yuan opened his eyes when someone suddenly knocked on the door.","\"About time,\" he sighed out loud, assuming Li Bowen had finally arrived to inform him that the training ground was ready.","He went to open the door a moment later, only to be surprised that it wasn’t Li Bowen who’d knocked on the door.","\"Uh... how can I help you?\" Yuan asked the beautiful young woman standing outside his door.","This woman had long silver hair and red eyes that glowed faintly. Unexpectedly, it was the Holy Sword Maiden.","The Holy Sword Maiden didn’t respond right away. Instead, she glanced into his room to confirm he was alone. Then, with a slightly puzzled expression, she said, \"I happened to be passing by when I sensed Enhanced Sword Aura coming from this room. I may be mistaken, but... was that you?\"","The Holy Sword Maiden spoke with a tone of disbelief. The Enhanced Sword Aura she had sensed was so powerful, it could only be compared to that of a Sword Emperor—yet the man before her was clearly just a mortal.","\"Yes, it was mine. I was training. Sorry, I didn’t realize it was leaking outside. I hope that didn’t bother you.\"","\"How...?\" she muttered in a low voice before asking in a loud and clear voice, \"How did you achieve that level of Enhanced Sword Aura?\"","\"I have already reached the level of Supreme Sword Aura, but my Enhanced Sword Aura couldn’t be compared to it. Can you also use Supreme Sword Aura?\"","\"No, I can’t.\"","\"That doesn’t make any sense. Can you explain how you did it?\"","\"I don’t know what to tell you... The strength of one’s weapon aura is based on their understanding, so...\"","The Holy Sword Maiden frowned slightly and said, \"Are you saying that you, who hasn’t even learned Supreme Sword Aura, somehow has a better understanding than I?\"","\"Well, each level of Sword Aura carries its own depth of understanding,\" Yuan said. \"So it’s possible for someone to grasp one level more profoundly than another.\"","\"I know that! But it still doesn’t make sense! How can a mortal understand more than I, who is at the God Ascension Realm?!\"","\"...\"","Yuan didn’t know what else to say, but he had a feeling that he’d get into trouble soon.","\"Come with me,\" she suddenly said.","\"I really shouldn’t... I was told to stay here by Elder Li,\" Yuan said.","\"Do you know who I am?\" she then asked.","He nodded and answered, \"You’re the Holy Sword Maiden, right?\"","\"That’s right, and my authority within the Holy Sword Clan is only second to the Sword Emperors. Nothing will happen to you if you come with me. I promise,\" she said.","\"Okay...\" Yuan responded with a stiff smile. It wasn’t Li Bowen he was concerned about. However, he couldn’t tell her that he was worried about getting involved with her, as that would definitely offend her.","Without saying another word, the Holy Sword Maiden turned around and began walking away. Seeing this, Yuan could only sigh inwardly and follow her.","They arrived at their destination a few minutes later. Unexpectedly, the Holy Sword Maiden brought him to the building with the metal wall. However, the place was empty.","Upon their arrival, the Holy Sword Maiden silently approached the wall, retrieving one of the Spirit-grade swords hanging nearby. She then stepped forward, positioning herself before the metal wall. After drawing a steady breath, she activated her Enhanced Sword Aura. In one graceful, fluid motion, she swung the sword, unleashing a streak of shimmering aura that sliced through the air toward the wall.","When her Enhanced Sword Aura struck the wall, it carved a six-inch-deep gash into the metal, leaving a clear mark that stood out amid the countless faint scratches left by others.","Before Yuan could even say anything, the Holy Sword Maiden tossed her sword at him and said, \"Your turn.\""]},{"number":2016,"title":"Chapter 2016: Holy Sword Clan(4)","paragraphs":["\"Um... before I strike at the wall, do you mind calling Elder Li here?\" Yuan asked after catching the Spirit-grade sword.","\"Why? Are you worried that I might do something to you?\" The Holy Sword Maiden spoke with a frown.","\"No, that’s not it. I just don’t want to do this again later.\"","\"Why would you—\"","The Holy Sword Maiden abruptly halted her sentence when she recalled something that was mentioned before.","\"So it was true. You’re here to qualify for the Holy Sword Temple,\" she said.","Yuan nodded, \"That’s right.\"","\"In that case, there’s no need to trouble Elder Li. I can verify it myself. Go ahead—whenever you’re ready,\" she said, urging him to proceed.","\"Alright.\"","Yuan approached the metal wall, took a deep breath, and fell silent. The next moment, Enhanced Sword Aura surged from his body before enveloping the sword.","The Holy Sword Maiden remained silent, but her fists were tightly clenched. From a single glance, she could tell that his Enhanced Sword Aura far surpassed hers. Yet, she couldn’t fathom just how vast that difference was.","Once he was ready, Yuan flicked his arm with lightning speed. In that instant, the sword in his grasp flickered like a phantom.","In the moments that followed, Yuan’s Enhanced Sword Aura struck the six-inch gash left by the Holy Sword Maiden. Not only did it erase her mark entirely, but it even pierced straight through the wall itself, leaving a clean hole in its wake.","\"No way...\"","The Holy Sword Maiden’s legs buckled beneath her, and she collapsed onto her buttocks with a soft thud, her eyes wide with disbelief.","Yuan’s Enhanced Sword Aura hadn’t merely exceeded her expectations—it likely surpassed even that of the Sword Emperors within the Holy Sword Clan.","\"Uh... sorry, but I didn’t mean to destroy the wall,\" Yuan muttered awkwardly, scratching his head. \"Elder Li made it sound indestructible, after all...\"","However, the Holy Sword Maiden was too shocked to even respond, and she merely continued staring at the hole with a dazed face.","Seeing her in a daze, Yuan could only wait patiently for her to return to reality.","However, his expression subtly shifted when he sensed several powerful presences drawing near. It was likely the Holy Sword King and the others.","Even without being told, Yuan understood how terrible the situation appeared. He could already picture himself trying to explain the situation to them, only for things to worsen. Hell, he could even forsee the Holy Sword King picking a fight with him over this.","With no other choice, Yuan hastily placed the Spirit-grade sword on the ground beside the Holy Sword Maiden, then turned around and exited through the hole he’d created.","Seeing this, the Holy Sword Maiden finally snapped out of her daze. However, Yuan had already left, and before she could give chase, the Holy Sword King and the others entered the building.","\"What the hell happened here?\" the Holy Sword King exclaimed as his gaze fell upon the gaping hole in the wall.","His first instinct was to assume the Holy Sword Maiden was responsible, yet he couldn’t fathom why she’d do such a thing.","However, before he could ask her anything, the Holy Sword Maiden stood up and ran toward the hole in the wall.","\"Wait! Where are you going?!\" The Holy Sword King immediately chased after her.","With the Holy Sword King close behind, the Holy Sword Maiden rushed after Yuan. However, even with her divine sense enveloping the entire area, she couldn’t detect his presence.","’Why can’t I find him? Don’t tell me he already left this place! But there’s no way he could’ve gone that far in such a short time!’","Of course, Yuan was still within the Holy Sword Clan’s territory. The reason the Holy Sword Maiden couldn’t find him was because he was concealing his presence with Shadow Veil.","Some time later, after giving up on finding Yuan, the Holy Sword Maiden went to find Li Bowen instead.","\"That young man who came to qualify for the Holy Sword Temple—who is he?\" she questioned him.","\"Excuse me?\" Li Bowen wore a dumbfounded look on his face. He couldn’t understand why the Holy Sword Maiden was suddenly looking for Yuan, who hadn’t left the guest room for over a month.","\"Just answer my question!\" she raised her voice, startling him and the Holy Sword King, who had never seen her so agitated before.","\"Are you looking for that mortal from a month ago?\" The Holy Sword King finally recalled.","\"Why? Did he do something to you? I’ll find and skin that bastard—\"","\"Why are you even here? This doesn’t concern you!\" she interrupted him.","\"But...\"","\"Get out!\" she pointed toward the exit.","Seeing how annoyed she was, the Holy Sword King reluctantly left the room.","Once they were alone, the Holy Sword Maiden continued questioning Li Bowen.","\"Tell me everything you know about that mortal with you a month ago,\" she demanded.","Li Bowen swallowed nervously before responding, \"The only thing I know about him is that he’s with the Celestial Overlords.\"","\"What about his name?\"","\"That’s... uhh...\" It was at this moment that Li Bowen realized he’d never asked Yuan for his name.","\"I’m sorry, but I never got the chance to ask for his name...\" he admitted a moment later.","\"Can you tell me what this is all about?\" he then asked.","The Holy Sword Maiden rubbed her eyes and sighed before explaining, \"He cut through the wall.\"","\"What?\" Li Bowen raised his eyebrows in a puzzled manner, unable to comprehend her words.","\"The Impenetrable Sword Wall! He cut through the entire thing with his Sword Aura!\" she repeated, this time with more detail.","\"HE WHAT?!\" Li Bowen exclaimed, his eyes as wide as saucers.","\"L-Let me go see!\"","Before the Holy Sword Maiden could respond, Li Bowen rushed to the training ground.","The moment Li Bowen laid eyes on the gaping hole in the wall, his jaw nearly hit the ground in disbelief. After all, the only time he’d witnessed such devastation was from Supreme Sword Aura—yet Yuan couldn’t possibly know it if he was seeking training at the Holy Sword Temple.","When the Holy Sword Maiden caught up, he asked her, \"How did he achieve this?\"","\"With Enhanced Sword Aura,\" she responded, confirming his suspicions.","\"...\"","Unsure of how to respond, Li Bowen quietly stood there, staring at the hole with a dazed face."]},{"number":2017,"title":"Chapter 2017: Holy Sword Clan(5)","paragraphs":["\"Hey.\"","The Holy Sword Maiden suddenly called out, snapping Li Bowen out of his daze.","When he turned to look at her, she held a sword-shaped badge in front of her, seemingly offering it to him.","This badge looked similar to the one in Yuan’s possession, but it was golden in color and had more refined details.","Li Bowen’s eyes widened at the sight of this badge, but before he could say anything, the Holy Sword Maiden spoke, \"The mortal left before I could give this to him. If he returns, give it to him for me. I promised to verify his qualifications, after all.\"","The sword badge was akin to a referral, but it came from none other than the Holy Sword Maiden, which guaranteed Yuan’s admission to the Holy Sword Temple.","\"Yes...\" Li Bowen accepted the badge with stiff movements. Even someone of his stature had never touched this object before.","\"Wait. Did you say he’d left?\" Li Bowen suddenly asked.","\"Yes, he left after destroying the wall. He probably thought he’d get in trouble or something. I don’t know why, but I have a feeling that he’s afraid of me.\"","\"I see...\" Li Bowen remarked in a flat voice. He couldn’t tell her that it was most likely due to what he told Yuan a month ago.","\"Anyway, I’ll be leaving now. If you ever find more about that mortal, let me know. We need him in the Holy Sword Clan,\" said the Holy Sword Maiden.","\"But he’s already with the Celestial Overlords,\" Li Bowen reminded her.","\"So what? As far as I am aware, the Celestial Overlords don’t restrict their members to a single faction. And since there are no grievances between our faction, there’s no reason he cannot join us as well.\"","Most factions out there allow their members to join multiple factions to keep their numbers up, so it wasn’t uncommon for someone to belong to multiple factions.","Li Bowen could only silently nod his head. He recalled Yuan being at the lowest rank for the Celestial Overlords, so there was a good chance they could recruit him into the Holy Sword Clan.","Some time later, the Holy Sword Maiden left the Holy Sword Clan. The Holy Sword King and the others were puzzled by her abrupt departure, but they still left with her.","\"Fuck, what am I supposed to do with this badge? If he doesn’t return...\" Li Bowen muttered as he stared at the golden badge resting on his palm.","However, he suddenly sensed a presence appear behind him like a ghost.","When he turned around and saw Yuan standing behind him, Li Bowen nearly had a heart attack.","\"Son of a bi—!\"","\"Sorry for startling you.\"","\"You! I thought you had left!\"","\"No, I only hid my presence since I didn’t want to deal with the Holy Sword Maiden after what happened. I’m glad she left so quickly,\" said Yuan.","Li Bowen rubbed his eyes and released a stressful sigh.","\"I told you to stay away from them, but you went ahead and caused such a scene.\"","Yuan shrugged, \"Don’t make it sound like it was my fault that she dragged me out of my room and forced me to do her bidding. If I had refused, it would have definitely offended her.\"","\"I am not blaming you...\" Li Bowen said, admitting that it wasn’t his fault.","\"In fact, I am quite thankful for what you did. Like you said, things could’ve turned out much worse, but it didn’t. Hell, the Holy Sword Maiden even approved of you.\"","Li Bowen extended his hand toward Yuan, showing the golden badge, and continued, \"She has granted you permission to enter the Holy Sword Temple.\"","\"Thank you.\" Yuan accepted the badge.","Then, he asked, \"About the wall... how much will the repairs cost? I’ll pay for it.\"","\"It’ll cost a few hundred million spirit stones, but you don’t need to worry about it. It’s pretty worn out, and we’ve been wanting to replace it, but we got lazy.\"","\"If you say so...\"","\"Anyway, when do you want to head to the Holy Sword Temple?\"","\"Can we go there now?\"","\"Unfortunately, it’ll take some time to prepare the transport, so the earliest you can go is three months.\"","\"Then I’ll leave as soon as possible.\"","\"I understand. Oh, one more thing. How would you like to join the Holy Sword Temple? This isn’t just my request, but also the Holy Sword Maiden’s.\"","\"But I am already part of the Celestial Overlords.\"","\"The Celestial Overlords doesn’t prevent its members from joining other factions. In fact, several of our members are also members of the Celestial Overlords. There’s no downside to having more backers, either.\"","Li Bowen’s words made sense to Yuan. It was common for people to join multiple factions to expand their influence. After all, having the support of several powerful backers was always advantageous.","However, Yuan didn’t want to just join any faction.","\"Can you give me some time to think about it? I would like to learn more about the Holy Sword Clan before I decide,\" he said.","Li Bowen’s face immediately lit up with excitement.","\"Of course! Though there’s not much to see here since we’re just a small branch location, I’ll try my best to answer any questions that you may have.\"","Some time later, Li Bowen left to get the transportation ready. In the meantime, Yuan wandered their territory. However, just as Li Bowen had warned, there wasn’t much to see, much less learn there.","However, he did find a library that contained the history of the Holy Sword Clan, and with nothing else better to do, he started reading it.","\"Hm?\"","After reading several scrolls, Yuan learned some peculiar information about the Holy Sword Temple.","According to the Holy Sword Clan, they weren’t the first owners of the Holy Sword Temple, and they’d merely acquired it from its creator, the Exalted Blacksmith. However, Yuan couldn’t recall creating it. Of course, he still lacked some of Tian Qiyuan’s memories, mostly of his time after becoming the God of Creation."]},{"number":2018,"title":"Chapter 2018: Entering the Starry Sky","paragraphs":["After spending a few days in the library, Yuan went back to his room, where he tried to learn Supreme Sword Aura.","Despite having the understanding, memories, and experience of using Supreme Sword Aura as Tian Xin, Yuan couldn’t use it for some reason, almost as if his attempt was being blocked by an unseen force.","After failing several times, Yuan stopped trying and began focusing on his soul strength instead. Since there was no limit to how strong his soul strength could get, it was his current priority.","Time passed, and in the blink of an eye, three months had passed since Yuan received permission to visit the Holy Sword Temple.","Once the preparations were complete, Li Bowen notified Yuan and brought him outside, where a golden carriage awaited. Naturally, this was no ordinary carriage. It was a flying treasure crafted by the Holy Sword Clan, reserved for journeys to the Holy Sword Temple.","\"The carriage will take you to the Holy Sword Temple, which will take two months. Also, just in case you didn’t know, you still have to pass a trial to enter the Holy Sword Temple. Right now, you only have permission to visit the place and partake in the trial,\" Li Bowen said.","Yuan nodded.","\"I am aware.\"","\"Alright. Whenever you’re ready.\" Li Bowen opened the door and gestured for him to enter.","The moment Yuan stepped into the carriage, he found himself in a surprisingly spacious room, as though he’d entered another world. High-grade flying treasures like the golden carriage were crafted with spatial techniques, allowing their interiors to be far larger than their outward appearance suggested.","\"Good luck at the Holy Sword Temple,\" Li Bowen said before closing the door.","The golden carriage departed soon after, ascending swiftly into the skies before piercing through the clouds and vanishing into the boundless void in the blink of an eye.","Inside the room, Yuan approached the window and gazed outside. Beyond the glass stretched a vast expanse of darkness, illuminated by countless flickering stars of varying sizes.","Lan Yingying emerged from Yuan’s dantian to look at the starry sky since this was her first time traveling beyond the Nine Heavens.","\"So this is what the starry sky looks like up close...\" Lan Yingying muttered with a look of awe on her face.","Feng Yuxiang and the others also appeared.","\"I find it rather dull,\" Feng Yuxiang remarked. \"The place is mostly empty, and when you do find something, it’s usually just useless rocks. That said, the starry sky holds some of the rarest and most precious treasures in the Nine Heavens—so there’s still reason to explore it.\"","\"How does one explore the starry sky?\" Lan Yingying asked.","\"Well, there are treasures out there that help you find other treasures. However, they are extremely rare and expensive. Other than that... I guess you’ll just have to rely on your luck and wander the place until you find something.\"","\"What if you get lost?\"","\"It’s hard to explain, but once you reach a certain cultivation, it’s almost impossible to get lost even in the starry sky. You will instinctively know where you are and where to go. Of course, people still take precautions and have teleporting treasures just in case. Nobody is foolish enough to enter the starry sky without life-saving treasures, either.\"","\"Life-saving treasures? Is the starry sky that dangerous?\" Lan Yingying asked.","\"Of course. With no rules in the starry sky and distances too vast to call for help, you can only rely on yourself,\" Feng Yuxiang said.","\"So what happens if we encounter someone?\"","\"Well, since we’re in a flying treasure and won’t be venturing too far away from the Nine Heavens, even if we do encounter someone, it is very unlikely that anything will happen. We’re also in the Holy Sword Clan’s signature carriage. I doubt anyone would be foolish enough to attack us.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"You’d be surprised at how many bold individuals are out there.\"","\"Even if someone attacks us, we’ll be fine since you’re here, Young Master.\" Feng Yuxiang chuckled.","However, Yuan shook his head and said, \"As long as they’re not in the God Ascension realm, I’ll be able to handle them.\"","\"But you’ve already defeated several God Ascension realm cultivators,\" she said.","\"No, I only destroyed their physical bodies,\" Yuan replied. \"Besides, God Ascension realm cultivators have restricted power within the Nine Heavens, just as the lower heavens impose their own cultivation limits. However, that restriction will be lifted once they leave the Nine Heavens.\"","\"Really? I didn’t know that God Ascension realm cultivators have their strength restricted in the Nine Heavens...\" Lan Yingying said with a surprised look on her face.","God Ascension realm cultivators possessed the strength to shatter stars with a mere clench of their fists. If they were free to wield such power within the Nine Heavens, that world would have long since ceased to exist.","\"I can only fight God Ascension realm cultivators in the Nine Heavens. Once we leave... even I am powerless against them until I learn Celestial Qi,\" said Yuan.","\"Is that so...\"","Lan Yingying continued asking questions, her curiosity about the starry sky growing with each passing moment as she gazed out the window. It was as if she were instinctively drawn to it, like a moth to a flame.","Time passed swiftly, and before they knew it, nearly two months had gone by.","\"Hey... I think I see something...\" Lan Yingying, who had spent most of her time gazing at the void, suddenly said.","\"What do you see?\" Feng Yuxiang asked as she sipped on her tea at the couch.","Lan Yingying narrowed her eyes and murmured uncertainly, \"I think... it’s some kind of serpent—a white serpent.\"","\"What?\" Feng Yuxiang raised her eyebrows.","\"And I think it’s consuming stars...\"","\"What?!\"","The moment Yuan heard this detail, he stopped cultivating at once and sprang to his feet, rushing to the window.","And sure enough, when he looked outside, he saw a tiny, serpent-like entity drifting through the void. Wherever it passed, the flickering stars vanished—almost as if they were being devoured.","\"It can’t be...\" Yuan murmured in disbelief."]},{"number":2019,"title":"Chapter 2019: White Serpent in the Starry Sky","paragraphs":["Yuan could scarcely believe his eyes as he watched the white serpent drift through the starry sky, devouring stars in its wake.","\"Xingrui...\" Yuan muttered this name.","It was likely that this entity was the Eater of Stars—one of the Nine Divine Supreme—who had vanished since the Immortal Monarch’s Era. The evidence wasn’t conclusive, but in Yuan’s eyes, there was no doubt.","After all, how many white serpents that could devour stars were out there?","\"Xingrui... Isn’t that one of the Nine Divine Supreme?\" Feng Yuxiang remarked when she heard this name.","Yuan nodded, \"Yes. According to Yeyou, she returned to the starry sky to consume stars after my—the Immortal Monarch’s death.\"","Feng Yuxiang set down her tea and walked to the window for a look herself, but by the time she arrived, the white serpent had already drifted so far into the void that it looked no more than a speck of white dust.","\"She’s... so far away,\" Feng Yuxiang murmured.","Hearing this, Yuan clenched his fists in frustration. Though they were fortunate to have glimpsed the Eater of Stars, that fortune was bittersweet, as there was no realistic way for them to pursue her.","The flying treasure was on autopilot, and even if Yuan could redirect its course to pursue Xingrui, their chances of catching up were nonexistent. After all, Xingrui was a colossal beast capable of devouring multiple stars in a single bite. For her to appear as nothing more than a speck of dust, she had to be light-years away.","Without the proper flying treasure and sufficient time, it was impossible to catch Xingrui.","’It’d be impossible to pursue Xingrui even if I were a God Ascension realm cultivator right now... If I really want to catch up to her, I’ll need to master the power of the void—at least to the point where I can teleport vast distances.’","’Just wait a little longer, Xingrui. I’ll find you again... soon.’ Yuan swore inwardly as he stood by the window, silently watching the tiny white speck fade into the depths of the void.","For the rest of their journey to the Holy Sword Temple, Yuan found himself reminiscing about his time with Xingrui. In the beginning, she had reminded him of Yingzi—aloof, curious, and utterly lacking in common sense. But as time passed, she grew more composed, and her loyalty to him deepened to unfathomable depths.","Eventually...","\"Yuan, we’ve arrived at the Holy Sword Temple,\" Lan Yingying said, pointing ahead at a massive floating island. At its center stood a towering, majestic structure that resembled a grand temple.","The Holy Sword Temple radiated a brilliant golden light, piercing through the surrounding darkness like a divine treasure suspended in the void.","The golden carriage descended onto the island, landing right in front of the temple gates.","Lan Yingying and the others returned to Yuan’s Dantian before he left the carriage.","\"Greetings.\"","A middle-aged woman wearing golden robes greeted Yuan when he exited the carriage.","\"Hello.\"","\"I am the Sixth Holy Sword of the Holy Sword Temple, but you may address me as the Sixth Elder. Can I see your referral?\"","Yuan nodded and retrieved not just the crimson badge he received from Xu Jiaqi but also the golden badge from the Holy Sword Maiden, handing it to the Sixth Elder.","\"This is...\"","The Sixth Elder’s eyes widened with surprise when she saw the golden badge.","\"So you’ve received the Holy Sword Maiden’s approval... I believe this is her first time handing out her badge to someone,\" revealed the Sixth Elder.","\"Is that so? I feel honored.\"","The Sixth Elder nodded and said, \"Just so you know, even with the Holy Sword Maiden’s approval, you must pass a trial before you can enter the Holy Sword Temple.\"","\"I am aware. What kind of trial is it?\"","The Sixth Elder turned to face a specific direction, where a colossal sword hovered silently above a circular platform, resembling that of an execution site.","\"To enter the Holy Sword Temple, you must survive the Blade of Tribulation, a Celestial-grade treasure imbued with Enhanced Sword Qi and a hint of Supreme Sword Aura, with nothing but your own Sword Qi. Even if you somehow manage to survive, it still counts as a fail if you allow the Blade of Tribulation to injure your body,\" explained the Sixth Elder.","\"In other words, using nothing but my Sword Aura, I have to emerge unscathed,\" said Yuan.","\"That is correct.\"","This meant that Yuan couldn’t exploit the trial with his regeneration abilities and had to rely solely on his Enhanced Sword Aura.","\"I’m curious... how many people die in this trial?\" Yuan asked.","A cold smile tugged at the corners of the Sixth Elder’s lips as she said, \"The Holy Sword Temple receives thousands of challengers each year, yet only five percent manage to pass its trial. In other words, for ninety-five percent, it becomes a graveyard. That said, only those who have yet to enter the God Ascension realm perish since they cannot live without a physical body.\"","\"If I survive but fail the trial, can I try it again?\" Yuan then asked.","\"Of course, but you’ll have to wait ten years before trying again,\" she said.","\"Alright. Let’s get this over with.\"","Yuan said as he approached the platform.","\"Are you sure? Everyone is given a month to prepare,\" she stopped him.","He nodded.","\"I am sure.\"","\"If you say so.\"","The moment Yuan stepped onto the platform, an overwhelming pressure crashed down upon him, and that was merely the natural aura of the Blade of Tribulation.","Yuan raised his head to gaze at the blade, a mysterious smile forming on his lips. The Holy Sword Clan likely wouldn’t believe him even if he told them, but this wasn’t his first time seeing the Blade of Tribulation. After all, he was the one who forged it when he was the Exalted Blacksmith. In fact, the Blade of Tribulation was crafted during the God of Creation Ceremony."]},{"number":2020,"title":"Chapter 2020: Holy Sword Temple","paragraphs":["\"Whenever you’re ready to begin the trial, activate your Sword Aura and use it to protect your body,\" said the Sixth Elder after Yuan stepped onto the platform. \"The Blade of Tribulation won’t attack unless it senses your Sword Aura.\"","Yuan silently nodded in acknowledgement and took a moment to prepare himself. Then, without hesitation, he unleashed as much Enhanced Sword Aura as he could muster.","The Sixth Elder’s eyes widened with awe when she sensed Yuan’s Enhanced Sword Aura.","’No wonder she gave him her sword badge!’ The Sixth Elder finally understood what caused the Holy Sword Maiden to approve of him.","In response to Yuan’s Sword Aura, the Blade of Tribulation began to tremble—then, within moments, it unleashed its own Enhanced Sword Aura.","And then, as if heralding an execution, the blade descended from the sky, hurling itself toward Yuan with terrifying speed.","Since the trial required him to endure the attack using only his Enhanced Sword Aura, Yuan concentrated solely on that. He remained motionless, calmly awaiting the blade’s descent.","Half a second later, the blade reached Yuan, colliding with his Enhanced Sword Aura. Despite its powerful descent, the Blade of Tribulation came to an abrupt halt the moment its tip touched his aura, frozen in midair.","But it didn’t end there, and the Blade of Tribulation suddenly surged with an even greater wave of Enhanced Sword Aura, this time laced with a faint trace of Supreme Sword Aura.","Yet, Yuan remained firm, his Enhanced Sword Aura unwavering.","\"How long do I have to resist this sword?\" Yuan turned to look at the Sixth Elder.","\"When the Blade of Tribulation stops its attack,\" she responded.","Even without waiting for the end results, the Sixth Elder could tell that Yuan was going to pass the trial with ease the moment she sensed his Sword Aura. His Enhanced Sword Aura was the most powerful she’d ever seen, and she’d met a lot of swordmasters, including Sword Emperors.","Sure enough, exactly thirty seconds after its descent, the Blade of Tribulation withdrew its Enhanced Sword Aura and silently returned to its place in the sky.","\"Congratulations on passing the trial,\" said the Sixth Elder. \"You are the first mortal in history to have ever succeeded—not that there were any mortals before you who’d attempted it.\"","Yuan calmly walked off the platform and said, \"So, when can I enter the Holy Sword Temple?\"","\"Only one person is allowed inside the Holy Sword Temple at a time, and someone is currently training inside,\" she explained. \"There’s also a waitlist, and...\"","She stopped there and retrieved a jade slip to look at the contents inside before continuing, \"You are currently 149th on the list.\"","Yuan’s jaw dropped after hearing this. He was never told about a waitlist, which could take years if not longer.","Noticing his expression, the Sixth Elder explained, \"There’s no strict time limit, but once you step outside, your training is considered complete. Also, there’s no opportunity to rest once you’re inside, so most cultivators only remain in the temple for a few years at a time before coming out to recuperate.\"","\"That’s too long. I don’t have the time to wait for my turn. Is there nothing that can be done?\"","\"Unfortunately, that’s just how the Holy Sword Temple was set up. There’s nothing we, the Holy Sword Clan, can do about it, either. However, there is one way to move up the waitlist...\"","\"How?\" Yuan instantly inquired.","\"You can try swapping places with the next person on the waitlist. It has happened before, but it’s extremely rare and often involves some sort of payment.\"","Yuan rubbed his eyes and muttered, \"What a pain in the ass.\"","Since most cultivators who trained at the Holy Sword Temple were Immortals, waiting a few hundred years to enter one of the Nine Heavens’ most effective training grounds was a small price to pay. But Yuan didn’t have that kind of time.","The Sixth Elder then continued, \"It just so happens that the person who is supposed to go next is already at the Holy Sword Temple. We can talk to them about a potential position swap, and if you want to increase your chances of even having a negotiation, you should make an offer.\"","\"Who is this individual? Knowing a bit more about them would help me prepare a suitable offer,\" Yuan said.","\"This person is the Sect Leader of the Sword Descending Pavilion. Unfortunately, I can’t tell you what he wants since we don’t like prying.\"","\"In that case, can you see if they’re willing to negotiate?\"","\"We can do that. Give me a few minutes.\"","The Sixth Elder flew away the next moment.","While she was away, Yuan pondered what he should do if the negotiations failed—if this Sect Leader even wanted to negotiate at all.","\"I really don’t want to leave empty-handed after spending so much time and effort getting here, but there’s really nothing I can do if I have to wait for my turn. It’s not like I can force my way inside, either,\" he sighed out loud.","The Sixth Elder returned about fifteen minutes later, and before Yuan could even ask her about the negotiation, she silently shook her head.","\"I see...\" Yuan sighed.","Was there truly nothing he could do but wait for his turn?","After another sigh, Yuan spoke, \"Do you think I can take a look at the Holy Sword Temple before I leave?\"","The Sixth Elder nodded, \"If it’s just looking around, there’s no harm in that. Follow me.\"","Yuan followed the Sixth Elder to the Holy Sword Temple, which was only a few minutes away.","Once he was standing before the majestic Holy Sword Temple, a sudden wave of nostalgia surged within Yuan.","\"It’s a pity, but it seems like I am not fated to train here today.\"","A few moments later, Yuan turned around and began walking away.","*Rumble*","However, before he could take even two steps, the ground began to tremble, prompting Yuan to turn around—just in time to see the doors of the Holy Sword Temple slowly begin to open."]},{"number":2021,"title":"Chapter 2021: Holy Sword Temple(2)","paragraphs":["\"The door is opening...?\" The Sixth Elder mumbled.","However, she didn’t think it had anything to do with Yuan and figured it was just a coincidence—that the person inside was finished with their training.","In the very next moment, the Sixth Elder watched as someone emerged from the Holy Sword Temple—no, they were launched out, as if forcefully ejected.","\"What the...?\"","The Sixth Elder followed the figure flying through the air with wide eyes.","\"Fuck!\" the individual shouted as they steadied themselves after being thrown from the Holy Sword Temple.","Once Yuan got a clear look at her, he saw an extraordinarily beautiful woman with shimmering silver hair and radiant jade-green eyes.","Then, she exclaimed in a loud voice, \"What the fuck was that about?!\"","\"Senior...\" The Sixth Elder didn’t understand where the woman’s anger came from. It was not uncommon for people to exit the Holy Sword Temple in ridiculous fashions, and she’d seen it many times.","\"Th-that doesn’t count!\" the woman suddenly said.","\"Excuse me...?\"","\"I said that doesn’t count! I was forcefully ejected from the Holy Sword Temple, so I didn’t come out on my own free will! I’m going back inside!\"","\"W-Wait! Even if you’re the Sword Empress, you cannot—\"","\"Shut up! I just told you that I was forcefully removed!\" said the woman, who turned out to be a Sword Emperor—a Sword Empress since she was female.","Even after one learns Supreme Sword Aura and becomes a Sword Emperor, the Holy Sword Temple remains an excellent training ground to further improve their Supreme Sword Aura, hence why Sword Emperors continue to return to the place even after they achieve their title.","\"But that’s not possible! The Holy Sword Temple doesn’t even have such a function! We’ve been managing the Holy Sword Temple for several eras now, but the only people it has ejected are those who have become corpses! You should know that since you’re also part of our Holy Sword Clan!\" The Sixth Elder exclaimed.","Surprisingly, the silver-haired also belonged to the Holy Sword Temple.","’She’s one of the three Sword Emperors in the Holy Sword Clan?’ Yuan thought to himself as he watched the situation unfold.","\"I know, but I am telling you that’s what happened! Why would I lie about this? It’s not like this is my first time entering the temple!\" said the Sword Empress.","The Sixth Elder was left speechless, but she couldn’t imagine the Sword Empress lying about such a thing, either.","\"Unfortunately, regardless of the circumstances, once you leave the Holy Sword Temple, you are not allowed to enter again until your next turn,\" she said a moment later.","\"Son of a bitch!\" The Sword Empress cursed again. \"I was so close to reaching the next level of Supreme Sword Aura, too!\"","The Sword Empress suddenly snapped her head at Yuan and shouted, \"What the fuck are you looking at, huh?!\"","\"Senior, let’s not take your anger out on a junior... Your reputation is already in the gutters because of your foul mouth,\" the Sixth Elder said as she shook her head.","\"That’s bullshit! He was staring at me so intensely, so I told him off!\"","Yuan couldn’t deny that he had been staring at her, though it was because of her potty mouth that was so out of place for someone of her stature and graceful appearance.","\"I apologize. I didn’t mean to stare.\" Yuan apologized.","The Sword Empress suddenly narrowed her eyes and asked, \"You... have we met before?\"","\"No, I don’t think so.\"","\"What’s your name?\"","\"Yuan.\"","The Sword Empress fell silent, seemingly in deep thought.","\"Whatever,\" she said a moment later.","\"I’ll go get the next person on the waitlist. Please don’t do anything rash while I am away,\" said the Sixth Elder.","\"What? You think I am going to sneak back inside while you leave? You’re mocking me.\"","\"I didn’t say that.\" The Sixth Elder said before leaving.","Instead of leaving, the Sword Empress decided to stay around. Of course, she didn’t have any intention of sneaking inside the Holy Sword Temple.","\"Hey.\"","The Sword Empress called out Yuan again.","\"What is it?\"","\"You’re quite calm despite being in the presence of a Sword Empress, even though you’re just a mortal. What are you even doing here?\"","\"I was going to enter the temple to train, but I don’t have the time to wait for my turn.\"","\"You? Enter the Holy Sword Temple? There’s no way. Don’t lie to me.\" The Sword Empress immediately doubted him since she couldn’t fathom a mortal passing the Blade of Tribulation trial.","\"Why would I lie?\" Yuan showed her the golden badge given to him by the Holy Sword Maiden.","Her eyes widened with surprise after seeing the badge, and she muttered, \"No way...\"","She fell silent again, but she was staring at him with a piercing gaze.","\"Are you sure we haven’t met before? I can’t shake this feeling that we have,\" she said.","Yuan looked at her face and quickly dug through his memories.","\"Sorry, but I really don’t think we’ve met before,\" he responded a moment later.","The Sword Empress remained silent, but she continued inspecting his appearance from head to toe.","The Sixth Elder returned a few minutes later with a handsome middle-aged man following behind.","\"Sword Empress Huang, it’s an honor to meet you today.\" The Sect Leader of the Sword Descending Pavilion greeted her the moment he saw her.","The Sword Empress merely nodded in acknowledgment.","The Sect Leader glanced at Yuan but quickly ignored him after seeing that he was a mortal.","\"You can enter the Holy Sword Temple whenever you’re ready,\" the Sixth Elder said to the Sect Leader a moment later.","The Sect Leader nodded before approaching the massive entrance, quickly disappearing into the temple.","But not even two seconds later, the Sect Leader could be see flying out of the temple, just as the Sword Empress had been ejected minutes earlier.","The Sixth Elder and the Sword Empress’ eyes widened with disbelief after seeing this.","\"What?\" they both muttered in a daze, unable to comprehend the situation."]},{"number":2022,"title":"Chapter 2022: Holy Sword Temple(3)","paragraphs":["\"What the hell was that?!\" The Sect Leader exclaimed with a confused face after stabilizing himself.","\"W-What just happened?\" The Sixth Elder asked even though she already had an idea of what he was going to say.","\"I don’t know. After I entered the temple, I felt a powerful force pulling me back before I even made it to the other side. The next thing I knew, I was outside again,\" said the Sect Leader, disbelief etched across his face.","\"So exactly what happened to me, but in my case, I was in the middle of training...\" said the Sword Empress.","\"Hey, that doesn’t count, right? I clearly didn’t even begin my training!\" The Sect Leader turned to look at the Sixth Elder, who wore a perplexed expression on her face.","Since this was the first time anything like this had happened at the Holy Sword Temple, she wasn’t sure how to deal with it. However, considering the situation, it wouldn’t be fair for the Sect Leader, who clearly didn’t get any training done, if they didn’t allow him to try again.","\"Since this is an unprecedented event, and it’s clear that you didn’t enter the temple properly, I’ll allow you to enter again.\"","The Sixth Elder eventually decided to do the unprecedented and allow someone to enter the temple again after they left.","The Sect Leader thanked her before walking toward the entrance again.","However, the Sword Empress stopped him and said, \"Wait a moment.\"","When the Sect Leader stopped and looked at her with a questioning gaze, she continued, \"You have already been rejected by the Holy Sword Temple once. If you try to enter again, there is a chance that it might hurt you instead of just ejecting you.\"","The Sect Leader’s body trembled slightly at this possibility.","\"Now that I think about this... she’s right.\" The Sixth Elder agreed. \"This is a highly unusual and unprecedented issue. If you attempt to enter again, we cannot guarantee your safety.\"","While countless people have died while training inside the Holy Sword Temple, this was a different situation.","The Sect Leader swallowed nervously. He wouldn’t have any regrets if he died while training inside the Holy Sword Temple, but he’d never be able to die peacefully if he died trying to enter the Holy Sword Temple.","\"Then what should I do...?\" The Sect Leader asked for their opinion even though he already knew the answer.","\"You can either try to enter again or just leave it as it is,\" said the Sword Empress.","The Sect Leader gritted his teeth in frustration. He’d waited hundreds of years for this moment, even leaving his sect for a prolonged period of time just to prepare for the Holy Sword Temple. Yet, after all that preparation, does he have to leave empty-handed? He couldn’t accept this result.","He started at the open entrance, which was now emitting an ominous aura, with a serious pondering face.","Eventually, he walked forward and said, \"I’ll take the risk.\"","The Sixth Elder and the Sword Empress didn’t say anything since they had no authority in his decision, and they’d already warned him of the potential danger.","They all watched as the Sect Leader disappeared into the Holy Sword Temple.","\"...\"","Time seemed to slow as everyone waited, tense and uncertain, to see if the Sect Leader would be ejected from the Holy Sword Temple once more.","Seconds passed, but nothing happened.","\"Did he manage to get inside?\" The Sixth Elder questioned out loud.","\"Looks like—\"","Before the Sword Empress could even finish her sentence, something came out of the Holy Sword Temple.","However, it wasn’t the Sect Leader, but a glowing orb of light.","\"Holy fuck...\" The Sword Empress subconsciously cursed when she saw this.","The Sect Leader had been ejected once more—but this time, it was only his soul. His physical body was nowhere to be seen. This could mean only one of two things: either his body had been destroyed, or he had been forcefully stripped from it as punishment for defying the Holy Sword Temple’s warning.","\"M-My physical body!\" The Sect Leader exclaimed in shock after realizing he’d emerged from the Holy Sword Temple as just his soul.","\"Sixth Elder! This is unacceptable! How are you going to compensate me for this?!\" The Sect Leader’s angry voice rippled throughout the place.","\"That’s...\"","Although they had warned him of the risks of entering again—and the Holy Sword Temple’s malfunction wasn’t directly their fault—others might not see it that way. After all, the Holy Sword Clan owned and managed the temple, and if anything went wrong, they would be held accountable.","The Sword Empress stepped forward and said, \"Listen here, you little bastard. I warned you loud and fucking clear that something like this would happen, but you went ahead and risked it. You’re lucky to have escaped with your life.\"","\"You—!\"","The Sect Leader wanted to say something but was immediately interrupted by the Sword Empress, \"However, it’s true that the Holy Sword Temple is malfunctioning, and while we currently have no idea why, we’ll compensate you for the trouble. We’ll pay for the resources for your new physical body and some more, and we’ll also allow you to enter the Holy Sword Temple without needing to wait once we figure out and fix the issue. Of course, that is if you want to come back here in the future.\"","\"If you’re not satisfied with the compensation, we can continue this at a later date in a more formal setting.\"","The Sect Leader remained silent for a moment before responding, \"This isn’t over. I’ll contact the Holy Sword Clan again after I deal with my physical body.\"","After saying that, the Sect Leader flew away, disappearing into the Starry Sky.","\"Fuck... what a pain in the ass...\" The Sword Empress cursed out loud after he left, rubbing her eyes in a stressed manner.","\"This is indeed quite troublesome... How are we supposed to fix a problem we don’t even understand?\" the Sixth Elder sighed."]},{"number":2023,"title":"Chapter 2023: Holy Sword Temple(4)","paragraphs":["\"So, what should we do about the Holy Sword Temple? We don’t know what’s causing it to reject people.\" The Sixth Elder looked at the Sword Empress for her thoughts.","The Sword Empress shrugged, \"How the hell am I supposed to know? Unless the creator of the temple is here, there’s no way we will know for sure.\"","\"The God of Creation...? He died several eras ago, so that’s impossible.\"","Unbeknownst to them, the individual they were talking about was standing right behind them.","\"Looks like we’ll have to shut down the Holy Sword Temple until we figure it out,\" said the Sword Empress.","\"We’re going to have a lot of complaints.\"","\"Fuck them.\" The Sword Empress calmly cursed. \"If they can’t understand why we have to shut the place down, then let them go inside and experience the reason for themselves. Of course, we won’t be compensating for anything.\"","\"And harm our reputation even more...?\" The Sixth Elder shook her head.","The two of them fell silent.","\"Umm...\" Yuan suddenly spoke out.","\"Huh? You’re still here? Get lost already,\" the Sword Empress said, waving him off with a dismissive gesture.","He continued, \"This might sound crazy, but I’d like to enter the Holy Sword Temple.\"","The two ladies turned to look at him with raised eyebrows.","\"Are you serious? Even after seeing everything that had happened?\" The Sixth Elder remarked with a dumbfounded look on her face.","Yuan nodded, \"Yes.\"","\"Listen here, you dumb brat. The Descending Sword Pavilion’s Sect Leader only survived because he was a God Ascension Realm cultivator and could live without a physical body. If you go inside, you’ll definitely die.\"","\"Even so, I’d like to try,\" Yuan said with a stubborn expression.","The Sword Empress rubbed her eyes and looked at the Sixth Elder, saying, \"Can you believe this fucking idiot?\"","The Sixth Elder could only shake her head in silence.","\"You know what? I don’t know why you’re so eager to die, but it’s none of our business. Go ahead and enter the temple if you want.\" The Sword Empress said a moment later.","\"Thank you.\" Yuan bowed to them and turned to face the temple’s entrance.","\"You’re not serious, are you? Please think this through. You are one of the most talented individuals I’ve come across. It’d be a waste to die here.\"","While the Sword Empress couldn’t care less if Yuan died, the Sixth Elder, who’d witnessed his talents, couldn’t bear to see him die such a pointless death and decided to block his path.","\"Since when were you such a busybody, Sixth Elder? Just let him die.\"","\"You’re only saying that because you didn’t see his trial. This young man... his Enhanced Sword Aura is likely even stronger than yours,\" she responded.","The Sword Empress’ eyes widened with bafflement after hearing such outrageous words.","\"Now that is a claim I cannot ignore. You think this stinking mortal brat’s Enhanced Sword Aura is stronger than mine? Have you gone senile from being in this place for too long?\"","Who was she? She was the Sword Empress—a swordmaster who had reached the pinnacle of swordsmanship. And yet, the Sixth Elder had the audacity to claim that a mere mortal surpassed her? The notion was utterly absurd.","Before the Sixth Elder could respond, the Sword Empress looked at Yuan and asked him, \"What do you think? Do you think your Enhanced Sword Aura is stronger than mine?\"","\"No,\" Yuan answered almost instantly without any hesitation.","The Sword Empress narrowed her eyes at him.","\"Your words are telling me one thing, but your eyes are telling me something else,\" she eventually said.","Then, without another word, she walked away from the temple and stopped in an open area.","\"Come, let me see your Enhanced Sword Aura for myself. If you can defeat me, I’ll let you enter the Holy Sword Temple,\" she said.","\"...\"","Yuan sighed inwardly at how the situation turned out. He only wanted to enter the Holy Sword Temple without any issue, but the Sixth Elder had to open her mouth.","When the Sixth Elder noticed Yuan glaring at her with blame in his eyes, she could only respond with an apologetic smile.","\"Are you really going to fight with a mortal? If this spreads, your reputation will truly hit rock bottom,\" said the Sixth Elder, trying to stop the farce.","\"Who the hell said we’re going to fight? We’re just clashing Enhanced Sword Auras with each other, nothing more, nothing less. Don’t worry, I won’t hurt him.\"","Seeing the Sword Empress’ stubborn face, Yuan knew he had no choice but to play along. Since he couldn’t sense any ill intent coming from her, he wasn’t worried that she might try to kill him.","Some time later, the two stood facing each other, separated by a distance of roughly a dozen meters.","\"Let’s keep this simple. When I say go, we’ll both release our Enhanced Sword Aura, and the one with the sharpest and strongest sword aura wins.\"","Yuan nodded in acknowledgement.","\"I’ll give you a few minutes to prepare.\"","\"No need.\" Yuan calmly rejected.","\"Well, would you look at that... Feeling confident, are you? Even after saying ’no’ to my question?\" the Sword Empress said with an irritated smile, feeling like she was being looked down upon by Yuan, a mere mortal.","She retrieved a spirit stone from her spatial ring and said, \"When this touches the ground, release your sword aura.\"","Then, she flicked the spirit stone into the air.","Once it dropped to the ground a moment later, both Yuan and the Sword Empress unleashed their Enhanced Sword Aura, instantly flooding the Holy Sword Temple with powerful ripples of energy. Had the place not been constructed from materials resistant to sword aura, their clash would have torn everything apart.","\"Son of a fucking bitch...\" The Sword Empress cursed under her breath as she compared their Enhanced Sword Auras, only to realize she was slightly inferior to Yuan, causing her face to twist with disbelief."]},{"number":2024,"title":"Chapter 2024: True Enhanced Sword Aura","paragraphs":["\"Are you satisfied now?\" Yuan asked the Sword Empress once it was clear whose Enhanced Sword Aura was stronger.","The Sword Empress withdrew her sword aura, but she remained silent, seemingly trying to comprehend the situation.","How can a mere mortal have a deeper understanding of sword aura than a Sword Emperor, someone who has hundreds of thousands of years of experience? It just didn’t make sense no matter how she thought about it.","’No... what if he’s a reincarnator who was a Sword Emperor in his past life?’","The Sword Empress thought of this possibility, which made the most sense.","After clicking her tongue, the Sword Empress spoke in a defeated tone, \"Fine, you win.\"","\"Then I’ll be entering the Holy Sword Temple now.\" Yuan turned toward the entrance and immediately began walking to it.","\"Wait!\" The Sword Empress suddenly stopped him.","\"What is it now?\" Yuan sighed.","Now that she had witnessed Yuan’s talent firsthand, she agreed with the Sixth Elder that letting someone like him throw his life away would be a waste.","\"Why are you so desperate? To the point of throwing your life away?\" she asked.","\"...\"","Of course, Yuan had no intention of throwing his life away. He was certain that the Holy Sword Temple’s unusual behavior was connected to him. But it wasn’t something he could reveal—and even if he tried, they wouldn’t believe him.","\"I won’t die,\" he said.","\"What makes you sound so sure?\"","\"Just a feeling,\" he shrugged.","And before they could say anything else, Yuan suddenly sped into the temple, disappearing before their eyes.","\"That fool...\" The Sword Empress shook her head.","Moments passed, but Yuan wasn’t ejected from the Holy Sword Temple. Seeing this, they believed that Yuan had been killed inside.","\"That idiot just wouldn’t listen...\" The Sword Empress sighed.","\"We can’t be sure he’s dead since there’s no corpse,\" said the Sixth Elder.","\"The Sword Descending Pavilion’s Sect Leader emerged with just his soul, so the Holy Sword Temple had likely destroyed his physical body. Since Yuan is just a mortal, he wouldn’t be able to survive without his body. It’s a pity that we lost such a talented individual, but there’s nothing we can do. Countless geniuses die every day.\"","However, just as the Sword Empress turned around and began walking away, the Sixth Elder suddenly shouted, \"Look! The temple’s door has closed!\"","\"What?\"","The Sword Empress halted in her tracks and turned around. And sure enough, the entrance to the Holy Sword Temple had been sealed—an occurrence that only took place when the trial had officially begun.","\"No way... he actually managed to make it inside? Then why the hell did it force the Sect Leader and me out?\" she muttered in a confused daze.","The Sixth Elder had no response and could only stare at the closed door with a dumbfounded face.","Meanwhile, inside the Holy Sword Temple, Yuan found himself standing in a vast room that had the aesthetic of an ancient temple. However, he wasn’t alone.","At the far end of the room stood another figure—tall and imposing, clad in white and silver robes, with a faceless mask concealing his identity.","\"Tian Xin...\" Yuan instantly recognized himself.","He had expected some sort of exchange, but without a word, Tian Xin suddenly raised his arm, summoning thousands of blades into the air, each forged from pure Enhanced Sword Aura.","\"What the—\"","With a swift motion, Tian Xin swung his arm downward, sending the countless blades hurtling toward him like a deadly rain of arrows.","Yuan instantly enveloped himself in Enhanced Sword Aura. Since his sword aura matched Tian Xin’s in strength, the incoming blades wouldn’t slice through him outright, but they would gradually wear down his defense, chipping away at the sword aura protecting his body.","\"I see... so the training has already begun.\"","Quickly realizing this, Yuan stopped thinking about anything else and immediately began fighting back.","Mirroring Tian Xin’s move, Yuan conjured thousands of blades formed from Enhanced Sword Aura, intercepting the incoming assault. With the barrage deflected, he surged forward, gripping Number One Under Heaven tightly in his hand.","To Yuan’s surprise, Tian Xin drew a sword of his own, and it was also Number One Under Heaven.","With every clash, their Enhanced Sword Auras erupted violently, scattering in all directions like sparks.","Time flew by, and in the blink of an eye, nearly two weeks had passed since Yuan’s battle with Tian Xin began. And yet, neither had managed to gain the upper hand—it was as if they were locked in a perfect stalemate.","This didn’t surprise Yuan, since they were essentially the same person.","However, after another two weeks, at the beginning of their second month fighting, Tian Xin suddenly spoke in a somewhat mocking tone, \"You are supposed to grow stronger with every reincarnation, yet you don’t seem any stronger than me. If you want to defeat me, you’ll have to become stronger than all of your incarnations!\"","Hearing this, Yuan felt something click inside his head.","’He’s right... I have stopped seriously trying to improve myself after I began regaining my memories...\"","He realized that he’d only been recovering his original strength, but he hadn’t been trying to become stronger than that.","Upon realizing this, Yuan stopped fighting with the intention to defeat Tian Xin, but to improve himself.","With tens of millions of years of experience under his belt, Yuan’s level of comprehension was unfathomable.","Soon, Yuan slipped into a trance mid-battle. Though his consciousness went elsewhere, his body moved instinctively, as if it were on autopilot.","As time continued to flow, Yuan’s Enhanced Sword Aura started growing stronger despite having reached the realm of perfection.","Tian Xin smiled behind his mask after seeing this.","After spending an entire year inside the Holy Sword Temple and fighting with Tian Xin nonstop, Yuan’s sword aura had reached a new level. While it wasn’t Supreme Sword Aura, it surpassed all Enhanced Sword Aura and came extremely close to Supreme Sword Aura.","\"Let’s just call this... True Enhanced Sword Aura.\" Yuan muttered with a satisfied smile on his face."]},{"number":2025,"title":"Chapter 2025: True Sword Body","paragraphs":["After attaining True Enhanced Sword Aura, Yuan’s combat prowess surged to a new level. Tian Xin’s perfected Enhanced Sword Aura was no longer a threat, and each clash ended the same, with Yuan’s aura shattering Tian Xin’s like a rock smashing through glass.","Just a few hours after acquiring True Enhanced Sword Aura, Yuan defeated Tian Xin, putting an end to their year-long battle.","Tian Xin sat on the ground with half of his body severed, but since he was just an illusion, there was no blood, and he could still talk.","\"Not bad,\" muttered Tian Xin.","\"However, this is just the beginning. Not only do you still have to learn Supreme Sword Aura, but you must eventually surpass it.\"","Suddenly, Tian Xin’s severed body reassembled itself, merging seamlessly back into one.","\"And I am here to help you achieve Supreme Sword Aura.\"","Once he was back on his feet, Tian Xin’s body surged with Supreme Sword Aura.","\"I’m sure you already have the understanding and experience to use Supreme Sword Aura, but you still can’t learn it for some reason, right?\"","Yuan nodded.","\"Then you just need to let it naturally reveal itself, and the best way to do that is through battle. It’s going to hurt, so brace yourself.\"","Tian Xin warned before attacking with Supreme Sword Aura, sending it toward Yuan like a relentless storm.","The moment Tian Xin’s Supreme Sword Aura collided with Yuan’s True Enhanced Sword Aura, a brief struggle ensued—but soon, Yuan’s aura began to erode under the overwhelming force. Had he relied on mere Enhanced Sword Aura, the Supreme Sword Aura would have torn through it instantly, destroying his physical body without resistance.","\"How are you going to deal with this?!\"","Tian Xin laughed maniacally as he continued his onslaught, his Supreme Sword Aura growing stronger with every passing moment until it eventually was strong enough to destroy Yuan’s True Enhanced Sword Aura instantly.","Unfortunately, there was little Yuan could do but endure the onslaught. Without his regeneration abilities, he would have perished in that very moment. Yet, he persevered, enduring relentless pain for months on end.","After another year of fighting Tian Xin, Yuan improved himself once more. His Sword Body, which had been attained after fusing his Sword Aura into his body, evolved.","<After perfecting fusing your Enhanced Sword Aura with your body, your Sword Body has evolved into Enhanced Sword Body>","After acquiring Enhanced Sword Body, Yuan’s body became untouchable by Enhanced Auras. Of course, since he was up against Supreme Sword Aura, Tian Xin could still damage him.","Half a month later, Yuan improved his Enhanced Sword Body again, this time fusing his True Enhanced Sword Aura with it.","<After perfecting fusing your True Enhanced Sword Aura with your body, your Sword Body has evolved into True Sword Body>","Throughout the history of the Nine Heavens, fewer than a hundred swordmasters have ever attained a Sword Body, most of them being Sword Emperors. Yet, the number of those who have achieved an Enhanced Sword Body is even rarer, numbering fewer than ten. To reach that level, one must not only master but also perfect Enhanced Sword Aura—a feat even more difficult than attaining Supreme Sword Aura","As for the True Sword Body, Yuan had just become the first in history to attain it. No one had ever reached the level of True Enhanced Sword Aura before, as most abandoned their pursuit of Enhanced Sword Aura after achieving the more prestigious Supreme Sword Aura.","Now with the True Sword Body, Tian Xin’s Supreme Sword Aura could only damage his skin and leave scratches.","By now, three years had passed since Yuan parted ways with the others to train in the Holy Sword Temple. Though he had yet to attain Supreme Sword Aura, his overall combat prowess had grown tremendously, and he could feel its manifestation drawing near.","Most cultivators who attain Supreme Sword Aura spend millions of years honing their craft to manifest even a trace of it, and the majority who pursue it never succeed at all, but Yuan was confident that he would acquire it within the next three years.","Empowered by his True Sword Body, Yuan fought Tian Xin with even greater ferocity. Each clash between them shook the entire temple to its core, but because they battled within a separate dimension, the world outside remained undisturbed.","Meanwhile, news of the Holy Sword Temple’s malfunction spread across the Nine Heavens, revealed by the Sect Leader of the Sword Descending Pavilion after his devastating experience. The news left many disheartened and anxious for the future of the sword path, as the vast majority of those who had attained Supreme Sword Aura had done so within the temple’s training grounds.","The Holy Sword Clan, responsible for overseeing the temple, scrambled to find someone capable of analyzing and repairing the issue. Although Yuan had managed to enter without any issue, they didn’t want to risk it, and until he came out, there was no concrete evidence that the temple was safe.","However, the Holy Sword Temple was no ordinary structure but a divine treasure forged by the Exalted Blacksmith, who has long perished. As such, their only option was to seek out the most experienced blacksmiths in the Nine Heavens, that being the current God of Creation.","Time passed, and in the blink of an eye, another year had passed, making it nearly half a decade since Yuan made his way to the Holy Sword Temple.","Inside, he was still fighting Tian Xin. However, Yuan’s sword aura had begun showing signs of Supreme Sword Aura.","After another month of relentless combat, Yuan’s body suddenly became shrouded in an aura so sharp and intense that it seemed ready to slice through space itself.","<You have learned Supreme Sword Aura>","In just four years, three years since he entered the Holy Sword Temple, Yuan had achieved Supreme Sword Aura, something that took the others millions of years to achieve.","If this were made public, it would cause an unprecedented uproar."]},{"number":2026,"title":"Chapter 2026: Supreme Sword Aura","paragraphs":["\"Supreme Sword Aura... I’ve missed this feeling,\" Yuan muttered to himself, savoring the overwhelming power coursing through him.","But he wasn’t content. If he intended to compete in the Sword Emperor Qualifications, his current mastery wouldn’t be enough. At the very least, he needed to gain true control over it.","\"Hey, I know you’re far more capable than what you’ve shown me so far.\" Yuan suddenly said to him. \"Fight me with all you’ve got.\"","\"With everything I’ve got? At your current level, I could instantly kill you.\" Tian Xin mocked.","\"I’m not asking you to kill me—just push me to my limits. Make me feel like I’m on the edge of death,\" Yuan said, a cold smile curling on his lips.","Tian Xin also smiled behind his mask.","\"Very well...\" he responded a moment later.","In the very next moment, Tian Xin’s aura erupted, instantly transforming the atmosphere of the training grounds into something grim and suffocating, like death itself had descended. He was no longer holding back as a True Immortal; his cultivation surged into the God Ascension Realm. At the same time, his Supreme Sword Aura intensified, rising to a state of perfection.","Under Tian Xin’s overwhelming pressure, Yuan could barely remain standing. Each breath felt like a struggle, as though an invisible hand was tightening around his throat.","\"Now, are you ready for the real training to begin?\" Tian Xin spoke in a somewhat sadistic tone, sending chills down Yuan’s spine.","\"Ready or not, here I come!\"","Without giving Yuan a chance to respond, Tian Xin activated Shadow Veil, vanishing in an instant and reappearing behind him, Number One Under Heaven already piercing through Yuan’s back.","Yuan coughed up a mouthful of blood but quickly steadied himself and swung behind him, only to strike nothing but air. In the blink of an eye, Tian Xin was in front of him, his blade already mid-swing.","Before Yuan could even register what was happening, all of his limbs had been severed.","Tian Xin’s attacks weren’t powered by Supreme Sword Qi alone—they were also reinforced with Celestial Qi. That was why he could so effortlessly tear through Yuan’s body.","For the next several months, Yuan was pushed to the brink of death again and again, enduring countless near-death experiences. However, he was also improving at a rapid rate, and his Supreme Sword Aura became more refined and powerful.","Eventually, after spending nearly six years in the Holy Sword Temple, Yuan perfected his Supreme Sword Aura and even began to merge it with his True Sword Body.","Once he was satisfied with the results of his training, Yuan exited the Holy Sword Temple.","Before departing, Tian Xin handed him a sword. At first glance, it looked like a simple steel blade, but intricate symbols were etched along its surface. Despite its craftsmanship, it didn’t radiate the aura of a treasure. Instead, it seemed more like a unique ornament with hidden meaning.","\"Do you know what this is?\" Tian Xin asked him.","Yuan pondered for a moment before recalling something, \"Yes, I do.\"","\"Then, do you know where to go?\"","\"Of course.\"","After passing the sword to him, Tian Xin turned around and calmly walked away, disappearing like a ghost after a few steps.","Yuan left the Holy Sword Temple shortly afterward.","Meanwhile, outside the Holy Sword Temple, the Holy Sword Clan had spent the past several years tirelessly inspecting the structure, desperately trying to uncover the source of the problem.","However, since the Holy Sword Temple had shut its door, they were unable to go inside and could only work from the outside.","\"Damn it... If only we could go inside the temple... It’s been closed for half a decade by now. When do you think it’ll open—if it’ll even open again?\"","\"The longest someone has spent inside the temple is about 100 years, but most people tend to leave after a decade or two, earlier if they come out as corpses.\"","\"But the one who went inside was a mortal, right? I’m surprised he hasn’t come out already.\"","\"He could already be long dead for all we know.\"","\"That’s true.\"","However, just moments later, the doors to the Holy Sword Temple slowly creaked open, drawing the attention of everyone present. All eyes widened as a handsome man stepped out. Though he had already withdrawn his Supreme Sword Aura, its remnants clung to him—residue from years of continuous use.","Everyone there was a Swordmaster, and the moment they sensed the lingering aura surrounding Yuan, they instinctively swallowed hard and lowered their heads, humbled by the overwhelming presence.","\"You’re alive!\"","A familiar face suddenly approached him.","\"It’s been a while, Sixth Elder,\" Yuan said with a gentle smile.","She swallowed hard, her voice trembling as she stammered, \"Y-Y-You... you learned Supreme Sword Aura?! In just five years?!\"","Even though it was right before her eyes, the Sixth Elder could scarcely believe it. Not only had Yuan achieved Supreme Sword Aura in record time, but he was also likely the first mortal in history to ever do so.","\"Looks like it.\" Yuan calmly responded.","\"Anyway, I’ll be leaving now.\"","\"W-Wait! Please wait!\" The Sixth Elder stopped him.","There was no way she could let him leave just like that.","\"Why don’t you join our Holy Sword Clan?\" the Sixth Elder said eagerly. \"Our Faction Leader isn’t here right now, but if he were, he’d be begging you himself! With your talent, you’re destined to become the greatest Swordmaster in history—perhaps even surpassing the Faceless Sword Emperor!\"","\"I’m flattered, but I don’t have time to talk about that now. I need to hurry to the Gates of Heaven for the Sword Emperor Qualification,\" he calmly responded.","\"Sword Emperor Qualification? You’re also going to participate?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"That’s perfect since our Faction Leader and the others are currently there to spectate it,\" she said. \"Come with me.\"","Yuan nodded and followed her, leaving the others behind, still staring in a daze and struggling to comprehend what they had just witnessed."]},{"number":2027,"title":"Chapter 2027: Leaving the Holy Sword Temple","paragraphs":["Yuan followed the Sixth Elder to the same golden carriage that had brought him to the Holy Sword Temple years ago. Once inside, the flying treasure immediately began to move, but it moved at a much quicker pace than before.","\"We will arrive directly at the Gates of Heaven in one month, so we have plenty of time to talk.\"","Yuan had hoped to visit the Super Perfect Physique Tempering Sect first, but time was short. Besides, he was fairly certain they would already be at the Gates of Heaven since he had mentioned his intention to enter the Sword Emperor Qualifications, after all.","\"You want me to join the Holy Sword Clan, right? While it wasn’t direct, I have already been recruited by the Holy Sword Maiden.\"","\"In that case... what do you think?\"","Most people would leap at the opportunity to join the Holy Sword Clan, so this was the first time the Sixth Elder had encountered someone who didn’t. Yet she wasn’t offended. In fact, with talent like his, she felt he had every right to be picky.","\"I said that I’d need some time to see whether the Holy Sword Clan was a place I wanted to be associated with. After all, I don’t want to join a place I know nothing about. What if I accidentally join a faction with a bad reputation? I don’t want that to happen.\"","\"Then you have nothing to worry about! Our Holy Sword Clan is not only reputable, but we’re also very respected. Besides the recent incident with the Holy Sword Temple, we don’t have any issues.\"","Hearing this, Yuan felt a little guilty. The Holy Sword Temple only acted it did because of him, but the Holy Sword Temple took the blame.","\"About the Holy Sword Temple... I think everything is functional again. I was able to train inside without any issues, after all,\" said Yuan.","The Sixth Elder nodded and said, \"I’m glad nothing happened to you, but we can’t assume it’s safe to enter again. We’ll need to conduct a thorough analysis.\"","Yuan wanted to tell her it wasn’t necessary, but chose to remain silent, as explaining everything would be too troublesome, and she likely wouldn’t believe him anyway.","Since there was nothing actually wrong with the Holy Sword Temple, they’d find nothing unusual. Most likely, they’d just waste time investigating, only to resume using it in the near future.","\"Anyway, I’ll consider joining the Holy Sword Clan, so you don’t need to try to convince me,\" he then said.","\"If you say so...\" Not wanting to annoy him, the Sixth Elder stopped mentioning it and closed her eyes to cultivate.","Yuan spent the following month by the window, gazing into the distance each day in hopes of seeing the Eater of Stars again, but alas, she never appeared.","A month later, they arrived at the Gates of Heaven in the Seventh Heaven. Since most cultivators from the Eighth and Ninth Heavens possessed treasures that allowed them to spectate from afar and had the resources to travel downward, hosting the Sword Emperor Qualifications in the Seventh Heaven ensured the greatest possible audience.","The Gates of Heaven’s territory spanned thousands of miles, making it one of the most prominent sects in the Seventh Heaven, with a disciple count exceeding one hundred thousand. Much of its popularity stemmed from its vast and unparalleled collection of cultivation techniques, and unlike many others, the sect was generous in sharing them with its disciples.","The sect’s leader, Bai Ling, was among the most respected cultivators in the Nine Heavens—hailed as a hero by many and regarded as a role model throughout the cultivation world.","His contributions to the Nine Heavens were nearly unparalleled. Beyond making techniques affordable through the Myriad of Techniques, Bai Ling was renowned for aiding anyone in need, regardless of their status or background.","Despite holding only the rank of Overlord within the Celestial Overlords, Bai Ling’s contributions were unmatched, even surpassing those of the Celestial Overlords themselves.","Of course, if he wished, he could easily claim the title, having been offered the position multiple times. Yet, for reasons unknown, he had declined each offer and remained as Xu Jiaqi’s closest aide.","Thanks to Bai Ling’s esteemed reputation, news that the next Sword Emperor Qualifications would be held at the Gates of Heaven quickly drew the attention of countless prominent figures across the Nine Heavens—many of whom chose to attend in person. Naturally, as a once-in-100,000-year event, the Sword Emperor Qualifications already commanded immense attention, drawing an endless sea of spectators from across the world.","Even before reaching the Gates of Heaven, Yuan could see thousands of cultivators converging from all directions, almost as if there was a massive banquet.","\"We’re here.\" The Sixth Elder said as she walked to the door.","\"Give me a moment.\"","Yuan retrieved his mask and wore it.","The Sixth Elder raised her eyebrows after seeing this, and she couldn’t help but ask, \"What’s with the mask?\"","\"There are too many people here, and I don’t like having too much attention,\" he calmly responded.","\"...\"","The Sixth Elder remained silent, her gaze fixed on Yuan, his appearance strikingly reminiscent of the Faceless Sword Emperor.","Unbeknownst to Yuan, all who trained in the Holy Sword Temple had to face Tian Xin in battle, so they were very familiar with his appearance.","\"Did you sign up for the event yet?\" she suddenly asked.","\"No, I haven’t. Is it too late?\"","\"No, you can still sign up now. Most people sign up a few days before the qualifications begin, anyway. Come with me. I’ll take you there.\"","Yuan nodded.","After stepping out of the golden carriage, Yuan followed the Sixth Elder to the sect’s entrance, where hundreds of people were streaming in through the gates.","While the crowd made their way to the spectators’ area, the Sixth Elder led Yuan to the inner court of the sect, a far quieter place, as guests were only permitted to roam the outer court."]},{"number":2028,"title":"Chapter 2028: You Better Remember My Name!","paragraphs":["When they arrived at their destination, Yuan noticed a few familiar faces, all standing before a fist-sized red crystal that floated on a circular platform.","The first familiar face was Li Bowen from the Holy Sword Clan, and then there was the potty-mouthed Sword Empress. The other familiar faces were obviously the Holy Sword Maiden and the Holy Sword King.","Right as their arrival, Yuan could see a handsome man standing before the red crystal with a sword in his grasp and his body gushing with Supreme Sword Aura.","\"You may begin,\" said a middle-aged man clad in the Gates of Heaven’s Sect Elder uniform.","Then, the handsome man swung his sword at the floating red crystal, striking it with his Supreme Sword Aura.","However, the red crystal remained undamaged, emitting a faint red glow the next moment.","\"I’m sorry, but your Supreme Sword Aura is not strong enough to participate,\" said the Sect Elder.","\"Damn it!\" The handsome man clenched his teeth in anger and frustration.","\"Hahaha!\" The Holy Sword King suddenly laughed as he stepped forward.","\"Let me show you how it’s done!\"","He retrieved his sword and immediately surged with Supreme Sword Aura that was noticeably much stronger than the man’s.","Once the Sect Elder nodded, the Holy Sword King swung at the red crystal, causing it to emit a bright crimson light.","\"Holy Sword King of the Holy Sword Clan, qualified,\" said the Sect Elder.","The man sucked his teeth in annoyance at the Holy Sword King but didn’t say anything since the Holy Sword King was clearly stronger than him.","After the Holy Sword King, the Holy Sword Maiden stepped forward and repeated the same thing, striking the red crystal with her Supreme Sword Aura.","The red crystal radiated a brilliant crimson light, comparable to that of the Holy Sword King, and perhaps even subtly stronger.","\"Holy Sword Maiden of the Holy Sword Clan, qualified.\"","\"Senior Huang, what do you think? Do you think we can become Sword Emperors?\" The Holy Sword King asked the Sword Empress.","She snorted and said, \"Just because you qualify to participate doesn’t mean you’ll qualify as a Sword Emperor. However, judging by your results, I think you’ll have a good chance of—\"","The Sword Empress abruptly cut herself off when two figures caught her eye from the corner of her vision. Normally, such a sight wouldn’t warrant her attention, but one was the Sixth Elder, and the other wore a mask.","Ignoring the Sixth Elder, the Sword Empress focused her attention on Yuan, her eyes wide with disbelief.","\"Faceless Sword Emperor?\" she muttered in a daze.","\"What?\" The others followed her gaze.","Since everyone who trained inside the Holy Sword Temple had fought the Faceless Sword Emperor, they were all familiar with his appearance.","\"No way...\"","The Holy Sword Maiden and the others were just as stunned as the Sword Empress.","After all, Yuan didn’t just resemble the Faceless Sword Emperor in stature—he was, in almost every way, his mirror image.","Yuan stepped up and asked the Sect Elder, \"I just need to hit this crystal with my Supreme Sword Aura, right?\"","\"Yes, but you’re...\" The Sect Elder looked at Yuan with raised eyebrows because of his low cultivation.","However, Yuan ignored him.","Without even drawing a sword, he simply extended a finger toward the crystal before channeling a vast amount of Supreme Sword Aura, all concentrated at his fingertip.","The Holy Sword Maiden and the Holy Sword King immediately frowned as they sensed his Supreme Sword Aura, as it was far superior to their own.","A moment later, Yuan unleashed his Supreme Sword Aura, directing it straight at the red crystal.","The crystal flared with a brilliant crimson light for a brief second, then abruptly dimmed as cracks began to spread across its surface.","\"Ah?!\" The Sect Elder exclaimed in a shocked and nervous voice when he saw the cracks.","The red crystal was renowned as the strongest and most durable material in the Nine Heavens when it came to withstanding sword auras, and only Sword Emperors would be able to damage it. Yet, Yuan had cracked it with such ease.","\"Sorry, I didn’t think it would be so fragile,\" Yuan quickly apologized to the Sect Elder, who was speechless.","\"Wait a second... that voice and cultivation!\" The Sword Empress suddenly realized something and approached Yuan.","However, as she stood before him, she began doubting herself.","\"No... it can’t be you...\" she muttered.","She thought he was Yuan, but he’d entered the Holy Sword Temple a few years ago. There was simply no way he could’ve learned Supreme Sword Aura and honed it to such a terrifying degree in such a short amount of time.","\"It is him.\" The Sixth Elder suddenly spoke.","The Sword Empress turned to look at her with wide eyes.","\"He came out of the Holy Sword Temple a month ago, and we came straight here because he wanted to participate in the Sword Emperor Qualifications,\" she continued.","After hearing this, the Sword Empress turned to look at Yuan again.","Then, she spoke in a somewhat trembling voice, \"I had expected you to be a True Reincarnator when I saw your talents at the Holy Sword Temple, and you’ve just confirmed it. If I had to gamble, I’d bet my entire fortune that you were the Faceless Sword Emperor in your past life.\"","\"Him?! A True Reincarnator?!\" The others exclaimed, their eyes wide with shock and disbelief.","Yuan smiled behind his mask and said, \"You’re giving me too much credit. I’m flattered.\"","\"Hmph!\" A cold snort suddenly resounded, and the Holy Sword King stepped forward.","\"Even if you’re the Faceless Sword Emperor’s reincarnation, I won’t lose to you! The Sword Emperor Qualifications are much more than just the strength of our Supreme Sword Aura!\"","\"...\"","After staring at him for a second, Yuan pretended not to know him and said, \"Sorry, but who are you?\"","The Holy Sword King trembled in anger before responding in a loud voice, \"I am the Holy Sword King, Zhang Wu Bing, the man who will defeat you! You better remember my name!\""]},{"number":2029,"title":"Chapter 2029: A Month Delay","paragraphs":["\"You’ll defeat me? I’ll look forward to it,\" Yuan calmly responded to the Holy Sword King’s aggression.","The Sword Empress merely shook her head in silence. Although she wanted to smack some sense into the Holy Sword King’s head, there was also no guarantee that Yuan would win the Sword Emperor Qualifications just because his Supreme Sword Aura was stronger.","The qualifications tested more than just the strength of one’s Supreme Sword Aura. It also evaluated the swordmaster’s skill, versatility, and overall mastery of their swordsmanship. After all, becoming a Sword Emperor demanded more than raw power, and only the most refined and knowledgeable swordmasters could earn such a prestigious title.","The Holy Sword Maiden silently watched the events unfold before her, her eyes staring at Yuan, feeling like she’d met him before, but she couldn’t remember when. Of course, she had no idea that the man before her was Yuan, the person she’d given her sword badge to.","\"Take this.\" The Sect Elder approached Yuan and handed him a medallion. \"This proves you’re qualified, and you’ll need it during the Sword Emperor Qualifications.\"","\"Thank you. And about the crystal...\"","The Sect Elder turned to look at the cracked red crystal and sighed, \"We’ll have to delay the Sword Emperor Qualifications until we receive another one.\"","\"Delay?! How long will it be delayed?!\" The Sword Empress asked.","\"A month at most.\"","\"Sorry...\" Yuan apologized.","\"Anyway, I have someplace to be, so I’ll talk to you guys later.\"","And without waiting for their response, he turned around and flew away.","\"Senior Huang... who was that man?\" The Holy Sword Maiden turned to ask the Sword Empress shortly after.","\"Hm? You don’t know?\" The Sword Empress looked at her with raised eyebrows.","\"Should I know him...?\"","\"Of course. Since you gave him your sword badge.\"","The Holy Sword Maiden’s eyes widened with shock after hearing this, and she finally realized who the masked figure was.","\"That was him?!\" she exclaimed.","The Holy Sword King didn’t say anything, but he was looking at the Holy Sword Maiden with a slight frown on his face, as he couldn’t remember the last time she seemed so engaged.","Though the Holy Sword King never openly admitted it, those close to him had long suspected his affection for the Holy Sword Maiden. Since their parents were both Sword Emperors in the Holy Sword Clan, the two had grown up together.","Unfortunately, the Holy Sword Maiden did not seem to have the same affection for him, for from the moment of her birth, the only thing she had ever pursued was the way of the sword.","Because of this, the Holy Sword King grew even more agitated and resentful, especially now that she was showing interest in some unknown figure she’d barely even met.","Meanwhile, Yuan wandered through the Gates of Heaven until he came across a disciple he could approach for directions.","\"Excuse me, do you know where I can find Senior Bai, your Sect Leader?\"","\"Sect Leader Bai? He’s not someone you can meet just because you want to,\" the disciple said, eyeing Yuan from head to toe. To him, Yuan looked like just another mortal wasting his time.","And before Yuan could say anything else, the disciple flew away.","Yuan wasn’t bothered by the encounter and immediately went to find someone else.","Eventually, he found someone who was willing to help.","\"The Sect Leader is currently greeting guests, so he could be anywhere. But if you really want to meet him, you’ll have a higher chance of meeting him at the venue.\"","\"Which direction is the venue?\"","The disciple pointed in a specific direction, and Yuan followed it after thanking the disciple.","Some time later, Yuan arrived at the venue where the Sword Emperor Qualifications would take place.","The venue was nothing like Yuan had imagined. Hundreds of smaller islands floated around a massive central island. The smaller islands were packed with spectator seating, while the central island featured a vast platform surrounded by several imposing doors. Above it all, enormous projections hovered in the air, serving as viewing screens for the crowd.","Though the event was still months away, tens of millions had already gathered, a testament to the event’s significance and popularity.","Upon his arrival, Yuan immediately used his divine sense to sweep the place to see if he could find Senior Bai or anyone that he recognized.","Very quickly, he found Meixiu and the others since they were all grouped together and sat in a private area reserved for Senior Bai’s close friends.","After finding them, Yuan immediately approached them.","\"Hey, everyone.\"","Yuan greeted them as he landed before them.","\"Yuan!\"","They immediately recognized him despite his mask.","\"You... you’re back already?\" Kelan, who was also there, muttered in a dumbfounded voice.","He silently nodded.","\"Does that mean you’ve learned Supreme Sword Aura?\" Li Jinxi asked.","\"There’s no way you learned Supreme Sword Aura in under a decade!\" Kelan exclaimed, his voice laced with disbelief.","In response, Yuan calmly raised his hand and extended his middle finger, sheathed in a brilliant layer of Supreme Sword Aura.","Li Jinxi and the others chuckled at his response.","Kelan fell to his knees with his mouth wide open.","Yuan patted his shoulder and said, \"I’m looking forward to checking out your treasury.\"","Kelan sighed deeply. \"Why did I ever agree to bet with you? I should’ve stood my ground and said no.\"","He stood up and continued, \"Are you really going to participate in the Sword Emperor Qualifications, though? Even though you’ve learned Supreme Sword Aura, you just learned it.\"","\"I’ve already qualified to enter the event,\" said Yuan.","\"Unbelievable...\"","\"Also, the Sword Emperor Qualification will be delayed for a month,\" he added.","\"Delay? Why?\"","\"Because I broke the thing needed to verify during my verification,\" he explained.","\"...\"","\"Why am I not surprised?\" Kelan shook his head after a moment of silence.","\"At least this will give me some time to spend with you guys before the event begins,\" Yuan chuckled."]},{"number":2030,"title":"Chapter 2030: Sword Emperor Qualifications","paragraphs":["\"I’ll let Overlord Bai know that you’re here,\" Kelan said as he sent a message to Senior Bai through his communication jade slip.","Meanwhile, Yuan began recalling his experience at the Holy Sword Clan and the Holy Sword Temple. The others didn’t have much to talk about since they spent all of their time training.","\"Although we’re spending all of our time training now, we’ll be leaving the sect to train outside and gain real experience soon,\" said Wang Ming.","Kelan nodded and said, \"Don’t worry, I’ll make sure to have some experts accompany them.\"","\"I’m not worried about them,\" Yuan said with a smile, and he continued, \"But I am worried about the trouble they might cause.\"","\"You’re one to talk!\" Shi Lang immediately said.","\"Right? You’re always getting into trouble, Yuan. At least that’s what it seems like from the stories you tell us,\" said Wang Bingbing.","\"As much as I love you, I have to agree with the others.\" Chu Liuxiang shook her head with a smile on her face.","Meixiu quietly nodded her head.","Seeing this, Yuan burst out laughing.","\"You’re right, but it’s not like I am purposefully looking for trouble. They just somehow come to me.\"","Some time later, a familiar figure approached from a distance, descending gracefully and landing right in front of them.","\"This makes it our first time seeing each other outside of the Myriad of Techniques,\" Senior Bai said to Yuan with a warm smile on his face.","Yuan returned the smile and said, \"Yes, it does. Thank you for always taking care of me.\"","\"Since you’re here... does that mean you’ve learned Supreme Sword Aura?\" Senior Bai then asked.","Kelan had only mentioned Yuan’s arrival and nothing else, so Senior Bai could experience the same surprise he’d felt.","Yuan nodded.","\"Yes, I have already qualified for the Sword Emperor Qualifications.\"","He revealed the medallion he received from the Sect Elder.","Senior Bai chuckled and said, \"I heard. I also know that you broke the crystal, causing us to delay the event for a whole month.\"","\"Sorry...\"","\"It’s fine.\"","Yuan then asked, \"Is Sister Xu here?\"","Senior Bai shook his head.","\"No, she’s too busy to come down to the Seventh Heaven, but she’ll be watching it.\"","\"I see...\"","\"Anyway, I have to return to work now. Let’s talk again later. If you need anything, just ask Kelan,\" said Senior Bai before flying away.","Shortly after he left, Senior Bai made a quick announcement to the people there.","\"Due to some unexpected circumstances, we have to delay the Sword Emperor Qualification for a month. We apologize for the delay and any inconvenience this may have caused and hope for your understanding.\"","Surprisingly, there were no complaints from the audience, or there were so few that it was unnoticeable.","\"The crowd is more calm than I had expected,\" Wang Ming commented, as he’d anticipated some complaints.\"The Sword Emperor Qualifications can easily last several years, so everyone here is already prepared for a long stay. An extra month is nothing,\" Kelan said.","\"Several years?! What about our training?\" Xi Murong exclaimed in shock, as he’d only anticipated spending a few weeks or months at most at this event.","Kelan shrugged and said, \"You’re free to leave at any time you want. The whole thing will be recorded anyway, so you won’t miss anything but the experience.\"","\"...\"","A few years may seem like nothing to Immortals or those who have already lived thousands of years. However, for Xi Murong and the others who have only lived for a few decades, a few years was a lot of time, and they were still at a point where their progress could be seen quickly.","\"You don’t have to force yourself to stay here,\" Yuan suddenly said. \"Just stay as long as you want.\"","\"I’m staying for the entire event,\" Chu Liuxiang said firmly. \"A few years mean nothing in the grand scheme of things—but missing such a pivotal moment in my partner’s life? That’s unthinkable.\"","\"Me too,\" Meixiu added. \"But you don’t have to force yourself to stay because we choose to stay. We all have different priorities, after all.\"","\"I guess we’ll see how things go,\" said Wu Zao. \"If it’s entertaining enough, I’ll stay. Otherwise, I’ll just return to my training.\"","\"Me too,\" said Hong Xiuquan.","\"You can’t even take a small break? And you call me a training addict?\" Li Jinxi shook her head.","Wang Bing chuckled and said, \"We’re all training addicts.\"","In the end, everyone but Li Jinxi, Meixiu, and Chu Liuxiang decided to watch until they couldn’t anymore.","Time passed, and two weeks later, while Yuan was chatting with everyone, a figure descended onto their area.","Kelan raised an eyebrow after seeing this individual, and he asked, \"What are you doing here, Sword Empress Huang?\"","\"I don’t have business with you,\" she said before pointing to Yuan.","\"Since we have some time, let’s spar.\"","\"No.\" Yuan immediately refused, which took her by surprise.","\"W-Why not?!\"","\"Why should I? The Sword Emperor Qualification is about to begin, and you want me to waste my energy sparring with you? If you’re trying to help those two, don’t bother.\" Yuan shook his head.","\"What? Are you talking about the Holy Sword Maiden and the Holy Sword King? I’m not asking for a spar because I want to help those two. I just want to experience your Supreme Sword Aura myself,\" she defended herself.","However, Yuan refused again, \"If you want to spar, we can do it after I become a Sword Emperor.\"","Sword Empress Huang’s eyes widened.","\"You speak as if you’ve already won. Do you really think the Sword Emperor Qualification is that easy?\"","\"I hope not, or it wouldn’t be fun.\"","\"Fun...? You think this is a game?\" Sword Empress Huang frowned, clearly offended by his words.","For the rare few swordmasters granted the chance to participate, the Sword Emperor Qualifications represented the pinnacle of their lives—an opportunity to carve their names into history. Yet Yuan spoke of it as if it were nothing more than a casual pastime.","Any swordmaster would have taken offense, as this was a sacred trial, not something to be taken lightly or treated as entertainment."]},{"number":2031,"title":"Chapter 2031: Nine Heavens’ Ranking","paragraphs":["\"I apologize if my words offended you, but I can assure you that I don’t think of the Sword Emperor Qualification as a game,\" said Yuan.","\"Hmph.\" The Sword Empress snorted. \"Whatever, I’ve lost my desire to spar now.\"","Without saying another word, she turned around and flew away.","\"That was a Sword Emperor?\" Wang Ming asked, his voice tinged with nervousness, sounding like he’d just witnessed something beyond comprehension.","Being a God Ascension realm cultivator and one of the strongest Swordmasters in the Nine Heavens, the Sword Empress naturally exuded an overwhelming presence that would make any Immortal timid, much less a mortal like Wang Ming.","\"I’m surprised you can speak with her so casually... I wouldn’t even be able to respond properly...\" Wu Zao remarked.","Kelan smiled and said, \"Although she’s known for having a foul mouth, her abilities are undeniable and within the top 20 in the entire Nine Heavens.\"","\"Top 20? Then where do you rank?\" Shi Lang asked, and everyone there stared at Kelan.","\"Hahaha! There’s no need to look at me. I don’t even rank in the top 1,000, much less the top 20! However, if we’re talking about physiques alone, I am definitely top 10 in the Nine Heavens!\" he proudly boasted.","\"What?! You’re that strong and can’t even reach the top 1,000? That’s hard to believe,\" Hong Xiuquan exclaimed.","\"You have no idea how vast and scary the Nine Heavens can be. There are countless geniuses, and many monsters are out there. Even someone like Senior Bai doesn’t rank in the top 20,\" said Kelan.","\"I wonder where someone like Yuan ranks,\" Wang Bingbing wondered out loud.","\"Yuan?\"","Kelan turned to look at him with a pondering face.","After a moment of serious thinking, he spoke, \"Although he may have the power to fight God Ascension cultivators, that is limited only to the Nine Heavens, where our powers are limited by the Heavens. He wouldn’t last more than a minute against them outside, where most of the newer powerhouses make their territory.\"","Due to the restrictions within the Nine Heavens, most powerful families and factions relocated their headquarters to the Starry Sky, where such limitations did not exist, allowing God Ascension cultivators to wield their full strength when necessary. Only those with deep, ancient roots—such as the Royal Dragon Clans—chose to remain in the Nine Heavens, enduring the drawbacks out of legacy and pride.","\"That said, he’s definitely in the top 1,000 as long as he’s within the Nine Heavens, and this is overall, where most are monsters with millions of years of experience. If we consider his age, then he’s definitely in the top 10 within the young generation ranking.\"","\"What do you consider the ’younger generation’?\" Li Jinxi asked.","\"Anyone under a hundred thousand years old,\" said Kelan.","\"A hundred thousand years is young...?\" Wang Ming muttered in a dumbfounded voice.","\"There’s no way Yuan is only top 10. He’s definitely top 3 if not number one,\" Chu Liuxiang remarked with certainty.","\"I know Yuan is immensely talented, but you shouldn’t underestimate others. For example, the Holy Sword Maiden, who will also be participating in the Sword Emperor Qualifications, is currently ranked 9th in the Nine Heavens. As for the current top three, they’re all monsters in the Ninth Heaven.\"","\"Who are the top three?\" Wang Xiuying asked.","\"Currently ranked third is the Bloodthirsty Monk of the Hell Temple, though the rankings shift every few years as the rest of the top ten close the gap. The top two are no different—first and second place frequently trade positions. As of now, second belongs to the Holy Maiden of the Divine Essence Monastery, while first is held by the Heavenly Son of the Tian Family,\" Kelan explained.","\"The Hell Temple is an elite sect within the Ninth Heaven, and the Divine Essence Monastery is currently the second most powerful sect in the Nine Heavens. As for the Tian Family, they’re a powerhouse in the Ninth Heaven, known for creating countless geniuses. In fact, they’re only right behind the Celestial Emperor’s family in terms of influence.\"","\"Divine Essence Monastery...\" Yuan muttered as he found this name familiar for some reason.","Then he remembered that his Soul Cultivation Technique had been given by Lady Xiang, who was from there.","\"Do you know Sister Biyu from the Divine Essence Monastery?\" Yuan suddenly asked Kelan.","\"Sister Biyu?\" Kelan raised his eyebrows in a puzzled manner for a second before he realized who Yuan was talking about.","\"There’s no way you’re talking about the Holy Empress...\" he said.","\"Last I spoke to her, she called herself the Holy Maiden.\"","\"So you are talking about the Holy Empress! Holy Empress Xiang, also known as Xiang Biyu, is the current leader of the Divine Essence Monastery. She acquired that title about a decade ago,\" explained Kelan.","He then asked, \"How did you meet someone like her...? She rarely leaves the Divine Essence Monastery. Even I have only ever seen her once. And for you to address her as Sister Biyu... you must be quite close with her.\"","\"I met her through Sister Xu, but that’s all I can say,\" said Yuan.","\"So, who’s the current Holy Maiden?\" he then asked.","\"That would be Azure.\"","\"What? Azure?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at this name.","\"Oh, her real name is Wei Lan, but she prefers to be called Azure,\" he explained. \"Why? Do you know her, too?\"","\"No... but her name reminds me of someone I once knew,\" he responded, a hint of regret and sorrow in his tone.","Though Kelan couldn’t understand it, the others knew who Yuan was referring to.","\"How does the ranking work, anyway?\" Xi Meili suddenly asked. \"Do they fight for it or something?\"","Kelan explained, \"Yes and no. With one exception, everyone in the top 10 has fought with each other, and the Heavenly Son came out on top after defeating the others. The only exception is Azure, who has never fought with anyone. However, she did reveal her prowess once, and that was enough to convince everyone that she could rival the Heavenly Son, hence her rank.\""]},{"number":2032,"title":"Chapter 2032: Heavenly Son","paragraphs":["\"Heavens... she managed to reach the top 2 just by showcasing her prowess? I cannot imagine how powerful she must’ve been,\" Wang Ming commented.","\"What about Cultivation Gods and entities like the Great One?\" Yuan then asked.","Kelan chuckled and said, \"Cultivation Gods? You can count the number of them with one hand. They’re too powerful to be in the ranking. The same goes for the Great One. The ranking is mostly for those within the God Ascension realm, after all.\"","\"What about this Heavenly Son guy? How powerful is he?\" Shi Lang suddenly asked.","\"Well, he’s not ranked first in the younger generation for no reason. If you want to see his prowess, you’ll be able to do so soon, since he’s also participating in the Sword Emperor Qualifications.\"","\"Really? Now this is interesting...\" Shi Lang remarked as he turned to look at Yuan.","The others knew what Shi Lang was thinking about and smiled, as they all thought the same.","\"What are you looking at? It’s not like we’ll fight each other in the Sword Emperor Qualifications,\" Yuan said.","\"No, but you’ll be fighting each other indirectly for the ranking. Since more than one person can qualify for the title of Sword Emperor, there’ll be a ranking for your achievements. If you rank first, you’ll be rewarded with something at the end.\"","\"What? More than one person can qualify as Sword Emperor?\" Wu Zao said.","The others were just as surprised since this was their first time hearing about it.","\"Anyone who passes the trials will qualify. Why do you think there are many Sword Emperors running around the Nine Heavens?\"","\"So being a Sword Emperor isn’t anything too special...\" Wang Ming shook his head. \"What about a Sword God? Surely, there must be only one of them out there.\"","\"Sword God?\" Kelan laughed out loud before responding, \"There’s no such thing.\"","\"What? There isn’t? That doesn’t make any sense. Why can’t the strongest Sword Emperor just become the Sword God or something?\" Wang Bingbing asked, clearly confused.","\"Well, that’s because it would get far too bloody,\" Kelan replied. \"There was once a Sword Emperor who declared himself the Sword God, and the moment he did, the other Sword Emperors challenged him. He was killed, and the one who defeated him then tried to claim the title for himself, only to be killed as well. It kept happening, one after another, until several Sword Emperors had fallen. Since then, no one’s dared to call themselves the Sword God.\"","\"So they’re scared of being attacked by other Sword Emperors? A true Sword God wouldn’t care about being challenged because they know they’re the strongest.\"","\"You are right, but nobody has ever reached that point...\" Kelan paused for a moment before continuing, \"Actually, there is one person who might’ve qualified for that title.\"","\"The Faceless Sword Emperor,\" Li Jinxi said.","Kelan nodded, \"That’s right. The Faceless Sword Emperor was known to be undefeated in history, so he would’ve probably been able to claim that title and get away with it, but he disappeared somewhere and hasn’t been seen since then.\"","\"Who knows? Maybe someone like the Faceless Sword Emperor will appear again,\" Li Jinxi said with a mysterious smile.","\"If you’re talking about Yuan, while I don’t doubt his talents, he’s far from the Faceless Sword Emperor’s level.\" Kelan shook his head.","Li Jinxi shrugged.","They continued chatting about the rankings and about some of the most powerful individuals in the Nine Heavens.","A few hours later, Kelan stopped talking when he noticed a powerful presence approaching in their direction.","\"Speak of the devil...\" he muttered.","Moments later, a handsome young man clad in golden robes landed before them, his sharp gaze scanning everyone there until it landed on Yuan.","\"You must be the one who broke the crystal,\" said the handsome young man.","\"Yes, and who are you?\"","\"You don’t know who I am? That’s impossible,\" the young man said, his tone dripping with disbelief, as if he were certain the entire world knew his name.","\"That’s the Heavenly Son, Tian Juexing,\" Kelan revealed the handsome young man’s identity.","\"So you’re ranked first in the younger generation, huh? We were just talking about you,\" Yuan said. \"What’s a bigshot like you want from me?\"","\"So you do know me,\" said Tian Juexing. \"I came here after hearing about the reason for the delay. Even I couldn’t crack the crystal, so I had to see for myself the kind of person who did.\"","\"Is that so? Well, what do you think?\" Yuan asked as he spread his arms, almost as if telling him to take a good look.","\"Honestly? I’m disappointed. You’re nothing more than a wannabe Faceless Sword Emperor with that appearance. That crystal probably cracked because I already weakened it.\"","Yuan smiled behind his mask and said, \"I could say the same about you. I had some high expectations after Kelan boasted about you, but you’re just some egotistic brat.\"","Despite Yuan’s rude remark, Tian Juexing did not seem offended.","\"I get that often, but so what? This is the norm for the truly strong. You wouldn’t understand it.\"","\"If you’re so strong, you will definitely rank higher than me in the Sword Emperor Qualifications, right?\"","\"Without a doubt.\" Tian Juexing answered without even the slightest hesitation.","\"Wanna bet on it?\"","Tian Juexing narrowed his eyes and pondered for a moment before retrieving a medallion.","\"If you somehow rank higher than me, I, Tian Juexing, will accept any one request from you as long as it’s not unreasonable.\"","\"A request?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"Are you looking down on my bet? My family is literally only second to the Celestial Emperor’s family in the Nine Heavens. There’s almost nothing I cannot do for you,\" he said.","\"In that case, I’ll bet—\"","Tian Juexing suddenly raised his hand and interrupted, \"You don’t need to bet anything since there’s nothing I want, nor is there anything that you can possibly do for me.\""]},{"number":2033,"title":"Chapter 2033: Sword Emperor Qualifications Begins!","paragraphs":["\"If you say so,\" Yuan calmly responded to Tian Yuexing’s words.","\"Then I’ll see you during the Sword Emperor Qualifications,\" said Tian Yuexing before flying away and disappearing in the blink of an eye.","\"My god, I can believe you actually picked a fight with the Heavenly Son...\" Kelan said with a dumbfounded look on his face.","Despite his status within the Celestial Overlords, even he didn’t have the guts to offend someone like Tian Yuexing.","\"You probably don’t know how horrifying the Tian Family truly is... they’re so bold that they’re even willing to pick a fight with the Celestial Emperor,\" he added.","\"Oh? Why did they fight with the Celestial Emperor?\" Yuan asked, clearly intrigued by this information.","\"I don’t know all the details, but it happened just a few decades ago,\" Kelan said. \"The two families have always been at odds since ancient times, but something recently pushed the Tian Family over the edge. Whatever it was, it enraged them so much that both their Patriarch and Matriarch stormed the Celestial Emperor’s family estate.\"","\"If you’re that interested, ask Celestial Overlord Xu or Overlord Bai. They probably know.\"","Yuan nodded, \"When I get the chance.\"","He reasoned that since he was already at odds with the Celestial Emperor, it might be wise to form alliances, and if the Tian Family also had grievances with the Celestial Emperor, they could prove to be valuable allies.","Meanwhile, Tian Yuexing returned to where his family was staying after his brief meeting with Yuan.","\"Where did you go?\" A beautiful young lady with black hair and brown eyes asked him.","\"I met someone interesting,\" answered Tian Yuexing.","The young lady raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Interesting? How?\"","\"I don’t quite know how to describe it,\" Tian Yuexing said, recalling his encounter with Yuan. \"At first, he seemed ordinary, but the more I spoke with him, the more I felt something deeper. It was as if he was wrapped in an indescribable aura... something beyond what the eye could see.\"","\"That’s quite the high praise from you, brother. Now I want to meet this guy,\" said the young lady, who turned out to be his sister.","\"That guy called me arrogant, but he is obviously even more arrogant than I.\" Tian Yuexing shook his head with an entertained smile.","\"Even more arrogant than you? That’s hard to believe.\"","\"Right? That’s mostly why I found him interesting. Anyway, I made a bet with him—that if he outranks me in the Sword Emperor Qualifications, I’d do any one thing for him.\"","\"What...? What if you lose?\"","Tian Yuexing frowned and said, \"You think I’ll lose to some nobody? I’ll crush him quickly and show him why I am ranked first in the Nine Heavens.\"","\"Anyway, will father and mother be coming to watch or what?\" he then asked.","\"No, but they’ll be watching from home,\" she said.","Tian Yuexing sighed out loud, \"I wonder how long this will continue. It’s already been several decades, and they still haven’t gotten over it.\"","His sister frowned and said, \"Don’t talk nonsense. You have no idea what they’re going through now.\"","Tian Yuexing looked at her with a curious gaze and asked, \"What about you? How are you feeling?\"","She shrugged, \"I’m a bit disappointed, but that’s about it.\"","\"You’re quite heartless.\"","\"I don’t want more competition. You’re already too much for me to handle,\" she sighed.","\"Whatever. I’m going to cultivate.\"","Without another word, Tian Yuexing sat down and closed his eyes.","The other participants also took this time to mentally prepare themselves. Whether it be the Holy Sword Maiden or the Holy Sword King, everyone took the Sword Emperor Qualifications seriously.","Only Yuan was spending his time casually chatting with his friends.","Time flew by, and in the blink of an eye, the moment everyone had been waiting for had arrived—the Sword Emperor Qualifications were about to begin.","\"Ladies and gentlemen, may I have a moment of your time before we begin the Sword Emperor Qualifications?\"","Senior Bai’s voice echoed through the skies just moments before his figure descended gracefully, coming to a halt above the platform on the central island.","Despite the presence of tens of millions of spectators, an eerie silence fell over the venue, as if the entire world had paused to listen.","\"Thank you.\"","Senior Bai then retrieved a long scroll with several names written on it and began calling them one by one.","\"These will be this year’s Sword Emperor Qualifications. Please come to me when you’re called.\"","\"Holy Sword Clan’s Holy Sword Maiden.\"","Seconds later, the Holy Sword Maiden’s beautiful figure appeared before Senior Bai, greeting him at her arrival.","\"Holy Sword Clan’s Holy Sword King.\"","The Holy Sword King appeared to greet him a moment later.","\"Ethereal Sword Clan’s Vanishing Sword.\"","A middle-aged man appeared and greeted him.","Several names later, \"Tian Family’s Heavenly Son.\"","Tian Yuexing made a grand entrance, radiating a powerful aura as he appeared before the crowd. His silky black hair shimmered under the sunlight, and a confident, handsome smile played across his face.","The moment he appeared, countless girls in the crowd erupted into cheers, swooning like fangirls at a concert.","Unsurprisingly, being the eldest son of the second most influential and powerful family in the Nine Heavens attracted a lot of attention and attraction.","Senior Bai cleared his throat loudly, instantly halting the loud noises.","Once the place calmed down, he continued, reading the last name on the list, \"Yuan.\"","\"???\"","The crowd raised their eyebrows at Yuan’s brief introduction.","The next moment, Yuan leaped from his island and flew toward Senior Bai with incredible speed, stopping right before him.","Both the Heavenly Son and the Holy Sword King narrowed their eyes at Yuan, but he ignored them and greeted Senior Bai.","\"Good luck.\"","Senior Bai responded to his greeting, which caught everyone off guard, as it was the first time he had acknowledged any participant. Both the spectators and the contestants were stunned, and whispers quickly spread as curiosity about Yuan’s identity began to grow."]},{"number":2034,"title":"Chapter 2034: Mystic Sword Tablet","paragraphs":["When the spectators looked closely at Yuan’s appearance, many raised their eyebrows.","\"Hey, isn’t that the Faceless Sword Emperor’s appearance?\"","\"Who is this guy, and why is he dressing up as one of the greatest Sword Emperors to ever exist?\"","\"Is he mocking the others or something? What a rude and disrespectful bastard!\"","\"People like him tend to come in last.\"","The spectators began cursing Yuan for his appearance.","\"W-Wait a second! Look at his cultivation! He’s only at the peak of Immortal Ascension! He’s still a mortal!\"","\"What?! That’s impossible! He must be hiding his cultivation. There’s no way a mortal could comprehend Supreme Sword Aura, much less qualify for the Sword Emperor Qualifications.\"","Almost everybody there figured Yuan was hiding his cultivation with some kind of trick.","Senior Bai ignored the slight commotion and continued to speak.","\"Now that all of the participants are here, allow me to explain the rules for the Sword Emperor Qualifications.\"","He gestured toward the standalone doors on the platform beneath them and continued, \"I’ll keep things simple. Each door represents a trial. In order to be acknowledged as a Sword Emperor, you must pass all trials. Of course, this means more than one of you can become a Sword Emperor.\"","\"However, there’ll also be a ranking depending on your results. Whoever comes in first place will be awarded a priceless and one-of-a-kind treasure that was recently discovered—the Mystic Sword Tablet, which was left behind by an unknown swordmaster who seemed to have glimpsed into a realm above Supreme Sword Aura!\"","\"What? Above Supreme Sword Aura?\"","The spectators expressed disbelief after hearing this.","To satisfy the doubters, Senior Bai retrieved a fist-sized jade tablet bearing a small sword cut, seemingly unremarkable and unassuming at first glance. To the ordinary eye, it was nothing special. But to swordmasters who had reached a certain level of mastery, that tiny cut held an unfathomable secret—an imprint of sword intent so profound it defied comprehension.","\"What the fuck is that?!\" Sword Empress Huang exclaimed in a shocked voice after seeing the tablet, her eyes wide with disbelief.","Not only Sword Empress Huang, but every swordmaster present trembled with a mix of shock and excitement upon seeing the Mystic Sword Tablet, as none of them had ever witnessed anything like it.","To them, Supreme Sword Aura was the pinnacle of swordsmanship. The mere suggestion that a higher realm of mastery existed shattered their understanding and left them in awe.","After giving everyone a glimpse of the Mystic Sword Tablet, Senior Bai quickly stored it back inside his spatial ring.","\"First place... I have to claim it,\" Tian Yuexing muttered, his eyes burning with determination and desire.","Around him, the other participants wore similar expressions—faces etched with ambition, each one ready to stake everything for the title.","Meanwhile, Yuan was looking at the notifications that had popped up before him when he glanced at the Mystic Sword Tablet.","<You have learned the existence of Flawless Sword Aura>","<You have met the criteria to learn Flawless Sword Aura>","<Your understanding of Flawless Sword Aura has increased slightly>","’Flawless Sword Aura, huh?’ Yuan smiled inwardly.","\"Where did you find something like that?\" Tian Yuexing asked Senior Bai a question that was on everyone’s mind.","\"I’m sorry, but that is not something I can disclose right now,\" said Senior Bai as he shook his head.","Although his answer left everyone disappointed, they understood why he’s keeping it a secret.","\"Anyway, let’s return to the topic. I’m sure you already know this, but your life is not guaranteed during the Sword Emperor Qualifications, and participants have died while attempting the trials before.\"","\"That said, we will provide you with a talisman that will take you out of the trial if you think you are unable to continue. Just know that using the talisman will automatically disqualify you.\"","Senior Bai retrieved a stack of black talismans and handed one to each participant.","\"You can activate it by destroying it. None of the mechanisms in the trial will be able to touch the talisman, so you don’t have to worry about it being destroyed by accident.\"","\"When the trial begins, you will all be transported to the same realm, but in different locations,\" Senior Bai explained. \"There is a chance you may encounter other participants, but be warned—combat or intentional interference with others is strictly forbidden. Anyone caught doing so will be immediately disqualified. There will be tens of millions of pairs of eyes watching each of you, so don’t think you’ll be able to get away with it, either.\"","\"Any questions so far?\"","When no one spoke, Senior Bai continued, \"One final note before we officially begin the Sword Emperor Qualifications: you are permitted to bring your own treasures into the trial. However, be aware—within the trial, all treasures will be automatically sealed, rendering them no more powerful than ordinary weapons.\"","\"Now then... the Sword Emperor Qualifications will officially begin!\"","The very next moment, one of the sealed doors opened, revealing a white portal within.","\"You may enter.\"","Hearing this, the dozen participants flew into the portal one by one, disappearing into the trial.","Meanwhile, the projections above the island began displaying the situation inside the trial.","\"Once again, good luck.\" Senior Bai said to Yuan before he left and entered the portal.","After stepping through the portal, Yuan found himself beneath a clear blue sky, standing on a wide dirt path flanked by dense tree lines on either side.","\"Since they didn’t mention any details about the trial, I guess it’s for us to figure it out ourselves...\" he mumbled as he began walking down the straight path.","After walking for a few minutes, he spotted a lone figure resting against a distant tree, seemingly lost in sleep.","Yuan focused on this individual, but he couldn’t see the man’s cultivation, almost as if he were an ordinary mortal. However, he also exuded a mysterious aura.","Moments later, Yuan continued walking again, only to stop again a few steps later when the man suddenly opened his eyes and slowly stood up."]},{"number":2035,"title":"Chapter 2035: Sword Emperor Qualifications’ First Trial","paragraphs":["As the man rose to his feet, Yuan came to a halt, his focus sharpening as he watched the stranger’s every move.","Without warning, the man drew the sword at his waist and unleashed a swift slash from afar, sending a powerful wave of ordinary Sword Aura hurtling toward Yuan.","Yet, Yuan didn’t move a muscle and allowed the Sword Aura to hit him, and when it did, the Sword Aura shattered into countless fragments like glass.","\"So it was just ordinary Sword Aura...\" Yuan muttered as he retrieved a random sword he had in his spatial ring.","Since all treasures were essentially the same in the trial, he didn’t need to use Number One Under Heaven, nor did he want to use it before so many spectators.","Then, without hesitation, he swung at the man, sending a wave of Supreme Sword Aura at the man. However, as if copying Yuan’s actions, the man did not attempt to block it and allowed it to strike his body.","Once the Supreme Sword Aura struck his body, the mysterious aura around him flared up, deflecting Yuan’s Supreme Sword Aura.","Seeing this, Yuan raised an eyebrow. The trial had just begun, yet he was already fighting an enemy immune to Supreme Sword Aura? Something felt off.","Just to make sure, he struck the man again with Supreme Sword Aura, and sure enough, the results were the same.","After blocking his second attack, the man suddenly moved, charging toward Yuan with his sword raised and gushing with ordinary Sword Aura.","\"If Supreme Sword Aura doesn’t work, then...\"","Yuan swung his sword at the man without channeling any Sword Aura, yet once again, his blade was effortlessly deflected by the aura.","Yuan was certain now that the trial required him to somehow get past the man’s mysterious aura, and for the next several minutes, he analyzed the man’s aura to the best of his abilities.","Unfortunately, he was unable to figure out its secrets.","’There’s gotta be a clue...’","Yuan glanced around, searching for anything that might offer a clue to counter the man’s mysterious aura, but aside from the silent figure before him, there was nothing in sight to guide him.","Suddenly, realization flickered across Yuan’s face.","\"Let’s see if this works...\" he murmured.","Lifting his sword, he gathered only ordinary Sword Aura, just as the man had been using all along, and unleashed a focused slash.","The very next moment, his sword tore right through the aura and sliced the man in half.","\"An aura that blocks Supreme Sword Aura but cannot resist ordinary Sword Aura, huh?\" Yuan muttered out loud, his voice filled with intrigue.","After defeating the man, Yuan searched his body to see if there was anything to loot.","\"Nothing.\"","With nothing left to do, Yuan continued walking the path.","Before long, he came to another halt. In the distance stood not one, but two masked men, each wielding a sword, and both radiating the same mysterious aura as the one he had faced before.","Without any words, the two masked men charged at Yuan, moving at a speed that was noticeably faster than that of his last opponent. Not just that, but their attacks were also much quicker and precise.","However, now that Yuan knew the trick, he quickly defeated them with ordinary Sword Aura and continued moving forward.","A few minutes later, Yuan came across four masked men, twice as many as in his previous encounter. Each one stood silently, swords in hand, their presence radiating the same eerie aura as before.","Seeing this, Yuan smiled faintly and muttered, \"Let’s see how many times you’ll multiply.\"","This time, he took the initiative, moving before his opponents could react. Though their strength had clearly increased compared to the previous group, it still wasn’t nearly enough to pose any real threat to him.","In less than a minute, Yuan dispatched all four masked men with ease and continued down the path, fully expecting to face eight opponents next.","However, to his surprise, only a single man stood in his path. Though the aura he emitted resembled that of the previous masked opponents, Yuan could sense a subtle difference.","As Yuan focused, trying to discern the subtle difference in the man’s aura, the masked figure suddenly made his move.","Unlike the others, he didn’t strike with ordinary Sword Aura but Enhanced Sword Aura instead.","Seeing this, Yuan attacked with Enhanced Sword Aura as well, and sure enough, it was able to cut through the masked man’s aura.","Having grasped the pattern, Yuan pressed on through the trial with a quicker, more confident pace.","After defeating two masked opponents simultaneously—and then another wave of four—he eventually came to a halt again, and standing before him was a lone masked man wielding Supreme Sword Aura.","When the masked man struck, his swordsmanship was precise, fluid, and refined to perfection. It was incomparably superior to that of Yuan’s previous opponents, leaving no doubt that this foe was on an entirely different level.","Not only did the man move like an expert with tens of thousands of years of experience, but he even used martial techniques.","Yet, despite the drastic improvements, Yuan defeated the man in just a few exchanges.","\"This can’t be the real trial. It’s too easy...\" Yuan mumbled as he continued forward.","After overcoming two more waves of opponents wielding Supreme Sword Aura, Yuan finally arrived at the end of the path. It opened into a vast, circular field, one that radiated an unmistakable pressure, as if silently declaring the beginning of the real trial.","Without hesitation, Yuan walked to the center of the field and waited for the trial to begin.","Moments later, Yuan could sense several—many presences appearing all around him.","In the blink of an eye, hundreds... no, thousands of masked men surrounded him, each radiating a mysterious aura. Yet not all were the same. The three distinct types of aura Yuan had faced earlier—ordinary, enhanced, and Supreme Sword Aura—were now interwoven throughout the crowd.","\"Now this is more like it.\" Yuan muttered with an excited smile on his face."]},{"number":2036,"title":"Chapter 2036: Sword Emperor Qualifications’ First Trial(2)","paragraphs":["While Yuan stood surrounded by thousands of masked men, the other participants were still making their way toward the end of the path. Although many had figured out the trial’s pattern just as quickly as Yuan, they struggled to overcome their opponents. Their Sword Auras lacked the overwhelming force Yuan possessed, requiring multiple strikes to break through the masked men’s defenses.","Of course, Tian Yuexing was an exception. As expected of the number one young genius in the Nine Heavens, he had reached the end of the path nearly at the same time as Yuan.","The spectators watching this were simply left dumbfounded by Yuan’s unexpected prowess and talents.","\"Heavens... his pace is slightly faster than the Heavenly Son! Maybe I’ve underestimated him a little too much!\"","\"His fighting experience is also terrifyingly high—something I’d only expect from the older generation...\"","\"Where did a genius like him come from? And how come I’ve never heard of him?\"","\"He’s probably already well-known but is hiding his identity for whatever reason.\"","The spectators began trying to speculate Yuan’s identity as he fought the thousands of masked men, constantly using all three types of Sword Aura.","Though everyone participating in the Sword Emperor Qualifications was at least in the God Ascension realm, their cultivation didn’t really matter since only Sword Aura could get past the masked men’s aura. That said, it didn’t mean their cultivation wasn’t important, since it allowed them to fight without getting tired easily.","Time continued to pass. Although the Sword Emperor Qualifications had just begun, the spectators were already on the edge of their seats from watching Yuan’s amazing performance.","Not only was he defeating his opponents with a single strike and progressing much quicker than the Heavenly Son, but he would likely finish the first trial in record time.","\"You’re telling me that wannabe Faceless Sword Emperor is a mortal? Would a mortal be able to do that?!\"","\"If he’s able to do that while suppressing his cultivation, can you imagine how powerful he truly is?\"","While it was difficult to imagine anyone willingly restraining their full strength during the Sword Emperor Qualifications, the spectators found it even harder to believe that Yuan was truly a mortal.","It only took a few hours, but Yuan finally defeated all of the masked men, and he’d done so without even getting hurt, as only Supreme Sword Aura could damage his body.","Of course, the spectators had noticed this.","\"He completely ignored every opponent using ordinary and Enhanced Sword Aura... This bastard didn’t just attain a Sword Body—he’s achieved the legendary Enhanced Sword Body, which renders all Enhanced Sword Aura useless...\" muttered one of the watching Sword Emperors, disbelief and awe lacing his voice.","While most of the Sword Emperors present possessed a Sword Body, not a single one among them had attained the Enhanced Sword Body. In terms of sword comprehension alone, Yuan had already surpassed them.","\"Just what the fuck is that bastard...?\" Sword Empress Huang clenched her fists in frustration after realizing Yuan had attained the Enhanced Sword Body before her, something she’d been trying to achieve for the past thirty thousand years.","If she’d known that it only took Yuan a few years to achieve it, she’d probably go crazy from envy.","After defeating all of the masked men, Yuan looked around and muttered, \"Am I done?\"","He waited for a while, but when nothing happened, he calmly sat down and began cultivating.","Hours passed in silence—until suddenly, Yuan’s eyes snapped open. He sensed something from above.","Lifting his gaze, he saw tens of thousands of semi-transparent swords materializing in the sky, each one forged from pure Supreme Sword Aura.","Without warning, they began to fall like a meteor shower, raining down upon him with the speed and force of a storm of arrows.","In response, Yuan activated his Limitless Sword Domain, unleashing a surge of Supreme Sword Aura to intercept the falling blades.","Yet to his surprise, despite his aura being clearly stronger, his sword aura was shattered upon contact, as though the incoming swords carried something beyond raw power, something deeper and more refined.","Seeing this, Yuan swiftly activated his movement technique, weaving through the rain of blades with precise, fluid motion. As he dodged, his mind raced, analyzing the clash, trying to understand why his Supreme Sword Aura had been so easily overwhelmed despite its superior strength.","However, the trial offered no mercy, and the blades pursued him relentlessly, tracking his every move like homing missiles.","It didn’t take long for Yuan to notice something unusual—that each sword was enveloped in a thin layer of mysterious aura, and each blade’s Supreme Sword Aura was slightly different, with some being more powerful than others.","Yuan narrowed his eyes, a glint of realization flashing within them.","To test his theory, he struck the nearest descending blade with a precise amount of Supreme Sword Aura, matching its level perfectly.","Sure enough, the sword shattered on impact. His guess had been correct—that he needed to strike these swords with perfectly matching Supreme Sword Aura, which tested his control and precision.","Now that he knew the trick, Yuan activated Limitless Sword Domain again. This time, he perfectly controlled the Supreme Sword Aura to match that of the incoming blades.","When the spectators witnessed Yuan’s unfathomable control over his Supreme Sword Aura, they were left in stunned silence.","The swordmasters among them, in particular, were overwhelmed with disbelief, for they understood how incredibly difficult it was to manipulate Supreme Sword Aura with such precision. And yet, Yuan made it look effortless.","By the time Yuan had finished destroying every last sword, Tian Yuexing was still locked in battle with the thousands of masked men. Even for a genius of his caliber, fending off so many powerful opponents at once was no simple feat, not to mention how he had to constantly swap his Sword Aura, something he wasn’t used to.","As for the others, they were still on the straight path, fighting their way to the end."]},{"number":2037,"title":"Chapter 2037: Immediately Starting the Second Trial","paragraphs":["Shortly after destroying all of the swords, a portal appeared before Yuan, prompting him to enter it.","\"I guess this is it for the first trial...\" Yuan mumbled as he walked straight into the portal, leaving the trial and returning to the platform.","\"Heavens... he’s already finished the first trial? And it hasn’t even been a full day!\"","The spectators were left in awe, their faces a mix of shock and disbelief. Yuan’s results weren’t just impressive, they were unprecedented. Even the most seasoned swordmasters found themselves speechless.","Yuan glanced around after returning, and upon seeing none of the other participants, he quickly realized he was the first to finish.","High above him, a massive display showed the names of all participants, and his name surged to the top, claiming first place with a perfect score of 100 points.","Senior Bai approached him with a smile and said, \"Welcome back. Words cannot describe my surprise when you finished the trial so quickly.\"","\"Thank you.\" Yuan said before asking, \"Do I have to wait for the others to come out, or can I continue to the next trial?\"","\"You can immediately continue onto the next trial if you want, but you are allowed a week of rest after each trial,\" said Senior Bai, and he continued, \"And while you’re allowed to cultivate during your rest, you are not allowed to consume any treasures or pills.\"","\"I’d like to begin the next trial,\" Yuan said calmly, choosing to forgo any rest.","The first trial had been little more than a warm-up for him, barely a walk in the park, and the brief conversation with Senior Bai had been enough for him to recover physically and mentally.","Senior Bai nodded and immediately opened the second door for him.","Without hesitation, Yuan walked into the second door, disappearing from the platform.","The spectators were stunned into silence. Not only had Yuan obliterated the first trial in record time, but now he was diving straight into the second without a moment’s rest.","The Sword Emperors present exchanged glances, recalling their own Sword Emperor Qualifications—how they had clung to every second of rest between trials.","\"Hahaha! At this rate, we’ll probably be here for a few months before he’s completely done!\" Wang Ming laughed out loud after seeing how fast Yuan was progressing through the Sword Emperor Qualifications.","Kelan wanted to respond, but he was left utterly speechless by Yuan’s performance. He had never imagined Yuan’s level of swordsmanship would be this high.","’How is his understanding of Supreme Sword Aura so profound when he’d only spent a few years inside the Holy Sword Temple?! This doesn’t make any sense! His existence doesn’t make any damn sense!’ Kelan cried inwardly.","It wasn’t just Kelan. The Sixth Elder and Supreme Empress Huang were just as puzzled as he, as they were also aware of how little time Yuan had spent inside the Holy Sword Temple.","Meanwhile, spectators from beyond the Seventh Heaven, such as those from the Eighth and Ninth Heavens, were stirred into action.","As Yuan’s performance was simply too outstanding, countless influential factions began investigating his origins, eager to uncover his true identity. Some even went so far as to dispatch recruiters, hoping to secure him for their ranks the moment the Sword Emperor Qualifications concluded.","Xu Jiaqi, who was watching from her own office, wore a warm smile on her face as she stared at Yuan’s figure through a treasure that broadcast the Sword Emperor Qualifications.","\"As expected of father’s reincarnation...\" she muttered.","Meanwhile, at the Divine Essence Monastery, a young lady wearing a white face veil approached Xiang Biyu and asked, \"Master, what are you watching?\"","\"It’s the Sword Emperor Qualifications. You should watch it with me, Azure,\" said Xiang Biyu.","\"Why? It’s a waste of time.\"","\"Even though your rival is currently participating in it?\"","\"The Heavenly Son? I don’t even consider him a rival,\" she said.","\"No, I wasn’t talking about the Heavenly Son.\" Xiang Biyu pointed at the masked man on the display and said, \"I’m talking about him.\"","Despite her disinterest, Azure asked, \"Who’s that?\"","She couldn’t fathom how someone she’s never met or heard of before could be her rival.","\"You have never met him before, but his name is Yuan, and he’s definitely worthy to be your rival. After all, he was able to learn my soul cultivation technique.\"","\"What did you just say...?\"","Behind her face veil, Azure’s eyes widened.","Xiang Biyu assumed she was talking about the soul cultivation technique, so she explained, \"Remember when I told you that a mortal had managed to learn my soul cultivation technique, and you didn’t believe me? This is him.\"","However, little did Xiang Biyu know—Azure couldn’t have cared less about the soul cultivation technique, and her attention was focused elsewhere.","\"His name. Can you repeat it?\"","\"Yuan? Why? You recognize it?\"","\"...\"","Azure didn’t respond, but she silently took a seat beside Xiang Biyu and began watching the Sword Emperor Qualifications, which surprised her master.","\"I thought you said it’s a waste of time,\" Xiang Biyu teased her.","\"Perhaps, but it’s not like I have anything else to do,\" Azure calmly responded.","Somewhere in the Ninth Heaven, the Heavenly Son’s family—the Tian Family—was also watching.","\"I can’t believe someone is actually ahead of our eldest...\" one of the elders muttered, his gaze shifting toward a nearby couple to see their reaction.","The two sat silently, their eyes sunken with exhaustion, dark circles beneath them as if they hadn’t slept in decades. Yet despite their weary appearance, their aura was unmistakably vast, commanding, and unfathomably powerful.","They were none other than Tian Yuexing’s parents.","\"The trial’s just begun. He’ll have plenty of time to catch up,\" said his father, his voice calm and full of confidence. He wore flowing black robes that matched the color of his long, neatly tied hair.","The woman beside him remained silent, her attention focused on Tian Yuexing, who was close to defeating all of his opponents.","While the entire world stirred in commotion over his existence, Yuan quietly stepped into his second trial."]},{"number":2038,"title":"Chapter 2038: Sword Emperor Qualifications’ Second Trial","paragraphs":["After stepping through the second door, Yuan found himself in a familiar setup—a solitary path stretching ahead, offering only one direction: forward.","But unlike before, it wasn’t a dirt path flanked by trees. This time, he stood on a narrow platform, sandwiched between two vast, seemingly endless seas on either side, their shimmering surfaces stretching out to the horizon.","Though the surface of the sea was calm and without any ripples, like that of a glass of water resting on a table, Yuan could sense countless sea beasts stirring beneath the tranquil waters, their presence concealed.","Once he took in his surroundings and grasped the nature of his situation, Yuan began walking forward at a calm, steady pace. With the trial’s rules still unknown to him, caution was essential.","After taking about a dozen careful steps, Yuan suddenly came to a halt when a faint ripple disturbed the otherwise motionless surface of the sea.","The very next second, a massive sea creature burst from the water, launching itself toward him with its jaws wide open, as if intending to swallow him whole in a single bite.","Yuan instinctively drew his sword, Supreme Sword Aura already surging to the surface. But just as he was about to strike, he paused—his eyes narrowing as he recognized the familiar aura enveloping the sea creature.","A knowing smile tugged at his lips. In the next instant, he withdrew his Supreme Sword Aura and channeled ordinary Sword Aura instead, slashing toward the creature with precision and confidence.","His sword cut right through the sea creature, killing it in a single strike. The sea creature not only had the same aura as his opponents from the last trial, but it also required Yuan to strike it with matching strength.","After dispatching the sea creature, Yuan resumed his path, his pace quickening slightly with confidence.","But just as he advanced a few more steps, his eyes narrowed sharply. Without hesitation, he raised his sword and swung it at the empty space in front of him, as if trying to hit an invisible enemy.","In the very next moment, a sharp shattering sound rang out as Yuan’s blade collided with something unseen. The invisible force became visible upon impact, revealing a sword forged from Supreme Sword Aura.","It functioned similarly to the swords from the previous trial, but with one critical difference: this one had been completely invisible to the naked eye.","\"He actually blocked that?!\" Sword Empress Huang exclaimed, eyes wide with disbelief.","Every Sword Emperor Qualification was unique, its trials ever-changing and unpredictable. Because of this, those who had passed them in the past couldn’t pass down any concrete knowledge to the next generation.","And when the current Sword Emperors witnessed the sudden invisible strike, many of them felt a rare twinge of uncertainty. Had they been in Yuan’s place, facing that same hidden assault, few were confident they could have blocked it as cleanly—or even at all.","\"Is it just me, or does this year’s Sword Emperor Qualifications seem much harder than the last?\" one of the Sword Emperors murmured aloud, his brows furrowed in concern.","\"Not just the last one...\" another replied solemnly. \"This year’s qualifications might be the hardest in history.\"","While it was normal, even expected, for the trials to gradually grow more difficult over time, reflecting the world’s constant evolution, such a sudden and immense spike in difficulty was completely unprecedented.","\"I was fairly confident those two would succeed,\" the Sixth Elder remarked, referring to the Holy Sword Maiden and the Holy Sword King. \"But after seeing the trials this year... I can’t help but feel a little worried.\"","\"Though this year’s trials are especially difficult, I have confidence in my son and his ability,\" said a fierce-looking red-haired man seated beside Sword Empress Huang.","He was one of the three Sword Emperors of the Holy Sword Clan, and his calm, unwavering tone reflected the confidence he had in his son, the Holy Sword King.","\"The same goes for my baby girl,\" said a handsome silver-haired man seated beside the red-haired Sword Emperor, a faint smile tugging at his lips.","He was the father of the Holy Sword Maiden, one of the most respected figures in the Holy Sword Clan as its faction leader, and his voice carried both pride and confidence.","Sword Empress Huang shook her head and said, \"It’s fine to have confidence in your children, but you’re fooling yourselves if you think they have a good chance. Even we would’ve struggled if we had faced trials this difficult during our own qualifications.\"","\"And you shouldn’t look down on other people’s children, especially when you don’t know what it’s like to have any,\" the red-haired Sword Emperor replied, a mocking smile tugging at his lips.","\"Why the fuck would I want any children? They’re too much of a pain in the ass,\" she quickly responded.","\"With that potty mouth of yours, I’m honestly glad you don’t have any children,\" said the silver-haired Sword Emperor, shaking his head with a sigh. \"I don’t think I could handle multiple potty mouths around me.\"","As word spread about the unprecedented difficulty of this year’s Sword Emperor Qualifications, more and more cultivators from across the heavens began tuning in, drawn by curiosity and the desire to witness history in the making.","Meanwhile, after handling the invisible strike, Yuan pressed onward.","The farther he traveled along the path, the more ripples appeared on the water’s surface—each one signaling an impending attack from the sea creatures below. And without fail, every time Yuan defeated a beast, an invisible sword would lash out from the air, attempting to catch him off guard.","This meant that the farther Yuan advanced, the more sea creatures he had to face at once, each wave more aggressive than the last. And as soon as he brought them down, invisible swords would strike without warning, giving him barely a moment to breathe.","The trial was no longer just a test of control—it had also become a relentless gauntlet of endurance, awareness, and speed."]},{"number":2039,"title":"Chapter 2039: Tian Yuexing’s First Trial","paragraphs":["It took almost an entire day, but Tian Yuexing finally defeated all of the masked men.","\"This is just the first trial, but I am already sweating. Why’d they make this year’s qualification so difficult? Is it because of my reputation?\" Tian Yuexing wondered out loud as he waited for the portal to appear so he could leave, unaware that the trial had yet to end.","However, he would soon learn the truth when nothing happened for several hours.","\"The trial’s still ongoing? In that case, where are the enemies?\" Tian Yuexing considered flying around, but just as he took to the sky, he noticed thousands of semi-transparent swords appearing in the sky above him.","His eyes widened with surprise, and he instinctively used a martial technique to attack all of the swords at once. However, his eyes widened even more after witnessing his martial technique unexpectedly shatter from clashing with the swords.","\"What?!\" he exclaimed, his voice filled with disbelief.","Soon, the sky above Tian Yuexing darkened as the swords descended upon him.","Refusing to even consider retreat, he chose to face them head-on, unleashing his full strength in a barrage of powerful strikes. Yet no matter how much force he poured into his attacks, his blows couldn’t even graze the falling swords, much less destroy them. It was as if the blades were untouchable, immune to brute strength alone.","After narrowly evading the descending swords, Tian Yuexing’s eyes narrowed. He noticed that the aura surrounding these swords was different from that of the masked men he had faced earlier.","Realization began to stir, but with the swords relentlessly pursuing him, he had little time to think. Forced to dodge while piecing together the puzzle, he racked his brain, desperately trying to decipher the key to passing the trial.","Eventually, Tian Yuexing uncovered the trick. Piece by piece, the puzzle came together, and he began destroying the swords one at a time.","Unlike Yuan, who possessed the skills and control to dismantle them all in a single sweeping motion, Tian Yuexing had to take a more methodical approach. He focused first on the swords imbued with Supreme Sword Aura, the type he was most familiar with.","After hours of relentless dodging and careful strikes, he cleared those away and shifted his attention to the blades carrying Enhanced Sword Aura. These proved more troublesome, often requiring multiple attempts to break through, each failure costing him precious energy and time.","After two more days of nonstop movement and relentless effort, Tian Yuexing finally destroyed the last sword. Despite his cultivation, exhaustion weighed heavily on him, and every fiber of his being longed to collapse onto the ground and sleep.","But then he remembered that his every movement was being watched by countless spectators across the Nine Heavens.","’I am the Heavenly Son—the number one genius in the Nine Heavens! I must not disgrace myself!’","With sheer willpower, he straightened his posture, composed himself, and stepped through the portal that appeared before him with graceful movements.","When Tian Yuexing returned to the platform outside, he glanced around and saw that no other participants had finished the first trial yet—a result he fully expected.","However, there was something off about the atmosphere, and the audience was oddly quiet.","But Tian Yuexing didn’t question it and turned to look at Senior Bai, who was standing not far away.","\"I get a week to rest, correct?\" he asked.","\"That’s right.\" Senior Bai nodded his head, confirming it.","Without wasting another second, Tian Yuexing sat down and began to cultivate, not to recover his spiritual energy, but to calm and steady his mind.","As a cultivator in the God Ascension Realm, it would take years of constant battle to deplete his spiritual energy. However, the trial had been mentally grueling, pushing his focus, perception, and discipline to their limits. Moreover, the constant swapping of sword aura depleted his soul strength much quicker than anticipated.","Shortly after, Tian Yuexing’s name jumped to the second rank with a score of 95. Of course, Tian Yuexing didn’t even bother to look at the ranking since he was convinced that he was first.","As Tian Yuexing focused on his cultivation, the spectators mumbled to each other.","\"Seeing the Heavenly Son in second place always invokes a weird feeling.\"","\"Right? He’s usually first at whatever he does.\"","Although Tian Yuexing was immersed in his cultivation, he had a strange feeling in his gut that prompted him to open his eyes, and when he saw the weird looks the spectators were giving him, he subconsciously tilted his head to look at the ranking, and when he did, he was left in disbelief.","Tian Yuexing’s eyes widened after seeing the name.","\"Yuan!\" he uttered, his voice laced with disbelief.","He then turned to ask Senior Bai, \"There must be some sort of mistake. How is he above me when I am the only one here?!\"","Senior Bai cleared his throat and calmly responded, \"He’s not here because he already started his second trial.\"","\"When?! When did he finish?!\" Tian Yuexing demanded answers.","\"A little over two days ago.\"","\"Over two days ago?! He finished the first trial in less than a day?!\" Tian Yuexing couldn’t believe what he was hearing, nor could he fathom how Yuan had accomplished such a feat.","’Damn it! I don’t have the time to rest if he’s already two days ahead of me!’","He immediately stood up and ran toward the second door, quickly disappearing from the platform after resting only for a few minutes.","Meanwhile, the rest of the participants had reached the end of the path and started fighting the thousands of masked men. Unfortunately for them, barely anyone was paying attention to their trial, as everyone was focused on Yuan, who was in the lead, and the Heavenly Son, who was playing catch-up—a rare sight for many.","As for Yuan, who was now two days deep into the second trial, he had killed tens of thousands of sea beasts and traveled dozens of miles on the path, but the end was still nowhere in sight."]},{"number":2040,"title":"Chapter 2040: Reaching the End of the Second Trial","paragraphs":["After spending two days in the second trial, Yuan progressed to the point where he had to face hundreds of sea creatures at once with each encounter. Fortunately, their attacks were still predictable and straightforward as long as he paid attention to the ripples appearing in the water.","Yuan had also realized that the sea creatures only appeared when he advanced, each encounter seemingly triggered by crossing an invisible threshold. This meant he could have paused between battles, taken breaks, and prepared for each wave.","But he chose not to, and for the past two days, he had moved without rest, facing each encounter head-on with unwavering resolve, as if testing the limits of both the trial and himself.","Yuan’s performance was nothing short of astonishing, leaving the spectators speechless, many with their mouths agape, unable to believe what they were witnessing.","When they watched the Heavenly Son and the other participants undergo their trials, the sheer difficulty was palpable. Every clash and every movement carried the weight of struggle.","But when they turned their gaze to Yuan, it was a different story entirely. He moved with such ease and speed that the trial itself seemed beneath him, almost as if he was mocking the efforts of every other participant.","\"You know, watching him... it reminds me of the Faceless Sword Emperor’s qualification,\" remarked one of the Sword Emperors, eyes fixed on the display.","Thanks to recorded archives of past trials, anyone with access could study them, and none were more watched or revered than the Faceless Sword Emperor’s, a trial he had dominated with unmatched grace and power.","\"Are we witnessing the birth of a second Faceless Sword Emperor?\" someone else murmured, the question lingering in the air like a prophecy waiting to be fulfilled.","Meanwhile, the moment Tian Yuexing stepped into the area for the second trial, he began walking forward without hesitation, wasting no time to observe his surroundings.","There was no room for delay in his mind. He knew he was already behind, and every second counted if he hoped to catch up to Yuan.","While his actions could be seen as reckless, Tian Yuexing was confident in his own abilities.","When the first sea creature attacked a few steps later, Tian Yuexing defeated it with a single strike.","’I don’t know how you managed to get ahead of me, but it won’t last!’ Tian Yuexing thought to himself, determination flaring in his eyes as he pressed forward.","But just a few steps later, his thoughts were abruptly cut off. His instincts flared like lightning, screaming danger. Without thinking, he raised his sword in front of him, just in time to somewhat block the invisible sword.","However, his reaction was just a moment too slow. Though he managed to intercept part of the strike, the invisible sword still slipped through his guard, slicing into his left arm and leaving a deep, bleeding gash.","Tian Yuexing gritted his teeth in frustration, his eyes narrowing at the wound.","The wound on his arm was minor, something he could easily ignore, but the fact that he’d been struck at all, and by such a simple trick, gnawed at his pride. He couldn’t accept making such a blunder—not with so many people watching.","Seconds later, Tian Yuexing sensed the invisible sword circling back for a second strike.","This time, fully alert and focused, he met it head-on. With a precise swing infused with his Supreme Sword Aura, he shattered the blade cleanly, redeeming his earlier mistake in a single, decisive motion.","After overcoming the first encounter, Tian Yuexing didn’t immediately charge forward to chase after Yuan.","Instead, he stood still, closed his eyes, and took a deep breath. The weight of his earlier misstep lingered, and he knew rushing in recklessly would only lead to more mistakes.","\"What the heck am I doing? There’s no need to rush or panic. I’ll definitely catch up and reclaim my rank. It’s only natural and a matter of time,\" he muttered to himself.","When he opened his eyes, they were filled with confidence and renewed focus, and he continued forward with immense concentration, no longer paying attention to Yuan being ahead.","Time passed swiftly, and Yuan had now entered his fourth day within the second trial.","Having advanced without pause, the difficulty had escalated dramatically; each encounter now unleashed thousands of sea creatures upon him at once, their numbers swelling like tidal waves with every step he took.","However, despite the overwhelming numbers, Yuan dispatched them all within moments, effortlessly cutting them down with his Limitless Sword Domain.","After days of honing his control to an even higher level, his manipulation of sword auras had become as natural as breathing. With each step forward, he moved calmly and gracefully, and what was meant to be a grueling trial now appeared more like a leisurely stroll through the park.","To the spectators, it was no longer just impressive—it was surreal.","\"How long do you think he’ll be able to keep up this pace?\" the Holy Sword Maiden’s father asked aloud, his gaze fixed on the image of Yuan effortlessly advancing the trial.","\"Well,\" the Holy Sword King’s father replied, arms crossed in thought, \"the first and second trials follow the same general structure, but the second is far more brutal in scale. He might breeze through this... but the real challenge begins in the later trials when everything changes. That’s when we’ll see if he can keep his pace.\"","By the end of the fourth day, Yuan finally caught sight of the path’s end in the distance, and just as he expected, it opened into another vast arena, its wide, circular expanse radiated an ominous stillness.","As Yuan stepped into the center of the arena, the stillness shattered. The calm water began to tremble, and a deep, resonating ripple spread outward across the surface.","Moments later, several glowing orbs appeared just beneath the water, pulsing with an eerie light. Then, with a thunderous roar and a violent surge, a colossal sea creature with many tentacles erupted from the depths like a volcanic explosion, water cascading from its body as it loomed high above Yuan.","\"This is...\"","Behind his mask, Yuan’s eyes widened in surprise the moment he laid eyes on the squid-like creature. He had encountered this beast before, and the sight of it stirred some unpleasant memories."]},{"number":2041,"title":"Chapter 2041: True Emperor of the Seas","paragraphs":["With a black body, pearlescent texture, and colorful circles all around its body, the squid-like sea creature that appeared before Yuan resembled the giant sea creature that killed Huang Xiao Li’s parents during their trip to the Desolate Continent.","Although it wasn’t as massive, and its aura was incomparably weaker than what he remembered, Yuan would never mistake its appearance.","’Just what is this sea creature...?’ he wondered inwardly.","After that one encounter during the Primordial Era, Yuan never encountered it again despite his efforts to find it.","Seeing this monster on the display, Chu Liuxiang’s body trembled, and she asked Kelan with a slight frown on her face, \"What is that sea creature?\"","In a calm voice, Kelan responded, \"If I am not mistaken, that is the True Emperor of the Seas, a mythical sea creature that has existed since the Primordial Era. Of course, the one in the trial isn’t the real thing but just an imitation.\"","\"True Emperor of the Seas?\" Chu Liuxiang mumbled its name.","Kelan nodded and explained further, \"This monster defies common sense, and it is neither a magical beast nor a divine beast. Nobody knows what it really is or where it came from, but it has existed since the Primordial Era, living deep beneath the sea. Also, it appears to have the ability to teleport from realm to realm, since it has been spotted in almost every single realm across the Nine Heavens.\"","\"How powerful is it?\" Chu Liuxiang asked.","\"Unfathomably powerful. A Cultivation God tried to hunt it before but was unsuccessful. Not only does it have regenerative abilities that rival even demons, but it has a unique power that completely renders spiritual energy useless,\" Kelan said.","\"It’s even stronger than a Cultivation God? That’s hard to believe...\" Xi Meili muttered.","Kelan smiled and said, \"In this world, there are a few entities that surpass our knowledge and defy common sense. They are known as the Four Mystic Wonders, and the True Emperor of the Seas is one of them.\"","\"Who are the other three?\" Shi Lang asked.","Kelan pondered for a moment before responding, \"I believe they are the Vanishing Emperor of the Skies, Immovable Emperor of the Earth, and the Calamity of the Void. They’re all heaven-defying entities that you do not want to mess with.\"","Meanwhile, shortly after the monster’s emergence, it wasted no time and launched a fierce assault. Its colossal tentacles, each pulsing with an overwhelming concentration of Supreme Sword Aura, lashed out with terrifying momentum.","Rising high above, the tentacles blocked out the sky, casting a looming shadow over the arena like an omen. Then, in a single moment that tore through the silence, they came crashing down toward Yuan with speed and power that could pulverize mountains.","Since the arena was too small, Yuan abandoned it and flew into the sky to face the monster. Without hesitation, he fought back with Limitless Sword Domain, striking the monster with thousands of swords.","The sea creature didn’t even flinch as the attacks tore into its flesh, allowing thousands of gaping holes to be carved into its massive body. Yet, within moments, those wounds sealed themselves completely, the flesh knitting back together.","Seeing this, Yuan’s eyes turned sharp, and his entire body erupted with Supreme Sword Aura, the sheer intensity distorting the space around him. If minor wounds couldn’t slow the creature down, then he would carve a wound so deep it would take more than regeneration to recover.","He raised his sword, Supreme Sword Aura coiling around it like a dragon preparing to strike, and with a single thought, unleashed a devastating slash aimed to split the sea creature in half.","[Immortal Rendering Sword Strike!]","The very next moment, the massive sea creature’s colossal body was cleaved cleanly in half, but the Supreme Sword Aura continued its rampage, splitting the sea itself in a straight, endless line that stretched all the way to the distant horizon.","However, just like a demon, the sea creature immediately combined its split body back together and resumed its attack like nothing had happened.","\"I see...\" Yuan suddenly mumbled.","Just before the sea creature’s body fully regenerated, Yuan’s sharp eyes noticed several crystal balls embedded deep within its flesh, each glowing faintly with a subtle aura. Their presence had been completely concealed until his strike had momentarily laid the creature bare.","Now that he knew its weakness, Yuan wasted no time. His sword flickered constantly, quickly unleashing powerful sword techniques that tore through the monster’s flesh.","The moment a crystal ball was exposed, he struck them with perfectly controlled sword aura, tuned to match the aura surrounding the crystal.","One by one, the crystal balls shattered, each explosion causing the creature’s regeneration to falter more severely than the last.","The monster had thousands of crystal balls hidden within its massive body, so it took Yuan a few days to reveal and destroy them. Eventually, Yuan destroyed the last crystal ball.","Then, as if all strength had been drained from its body, the behemoth began to sink into the depths of the shimmering sea below.","\"One day I will find the real you and kill you for real...\" Yuan silently swore to himself as he watched the water swallow its massive form without resistance, leaving only ripples and the fading echo of its defeat.","Shortly after defeating the sea creature, the exit appeared, and Yuan left the second trial.","The first trial had taken him less than a day, but the second trial took ten days to clear.","When Yuan returned to the platform, he could see the other participants cultivating in silence, clearly resting after clearing their first trial.","Besides the Heavenly Son, every single participant was there.","After giving the other participants only a brief moment of his attention, Yuan turned to look at Senior Bai and said, \"I’d like to start the next trial.\"","When the other participants heard his words, they opened their eyes to look at him with disbelief all over their faces."]},{"number":2042,"title":"Chapter 2042: Sword Emperor Qualifications’ Third Trial","paragraphs":["Hearing that Yuan wanted to proceed to the next trial immediately after completing his second left the other participants feeling weak and inadequate, as they themselves still needed time to recover.","The Holy Sword King could only grit his teeth in frustration as he glared at Yuan, still reeling from the shock of learning that Yuan was ranked first, above even the Heavenly Son, a figure he could only dream of surpassing.","’There’s no way he’s completed two trials while I’d just finished my first! He must be cheating somehow!’ The Holy Sword King scowled inwardly, racking his brain for an explanation, but no matter how hard he tried, he couldn’t think of a single way Yuan might have cheated.","In the end, he decided to let the others investigate instead, confident that he wasn’t the only one harboring such suspicions.","Naturally, some of the spectators did question Yuan’s astonishing pace and progress. However, having witnessed his performance firsthand, they found nothing that hinted at foul play, so they could only continue to look for anything suspicious.","\"Honestly, I didn’t think you’d finish the second trial so quickly.\" Senior Bai spoke as he approached the sealed door that led to the third trial.","After removing the seal on the door and opening it for Yuan, he continued, \"Good luck.\"","Yuan nodded and entered the third trial—but not before saying to Senior Bai, \"See you soon.\"","After Yuan left, the Holy Sword King asked out loud, \"Senior, pardon me for asking, but are we all really taking the same trial?\"","The other participants turned to look at Senior Bai. Though they all knew the answer in their hearts, they still hoped for a different answer.","\"The trials are the same for everyone. There is no exception,\" said Senior Bai. \"If you’re worried that might not be the case, you may watch the recordings afterward.\"","The Holy Sword King became silent and, without saying another word, returned to cultivating.","Meanwhile, within the second trial, Tian Yuexing steadily made his way forward. Though his pace couldn’t compare to Yuan’s, and he occasionally paused to recover between encounters, his progress was still remarkably swift. Had it not been for Yuan’s overwhelming presence, he would have undoubtedly claimed the spotlight in the Sword Emperor Qualifications.","’Fuck... which bastard created this year’s Sword Emperor Qualifications? I’d like to have a word with them after this!’ Tian Yuexing cursed the creator inwardly as he continued to advance.","At the same time, Yuan began his third trial. Shortly after stepping through the door, Yuan found himself standing in the middle of a vast, barren field, surrounded by nothing but dirt and scattered pebbles.","He looked around but sensed nothing until the ground suddenly began to tremble, as if an earthquake had erupted beneath his feet.","Soon, the source of the tremor revealed itself—a horde of magical beasts surged over the horizon, thundering toward Yuan like a relentless stampede.","Yuan immediately shifted into a battle stance. But just as he was about to strike, a sharp and powerful ripple swept across the field. Before he could even react, the entire horde of magical beasts was slain in the blink of an eye, their bodies cleanly severed in half.","The next moment, Yuan watched as a figure descended from the sky, landing just a few meters away.","He was a handsome man clad in green robes, with short silver hair and a black sword gripped firmly in his hand. Though Yuan didn’t recognize him, many among the spectators did, especially the swordmasters, whose expressions filled with awe the moment they saw him.","\"The Jade Sword Emperor!\" Kelan remarked after seeing this handsome man.","\"Who?\" Wang Ming asked.","Li Jinxi answered instead, \"The first swordmaster to claim the title of Sword Emperor. He’s basically the first officially recognized Sword Emperor in history.\"","Moments after his arrival, the Jade Sword Emperor raised his black sword and, without the slightest warning, unleashed a relentless barrage of sword techniques at Yuan.","Thousands of green swords materialized around Yuan, swirling rapidly to form a powerful, sword-laced tornado that howled with destructive force.","However, despite its impressive display, the technique lacked the strength to truly threaten Yuan, as the Jade Sword Emperor’s cultivation was only at the Bronze Immortal level.","Realizing that his opponent possessed only the strength of a Bronze Immortal, Yuan paid no heed to the raging tornado around him and flew straight through it. In a flash, he closed the distance to the Jade Sword Emperor and, with a single decisive strike, cut down the handsome swordsman where he stood.","\"...\"","The spectators were left stunned by the outcome, not because of Yuan’s overwhelming prowess but because his opponent appeared too weak.","\"What just happened? Why was his opponent so weak?\" someone in the crowd exclaimed, their voice echoing through the area.","\"Is there something wrong with the trial? He didn’t even do anything special to defeat the Jade Sword Emperor.\"","\"That’s...\"","Senior Bai pondered a proper response.","The third trial was meant to test a participant’s talents and limits by pitting them against an opponent with superior cultivation, hence why Yuan, who was only at the peak of Immortal Ascension, had to fight against a Bronze Immortal.","However, Yuan was powerful enough to slay even True Immortals at his current level, making a mere Bronze Immortal hardly worth his attention.","Naturally, the spectators were unaware of the truth. In fact, most were convinced that Yuan was suppressing his cultivation to the Immortal Ascension realm, firmly believing that his true strength lay within the God Ascension Realm, hence why they were confused when the trial gave Yuan such an easy opponent.","But before Senior Bai could clear the misunderstanding, Yuan’s next opponent appeared—another Sword Emperor from the past, this one possessing the cultivation of a Silver Immortal.","In Yuan’s eyes, the third trial felt a little too easy. Still, he assumed it was merely the warm-up phase and that the real challenge had yet to begin. So, without giving it much thought, he effortlessly defeated the Silver Immortal."]},{"number":2043,"title":"Chapter 2043: Sword Emperor Qualifications’ Third Trial(2)","paragraphs":["Shortly after Yuan defeated his second opponent, a third figure emerged—once known as the Mad Sword Emperor, one of the most infamous Sword Emperors in history for the atrocities he committed. However, with his cultivation only at the Silver Immortal level, he posed little challenge to Yuan and was swiftly defeated as well.","The fourth and fifth Sword Emperors arrived soon after, and, as expected, Yuan defeated them both with ease.","The spectators were left utterly speechless—and some, especially those who had suspected Yuan of cheating, were visibly enraged.","\"What the hell is this?! Why are all of his opponents so damn weak?! Compared to the first two trials, this one is laughably easy! Hell, many of us here can clear it without any issues!\"","\"Right?! Are we still watching the Sword Emperor Qualifications or something else?!\"","\"I’ll be right back,\" Senior Bai said to the resting participants before stepping off the platform to address the situation.","The platform was protected by a soundproof formation, preventing any of the spectators’ voices from reaching the participants. Still, the participants could sense that something was wrong, judging by the crowd’s restless movements and increasingly agitated expressions.","It wasn’t just the spectators’ voices that were blocked—the participants were also unable to see the display screens showing the ongoing trials. This measure was in place to prevent them from gaining any foresight, ensuring the trials remained fair for everyone.","After leaving the platform, Senior Bai used a voice amplification technique, his words rippling through the entire space, reaching every corner, no matter how far the listeners were.","\"I understand your confusion, but I assure you there is nothing wrong with the trials,\" Senior Bai began, his voice steady as it echoed through the space. \"Everything is progressing exactly as intended.\"","He then went on to explain the nature of the third trial.","\"In the third trial, participants must face a series of opponents, each possessing superior cultivation. These opponents are none other than Sword Emperors from the past, and the participants must rely solely on their sword techniques to prevail.\"","Lastly, he addressed the reason behind the apparent disparity in Yuan’s opponents.","\"As for why Yuan’s opponents are only at the Immortal Realm,\" Senior Bai continued, \"it is because his true cultivation is only at the peak of the Immortal Ascension Realm.\"","\"What?!\"","\"Impossible!\"","Upon hearing that Yuan was only at the Immortal Ascension Realm, countless figures sprang to their feet in utter disbelief, their faces frozen in shock. Across the Nine Heavens, stunned gasps echoed from those watching from afar, unable to comprehend what they had just heard.","\"Th-that’s his true cultivation...? He’s participating in the Sword Emperor Qualification as a mortal...?\"","From the spectators gathered at the Gates of Heaven to the Tian Family watching from their estate in the Supreme Heaven, it was, without question, the most shocking revelation of the entire event.","None of them had ever heard of a mortal comprehending the Supreme Sword Aura, let alone participating in the Sword Emperor Qualifications.","\"If you still doubt my words, I will verify his cultivation before everyone once he comes out of the third trial,\" Senior Bai added.","Hearing this, the crowd could no longer complain without looking foolish and disrespectful. And so, everyone waited in quiet anticipation for Yuan to complete his third trial, which, unsurprisingly, didn’t take long at all.","Just a few hours after it began, Yuan had defeated a total of ten opponents and cleared the trial, completing it even faster than his first.","When Yuan returned to the platform, the others were still resting—at least until they saw him emerge so soon.","\"For you to be back already, you must’ve given up on the trial! Hahaha!\" the Holy Sword King laughed loudly, assuming Yuan had used the talisman to forfeit and disqualify himself.","Yuan slowly turned to the Holy Sword King, his voice calm and composed.","\"If you have the energy to laugh that loudly, perhaps you should start your second trial. You won’t beat me by sitting there.\"","The Holy Sword King scoffed, his tone defiant.","\"So what if I’m a little behind? In the end, only the final result matters—and you’ve already forfeited! Once I pass the third trial, that’s my victory!\"","\"Forfeited? Says who?\" Yuan replied.","\"What...?\" The Holy Sword King’s expression stiffened. If Yuan hadn’t forfeited, had he actually completed the third trial, which was supposed to be even more difficult than the first two, in even less time?","\"There’s no way...\" he muttered under his breath, his voice barely audible, like a whisper carried by a mosquito.","\"Speaking of the third trial...\" Senior Bai’s voice suddenly resounded, and moments later, he approached Yuan.","\"I’m sorry, but due to some complications, I have to verify your cultivation.\"","\"Complications...? I knew it! You were cheating this whole time!\" The Holy Sword King exclaimed.","However, Senior Bai quickly corrected him, \"No, he’s not being accused of cheating. We just need to verify his cultivation to clear up some misunderstanding and confusion.\"","\"That doesn’t make any sense!\"","Senior Bai didn’t bother trying to explain further and merely said, \"The trial is still ongoing. If you continue to disturb the other participants, I’ll have to disqualify you.\"","The Holy Sword King clicked his tongue in annoyance but said nothing further. Rising to his feet, he turned and silently made his way toward the door leading to the second trial.","Meanwhile, the other participants stayed behind to see what the deal with Yuan was.","\"Go ahead and test my cultivation,\" Yuan said to Senior Bai, his voice calm and without the slightest trace of displeasure. He trusted Senior Bai and knew he wasn’t acting out of malice.","Senior Bai gave a silent nod and signaled to someone. Moments later, a middle-aged man stepped onto the platform, carrying a cultivation-measuring device—one of the most advanced and accurate tools in all the Nine Heavens.","The middle-aged man activated the treasure, and without requiring any action from Yuan, a series of intricate formations unfolded around him, encircling him in a shimmering array of light."]},{"number":2044,"title":"Chapter 2044: Sword Emperor Qualifications’ Fourth Trial","paragraphs":["Every spectator watched with immense attention as the cultivation-measuring device assessed Yuan’s true cultivation.","Moments later, the device completed its assessment, and the words \"Ninth Level Immortal Ascension\" appeared in glowing script for all to see.","\"He’s really a mortal!\"","Several voices rang out across the crowd, filled with disbelief, awe, and a hint of reverence.","Though nobody there could comprehend how a mortal managed to learn Supreme Sword Aura or qualify for the Sword Emperor Qualifications, they were unable to deny the evidence before their very eyes.","\"To think our son is being surpassed by a mere mortal...\" Tian Yuexing’s father muttered, his face marked with bewilderment.","Even his wife, typically nonchalant and expressionless, couldn’t hide the surprise in her eyes.","\"My god... where did such a genius come from? If we recruit him into our family and pair him with Tian Jinhui, the Tian Family might finally surpass the Celestial Family,\" one of the elders remarked, eyes gleaming with ambition.","\"...\"","Though no one responded aloud, everyone was thinking the same thing.","Of course, the Tian Family wasn’t the only one thinking about recruiting Yuan into their family or sect, as nearly every influential background harbored the same intention and desire.","\"H-He’s a mortal...?\"","Every participant, except the Holy Sword Maiden, stared at Yuan in shock, their faces frozen with disbelief. It was a simple fact, yet none of them could fully grasp the weight of such an outrageous revelation.","They had been competing and losing against a mortal this whole time? None of them wanted to believe such a thing. They were all some of the most talented swordmasters across the Nine Heavens, but they were losing to a mere mortal? It wouldn’t make sense even in their dreams.","\"Haha... someone slap me and tell me I’m dreaming...\" one of the participants muttered with a dazed chuckle, his expression blank—like someone who had just suffered a mental blow.","\"Was that satisfactory?\" Yuan asked Senior Bai, who nodded with a warm smile on his face.","\"Yes, it was. Once again, I apologize for the inconvenience.\"","\"Then I would like to start my next trial,\" Yuan continued.","\"Of course...\"","Without delay, Senior Bai opened the fourth door for him.","And without a word, Yuan stepped through and vanished, beginning his fourth trial and widening the gap between himself and the other participants even further.","Shortly after Yuan’s departure, a heavy atmosphere settled over the remaining participants. One by one, without saying a word, they rose and stepped through the second door, each of them feeling an immense pressure not to be outshone by a mortal.","\"This guy is quite the monster,\" remarked Azure after she watched the events unfold.","Xiang Biyu smiled faintly and said, \"I always knew he would shake the world with his existence, but even I couldn’t have imagined how far he’d come in just a few decades. You probably won’t believe this, but he was still a Spirit King when I met him about twenty years ago.\"","Meanwhile, within the fourth trial, Yuan found himself standing before a majestic mountain, its towering peak pierced by a colossal sword embedded deep into the summit. A single path spiraled upward along the mountainside, reminiscent of the famed Dragon Spiral Mountain.","Yuan quickly noticed that his cultivation had been sealed, which meant it was likely that there would be no combat for this trial. After taking a moment to survey his surroundings, he stepped onto the path and began his ascent up the mountain.","Shortly after beginning his ascent, Yuan came across rows of swords embedded in the ground on either side of the path, positioned in perfect parallel, resembling a line of guardrails guiding the way.","At first, the swords appeared to be nothing more than ordinary weapons. But as Yuan climbed higher, they began to emit Sword Aura—faint at first, then gradually intensifying with every step, growing stronger the farther he ascended.","When the swords first began to emit Sword Aura, Yuan quickly realized he couldn’t proceed any farther unless he cloaked himself in Sword Aura stronger than that radiating from the swords themselves. If he tried to advance without doing so, he’d be blocked by an invisible barrier.","Meanwhile, outside the trial grounds, Senior Bai addressed the spectators, offering a detailed explanation of the fourth trial.","\"To pass the fourth trial, participants must ascend the mountain,\" he said. \"But to do so, they must possess a sufficient level of comprehension in Sword Aura. The higher they climb, the deeper their understanding must be, or they will be blocked.\"","He continued, \"That said, reaching the peak is not required to pass the fourth trial. Once a participant reaches a certain height, an exit will appear, allowing them to leave. However, if they choose to continue climbing, additional rewards will be granted based on how far they go.\"","\"What level of comprehension is required to reach the peak?\" someone suddenly asked.","\"A good question,\" Senior Bai responded. \"To reach the summit, one must possess a near-perfect mastery of the Supreme Sword Aura, a level reached only by experienced Sword Emperors.\"","The spectators were visibly surprised by the steep requirement. After all, most participants in the Sword Emperor Qualifications had yet to master the Supreme Sword Aura—an achievement so profound it was usually attained only after one became a Sword Emperor. For many, pursuing such mastery beforehand was seen as impractical, as it demanded an immense amount of time.","A few hours later, Yuan reached the point where the swords began to emit Enhanced Sword Aura. Though he could have arrived much sooner, he had chosen to walk at a leisurely pace, treating the climb as a peaceful stroll rather than a race. In fact, he would occasionally stop just to admire the view.","A day later, the swords around him started to emit Supreme Sword Aura.","Meanwhile, Tian Yuexing and the other participants were still struggling through the second trial. For those who had only recently entered, the harsh reality of the trial’s difficulty was just beginning to sink in, and with it, their hopes for the trials ahead quickly began to wither."]},{"number":2045,"title":"Chapter 2045: A Freak","paragraphs":["\"That mortal managed to pass this trial in just ten days?! That’s ridiculous!\"","When the other participants experienced the brutality of the second trial for themselves, none of them could believe that a mortal had managed to pass it in such a short time.","Though everyone progressed swiftly at first, they eventually slowed down after the number of enemies they had to deal with increased with each counter.","Moreover, one of the participants had already fallen, losing their physical body to the first invisible sword and being forced to forfeit the remainder of the Sword Emperor Qualifications.","Several others sustained injuries from the same unseen force, but as God Ascension cultivators, such wounds were easily endured and largely ignored.","Meanwhile, Yuan continued his steady ascent up the mountain, his body enveloped in Supreme Sword Aura.","Since maintaining Sword Aura required Soul Strength, Yuan had no difficulty keeping it active without rest. However, the audience was astonished by how effortlessly he sustained it, especially now that they knew he was only a mortal.","At first, they hadn’t thought much of it, assuming he was a God Ascension Realm cultivator. But after the truth was revealed, their shock deepened. For a mere mortal to possess Soul Strength on par with gods was nothing short of inconceivable.","Five days later, Yuan was still ascending the mountain. With each step, he had to gradually intensify the strength of his Supreme Sword Aura and keep it constantly active.","After a week within the fourth trial, Yuan finally reached the point required to pass. A shimmering exit portal quietly appeared behind him, signaling the trial’s completion.","Yuan raised an eyebrow at the sight of the exit. He could clearly see that the path continued upward.","After a brief moment of thought, he turned away from the portal and resumed his climb, completely ignoring it. In his eyes, the exit was nothing more than a distraction—placed there to tempt him into leaving before the true trial had ended.","Another week passed, and after spending a total of two weeks within the fourth trial, Yuan finally reached a point where he could no longer advance, as his current understanding of the Supreme Sword Aura had reached its limit.","But he didn’t turn back.","Instead, he sat down calmly, closed his eyes, and began to meditate, determined to push his comprehension even further.","\"There’s no way...\"","The audience almost couldn’t believe what they were seeing.","\"Is he... trying to advance his Supreme Sword Aura? In the middle of the trial?\"","Although Yuan was now close to the mountain’s peak, the remaining distance—though seemingly short—was as vast as the gap between heaven and earth. After all, even Sword Emperors required hundreds of thousands of years to approach perfection in their Supreme Sword Aura. For Yuan to attempt the same within the trial meant he was willingly giving away his first-place position.","\"There’s no denying his talent, but he’s too arrogant,\" one of the spectators scoffed.","\"Does he really think he can perfect his Supreme Sword Aura in just a few years? It’s like he’s mocking every swordmaster who’s ever lived.\"","The Sword Emperors present remained silent, but subtle displeasure flickered in their expressions. Though their faces betrayed little, a quiet tension hung around them.","If Yuan managed to deepen his mastery of the Supreme Sword Aura during the trial—even by a small margin—it would cast a shadow over their own accomplishments, making a mockery of the centuries, even millennia, they had spent refining their Supreme Sword Aura.","As time went on, the other participants steadily advanced through the second trial.","After nearly three months into his trial, the Heavenly Son, who was far ahead of the rest, finally reached the end of the path, where he was met by the final challenge: a replica of the legendary True Emperor of the Seas.","As for the other participants, a few were forced to forfeit midway, unable to endure the relentless pressure of the trial.","Just as the Heavenly Son began his battle with the True Emperor of the Seas, Yuan suddenly opened his eyes and rose to his feet.","The audience, who had shifted their attention away from him to focus on the others, immediately snapped their heads back toward him.","\"There’s no chance in hell he improved his Supreme Sword Aura in just a few months...\" someone muttered in disbelief, echoing the thoughts of many.","However, Yuan wasted no time in proving them wrong.","In the very next moment, his Supreme Sword Aura—previously stagnant—began to surge, its intensity rising steadily, shocking all who watched.","\"He actually improved his Supreme Sword Aura in months! This guy is a monster—a freak!\"","\"A sword freak!\"","At that moment, many had already made up their minds—if Yuan truly became a Sword Emperor, they would call him the Freak Sword Emperor.","However, despite the clear advancement in his Supreme Sword Aura, Yuan still couldn’t reach the peak. After only a few more steps, he was once again forced to stop.","Without hesitation, he sat down and resumed his cultivation, determined to break through the next threshold.","\"H-He’s trying to improve his Supreme Sword Aura again!\"","\"This guy is ridiculous!\"","\"Call me crazy, but I think this guy might be even more monstrous than the Faceless Sword Emperor.\"","\"I don’t doubt it.\"","\"My god... does he not intend to leave us even a shred of face?\" muttered the Holy Sword King’s father, his expression frozen in utter disbelief.","\"If ’that’ guy is watching now, I wonder what he’s thinking,\" said the Holy Sword Maiden’s father.","\"You mean the Peerless Sword Emperor?\" Sword Empress Huang said.","The Peerless Sword Emperor was the current strongest Sword Emperor in the Nine Heavens, widely believed by many to have even surpassed the legendary Faceless Sword Emperor.","\"That guy’s probably itching to fight with him, but with the disparity between their cultivation... he’ll have no choice but to wait.\"","Soon, another month passed, and the Heavenly Son had finally defeated the fake True Emperor of the Seas, passing the second trial."]},{"number":2046,"title":"Chapter 2046: A True Freak","paragraphs":["After defeating the final opponent and clearing the second trial, the Heavenly Son, Tian Yuexing, returned to the platform outside with a weary expression.","Though he had experienced battles that stretched for years without pause, none of them compared to the sheer strain and intensity of the past few months within the trial.","When Tian Yuexing returned to the platform, the first thing he did was glance around, searching for Yuan. After confirming he was alone, he lifted his gaze to the rankings above, hoping—perhaps even expecting—that he had finally surpassed him.","But the moment his eyes landed on the display, they widened in disbelief.","Yuan’s name still stood firmly above his own, now marked with 300 points, while his score remained at 190.","\"Three hundred points?!\" Tian Yuexing exclaimed aloud, his voice filled with disbelief.","\"Does that mean he’s already completed the second and the third trial?!\"","Realizing that the gap between him and Yuan had widened, Tian Yuexing immediately turned to look at the door to the third trial, and after a brief moment of hesitation, entered it without resting.","When his parents saw this, they could only shake their heads inwardly at his rash decision.","\"Though he’s undoubtedly one of the most talented individuals in the Nine Heavens, he still lacks the patience his sister possesses,\" remarked one of the Tian Family elders.","\"What can we do? He’s too prideful for his own good sometimes,\" another elder said with a sigh.","Meanwhile, Tian Jinhui, who had been quietly observing from one of the spectators’ islands, shook her head and let out a soft sigh.","\"Will it kill you to stop comparing yourself to others?\" she muttered. \"You don’t have to be the best at everything.\"","Ever since his birth, Tian Yuexing had been first in pretty much everything he did, as if he were destined to be number one. In his mind, not being number one meant something was wrong, and he would stop at nothing to correct it.","Of course, it wasn’t as though Tian Yuexing had never experienced defeat. It was just never at the hands of someone from his own generation.","\"I’ve never seen the Heavenly Son acting like this before.\"","\"Probably because he’s never had to chase after someone this badly. It’s honestly quite refreshing.\"","Those who had once been defeated by Tian Yuexing—or had long harbored envy toward his overwhelming talent—couldn’t help but rejoice at the sight of him finally being the inferior one.","Shortly after entering the third trial, Tian Yuexing encountered the Jade Sword Emperor.","However, unlike during Yuan’s trial, the Jade Sword Emperor now possessed the cultivation of a fourth-level God Ascension expert, one full level above Tian Yuexing, who was only at the third level.","Although being at the third level of God Ascension might not seem particularly impressive at first glance—especially for the number one genius in the Nine Heavens—one had to consider Tian Yuexing’s age. He was still under a hundred thousand years old, making his cultivation level nothing short of extraordinary.","At birth, Tian Yuexing’s cultivation was already at the Immortal Ascension Realm. It took him less than a thousand years to step into immortality, and before reaching ten thousand years of age, he had already ascended to the True Immortal Realm.","As for the other participants, they were all only at the first level of God Ascension realm while being older than Tian Yuexing.","\"That appearance... You must be the Jade Sword Emperor!\" Tian Yuexing exclaimed, a glint of excitement in his eyes. \"If I weren’t in a hurry, I’d relish the chance for a proper duel!\"","Without wasting another moment, he unleashed his full power right from the start.","Though he lagged behind Yuan in the Sword Emperor Qualifications, Tian Yuexing was a true prodigy, hailed as the number one genius of the Nine Heavens for good reason.","During his battle with the Jade Sword Emperor, he reminded everyone of exactly why he held that title, defeating his opponent decisively in just a few days.","Yet, when the audience compared his performance to Yuan’s—who had defeated the Jade Sword Emperor in just a few strikes—Tian Yuexing’s victory, while impressive, no longer seemed extraordinary.","While Tian Yuexing continued to chase after him with everything he had, Yuan had already advanced his Supreme Sword Aura again—this time, in even less time than before.","\"What?! He’s improved his Supreme Sword Aura already?!\" The spectators had to do a double-take when they saw Yuan ascending the mountain again.","\"How did it take him even less time to improve this time?! Shouldn’t it take even longer than before?! It doesn’t make any sense!\"","\"A freak! He’s a true freak!\"","\"Good heavens... I’d do anything for his genes...\" one of the female spectators suddenly muttered, drawing startled stares from those around her.","Yet, no one could truly blame her. After all, who in their right mind would refuse the chance to bear the child of a once-in-a-lifetime genius?","Forget about the females. Even the males there wouldn’t mind if they could give birth.","After taking just a few more steps, Yuan came to a halt once again.","Now, he stood mere steps away from the mountain’s peak. The summit was within sight, yet still just barely out of reach.","While Yuan continued refining his Supreme Sword Aura with steady progress, the Heavenly Son found himself struggling.","Having expended too much energy early on in an attempt to rush through the trial, he was now forced to slow down, and he had only defeated six opponents so far.","As for the other participants, aside from the Holy Sword King and the Holy Sword Maiden, they were hardly worth mentioning. In fact, the spectators had long since lost interest in them, their attention wholly consumed by Yuan and the Heavenly Son.","At the Tian Family, Tian Yuexing’s father, who had been sitting down since the beginning of the Sword Emperor Qualifications, suddenly stood up and left his seat.","\"My lord, where are you going?\" one of the elders asked.","Without turning around, he spoke as he walked toward the exit, \"The Seventh Heaven.\""]},{"number":2047,"title":"Chapter 2047: I Caught Up!","paragraphs":["\"The Seventh Heaven? Is it for that mortal?\" another elder asked, raising an eyebrow.","\"If you’re thinking of recruiting him, we’ve already sent someone,\" another replied. \"The Young Lady is there as well—there’s no need for you to go personally.\"","Tian Yuexing’s father shook his head and sighed.","\"Do any of you even understand what sincerity is? We’re talking about a mortal who not only qualifies as a Sword Emperor, but whose talent points to a future without limits.\"","\"But to send the head of the family so soon... we might come across as desperate,\" someone else remarked.","Once a background or individual reached a certain level of influence and power, there was little left to pursue but reputation. At that point, face became everything—an asset so valuable that countless experts would willingly risk their lives just to preserve it.","\"So what if we lose a little face? If it helps us surpass that arrogant Celestial Family, then it’s a small price to pay!\"","\"Even if you say that...\" one of the elders began, hesitating. \"Wouldn’t it be better to let the Young Lady recruit him instead? That way, not only would a connection be established, but it would deepen far more quickly.\"","\"I agree,\" another elder chimed in. \"The Young Lady isn’t just a top beauty, but she’s also exceptionally persuasive. It would be best to let her handle the recruitment.\"","Tian Yuexing’s father fell silent, deep in thought. After a brief pause, he returned to his seat.","\"Very well,\" he said at last. \"We’ll let Jinhui handle this—for now.\"","He then added, \"Also, you’re all moving too fast. Forming a connection with him is one thing—having him join our family is another matter entirely. No matter how talented he is, I won’t simply hand Jinhui over without first testing him thoroughly. He must prove that he’s truly worthy.\"","\"That’s only natural.\" The others nodded their heads in agreement.","After another month, Tian Yuexing finally defeated his tenth opponent, successfully passing the third trial.","Upon returning to the platform, Tian Yuexing immediately looked up at the rankings. He let out a quiet sigh of relief when he saw that Yuan’s score hadn’t changed. He had managed to narrow the gap.","\"I can do it... I will catch up to him,\" he muttered to himself, determination flashing in his eyes as he turned to face the door to the fourth trial.","He considered resting for a moment since the third trial had taken a serious toll on him, both physically and mentally.","But in the end, he couldn’t bring himself to stop. After all the effort it had taken to close the gap, he couldn’t risk falling behind again.","After taking a deep breath, Tian Yuexing entered the fourth door, beginning his fourth trial.","\"The Heavenly Son has caught up! They’re both in the fourth trial now!\" The spectators exclaimed with excitement.","\"No, the Heavenly Son is still behind the mortal.\"","\"For now, but he’ll definitely catch up. Look at how fast he’s sprinting up the mountain,\" said another spectator.","Once Tian Yuexing understood the objective of the fourth trial, he didn’t hesitate, immediately beginning his ascent with unwavering determination.","While Yuan had taken his time, even pausing to enjoy the scenery along the way, Tian Yuexing advanced with immense focus. His eyes never wavered from the path ahead, and he had no interest in anything but reaching the peak as fast as possible.","Within just a few hours, Tian Yuexing reached the section of the mountain that required Supreme Sword Aura.","By the next day, he had climbed far enough to meet the requirement for passing the trial, and a glowing exit portal appeared before him.","Tian Yuexing paused at the threshold, taking a moment to consider his next move. It was the first time he had truly rested since completing the third trial.","Lifting his gaze toward the mountain peak, he could sense the overwhelming Supreme Sword Aura radiating from above—it was far beyond what he could currently withstand. Reaching the summit was, for now, out of the question.","Accepting this, Tian Yuexing turned toward the portal and prepared to exit the trial.","Moments later, Tian Yuexing stepped back onto the platform. Just like before, the first thing he did was lift his head to check the rankings.","\"I—I did it! I caught up!\" Tian Yuexing exclaimed, eyes wide with satisfaction and triumph.","Clenching his fists, he stood tall with excitement surging through him, as his name now shone at the top of the rankings, just above Yuan’s.","It was the first time Tian Yuexing had ever felt such genuine excitement from being in first place.","Normally, it was something he accepted with calm indifference—an expectation rather than a thrill. But this time was different. This victory felt earned.","Yet, despite Tian Yuexing finally claiming first place, nobody seemed to be paying attention to him. Their eyes were fixed elsewhere, their attention completely consumed by another presence.","A few seconds before Tian Yuexiang completed the fourth trial, Yuan, who had been cultivating in silence this whole time, opened his eyes and slowly stood up.","The instant the spectators saw his aura, a wave of shock swept through the crowd. Their eyes widened, expressions frozen in disbelief.","\"H-He didn’t just reach near-perfection...\" someone gasped. \"This freak actually perfected his Supreme Sword Aura!\"","Yuan only needed to reach near perfection to climb to the mountain’s peak, but he went above and beyond by perfecting his Supreme Sword Aura.","Shrouded in perfected Supreme Sword Aura, a level attained only by true Sword Emperors, Yuan took the final few steps that brought him to the summit of the mountain.","As Yuan returned to the platform, his gaze immediately landed on Tian Yuexing, who stood not far away.","Tian Yuexing’s eyes were fixed on the rankings, and a look of satisfaction lingered on his face, completely unaware that Yuan had returned.","A second later, Yuan watched as Tian Yuexing’s blissful expression twisted with shock and horror.","The ranking had updated, and the position had changed again. Now, Tian Yuexing was once again behind Yuan.","\"What?!\" Tian Yuexing cried out loud, sounding as if a ghost spooked him."]},{"number":2048,"title":"Chapter 2048: Esteemed Guests","paragraphs":["After staring at the rankings for a moment, Tian Yuexing suddenly snapped out of his daze.","His head whipped around—","\"You!\" he exclaimed, eyes locking onto Yuan.","\"What about me?\" Yuan calmly responded.","\"How did you acquire 200 points when I clearly finished the fourth trial first?! You cheated!\" Tian Yuexing questioned, even throwing cheating accusations.","Yuan lifted his head to look at the points, and sure enough, he had 500 points while Tian Yuexing only had 385 points.","He shrugged and replied, \"How am I supposed to know? I didn’t make the rules, nor do I know how it works.\"","Hearing their exchange, Senior Bai stepped forward and said, \"Allow me to explain the scoring system.\"","\"The first person to complete a trial is awarded a full one hundred points, and each person who finishes after that receives five points fewer than the one before.\"","\"In this case, you received a hundred points for finishing first,\" Senior Bai said, glancing at Tian Yuexing.","\"However, the fourth trial is unique in the way that it has two finish lines. While you completed the first, Yuan went above and beyond and managed to reach the peak of the mountain, which is substantially harder, hence the two hundred points.\"","\"He climbed to the peak of the mountain?! That’s impossible!\" Tian Yuexing exclaimed, his voice tinged with disbelief.","He vividly remembers the Supreme Sword Aura radiating from the summit being near perfection. Even with his level of talent, he was still far from reaching that level.","The thought that Yuan’s Supreme Sword Aura was so vastly superior to his own was almost too much for Tian Yuexing to accept.","However, what truly irritated him was the possibility that he might never get to surpass Yuan again and reclaim first place.","There was only one trial left, and he was still 115 points behind. Even if he finished first and earned the full 100 points, he would still fall short—unless, by some miracle, Yuan were to be disqualified during the trial.","As if Senior Bai could read Tian Yuexing’s mind, he suddenly spoke, \"There is still a chance to catch up in the final trial. Though it won’t be easy, it’s possible.\"","\"Is that true?!\" Tian Yuexing trembled with excitement, and his eyes reignited with ambition.","Senior Bai nodded, \"Yes. I can’t give you any details, but it’s definitely possible.\"","Hearing this, Tian Yuexing turned to look at Yuan and said, \"Why don’t we both take a rest and enter the final trial at the same time, a week from now? Unless you’re too afraid of me passing you, that is.\"","Yuan smiled behind his mask and said, \"You don’t need to provoke me. If you want me to slow down for you, just ask.\"","\"T-That’s not it!\" Tian Yuexing blurted out, clearly flustered by Yuan’s words.","Yuan casually took a seat on the platform and said, \"Clearly, the last few trials have worn you out. I’ll give you a week to catch your breath.\"","Tian Yuexing trembled, a burning sensation creeping across his face, as if Yuan’s words had slapped him harder than any hand ever could.","But he held his tongue, afraid that saying anything might make Yuan change his mind and proceed to the final trial immediately.","Though he had managed to get some rest during the fourth trial, the mental strain still weighed heavily on him. He needed the time, whether he admitted it or not.","And so, the two began their rest in preparation for the final trial.","However, while Tian Yuexing focused on restoring every ounce of his strength, Yuan appeared far more relaxed. Though his expression was hidden behind a mask, the audience couldn’t shake the feeling that he wasn’t cultivating at all but just sitting there casually, as if simply waiting for Tian Yuexing to finish.","As the two rested, the audience buzzed with speculation over who would ultimately claim first place.","While many were undeniably impressed by Yuan, the majority still placed their bets on Tian Yuexing. Despite everything that had happened, they believed that the number one genius of the Nine Heavens would not allow himself to be overtaken in the end.","As the days went by, more and more people gathered at the Gates of Heaven, drawn by the growing anticipation surrounding the final trial and the rivalry between Yuan and Tian Yuexing.","On the sixth day of their rest—just one day before the final trial was set to begin—a new commotion stirred within the Gates of Heaven.","But this time, it wasn’t caused by any of the participants.","The source of the commotion was a grand silver carriage, steadily approaching from a distance. Draped in a majestic silver-and-blue flag bearing an unmistakable emblem, it radiated an aura of unquestionable prestige and authority.","Surrounding the carriage was a formidable escort—an entire contingent of God Ascension realm cultivators—moving in perfect formation as it advanced, further emphasizing the significance of its arrival.","The moment the audience caught sight of the emblem, a hush fell over the crowd. Regardless of status or cultivation, everyone rose to their feet and bowed their heads in silent respect, paying wordless tribute to the ones within the carriage.","Noticing the sudden shift in the crowd’s behavior, Yuan turned his gaze toward the approaching carriage. His eyes narrowed at the emblem, a flicker of recognition flashing behind his mask.","When Senior Bai noticed them, he flew off the platform without a word, making his way toward the newcomers to personally welcome them.","The carriage came to a halt moments later, and one of the God Ascension realm cultivators opened the door. From within, two figures emerged, each exuding a presence that immediately commanded the crowd’s attention and awe.","\"Welcome to the Gates of Heaven, esteemed guests from the Celestial Family,\" Senior Bai greeted them respectfully.","The newcomers were none other than members of the Celestial Family—the number one family in the Nine Heavens and the direct bloodline of the Celestial Emperor himself."]},{"number":2049,"title":"Chapter 2049: Celestial Family","paragraphs":["\"It’s been a while, Sect Leader Bai,\" said one of the two figures—a stunning woman clad in pure white robes, her silver accessories shimmering with grace. Her beauty was ethereal, almost otherworldly, resembling that of a celestial fairy descended from the heavens.","\"It has indeed been a while, Madam Jun,\" Senior Bai responded with a respectful nod. \"Had I known of your arrival in advance, I would have prepared a more fitting welcome.\"","\"Don’t sweat about it,\" Madam Jun replied with a gentle smile. \"My daughter and I were simply passing through when I remembered the Sword Emperor Qualifications were underway, so we thought we’d stop by for a quick look. Don’t mind us and act like we’re not even here.\"","Senior Bai nodded and returned to the platform.","\"Who are they?\" Yuan asked Senior Bai, pretending not to know about the Celestial Family.","\"You don’t know—oh, right.\" Senior Bai almost forgot that Yuan was originally from Earth.","\"That is the Celestial Family. They’re the Celestial Emperor’s family,\" he gave a brief explanation.","\"Are they here to watch the Sword Emperor Qualifications?\" Yuan continued to ask.","Senior Bai nodded, \"Yes, they showed up on a whim since they were nearby.\"","\"I see...\" Yuan breathed an inward sigh of relief upon realizing that the Celestial Family hadn’t come because of him. For now, their presence was merely a coincidence and not a confrontation, and he hoped it stayed that way.","While Yuan waited for Tian Yuexing to finish resting, the Celestial Family analyzed the situation.","\"The Heavenly Son, huh? I’d almost forgotten he was participating,\" Madam Jun muttered as her gaze settled on Tian Yuexing.","She spared a brief glance at Yuan, but quickly lost interest—until her eyes shifted to the ranking board.","\"Huh?\" A soft, dumbfounded sound escaped her lips as she noticed something unexpected: Tian Yuexing’s name was not at the top.","\"Yuan?\" the young lady beside her echoed softly, a flicker of curiosity lighting up her eyes as she spoke this name, her voice tinged with intrigue.","No one was more familiar with Tian Yuexing and the Tian Family than the Celestial Family, whose rivalry with them stretched back long before they were ever granted the title of Celestial.","Though they were known as the Celestial Family now—thanks to their connection to the current Celestial Emperor—that hadn’t always been their name.","In truth, the Celestial Family was more of a title than a permanent lineage. Whenever a new Celestial Emperor was chosen, their family would inherit the title, becoming the next Celestial Family for the duration of their reign.","\"Now this is a real surprise,\" Madam Jun chuckled, amusement glinting in her eyes. \"Who would’ve thought that arrogant little prick would end up beneath someone? Just witnessing this made the entire trip worthwhile.\"","However, what puzzled her was the unfamiliar name. If someone more talented than Tian Yuexing existed, there was no way she wouldn’t have heard of him before now.","Madam Jun turned her gaze to the screen displaying the participants’ trials, intent on finding Yuan, unaware that she had been looking directly at him just moments earlier.","When she saw that all of the participants being displayed were doing the same trial, Madam Jun turned to look at the masked figure again, this time with more attention.","\"He’s... a mortal?\" Madam Jun almost couldn’t believe her eyes.","What was a mortal doing in the Sword Emperor Qualifications? Was he Yuan? How did he manage to overtake Tian Yuexing?","Madam Jun had many questions in her mind.","Instead of asking Senior Bai—the quickest and most direct way to learn about Yuan—Madam Jun chose another approach. She turned to one of her guards and gave a quiet command to gather information on him.","After receiving her command, the God Ascension realm cultivator swiftly made his way to the spectator area and began questioning those nearby. The spectators, eager to speak, wasted no time in revealing everything they knew about Yuan, from his feats to the remarkable achievements he had displayed throughout the trials.","As the God Ascension realm cultivator listened to the spectators, he couldn’t help but feel dumbfounded.","The details they provided sounded so exaggerated and unbelievable that it felt more like they were reciting a fantasy story.","However, he knew there was no way the spectators would dare lie so blatantly in front of the Celestial Family.","With that in mind, the God Ascension cultivator returned to Madam Jun shortly after and dutifully recited everything he had learned.","Madam Jun and the young lady beside her listened with wide eyes, their faces full of disbelief and shock.","\"He’s an actual mortal?\" Madam Jun repeated, disbelief flickering in her eyes.","The idea of a mere mortal not only entering the Sword Emperor Qualifications but also outperforming the top genius in the Nine Heavens was something she struggled to comprehend.","Suddenly, Madam Jun retrieved an elegant chair from her spatial ring and placed it behind her, where it hovered effortlessly in midair, as if supported by an invisible platform beneath her.","\"You might want to get comfortable,\" she said to the young lady at her side, a hint of amusement in her voice. \"Looks like we’ll be staying a bit longer than planned.\"","The young lady nodded and also retrieved a chair.","A day later, Senior Bai said, \"Your time for resting is over. Please head to the next trial immediately.\"","Tian Yuexing opened his eyes for the first time in a week, a resolute flame burning within them.","The week of rest had worked wonders. His mind had cleared, and his energy was fully restored. In that moment, he felt unstoppable, as if there was nothing he couldn’t overcome.","Tian Yuexing rose to his feet, his gaze locked onto Yuan.","\"About our bet... I’m changing the terms,\" he said firmly. \"Once I win, I want you to remove that mask.\"","Yuan stood as well, saying nothing, only offering a silent nod of acknowledgment.","Without another word, the two of them turned and approached the final door, ready to begin the last trial of the Sword Emperor Qualifications."]},{"number":2050,"title":"Chapter 2050: Sword Emperor Qualifications’ Final Trial","paragraphs":["Upon stepping through the final door, Yuan found himself standing just a few meters away from a towering pagoda, its vast structure rising endlessly into the heavens, disappearing beyond the clouds as if it pierced the very fabric of the sky.","However, Yuan wasn’t alone. Standing beside him was Tian Yuexing, who had entered just moments earlier.","Tian Yuexing cast a brief glance in Yuan’s direction, then turned away without a word and began making his way toward the pagoda.","Yuan also made his way toward the pagoda shortly after.","Moments later, the two came to a halt before the entrance of the pagoda, where a sign stood prominently beside the doorway.","The sign read:","Welcome to the Endless Pagoda—the final trial of the Sword Emperor Qualifications.","The rules are simple. Reach the 40th floor to pass the trial. The difficulty will increase with each floor. You will earn two points for every floor successfully cleared. Once you start the trial, you will not be able to rest.","After reading the sign, Tian Yuexing silently entered the pagoda, disappearing inside.","\"Two points per floor, huh?\" Yuan muttered as he also entered the pagoda.","Once inside, Yuan found himself standing on a vast, flat surface that stretched endlessly toward the horizon, reminiscent of the training ground at Kelan’s sect.","Shortly after, a black circle manifested on the ground a few dozen meters away from Yuan. From its swirling depths emerged a shadowy figure wielding a sword, its cultivation at the peak of the Immortal Ascension Realm.","Yuan remained motionless, his gaze fixed on the shadowy figure. He chose not to attack, opting instead to let his opponent make the first move to gauge its combat capabilities before taking action.","At the same time, Tian Yuexing immediately began his fight with the shadowy figure that mirrored his cultivation at the 3rd level of God Ascension.","A few exchanges later, Tian Yuexing defeated his opponent and was teleported to the next floor.","Meanwhile, Yuan spent a few minutes playing with his opponent.","Once he was satisfied and understood the opponent’s combat prowess, which was no different from someone without any talents, Yuan defeated the shadowy figure in one strike and teleported to the next floor.","\"How far do you think Yuan will be able to climb?\" Wang Bingbing questioned out loud, and the others began pondering.","\"We’ll have to see how much difficulty each floor adds before we can make any educated guess,\" said Kelan.","\"That makes sense...\"","Thus, they continued watching.","Yuan, who wanted to know the same thing, began testing the second floor’s opponent. Very quickly, he realized that his opponent on the second floor wasn’t much stronger than the first.","And for the next several floors, there was little change in his opponents’ strength. However, upon reaching the 10th floor, everything changed. His opponent’s power surged dramatically, leaping into the Bronze Immortal Realm.","Moreover, his opponent started using Enhanced Sword Aura when they’d only been using ordinary Sword Aura before.","Of course, despite the spike in difficulty, Yuan dispatched his opponent with ease, barely breaking a sweat.","Both he and Tian Yuexing continued ascending the Endless Pagoda at a similar pace, though Tian Yuexing maintained a slight lead. Unlike Yuan, he didn’t waste time gauging his opponents and simply overwhelmed them the moment they showed up.","\"At this pace, he should be able to clear 40 floors without any issues,\" Kelan commented after seeing the change in difficulty on the 10th floor.","\"If his opponent on the 20th floor is a Silver Immortal, then on the 40th floor, he should be fighting True Immortals, which shouldn’t be any issue for him,\" said Wang Ming.","\"But he can defeat even Kelan, who is a God Ascension cultivator. Surely, he’ll be able to climb much higher,\" said Hong Xiuquan.","\"Hah!\" Kelan sneered and said, \"Do you really think I went all out on him? God Ascension cultivators have their powers restricted within the Nine Heavens. I also didn’t use my Celestial Qi during our spar. As talented as he may be, he won’t be able to defeat a God Ascension cultivator at their full strength.\"","Meanwhile, on the tenth floor, Tian Yuexing’s opponent remained at the third level of the God Ascension Realm. However, despite the identical cultivation, the opponent’s strength had grown exponentially. This was due to the immense power gap between levels within the God Ascension Realm.","By the end of the next day, Yuan had already ascended to the 30th floor. At this stage, all of his opponents were Silver Immortals. Meanwhile, Tian Yuexing had only reached the 20th floor, his pace beginning to fall behind as the gap between them gradually widened.","\"Doesn’t Yuan have an immense advantage because of his lower cultivation?\" someone in the crowd suddenly remarked, drawing curious looks from those around them.","\"While their cultivations may differ, that doesn’t mean the one with the lower cultivation has it easier,\" another spectator replied, shaking their head. \"Tell me—how many Immortal Ascension cultivators do you know who can defeat a Bronze Immortal, much less a Silver Immortal?\"","\"Then why does it seem like Yuan is progressing with much more ease?\"","\"Isn’t that simple? He’s more talented than Tian Yuexing, hence why he’s able to advance quicker and with less effort.\"","While there had been uncertainty before the final trial about whether Yuan was truly more talented than Tian Yuexing, that doubt had now vanished.","It was clear as day—Yuan’s potential far surpassed that of Tian Yuexing.","By the time Tian Yuexing reached the 30th floor, Yuan had already soared to the 50th.","Tian Yuexing’s pace had noticeably slowed compared to when he first began, each battle demanding more from him.","Yuan, on the other hand, was still cutting through his opponents with the same effortless ease he’d displayed on the very first floor.","\"Heavens... he’s defeating Golden Immortals like nothing—treating them as if they’re Bronze Immortals...\"","The spectators were left utterly dumbfounded by Yuan’s heaven-defying prowess, and they all wondered how far he’d be able to climb."]},{"number":2051,"title":"Chapter 2051: Sword Emperor Qualifications’ Final Trial(2)","paragraphs":["A week had passed since Yuan entered the Endless Pagoda, and he had already ascended to the 90th floor.","From the 60th floor onward, his opponents were Golden Immortals, and it wasn’t until the 90th floor that he finally faced a True Immortal.","The spectators expected him to struggle against a True Immortal. Yet, to their utter shock and disbelief, Yuan defeated his opponent with ease.","\"How is this possible?! Where is his power coming from?!\"","For many, this was their first time witnessing a mortal defeat an immortal, let alone a True Immortal.","\"Daughter, do you think you could’ve defeated a True Immortal when you were still in the Immortal Ascension Realm?\" Madam Jun asked, her gaze fixed on the display.","The young woman beside her remained silent for a moment before replying, \"I never had the chance to face an Immortal back then, so it’s hard to say. But even if I could’ve won, it wouldn’t have been an easy fight. That’s for sure.\"","\"And yet, this ’nobody’ can defeat True Immortals with ease? I’m truly curious about his background now. I wonder which hidden family he belongs to...\"","Madam Jun narrowed her eyes slightly. In her experience, when prodigies appeared out of nowhere like ghosts, they almost always hail from one of the many hidden families in the Ninth Heaven.","A few days later, Yuan arrived at the 100th floor. However, his opponent was still at True Immortal, albeit much stronger than the one on the 90th floor.","\"Heavens... he’s already on the 100th floor. That’s already twice as much as my earlier prediction...\" Kelan muttered with a dumbfounded expression on his face.","\"The Heavenly Son is only on the 40th floor. That’s quite the difference,\" remarked Wang Ming.","\"So, what were you saying about Yuan only being top 10 amongst the younger generation?\" Chu Liuxiang said, glaring at Kelan.","Kelan awkwardly cleared his throat before responding, \"Fine, I underestimated him a little, but can you really blame me? I’ve known the others for far longer than I’ve known Yuan, and while he’s definitely impressive, he doesn’t have any achievements.\"","At the Holy Sword Clan’s area, the Sixth Elder spoke, \"We have to recruit him into our faction no matter the cost. He’s too talented for us to ignore.\"","The silver-haired Sword Emperor sighed, \"Do you have any idea how many others are thinking the same thing? It’s not going to be an easy fight. In fact, it might become a bloodbath.\"","\"We have the upper hand because we already have a connection with him,\" said Sword Empress Huang.","As the days passed, more and more people gathered at the Gates of Heaven to witness Yuan’s relentless ascent through the Endless Pagoda—many of them hoping to recruit him once it was over.","By the end of the second week, Yuan had already reached the 199th floor, while Tian Yuexing lagged far behind on the 50th—only a quarter of Yuan’s progress.","\"Is the Endless Pagoda truly endless? Surely, there must be an end, like the mountain from the last trial,\" someone wondered out loud.","\"The Endless Pagoda is clearly inspired by the Heaven’s Thousand Trials. If it’s like the real thing, there should be 1,000 floors in total.\"","\"A thousand floors...? I doubt it. There would be no point since nobody would be able to finish it.\"","\"Right? The Endless Pagoda is clearly more difficult than Heaven’s Thousand Trials, which has existed for millions of years and has been challenged by countless cultivators. Yet the record is only 600 floors.\"","\"Hm? Look! He’s reached the 200th floor—and something’s different!\" one of the spectators suddenly exclaimed.","At once, all eyes turned to Yuan’s screen.","Sure enough, the 200th floor stood apart from the rest.","Yuan’s opponent was no longer a vague, shadowy figure but a masked man. At first glance, he looked oddly familiar, and then the realization struck the crowd like thunder.","\"It’s the Faceless Sword Emperor!\"","When Yuan saw the Faceless Sword Emperor, he smiled faintly and muttered, \"So this place isn’t endless after all.\"","Not only was his final opponent the legendary Faceless Sword Emperor himself, but his cultivation had also reached the first level of God Ascension.","\"Asking a mortal to fight a god... this is too much.\" Yuan shook his head.","Moments after his appearance, the Faceless Sword Emperor lunged at Yuan, a silver sword flashing in his grasp.","Yuan didn’t dare to underestimate his opponent and fought with caution.","When their swords clashed, Yuan was pushed back for the first time since he began the trial. Though both wielded perfected Supreme Sword Aura, the Faceless Sword Emperor’s higher cultivation gave him the upper hand, just enough to overpower Yuan slightly.","Despite losing the first exchange, Yuan remained calm and struck back without hesitation.","Yet with each clash, he was steadily pushed back, narrowly losing to the Faceless Sword Emperor time and again.","Seeing this, the audience began to believe that Yuan stood no chance against the Faceless Sword Emperor—that it was only a matter of time before he was defeated.","Of course, Yuan didn’t think he’d lose. If anything, he was pretty confident that he’d be able to win.","\"So you can’t use Celestial Qi, huh? In that case, you stand no chance.\"","Realizing that the Faceless Sword Emperor couldn’t use Celestial Qi, Yuan felt no fear. He continued the battle calmly, gradually increasing his strength over time.","Before long, Yuan was no longer the one being pushed back, and he was the one driving the Faceless Sword Emperor backward.","\"What?! How is he still getting stronger?!\"","Shock rippled through the crowd as Yuan reversed the momentum in an instant, leaving everyone speechless.","Of course, it didn’t take long for them to realize that Yuan had never been fighting at full strength. No... even now, they couldn’t be certain he was using everything he had.","Two days and tens of thousands of exchanges later, Yuan defeated the Faceless Sword Emperor, clearing the 200th floor."]},{"number":2052,"title":"Chapter 2052: Acquiring the Title of Sword Emperor","paragraphs":["Chapter 2052: Acquiring the Title of Sword Emperor","“That freak has actually done it... He’s passed the Sword Emperor Qualifications with a perfect score, and as a mortal, no less!”","The audience wasn’t just left in awe of Yuan’s feat. They felt a tinge of fear as well.","After all, there was nothing more terrifying than the unknown, and Yuan was the embodiment of that right now. From his identity to his true potential, nobody there knew anything about him.","Once it became clear that Yuan had conquered the final trial, the atmosphere at the Gates of Heaven shifted dramatically. Every recruiter present was poised to approach him the instant he emerged.","However, Senior Bai suddenly spoke, “Please refrain from approaching the participants until after the ceremony.”","At his words, those who had already begun inching toward the platform froze in place.","Defying Senior Bai’s warning wouldn’t just be disrespectful—it would make them look bad in front of the countless spectators, and worse, in the eyes of the very person they hoped to recruit.","Thus, these recruiters had no choice but to hold back their desire for now.","Moments after clearing the final trial, Yuan stepped through the portal and returned to the platform.","Under normal circumstances, such a feat would be met with thunderous applause, but this time, not a single voice was raised. The crowd was silent.","“Congratulations on completing the Sword Emperor Qualifications. You are now officially recognized as a Sword Emperor,” Senior Bai announced as he approached Yuan.","He then retrieved a beautifully crafted, sword-shaped badge, forged from a crystal that shimmered like a diamond, yet gleamed with a deep emerald hue.","“This is proof that you’re a Sword Emperor.”","He handed the badge to Yuan, who calmly accepted it.","Senior Bai continued, “Traditionally, those who earn the title of Sword Emperor are given the right to choose their own epithet. Have you decided on one yet?”","Yuan shook his head.","“That’s fine,” Senior Bai said with a slight nod. “You can reveal it whenever you’re ready.”","Of course, regardless of what name Yuan would eventually choose, the people had already given him one of their own—the Freak Sword Emperor.","“Then, do you have any words for everyone watching? A lot of them will try to recruit you after this.”","Yuan paused in thought for a moment before speaking, “There is one thing I’d like to say.”","At those words, every eye locked onto him, like hawks fixing their gaze on prey.","“I’ve heard that many of you wish to recruit me. I’m honored, but I simply don’t have the time to meet with everyone individually. So, if you’re serious about recruiting me, please direct your intentions to Celestial Overlord Qiang of the Celestial Overlords.”","A stunned silence followed. Not just the crowd, but even Senior Bai wore a dumbfounded expression.","‘He’s going to use Celestial Overlord Qiang as a scapegoat?!’ Senior Bai cried inwardly.","A few members of the Celestial Overlords were watching, and none of them had expected Yuan to already be part of their faction. While they were pleasantly surprised, they were also curious about how Celestial Overlord Qiang managed to find him.","The recruiters exchanged perplexed glances. Now that Yuan had revealed his affiliation with the Celestial Overlords and even invoked Celestial Overlord Qiang by name, they couldn’t approach him directly without speaking to her first, even if it’s just to let her know their intentions, as doing so could be seen as disrespect.","However, one individual clearly couldn’t care less about propriety and began approaching Yuan without hesitation. The moment the others saw who it was, a wave of tension swept through them, causing them to swallow nervously.","And of all people, it was the one Yuan least wanted to deal with—Madam Jun.","The moment he saw her approaching, a subtle frown formed on his face. Of all the recruiters present, she was the one he had hoped would stay far away.","Madam Jun landed gracefully on the platform, stopping just a few meters from Yuan.","Before he could say a word, she offered a warm smile and said, “Don’t worry, I’m not here to recruit you.”","“Then you must be here to invite me for tea,” he calmly replied.","A deafening silence fell over the crowd as they were left in disbelief by Yuan’s casual response to someone of her stature.","However, instead of being offended, the smile on Madam Jun’s face widened, and she spoke, “If that’s what you want.”","“Maybe another time. I have a lot of things to do right now.”","“I don’t doubt it.” Madam Jun suddenly retrieved a silver medallion and casually tossed it at Yuan, who instinctively caught it.","“Whenever you do have time for tea, come find me with that medallion.”","After saying that, she turned to look at Senior Bai and said, “This year’s Sword Emperor Qualifications was quite entertaining.”","Without saying another word, Madam Jun turned around and returned to her carriage. Moments later, she entered it with her daughter and left the Gates of Heaven.","‘That’s it...?’ Yuan wore a stunned look behind his mask, as he was expecting the worst.","Once the Celestial Family had departed, Senior Bai sent a voice transmission to Yuan, “I understand you may not have the best relationship with the Celestial Emperor, but Madam Jun is a righteous individual. Try not to antagonize her so hastily.”","“In truth, the Celestial Family has had little to do with the Celestial Emperor ever since he attained that title. They’re forbidden from direct involvement to prevent one family from becoming too powerful.”","Yuan was quite surprised to hear this, “Is this how it works now?”","Senior Bai nodded and elaborated, “While it’s inevitable that the Celestial Family holds some influence due to their connection to the Celestial Emperor, they’re strictly prohibited from using his name for personal gain—be it in politics, business, or otherwise. As for the Celestial Emperor, he is also not allowed to use his family while bearing that title.”","“That’s good to know. Thank you,” Yuan said."]},{"number":2053,"title":"Chapter 2053: Sword Emperor Yuan","paragraphs":["Chapter 2053: Sword Emperor Yuan","Sometime later, Senior Bai said to Yuan out loud, “Normally, we’d have a ceremony for the new Sword Emperors, but as you can see, the other participants are still nowhere near done, so we’ll have to postpone it until every participant is finished.”","“Do I have to participate in this ceremony?” Yuan asked with raised eyebrows, as it sounded like a hassle.","“While we can’t force you, it should be noted that every Sword Emperor before you has participated in the ceremony,” said Senior Bai.","“I’ll think about it,” Yuan said.","Senior Bai then retrieved the Mystic Sword Tablet and handed it to him.","“This is your reward for ranking first place. Once again, congratulations, Sword Emperor Yuan.”","Since Yuan had completed the final trial with a perfect score, Tian Yuexing was guaranteed to take second place, regardless of whether he managed to clear all 200 floors or not.","“Thank you.” Yuan tossed the Mystic Sword Tablet into his spatial ring without even looking at it.","But before he could do anything else, another figure stepped forward.","“I’m allowed to approach you as long as I’m not trying to recruit you, right?” the man asked with a faint smile.","Yuan turned to face him and said calmly, “If you’re here to ask about the Mystic Sword Tablet, I don’t have time for that right now. That said, I don’t intend to keep it for myself forever. Once I’ve finished studying it, I’ll make sure everyone has a chance to examine it as well.”","Hearing this, the man’s smile widened, and a wave of relief spread through the crowd.","Many of the swordmasters had been silently wondering the same thing ever since the tablet appeared.","“Then I won’t bother you any longer.”","Satisfied with Yuan’s response, the man turned around and flew away.","“Where are you going to go now?” Senior Bai asked Yuan shortly after.","He responded through voice transmission, “I’ll stay in the Myriad of Techniques for a while first. Can you let the others know for me?”","“Sure.”","“Thank you.”","Yuan activated Shadow Veil the next moment, and before anyone could react, he vanished like a ghost beneath their very eyes.","“Where did he go?!” someone in the audience exclaimed, eyes darting around in confusion.","Several individuals had planned to follow Yuan the moment he left, but he didn’t even give them the chance.","After leaving the platform, Yuan entered the Myriad of Techniques and waited for the others to arrive.","Meanwhile, Senior Bai relayed Yuan’s location to Kelan.","“Do you guys want to continue watching?” Kelan asked the others.","“What’s the point?”","They all shook their heads.","“Then let’s go see him,” Kelan said as he stood up.","Thus, they quietly left to meet Yuan.","Some time later, they arrived at the Myriad of Techniques.","“Congratulations on your new title, Sword Emperor Yuan.”","They congratulated him the moment they met.","“What did you think of the Sword Emperor Qualifications? Was it as easy as you made it look?” Wang Ming asked.","Yuan chuckled and said, “While it wasn’t easy, it definitely wasn’t as difficult as I was expecting. I had more trouble training at the Holy Sword Temple, if I have to be honest.”","“As expected from the Freak Sword Emperor,” Shi Lang spoke in a teasing voice.","“Freak Sword Emperor?” Yuan raised his eyebrows at this unfamiliar nickname.","“That’s what the others are calling you,” explained Li Jinxi.","“Because you’re a freak,” Wang Bingbing elaborated.","After chatting for a bit, Yuan said, “Can one of you let Yu Rou know that I have returned so that we can spend some time together before I leave again?”","“I can do that, but where will you be going next?” Meixiu asked.","With a serious look on his face, he spoke, “The Primordial Realm.”","“The Primordial Realm? Isn’t that where Xiao Hua is from?”","He nodded and continued, “She hasn’t woken up once in several years. I’m worried about her.”","“W-Wait a second. The Primordial Realm? What are you talking about? That’s not a place you can enter whenever you want,” Kelan said after hearing Yuan’s plans.","“I am aware,” said Yuan, and he proceeded to explain Xiao Hua’s situation to him.","“I understand your situation, but not only does the Primordial Realm house some of the most dangerous criminals within the Nine Heavens, you’ll definitely become a wanted criminal if you try to enter without the Celestial Emperor’s permission,” Kelan said afterward.","“Permission from the Celestial Emperor? That’s definitely not possible. Regardless, I am already targeted by him, so it won’t make any difference.”","“It makes a huge difference! If you do something that reckless, not even Celestial Overlord Xu can protect you!” Kelan exclaimed with a deep frown on his face.","“In any case, don’t even think about approaching the Primordial Realm because I’ll stop you with everything I’ve got!” Kelan declared firmly.","Yuan didn’t blame him. He understood that Kelan was only trying to protect him. Unfortunately, he was fated to enter the Primordial Realm.","“Fine, I’ll give up on the Primordial Realm—for now,” Yuan said, raising his hands in a gesture of surrender.","“Good. As for your Exile friend, I’ll find an expert to treat her,” Kelan replied, his tone softening.","Yuan nodded calmly.","But in truth, he had no intention of giving up.","No matter what he said on the surface, his resolve remained unchanged.","A few days later, Yu Rou visited the Myriad of Techniques, and the two of them started catching up with each other.","Meanwhile, the Demon Sealing Faction members returned to the Super Perfect Physique Tempering Sect with Kelan to continue their training.","Time flew by, and in the blink of an eye, two months had passed since Yuan earned the title of Sword Emperor.","The Sword Emperor Qualifications were still underway, with every participant—except for the Heavenly Son—still struggling to clear the second trial.","As for Tian Yuexing, he had managed to push his way up to the 84th floor of the Endless Pagoda. Though it was taking him longer and longer to clear each floor, it was clear to the spectators that he wasn’t close to his limit, and they wondered how long it would take him to finish."]},{"number":2054,"title":"Chapter 2054: God of War, Tian Xian(End of Leaving Earth Arc)","paragraphs":["\"Brother, is it strange that even though it’s been years since we last saw each other, it didn’t feel nearly as long as the last time?\" Yu Rou asked aloud.","Yuan smiled gently and responded, \"That’s because as your cultivation deepens, your sense of time changes. The more accustomed you become to it, the less you notice time passing.\"","\"I see... I don’t know if that’s a good or bad thing.\"","\"It can be both.\"","\"You’ll be leaving again soon, right?\" Yu Rou asked, the expression on her face turning sour.","He nodded, \"Yes, I’m going to the Primordial Realm to see if Xiao Hua’s family can cure her.\"","\"Xiao Hua... I miss her,\" Yu Rou sighed.","\"Me too.\"","\"Since this is for Xiao Hua, I won’t say much. Just be safe, okay?\"","\"I won’t go unprepared. I promise.\"","After spending two months together, Yu Rou left the Myriad of Techniques to resume her journey while Yuan prepared for the Primordial Realm.","However, he was still missing two of the four Ancient Seals required to open the Primordial Realm. While he could force his way inside the Primordial Realm, that would cause too much of a commotion, and he’d attract the Celestial Emperor’s attention, something he wished to avoid at all costs.","Fortunately, the Evil God’s Shadow Army had been investigating the last two Ancient Seal holders.","After leaving the Myriad of Techniques, Yuan went to find Xi Meili, who was given a method to contact the Evil God’s Shadow Army by Dong Ye.","\"Dong Ye told you how to contact the Shadow Army, right?\" Yuan asked for confirmation after interrupting her cultivation.","\"Yes. Are you going to contact them now?\" Xi Meili asked.","He nodded.","Xi Meili then retrieved a jade slip and a purple token from her spatial ring and handed it to Yuan, saying, \"Dong Ye said the instructions are inside.\"","\"Like usual, I’ll leave Liya in your hands,\" Yuan then said.","Xi Meili responded with a smile, \"Don’t worry about us. We’re practically like sisters now.\"","After bringing Liya to the Nine Heavens, he asked her what she wanted to do. Unsurprisingly, she said that she wanted to become stronger, as she was bottlenecked on Earth by its lack of spiritual energy. Thus, she started training with Xi Meili, who was a fellow dragon.","Of course, Yuan hadn’t forgotten about the Lord’s request, and he still planned on bringing her to the Red Heaven Dragon Clan.","Some time later, Yuan went to say goodbye to Meixiu and the others. He also left them some spirit stones for their future journey outside the sect.","\"Until next time, everyone.\"","Before leaving, Yuan created a new identity and disguised himself.","Then, he left Kelan’s sect through the teleportation device.","After a few days and several teleportations, Yuan arrived at a renowned commercial hub known as Red Dusk City. However, most of the businesses in this city revolved around information brokerage. It was a place people went to seek answers.","Upon entering the city, the first thing Yuan noticed was the abundance of tent-like structures lining the streets, each exuding a shady atmosphere.","Despite their shady appearance, the tents saw a steady stream of people entering and leaving. Most of them wore masks, clearly intent on concealing their identities.","Yuan wasn’t wearing a mask at the moment, but that was only because he was already in disguise. Following the instructions inscribed in the jade slip Xi Meili had given him, he soon arrived before a large building known as Dusk Intelligence.","Dusk Intelligence was a well-established information market that had existed for tens of thousands of years. Not only do they have a stellar reputation with many branches throughout the Nine Heavens, but they were also ranked among the top businesses in Red Dusk City.","Of course, in truth, it was operated by the Evil God’s Shadow Army, serving as a front to gather intelligence from all corners of the world.","When Yuan entered the building, he was greeted by a young man.","\"Hello, are you here to buy or sell information?\"","\"I’m here to buy information.\"","\"I understand. Please head to the waiting room over there and wait for your number to be called.\" The young man handed Yuan a small wooden token before pointing toward a large waiting area where hundreds of people could be seen sitting around.","Yuan then said, \"Actually, I already have a reservation.\"","\"In that case, may I have your name?\"","Yuan responded through Voice Transmission, \"God of War, Tian Xian.\"","The young man’s face immediately froze. Then, after taking a moment to comprehend what he’d just heard, his eyes widened with shock and disbelief.","\"P-P-Please follow me, Esteemed Guest!\" The young man stuttered, his entire body trembling uncontrollably.","Minutes later, after Yuan followed the young man into a private room and the door closed softly behind them, the young man hesitantly asked, \"E-Esteemed Guest... may I be so bold as to request proof of your reservation?\"","Yuan silently retrieved the purple token and showed it to the young man.","The moment his eyes fell upon the purple token, the young man dropped to his knees, his voice filled with reverence and awe as he said, \"This lowly servant greets the God of War.\"","\"Were you expecting my presence?\" Yuan asked.","\"Yes.\"","\"Then do you know why I am here?\"","\"I do not, but our leader should. May I notify him of your presence?\"","\"Go ahead.\"","\"Please allow me to prepare you some tea before I—\"","\"No need. Just get your leader.\"","\"As you command.\"","The young man didn’t dare to waste another second and immediately left to find the leader of the Dusk Intelligence.","Not even a minute later, Yuan heard a gentle knock on the door.","\"Come inside.\"","The door opened at Yuan’s command, and a middle-aged man hurriedly entered the room.","\"This lowly servant is honored to stand in the presence of the God of War,\" the man said as he kowtowed deeply before Yuan."]},{"number":2055,"title":"Chapter 2055: Location of the Remaining Two Ancient Seals","paragraphs":["\"Stand up. There’s no need to be so formal. Just tell me what I need to know, and I’ll quickly be on my way,\" Yuan said to the man kowtowing on the floor.","The man nodded and stood up before asking, \"What do you wish to know, God of War? All of our intel is at your disposal.\"","\"I’d like to know where the Ancient Seals to unlock the Primordial Realm are right now,\" Yuan said.","\"The Ancient Seals, huh... We’ll have to look at our records, but I’m sure we already have this information since the Commander asked us to look into it several years ago.\"","\"How long will it take?\"","\"It shouldn’t take long. A few hours at most.\"","\"Alright. I’ll wait here then.\"","\"Would you like some tea while you wait?\"","Yuan shook his head.","\"As you wish. Please excuse me while I retrieve the information now.\"","The man bowed to Yuan again before leaving the room to look for the information he requested.","While he waited, Yuan retrieved the Mystic Sword Tablet to study it. Now that he’d perfected Supreme Sword Aura, he only had two things he needed to do—fuse it with his body and attain the Supreme Sword Body and achieve a realm even higher than Supreme Sword Aura.","A few hours later, the leader of the Dusk Intelligence returned to the room with two scrolls in his grasp.","\"This is the information you requested, God of War.\" The leader said as he offered it to Yuan as if he were giving an offering to a god.","\"Thank you.\"","Yuan accepted the scrolls and immediately opened them to read.","Moments later, he rubbed his eyes and sighed.","\"A-Are the information not satisfactory...?\" The leader swallowed nervously after seeing Yuan’s reaction.","\"Hm? No, that’s not it. I was just thinking that this will become a bit pain in the ass,\" said Yuan as he waved the scrolls in the air.","\"Is that so...\"","\"Anyway, I’d like to request more information, specifically about the two families listed here,\" he continued.","\"As you command. I will be right back.\" The leader bowed before leaving again.","Once he was alone again, Yuan looked at the scrolls and mumbled, \"The Rising Phoenix Clan and the Heavenly White Tiger Clan, huh?\"","He was already familiar with one of these names, the Heavenly White Tiger Clan. Not only was their Ancestor one of the Nine Divine Supremes, but he had some run-ins with their current young generation.","\"Young Master, I know the Rising Phoenix Clan,\" Feng Yuxiang’s voice suddenly resounded, snapping him out of his thoughts.","\"Oh?\"","Feng Yuxiang emerged from his Dantian to continue, \"In fact, I was staying with the Rising Phoenix Clan before I was cursed and was chased to the Lower Heaven.\"","\"So you have quite the relationship with them, huh?\"","Feng Yuxiang nodded and said, \"Most phoenixes today are born from other phoenixes, but I am one of the rare few naturally born directly from the flames themselves. I spent most of my earlier days wandering the Nine Heavens alone, but when I met the Rising Phoenix Clan, they offered me a place to stay, and wanting to experience what it was like living with other phoenixes, I accepted it.\"","She continued, \"Honestly, it was a pain. Everything seemed normal at first, but they eventually started trying to rope me into their clan by pushing their sons on me. That’s when I left and returned to wandering the Nine Heavens.\"","\"Oh, right. They’re also among the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans, ranked fifth.\"","Yuan continued asking questions about the Rising Phoenix Clan until the leader returned with a tray holding several spatial rings.","\"Here is all the information we have on the Rising Phoenix Clan and the Heavenly White Tiger Clan.\"","Yuan stared at the spatial rings and asked in a somewhat nervous voice, \"How many scrolls are inside?\"","\"One thousand three hundred and fifty-two scrolls in total.\" The leader responded without any pause.","Yuan was speechless. He only anticipated a few scrolls—a few dozen at most.","\"T-Thank you... I will read them later.\" Yuan said, even though he had no intention of reading all of them, as there was simply too much.","\"Will you be leaving now?\" The leader then asked.","\"I’ll leave in a bit.\"","The leader then retrieved a black medallion and offered it to him, \"Please accept this. As long as you have this token, we, the Shadow Army, recognize your identity no matter where you are.\"","After accepting the medallion, Yuan spent a few more hours in the room to read a few scrolls of each clan and to ponder which of the two places he should visit first.","However, when he realized that both the Rising Phoenix Clan and the Heavenly White Tiger Clan existed in the Eighth Heaven, Yuan decided to visit the Stairway to Heaven first. Now that he had gotten rid of the Celestial Emperor’s curse and his presence was known, he no longer had any reason not to use it.","After leaving Dusk Intelligence, Yuan made his way to the teleportation device and teleported to the city nearest to the Stairway to Heaven.","A few days later, he arrived at his destination.","When he arrived, he was surprised to see many people at the Stairway to Heaven, counting hundreds at a glance.","Yuan wondered if there was a special occasion, but in reality, this is just a typical day at the Stairway to Heaven in the Seventh Heaven.","Unlike the lower heavens, there were simply many more incentives for cultivators in the Seventh Heaven to want to ascend. Moreover, it was much easier to ascend to the Eighth and Ninth Heaven, which the Celestial Emperor himself purposefully set.","After acquiring a token with a number, Yuan patiently waited for his turn.","A few days later, Yuan approached the Stairway to Heaven and entered it.","\"Welcome back, Master.\" Tian’er greeted him inside.","\"It’s been a while.\"","\"Are you here to take the trial?\"","He nodded and said, \"Yes, and I’ll take the trial for the Seventh Heaven while I am at it.\""]},{"number":2056,"title":"Chapter 2056: Returning to the Stairway to Heaven","paragraphs":["\"The trial for the Seventh Heaven and the Eighth Heaven, correct? We can do that.\" Tian’er nodded.","\"Would you like to start now?\"","\"Let’s.\"","Shortly later, Yuan began his trial, which was supposed to be meant for the Seventh Heaven.","When the trial began, Yuan found himself in an unusual location. He was not in the wilderness or a city. Instead, he was surrounded by the void with countless stars flickering in the distance.","He was outside the Nine Heavens in the Starry Sky.","<You have started your trial in the Stairway to Heaven>","<You are currently being hunted by cultivators all around the Nine Heavens>","<You must survive for one year to pass the trial>","<Defeat all of your enemies within a year to receive a reward>","\"I have to survive for a whole year?\" Yuan raised his eyebrows after seeing the trial.","The very next moment, before he could even start to ponder, Yuan sensed hundreds of powerful presences appearing behind him.","When he turned around, he could see an army of people chasing after him. However, most of their cultivation was between Bronze Immortal and Silver Immortal, with a few Golden Immortals.","Seeing this, the thought of escaping didn’t even cross Yuan’s mind. Wielding Number One Under Heaven in his grasp, he charged at the incoming army of cultivators with a calm smile on his face, looking like he was going on a stroll in the park.","However, Yuan didn’t just fight normally. He fought while training at the same time, fusing his Supreme Sword Aura with his body and slowly inching toward attaining the Supreme Sword Body.","After slaying all of the cultivators, Yuan was given two hours of rest before another wave of enemies appeared, their numbers increased compared to the first wave.","This reminded Yuan of the Sword Emperor Qualifications, which tested his endurance and ability to overcome a large number of enemies at once.","Meanwhile, as Yuan remained inside the Stairway to Heaven, Meixiu and the others prepared to leave Kelan’s sect to gain experience outside.","Although Kelan wanted to follow them, he had other responsibilities as the Sect Leader, and he’d already pushed back some just training them. Of course, he wasn’t going to let them travel alone, and for their safety, had several experts watch them from a distance.","These experts were not allowed to intervene with their training unless their lives were in danger.","Also, since their group was a little big, they decided to split up into smaller groups.","For the first group, Meixiu, Chu Liuxiang, and Li Jinxi were together.","For the second group, it was Wang Ming, Wang Bingbing, and Xi Murong.","The third group had Shi Lang, Wu Zao, and Hong Xiuquan.","The fourth and final group consisted of Xi Meili, Liya, and Wang Xiuying.","After splitting into four smaller groups, they wandered the Seventh Heaven separately, experiencing their own journeys.","Four months later, at the Gates of Heaven, the Holy Sword Maiden finally finished her second trial and returned to the platform.","When she looked at the ranking, her eyes widened with shock.","\"900 points?! What did he do to acquire so many points?!\" The Holy Sword Maiden muttered in a dumbfounded voice, completely unaware that Yuan had long passed the Sword Emperor Qualifications and earned his title as Sword Emperor.","After realizing that she had no chance of catching up, the Holy Sword Maiden didn’t immediately rush to the third trial. Instead, she sat down and used what little time she had to rest.","Seven days later, just as the Holy Sword Maiden entered the third trial, the Holy Sword King finished his trial and returned to the platform.","He was just as bewildered as the Holy Sword Maiden when he saw the ranking, but he also felt much more irritated.","’Is the difference between us this vast...? Just who the hell did I challenge?’ The Holy Sword King felt embarrassed just recalling how he’d challenged Yuan.","Instead of resting like the Holy Sword Maiden, the Holy Sword King immediately went into the third trial.","As for the Heavenly Son, he’d managed to pass the 110th floor of the Endless Pagoda. While he was still climbing, the time it took to pass each floor increased with every floor.","After another four months, Yuan completed his trial after defeating over 100,000 Immortals.","<You have successfully defeated all enemies before the time limit>","A glowing orb of light appeared before him.","After consuming the orb, Yuan recalled more memories of his past lives.","\"Congratulations on passing the trial for the Seventh Heaven,\" said Tian’er.","\"Hm? That was it?\"","Tian’er nodded and said, \"Master, you’ve already reached the point where the trials won’t be much of a challenge. It’d only be a waste of time to give you more.\"","\"Is that so? Then let’s start the trial for the Eighth Heaven,\" said Yuan.","Moments later, the scenery shifted as Yuan began his trial for the Eighth Heaven.","\"This place...\"","The landscape, the structure—it all felt strikingly familiar. Yuan’s gaze settled on the towering mountain ahead, its spiraling path coiling upward like a serpent. It was none other than Dragon Spiral Mountain.","<You have started your first trial>","<Defeat your opponent to pass the trial>","<Defeat your opponent within ten years to receive a reward>","\"Ten years to defeat my opponent?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at this seemingly generous amount of time.","However, in the very next moment, Yuan sensed an unfathomable pressure descend upon Dragon Spiral Mountain, causing the air around him to tremble.","When he looked up, he saw a half-naked, strikingly handsome man hovering above Dragon Spiral Mountain, his long golden hair flowing behind him like a river of light.","\"The Great One...\" Yuan mumbled, recognizing this man almost instantly.","\"Immortal Monarch!\" the Great One suddenly declared, his voice thundering like a lightning strike. \"I have come to defeat you and to claim Dragon Goddess Yeyou! A human like you is not worthy of her!\""]},{"number":2057,"title":"Chapter 2057: Fighting the Great One","paragraphs":["Shortly after his appearance, the Great One unleashed his cultivation, which was at the first level of God Ascension realm.","\"I’m at a point where the trials won’t be much of a challenge, huh?\" Yuan repeated what Tian’er had said in a low voice and a stiff smile.","Although the Great One was only at the first level of God Ascension, he might be the toughest opponent Yuan has encountered up until now.","The Great One was not just a Divine Beast—he was a Dragon of Origin, one of the most ancient dragons to ever exist. His existence traced back to the Primordial Era, and in terms of experience, he rivaled Yuan, perhaps even surpassed him.","Yuan didn’t bother responding to the Great One and immediately prepared for combat.","Seeing this, the Great One charged at Yuan, his body enveloped in a golden aura.","Yuan didn’t dare to underestimate the Great One and fought seriously from the get-go.","Seconds later, the two clashed, unleashing a powerful shockwave that swept across the area, sending violent ripples surging across the waters surrounding Dragon Spiral Mountain.","For the first several days, the two fought using only their physical bodies. Despite possessing the Golden Immortal Physique, Yuan found himself merely on par with the Great One.","While the Golden Immortal Physique was considered the best physique in the Nine Heavens, that was only in human standards.","That said, matching the Great One in physical combat—one of the mightiest beings in the Nine Heavens—was an achievement worthy of pride.","\"You’re an eyesore!\" the Great One suddenly roared. \"If not for you, Yeyou would already be mine!\"","His aura surged violently, growing stronger with each passing moment, shaking the very air around him.","Hearing this, Yuan responded with a calm smile, \"Is that really the case? From what I’ve heard, you’re nothing more than an obsessive stalker in her eyes. Even if I never existed, you never had a chance.\"","\"Shut up! What do you know about our relationship?! You’re just an outsider! A mere human!\"","\"If I am just a mere human, then why are you so upset? So scared of my presence? Aren’t we like ants in your eyes?\"","\"Scared? You think I’m scared of you?!\" the Great One bellowed with laughter, as though he’d just heard the most absurd joke in the world.","\"Allow me to show the insurmountable difference between us! Golden Scale Armor!\"","A semi-transparent armor shimmering with a golden glow materialized around the Great One, exuding a majestic and overwhelming pressure.","In an instant, the Great One’s power surged to new heights. When they clashed again moments later, he effortlessly overwhelmed Yuan.","Like an unstoppable force, the Great One drove Yuan back hundreds of meters with every clash.","In response, Yuan activated the God of War’s Astral Arts, cloaking himself in its celestial avatar as though donning a suit of divine armor. Though it helped him close the gap between their strength, it was still not enough.","\"Do you understand it now? The difference between me and your inferior existence?!\" The Great One laughed out loud as he continued his relentless assault.","Yuan smiled at the Great One’s provocation and said, \"You put on this act of strength, but deep down, it’s just a mask to hide how fragile you really are. You hoard treasures not out of desire, but to fill the void left by the one treasure you’ll never obtain.\"","The moment the Great One heard those words, his movements faltered. Then, his aura erupted with renewed fury, surging to even greater heights as his expression twisted with rage.","\"How dare you mock me?!\" he roared.","From that moment on, the Great One ceased speaking, focusing entirely on the battle, and Yuan did the same. With each passing exchange, their strength and intensity steadily escalated, shaking the heavens with their clash.","Time passed in the blink of an eye, and it’s been a whole year since Yuan started fighting the Great One in the Stairway to Heaven.","The Sword Emperor Qualifications were still ongoing, and all of the participants—at least the ones that still remained—had passed the second trial and had begun their third trial. The Holy Sword Maiden and the Holy Sword King also finished their third trial and had begun their fourth trial.","As for the Heavenly Son, he was still climbing the Endless Pagoda, now on the 145th floor.","After another year, the Heavenly Son reached the 170th floor.","\"Do you think the Heavenly Son will be able to clear the Endless Pagoda?\" The audience asked each other.","\"Most likely. While he wasn’t able to clear it as fast as the Freak Sword Emperor, he has the capabilities to clear it.\"","The audience has already begun calling Yuan the Freak Sword Emperor.","The Holy Sword Maiden and the Holy Sword King also started climbing the Endless Pagoda a few months ago, as the fourth trial was the quickest to clear.","It wasn’t until they entered the final trial that these two realized Yuan had actually already completed the Sword Emperor Qualifications and had become a Sword Emperor, which left him utterly dumbfounded.","\"He became a Sword Emperor even before I completed the second trial...?\" The Holy Sword Maiden muttered in a daze. \"I know he’s talented, but this is just too much...\"","The Holy Sword King could only stare at the Endless Pagoda with a blank expression on his face, his thoughts unknown. However, the audience could tell that he was devastated, looking like someone experiencing an existential crisis.","Seeing this, the audience wondered if the Holy Sword King would give up there. Many believed that even if he continued, he was not in the right state of mind and might fail because of it.","Eventually, the Holy Sword King entered the Endless Pagoda and began his climb.","Then, after another two years, the Heavenly Son finally arrived at the 200th floor and began his final challenge with the Faceless Sword Emperor.","As for Yuan, his battle with the Great One raged on with seemingly no end in sight."]},{"number":2058,"title":"Chapter 2058: Entering the Immortal Realm","paragraphs":["When the Heavenly Son realized he was fighting the Faceless Sword Emperor, an excited smile appeared on his face, as this meant that he had finally reached the end of the trial.","However, he didn’t dare to underestimate his opponent, who was several times stronger than his previous opponent on the 199th floor.","That said, he was very confident that he would be able to defeat the Faceless Sword Emperor.","Moments later, they clashed, their battle sending violent tremors rippling through the surrounding space without pause. Had they been fighting within the Nine Heavens, their clash would surely have brought unimaginable devastation.","Meanwhile, Yuan and the Great One’s battle raged on with undiminished ferocity. Their clash had endured for so long that Dragon Spiral Mountain had been worn down to an unrecognizable shape. It no longer resembled a towering mountain, but a mere hill.","<Your understanding of Celestial Qi has slightly improved>","Over these past several years, Yuan had been constantly exposed to Celestial Qi. Though it wasn’t potent enough to kill him, it inflicted just enough pain to deepen his understanding of its nature.","However, he was still nowhere near learning it. That was just how difficult it was to learn Celestial Qi.","\"Dragon’s Gaze!\"","The Great One suddenly used Dragon’s Gaze for the first time.","Yet, it didn’t even make Yuan flinch, as his Soul Strength was simply too overwhelming.","In response, the Great One used Dragon’s Gaze again, but it was somewhat different this time.","\"Dragon’s Authority!\"","This Dragon’s Gaze was several times stronger, and it was something only a few dragons in the world could use.","The Great One’s Dragon Authority was strong enough to shake Yuan’s soul slightly, but that was all it could do.","\"I guess it’s about time we put an end to this farce,\" said Yuan.","For the first year, he had been slightly behind the Great One in terms of prowess, but as his soul continued to merge with his body, Yuan’s strength climbed steadily. Now, he was the one pushing the Great One back.","Ding!","<The Sacred Chalice of Purification has successfully purified ???>","<The Sacred Chalice of Purification has begun purifying the next curse>","The moment Yuan received the notification, he felt as if an invisible chain had been lifted from his body, leaving him feeling incomparably lighter.","\"What?!\"","The Great One exclaimed in shock when Yuan’s aura suddenly exploded.","Then, like a volcano, Yuan’s cultivation erupted.","<You have met the requirements for a breakthrough>","<You have reached Early-stage Bronze Immortal>","<You have met the requirements for a breakthrough>","<You have reached Mid-stage Bronze Immortal>","<You have met the requirements for a breakthrough>","<You have reached Late-stage Bronze Immortal>","<You have met the requirements for a breakthrough>","<You have reached Peak-stage Bronze Immortal>","In the blink of an eye, Yuan’s cultivation soared to the peak of Bronze Immortal, on the verge of Silver Immortal.","After finally stepping into the Immortal Realm, Yuan’s Immortal Qi underwent a profound surge in both depth and potency, and it was at least several times stronger than before.","<True Dragon Awakening>","<God of War’s Astral Arts>","<God of War’s Final Execution>","Yuan unleashed a relentless onslaught against the Great One, wielding all of his most formidable techniques.","Already struggling to hold his ground, the Great One suddenly found himself utterly unable to retaliate, crushed beneath the sheer force of Yuan’s overwhelming power.","\"Just stand there and accept your defeat!\" Yuan shouted, using the Immortal Monarch’s authority.","The Great One’s movement froze at his command, even if it was just for a split second. However, a split second was more than enough for Yuan to land his attack.","As the God of War’s Final Execution grew more devastating with each strike, relentlessly building in power until its target was utterly annihilated, the Great One managed to withstand a total of seventy-two blows before he could no longer defend himself.","After several years of relentless battle, Yuan finally defeated the Great One, marking this as the longest time he had ever spent within a single trial of the Stairway to Heaven.","\"You’ve won this time... but I will never give up on Yeyou...\" The Great One’s voice echoed faintly as his form faded into the thin air.","<You have successfully defeated your enemy before the time limit>","A glowing orb of light appeared before him, and as Yuan absorbed it, fragments of his lost memories began to return.","However, that wasn’t all he received from clearing the trial.","Tian’er appeared before him with a wooden box, offering it to him.","\"This is...\"","When Yuan opened the box and saw the object resting inside, he raised his eyebrows, wondering why he had been given it. However, he didn’t question it and figured that it would come in handy one day.","At the same time, the Heavenly Son’s battle with the Faceless Sword Emperor reached its conclusion.","\"Damn it! I was so close to defeating him!\" Tian Yuexing cursed aloud, moments after being teleported out of the Endless Pagoda upon his loss to the Faceless Sword Emperor.","Had he faced the Faceless Sword Emperor from the very start, he would have surely won. But after climbing 199 floors, exhaustion took its toll, leading him to make a fatal mistake at the very end.","Fortunately, since he had surpassed the threshold needed to complete the Sword Emperor Qualifications, he still earned the title of Sword Emperor.","When Tian Yuexing exited the trial and returned to the platform, the first thing he did was look at the ranking.","\"N-Nine hundred points?! That means he cleared all 200 floors!\" Tian Yuexing was in disbelief.","He turned to Senior Bai and demanded, \"Where is he?!\"","\"If you’re asking about Yuan, he finished quite some time ago, and he’s already gone,\" Senior Bai replied calmly.","\"Some time ago...?\" Tian Yuexing frowned.","Senior Bai nodded and continued, \"He finished the trial in a little over two weeks.\"","Upon hearing this shocking revelation, Tian Yuexing’s expression went blank, as if he couldn’t quite comprehend what he had just heard."]},{"number":2059,"title":"Chapter 2059: Arriving at the Eighth Heaven","paragraphs":["\"He finished the trial in just two weeks? There’s no way that’s possible...\" Tian Yuexing mumbled with a bewildered expression on his face.","\"Y-You’re lying! There’s no way anyone could’ve finished that trial in just two weeks! Unless he took a different trial than I!\" he exclaimed a moment later, refusing to believe such an outrageous result.","Senior Bai merely shook his head and responded calmly, \"What would I gain from lying to you? If you don’t want to believe me, you can watch the recordings later.\"","Tian Yuexing fell silent.","\"I really lost...? To a mere mortal? But I am the Heavenly Son...\" he muttered, his voice distant, as if trapped in a waking nightmare.","Though this wasn’t his first defeat, he’d never experienced such a crushing defeat before from anyone, much less to a nobody like Yuan, who had seemingly crawled out from nowhere.","He was the Heavenly Son—born to stand at the pinnacle, number one in nearly everything he did. He had always been the one ahead, the one others chased endlessly. But now, for the first time, he found himself in pursuit of another, and he finally tasted the frustration and helplessness that others had felt trying to catch up to him. It was a surreal feeling.","Eventually, Tian Yuexing accepted his defeat and asked Senior Bai, \"Where did he go?\"","\"I don’t know.\" Senior Bai shook his head.","\"Do you know how I can contact him? I want to pay my debt as soon as possible.\"","Senior Bai wanted to lie and say he didn’t, but with Yuan having already revealed to everyone that he was part of the Celestial Overlords, it would be far too easy to catch him in a lie.","\"I’ll let him know that you want to speak with him,\" Senior Bai said.","\"Tell him to find me at the True Heaven Sect or the Tian Family. If he cannot reach me for some reason, I’ll go to him,\" said Tian Yuexing.","\"I understand. Now, do you have a word for the audience?\"","Hearing this, Tian Yuexing turned to face the crowd. Yet his eyes didn’t truly see them. Instead, his gaze seemed fixed on some distant place far beyond their reach.","After a moment of silence, he spoke in a loud and clear voice, \"I may have lost this time, but it will not happen again! Mark my words, I will defeat you the next time we cross paths!\"","It was clear to everyone there that Tian Yuexing was addressing Yuan, who may or may not be watching from afar.","\"Do you have a name in mind for your new title?\" Senior Bai then asked.","\"I don’t care what I am called, but I will only respond to the name Heavenly Sword Emperor,\" he spoke in an adamant tone.","\"Congratulations, Heavenly Sword Emperor. Regarding the Sword Emperor Ceremony, it will take place at a later date once all of the participants are done.\"","Tian Yuexing narrowed his eyes slightly at the mention of the ceremony. He had little interest in it himself, but realizing that Yuan might attend, he said, \"I’ll be there.\"","Without saying another word, he left the platform and flew directly to where his sister was.","\"I’m heading home.\"","He knew that his sister would mock him for losing, so before she could even open her mouth, Tian Yuexing turned around and sped away.","\"What a loser,\" Tian Jinhui muttered before leaving as well.","Meanwhile, after passing his trial, Yuan arrived at the Eighth Heaven.","\"Eighth Heaven, huh? Now I am only one away from reaching the Supreme Heaven...\" Yuan muttered.","\"So, which clan will you be visiting first?\" Feng Yuxiang asked him a few moments later.","\"Probably the Rising Phoenix Clan,\" he said.","\"Are you going to disguise yourself as a phoenix like you disguised yourself as a Dragon Emperor for the previous Ancient Seals?\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"That’s only because I have the resources to disguise myself as a Dragon Emperor. But as for pretending to be a phoenix... I don’t think I have what I need for that. Other than my Heaven Freezing Flame and your movement technique, I don’t really have anything that could help me pull off a phoenix disguise.\"","\"What about your Fire Harmony? That’s something even phoenixes have a hard time achieving. Also, I have plenty of things that you can use to pull off the perfect phoenix disguise.\"","Feng Yuxiang emerged from his Dantian and began looking through her spatial ring.","A few moments later, she pulled out several items, and Yuan recognized them, as he’d peeked inside her spatial ring during his time at the Primal Expanse.","\"The Ancient Phoenix Robes? But only those with a phoenix bloodline can wear it,\" Yuan said.","\"Hm? You know this treasure?\" Feng Yuxiang looked at him with a surprised face.","Yuan scratched his head and explained in an apologetic tone, \"I forgot to tell you, but I looked through your spatial ring in the Primal Expanse to find anything that could help me approach the phoenixes there. I wore the Ancient Phoenix Robe and even used it to train my fire resistance.\"","He revealed everything to her, including what treasures he’d used.","Feng Yuxiang listened to every word with a calm expression. When he finished, she said softly, \"There’s no need to apologize, Young Master. You did it for my sake, after all. And even if that weren’t true, I still wouldn’t mind—because everything I have is already yours, including my body and soul.\"","She continued, \"Also, I am aware of the Ancient Phoenix Robe’s effect. However, that can easily be fixed with this.\"","Feng Yuxiang showed him the small bottle that contained a single drop of blood within.","\"Isn’t this...\" Yuan instantly recognized this treasure.","\"Yup. This is the Primordial Phoenix Blood Essence. If you consume it, you should acquire the power and bloodline of a phoenix.\"","Yuan swallowed nervously, but he didn’t dare to accept it so easily.","\"Are you sure?\" he asked."]},{"number":2060,"title":"Chapter 2060: Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence","paragraphs":["\"Of course. Like I said, what’s mine is yours,\" Feng Yuxiang said with a calm nod.","She continued, \"To be honest with you, Young Master, I’ve always been a little envious that you possess so much dragon power but almost no phoenix power. It makes my bloodline feel a little inferior. Hopefully, this will help balance things out.\"","\"It’s not like I am purposefully picking dragon powers over phoenix powers. It’s just that I’ve had more encounters with dragons than phoenixes,\" Yuan said. \"In any case, I’ll accept it. Thank you.\"","Feng Yuxiang handed the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence to him the next moment. This then reminded Yuan that he still had the Dragon Ancestor’s Blood Essence.","\"I will need a quiet and secure place to absorb this blood essence, especially since I don’t know how long it’d take...\"","At first, he considered absorbing the blood essence in Senior Bai’s world within the Myriad of Techniques, since he was familiar with the place and it was accessible to only a select few. However, there was a chance that his cultivation might become violent, and he didn’t want to risk causing damage to the place.","Eventually, Yuan decided to find a secluded place somewhere in the Eighth Heaven to consume the blood essence. However, he didn’t know where to go.","This was when Feng Yuxiang spoke up again, \"Young Master, if you’re looking for a place to enter seclusion, why don’t you visit my Immortal Cave? It’s located in the Eighth Heaven.\"","\"Oh? That sounds like a good idea. Where is it?\"","\"I’ll take you there.\"","She retrieved her flying treasure and boarded it a moment later. Once Yuan was aboard, she guided it into motion.","\"It might take some time to get there since it’s quite far away,\" she said.","Yuan nodded, and in the meantime, studied the Mystic Sword Tablet.","Several months later, they arrived at a place of searing heat, where volcanoes and rivers of flowing magma stretched in every direction, as if an apocalypse had recently swept through the land.","This sort of extreme environment would’ve been great for Yuan to train his fire resistance before, but he was already at the point where the heat didn’t affect him in the slightest.","Feng Yuxiang finally brought the flying treasure to a halt and said, \"Young Master, we’ve arrived at the location, but there’s a problem...\"","Yuan stowed away the Mystic Sword Tablet and stepped to the edge of the flying treasure to see for himself.","In the distance, he spotted several groups of cultivators encircling a particular area. Judging by their distinct robes, each group appeared to hail from a different faction.","\"Is that where your Immortal Cave is located?\" Yuan asked Feng Yuxiang.","However, Feng Yuxiang shook her head and said, \"No, my Immortal Cave is a little further ahead. However, with so many people here, I don’t think it’ll be a good idea to use it anymore.\"","Yuan then said, \"There’s no need to come to a conclusion so quickly. Let’s check out the situation first before we decide what to do next.\"","Yuan leapt from the flying treasure and flew toward these cultivators, who were all within the Immortal Realm.","There were about seven hundred cultivators gathered there, most of them ranging from Bronze Immortal to Silver Immortal. Within each group, a single Golden Immortal stood at the forefront, acting as their leader.","When these cultivators noticed Yuan, they immediately became alert.","\"Stop right there.\" One of the Golden Immortals demanded in a tone of authority.","Yuan slowly came to a halt, but before he could even open his mouth, the Golden Immortal continued, \"Turn around and leave immediately. We’re busy.\"","Because Yuan’s cultivation was only at the Bronze Immortal stage, the Golden Immortal didn’t even bother to show him any courtesy and brazenly ordered him to leave.","\"That would be difficult, as I have some business ahead,\" Yuan said.","\"That business will have to wait. If you know what’s good for you, leave while I’m still patient enough to let you!\" the Golden Immortal snapped, his voice rising sharply.","\"This bastard... Who the hell do you think you are to speak to my Young Master in that tone? Have you lost your damn mind?!\" Feng Yuxiang snapped as she caught up with Yuan.","Instantly, all eyes shifted to her—a peerless beauty with flaming red hair and golden eyes, unmistakably marking her as a beast in human form. Yet what truly seized their attention was the terrifying aura of her True Immortal cultivation.","Over the past several years, her cultivation had recovered enough to surpass Yuan once more, now just a hair’s breadth away from stepping into the God Ascension Realm.","The Golden Immortal who commanded Yuan tried to respond but was quickly interrupted, \"First of all, you’re all in my territory. If anyone should leave, it’s you lot.\"","\"Your territory...? I’m sorry, but we’ve traveled through this region for the past hundred years, and this is the first time we’ve ever seen you. Who exactly are you people?\" another Golden Immortal asked, his tone far more respectful now that they were standing before a True Immortal—someone who could easily kill them all.","\"A mere hundred years?\" Feng Yuxiang scoffed with a cold sneer. \"To an Immortal, a hundred years could easily pass in the blink of an eye. You might as well admit you’ve only just arrived with such a trivial span of time.\"","What Feng Yuxiang said made sense, but it was not like they could just leave, especially after pouring so many resources into their business.","\"Ah, it seems we’ve forgotten to introduce ourselves. I am the Second Elder of the Blazing Orchid Sect, and—\" The Golden Immortal tried to reveal his background, but Feng Yuxiang couldn’t care less and said.","\"I don’t give a hot damn about your identity or where you came from. If you don’t apologize to my Young Master and get lost within ten seconds, I’ll turn you all into ashes.\"","Feng Yuxiang threatened as she revealed some of her flames and unique aura.","\"A phoenix!\" These Immortals quickly realized her identity and swallowed nervously."]},{"number":2061,"title":"Chapter 2061: Hell Molten Eel","paragraphs":["The cultivators trembled at Feng Yuxiang’s threatening pressure, but before any of them could respond, Yuan spoke in a calm voice, \"Relax, Feng Feng. There’s no need to spill blood over something like this.\"","Feng Yuxiang immediately retrieved her aura and fell silent, but she continued staring at them, especially the Golden Immortal who spoke first.","Yuan continued, \"I’m sure you all want to resolve this without unnecessary deaths, right?\"","They silently nodded their heads.","\"In that case, why don’t we start by explaining your situation?\" Yuan said.","The Golden Immortals exchanged uneasy glances, clearly reluctant to reveal their true purpose.","Seeing this, Feng Yuxiang let out a cold sneer and said, \"They’re probably here to seize some natural treasure—this place is perfect for birthing treasures rich in yang energy, after all.\"","The Golden Immortals flinched slightly at her words, their reactions speaking louder than any words could.","\"A treasure, huh? If you’re worried that I’ll fight you over it, rest assured—I have no interest in it,\" Yuan said calmly a moment later. \"However, I’d like to know when you’ll be done with your business and on your way.\"","After a moment of silence, one of the Golden Immortals answered without revealing any details, \"We should be out of your territory within a month.\"","Yuan nodded and said, \"Then we’ll wait for you to finish your business.\"","He turned and returned to the flying treasure with Feng Yuxiang shortly after.","Though he had left, his presence still lingered like an invisible weight, forcing the cultivators to remain on high alert.","\"What sort of treasure do you think they’re trying to acquire?\" Yuan asked out of curiosity.","\"Well, the most common treasures found in the Infernal Gorge are minerals for forging artifacts and rare yang element herbs that can only grow in extreme environments like this,\" Feng Yuxiang explained.","\"But for so many people to gather here—and given that we’re right above the Flowing Molten Serpent—the treasure is likely the Hell Molten Eel, a rare creature that only appears once every few thousand years,\" she continued.","Directly beneath them lay a massive river of flowing magma that resembled a serpent from afar, hence why it was known as the Flowing Molten Serpent. Though it might seem far too extreme to sustain life, there were actually magical beasts born and thriving within its fiery depths. The Hell Molten Eel was one such creature.","\"What’s so special about this creature?\" Yuan asked.","\"Well, consuming its meat can drastically enhance one’s fire resistance and improve one’s yang qi. Beyond that, its skin and heart are prized ingredients for various pills and are highly sought after by alchemists.\"","\"I see... but why are they all just waiting there?\"","\"They probably lack the fire resistance to enter the Flowing Molten Serpent to capture the Hell Molten Eel. The creature surfaces once a month, so they might be waiting for that chance.\"","A few days later, Yuan sensed new presences approaching in the distance, prompting him to pause his cultivation.","The moment the newcomers arrived, they immediately demanded that those already present leave at once. Naturally, their demand was refused, and not long after, a battle erupted.","As for Yuan, he simply observed the chaos from a distance, intending to stay uninvolved. However, the newcomers, unaware of who he was, foolishly targeted him as well in the heat of battle.","Seeing this, Feng Yuxiang said, \"Young Master, please leave this to me. There’s no need for you to lift a finger for these weaklings.\"","Yuan nodded.","In the next instant, Feng Yuxiang leapt from the flying treasure, intercepting the seven Silver Immortals who had charged toward them.","\"How dare you weaklings raise your weapons against the Young Master?! Do you even know who you’re dealing with?!\" Feng Yuxiang shouted as she unleashed her flames, instantly trapping them in a massive sphere of fire.","\"Phoenix flames?!\" The Silver Immortals recoiled in shock, stunned by the true identity of their opponent.","\"For your crime, you shall be punished with death!\" Feng Yuxiang declared, making a squeezing motion with her hand. Instantly, the sphere of flames began to contract, shrinking rapidly around her helpless prey.","\"W-Wait! We were wrong!\" the Immortals cried out, begging for their lives as their skin began to blister and burn away under the relentless flames.","\"Of course you were in the wrong. Why else would you be dying?\" Feng Yuxiang said coldly, shaking her head as she ignored their desperate pleas and mercilessly reduced them to ashes.","\"I never knew she could be this scary...\" Yu Ning commented after seeing Feng Yuxiang’s brutal side for the first time.","Meanwhile, the cultivators fighting nearby witnessed this scene and trembled in fear. Those who had chosen to ignore Yuan and Feng Yuxiang let out a sigh of relief, grateful they hadn’t provoked them earlier. As for the newcomers, they stood frozen in shock at the sight of a phoenix—a rare and mighty mythical being that many of them were encountering for the first time.","Feng Yuxiang then proclaimed in a clear, commanding voice, \"I don’t care if you fight among yourselves, but if you dare disturb us, I’ll kill you without a second thought!\"","Soon, the newcomers, unaware that Yuan had no interest in the Hell Molten Eel, quickly chose to retreat once they realized they were facing a phoenix at the True Immortal Realm.","However, that was far from the end of the commotion, as more and more cultivators continued to arrive, drawn by rumors of the Hell Molten Eel’s appearance, each ready to fight for a share of the prize.","Those who had arrived first refrained from fighting among themselves, as they had already agreed to share the treasure peacefully.","As for the newcomers, they would all attack Yuan’s flying treasure, only to be met with Feng Yuxiang’s wrath.","Despite the chaos, Yuan chose to remain at the Infernal Gorge, knowing that things would quiet down once the treasure was claimed, giving him the chance to absorb the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence in peace."]},{"number":2062,"title":"Chapter 2062: Hell Molten Eel(2)","paragraphs":["\"This Hell Molten Serpent must be really valuable for so many people to show up for it,\" Yuan remarked after being attacked for the fifth time in just two weeks.","\"It’s not just the Hell Molten Serpent,\" Feng Yuxiang replied. \"That’s simply how things are in the higher Heavens. It’s common for cultivators to clash over every resource they can get their hands on.\"","\"Why? It’s not like there’s a shortage of resources.\"","\"I suppose that’s just the nature of the higher heavens—competition is simply a way of life.\"","Yuan’s gaze suddenly shifted to a certain direction, and he said, \"Looks like we have more newcomers.\"","\"Time to take out more trash,\" Feng Yuxiang said as she excitedly prepared for battle.","\"Why don’t you just put up a sign or something if you don’t want them attacking us?\" Yuan asked.","Feng Yuxiang chuckled and said, \"That would ruin all the fun. Do you have any idea how bored I was when I lost my powers? Now that they’re back, I intend to enjoy them to the fullest!\"","Yuan merely shook his head at her response, having no intention of stopping her, even if it would spare some lives. After all, those who attacked them had only themselves to blame.","Soon enough, the newcomers launched their attack, and as before, a few broke away from the main battle to target the lone flying treasure that had been quietly minding its own business in the distance.","Before long, Feng Yuxiang’s beautiful flames swept across the sky like a crimson tsunami, and the Immortals who dared attack them were reduced to ashes in an instant.","\"A phoenix?!\" the newcomers exclaimed in shock, their reaction mirroring the disbelief of the cultivators who had come before them.","However, instead of fleeing like the others, one of them shouted, \"C-Contact the Elders! Tell them there’s a True Immortal Phoenix here and that we need their assistance!\"","At his command, one of the cultivators broke from the group and vanished into the distance.","A few minutes later, a massive flying ship appeared on the horizon, its arrival heralded by the unmistakable aura of three approaching True Immortals.","Once the ship arrived, three figures leapt from its deck and swiftly closed in on Yuan’s flying treasure, surrounding it in a tight triangular formation.","\"Need my help?\" Yuan asked Feng Yuxiang, who responded with a smile on her face, \"No need, Young Master. I can handle them alone.\"","She left the flying treasure to face the three True Immortals shortly later.","Once they were face to face, one of the True Immortals questioned, \"You’re a phoenix—why would you need the Hell Molten Serpent?\"","\"Who said I need it?\" Feng Yuxiang replied calmly.","\"Then why are you here, fighting over it with us?!\"","\"Your people attacked us first, so it’s self-defense.\"","\"Are you telling me you’re just here to watch the spectacle?!\" another True Immortal snapped, his voice trembling with anger.","\"Something like that, I guess.\"","The three True Immortals exchanged glances with one another. After a brief moment of silence, they all gave a slight nod, as if having come to an unspoken agreement.","Then, without warning, they began attacking Feng Yuxiang.","Though they would’ve preferred not to clash with a Divine Beast—a Phoenix, no less—they couldn’t let the Hell Molten Eel be taken away.","However, knowing there was a chance that Feng Yuxiang belonged to one of the Royal Phoenix Clans, they didn’t dare risk killing her outright. Instead, they attacked with the sole intention of subduing and suppressing her.","\"Are you bastards looking down on me?\" Feng Yuxiang snarled, realizing exactly what they were doing as flames surged violently around her.","The battle’s intensity escalated, and despite being outnumbered, Feng Yuxiang still managed to drive the three True Immortals back.","However, a few hours later, as the battle neared its conclusion and the True Immortals began to falter, a sudden tremor shook the land, and the surrounding volcanoes erupted in a roaring cascade of fire and molten rock.","Everyone on the battlefield froze mid-motion, their eyes instinctively drawn to the Flowing Molten Serpent below.","The river of lava suddenly began to churn and bubble ominously, as if something was emerging.","Seeing this, the Golden Immortal who had once tried to drive Yuan away shouted, \"The Hell Molten Serpent is surfacing! Prepare to activate the formation! We’ll hold them off!\"","Although their numbers had dwindled drastically over the past two weeks of constant fighting, they decided to remain there because of Feng Yuxiang’s presence.","Moments later, the surface of the lava river began to swell and rise, until a massive black eel emerged, its body etched with glowing cracks that pulsed like molten veins.","The cultivators activated the formation, instantly binding the Hell Molten Serpent with powerful chains that prevented it from escaping. However, that was all they could manage for now, as they were still under relentless attack from rival factions.","Unfortunately, they were hopelessly outnumbered, and the opposing forces kept whittling away at their ranks with relentless assaults.","With no other choice, they turned to Yuan for help.","\"Please! Young Master! Help us!\"","But Yuan had no reason to intervene. They were there to hunt for treasures, and he was merely a passerby.","While Feng Yuxiang had indirectly aided them by eliminating those who attacked their flying treasure, it didn’t make them allies in any sense of the word.","While it might seem right to save them, doing so would be unfair to everyone else who had come to compete for the treasure. After all, they hadn’t been attacked by bandits. They were simply participants in the same ruthless struggle for the Hell Molten Eel.","\"If you want to survive, just give up on the treasure and leave,\" Yuan told them calmly.","\"Impossible!\" one of them shouted back. \"We’ve already lost so many trying to claim it! If we abandon it now, all those deaths would be meaningless!\"","Yuan shook his head and sighed. \"Use your brain a little. Since it’s clear you don’t have what it takes to claim it, you’ll also die a meaningless death if you continue to struggle for it. You might as well save the lives you still can.\""]},{"number":2063,"title":"Chapter 2063: Hell Molten Eel(3)","paragraphs":["Upon hearing Yuan’s words, it was as if a switch had been flipped inside their minds, snapping them back to their senses.","\"He’s right... We’d just be throwing away our lives at this point...\"","Moreover, it was clear that Yuan had no intention of helping them.","Very quickly, the cultivators who had been there from the start began to retreat, abandoning the Hell Molten Eel, which remained bound by the formation.","Seeing this, the opposing faction shouted, \"Don’t let them escape! Hunt them down!\"","But just as they surged forward to give chase, a figure silently appeared before them, like a ghost materializing from thin air.","After blocking them from the retreating cultivators, Yuan spoke in a cold voice, \"I can’t tell if you’re bold or just stupid.\"","Upon hearing Yuan’s voice, they realized that he was the one who had advised the others to run. However, when they saw that he was just a Bronze Immortal, they lowered their guard slightly.","\"I thought you weren’t going to intervene,\" said one of the Immortals there.","\"I wasn’t, but that was because I had no reason to.\"","\"What’s your reason for intervening now, then?\"","\"Are you really asking me that?\" Yuan replied calmly. \"Those people behind me have already given up on the Hell Molten Eel, so why go out of your way to slaughter them? If you were still fighting for the treasure, I could understand, but this... this makes you no different from bandits.\"","The Immortals scoffed and retorted, \"What do you think this is—a game you can just walk away from whenever you feel like it? We’re all risking our lives here, you know?\"","Yuan shrugged. \"Where I come from, even in the midst of war, if your enemy surrenders, you have no right to kill them.\"","\"Where are you from? The boonies?\" The Immortals laughed out loud.","Realizing his words were falling on deaf ears, Yuan let out a quiet sigh and said, \"If you’re determined to kill them, then you’ll have to get through me first.\"","\"Who the fuck do you think you are? You’re just a Bronze Immortal, and we outnumber you three hundred to one!\"","\"If you think your phoenix friend can help you, she’s busy dealing with the Elders right now!\"","Yuan glanced at Feng Yuxiang and smiled faintly.","\"Judging by how things look, she’ll be done with them soon enough. But I should be able to deal with you lot long before that.\"","\"Arrogant bastard! Let’s see you try!\"","The cultivators immediately surrounded Yuan and launched their assault.","Yuan could have easily wiped them all out with his Supreme Sword Aura, but instead, he chose to practice his phoenix disguise and unleashed his Heaven Freezing Flames instead.","In the next moment, beautiful light blue flames—clear and pure as an unpolluted sea—suddenly erupted from his body, surrounding him in a radiant blaze.","\"This is—! He’s a phoenix, too?!\"","The cultivators recoiled in shock at the sight of Yuan’s flames.","While they stood frozen in shock, Yuan conjured a massive ring of azure flames, forming a blazing arena that trapped them within its searing walls.","The Heaven Freezing Flames weren’t merely scorching hot—they were freezing cold as well. Those caught near them felt as if they were being burned and frozen simultaneously.","\"I will give you all one last chance to lower your weapons and focus on that thing instead,\" said Yuan as he pointed at the Hell Molten Eel beneath them. \"Otherwise, I’ll turn everyone here into popsicles.\"","\"Hmph! Empty threats! Get him! Once we kill him, we’ll help the Elders with the other one!\"","Without another word, these cultivators began bombarding Yuan with their martial techniques, some even using treasures to suppress his movements.","Yuan merely shook his head and mumbled, \"Ask and you shall receive...\"","In the moments that followed, Yuan unleashed his Heaven Freezing Flames upon the cultivators. Even the slightest touch of the flames caused their bodies to freeze over in an instant, like demons being sealed away, except instead of turning to stone, they became lifeless statues of ice.","The flames also inflicted an agony beyond description—burning their internal organs while encasing their outer bodies in bitter, unyielding ice.","In the blink of an eye, more than half of the three hundred cultivators were frozen into lifeless ice statues. Their frozen bodies then fell into the Flowing Molten Serpent below, vanishing beneath the roiling lava.","Realizing they stood no chance against Yuan, the remaining cultivators fell to their knees, begging for their lives.","\"Please, spare us! Didn’t you say you’d even show mercy to your enemies in war if they surrendered where you’re from? This isn’t even close to that level of conflict!\"","Yuan’s icy gaze stayed steady as he replied, \"You’re right. This isn’t war—nowhere near it. I’m simply taking out the trash.\"","Before the cultivators could utter another word, Yuan flicked his sleeve, unleashing his Heaven Freezing Flames once again and engulfing them like a tidal wave. In an instant, the remaining cultivators were frozen solid, their lifeless statues dropping into the lava river below like scattered pebbles, sending ripples across the molten surface.","Shortly later, Feng Yuxiang also dealt with the three True Immortals.","\"What now?\" Feng Yuxiang asked him after things calmed down and they were alone again.","Yuan lowered his gaze to the Hell Molten Eel, only to find that it had broken free from its bindings during the chaos and slipped back into the depths of the Flowing Molten Serpent.","\"I’ll be right back.\"","Without another word, he abruptly dove toward the lava river, vanishing beneath its molten surface.","Thanks to his Fire Harmony, the lava felt comforting—like being wrapped in a warm blanket on a cold winter’s night—and it even replenished his energy as he moved through it.","Eventually, he caught up to the Hell Molten Serpent, seized it effortlessly, and returned to Feng Yuxiang.","\"What are you going to do with that? It won’t benefit your fire resistance at that level,\" Feng Yuxiang asked him."]},{"number":2064,"title":"Chapter 2064: Consuming the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence","paragraphs":["Yuan looked at the Hell Molten Eel and shrugged, \"No clue, but I’ll think of something.\"","He then tossed the entire thing inside his spatial ring.","\"Alright, now that things are peaceful and quiet, let’s head to my Immortal Cave,\" Feng Yuxiang said a moment later.","Yuan nodded and followed her to a massive volcano that rivaled the Dragon Spiral Mountain in size, located just a few hundred miles from where they had found the Hell Molten Eel.","The temperature in this area was nearly unbearable for anyone lacking at least Supreme Fire Resistance. The volcano would also constantly erupt with lava, sending showers of molten rock and scorching debris that could easily kill any cultivator who wasn’t an Immortal.","Some time later, Feng Yuxiang came to a stop above the volcano and said, \"My Immortal Cave is just inside.\"","When Yuan looked down into the massive crater, he saw a seething world of flames within, greatly resembling that of the Nine Levels of Hell from the Primal Expanse.","Of course, it wasn’t nearly as intensive and dangerous as the training ground from the Primal Expanse, and he followed Feng Yuxiang inside without any hesitation.","After descending to about halfway down the mountain, stopping just above the roiling sea of lava, they finally reached their destination.","\"So, where’s the Immortal Cave?\" Yuan asked aloud, glancing around but seeing nothing that even remotely resembled a cave.","\"Give me a moment to bring it out,\" said Feng Yuxiang.","Then, she retrieved an object from her spatial ring and pointed it toward the lava below.","The volcano began to tremble almost immediately, and Yuan watched as something slowly rose from the molten depths. When it fully emerged, it revealed a massive cave entrance with a path that appeared to descend beneath the lava’s surface.","\"Let’s go, Young Master. We’re almost there,\" Feng Yuxiang said, speaking calmly as she stepped into the cave entrance without hesitation.","Yuan followed her into the darkness. However, after just a few steps, the scenery suddenly brightened, and he found himself in an entirely different place. The volcano and its blistering heat were gone, replaced by a cool forest filled with the fresh scent of greenery. Dense trees surrounded them, and not far away stood a massive tree, towering a hundred times larger than the rest, like some ancient, grand sentinel at the heart of the forest.","\"This is your Immortal Cave?\" Yuan muttered, raising an eyebrow.","Her ’cave’ was, in truth, an entire world of its own, much like Senior Bai’s realm within the Myriad of Techniques.","Feng Yuxiang smiled and asked teasingly, \"Did you think it would be an actual cave? Maybe something like that would satisfy human cultivators, but for me, it has to be something like this.\"","Yuan glanced at the massive tree and remarked, \"Honestly, this scenery doesn’t really match a phoenix’s image. After all, fire and nature don’t exactly mix well.\"","\"Maybe not an ordinary forest, where the trees would burn to ash at the slightest spark. But this place is different,\" she said with a smile. \"Even if you tried to set the entire forest ablaze, nothing would happen.\"","\"Anyway, you can consume the blood essence here without worrying about being disturbed. I’ll also keep guard from the outside just in case,\" she continued.","\"Alright. Thank you.\" Yuan nodded.","Feng Yuxiang left the Immortal Cave shortly after to stand guard, even though it was highly unlikely anyone would come to cause trouble. After all, she had spent thousands of years here without a single disturbance.","Once outside, Feng Yuxiang sat outside the entrance like a guardian and closed her eyes to cultivate.","Meanwhile, Yuan flew to the top of the grand tree and settled at its peak, where a large nest was nestled among the branches, clearly Feng Yuxiang’s resting place.","He sat in the nest and gazed out at the breathtaking scenery before him—an unobstructed view of the entire forest stretching out in every direction.","A few minutes later, he retrieved the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence and stared at it in silence. Once he felt ready, he removed the seal on the vial.","The moment he broke the seal, a searing wave of heat surged out. The heat was so intense that, even with his Fire Harmony, Yuan felt a burning sting on his face, and this overwhelming heat radiated from just a single drop of blood.","Yuan swallowed nervously after this experience.","\"It’s been a while since I last felt this nervous...\" he muttered with a stiff smile on his face.","He closed his eyes and took several deep breaths to steady himself. Once ready, Yuan raised the vial to his lips and let the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence pour into his mouth.","The moment the blood essence touched his tongue, it was instantly absorbed into his body.","<You have consumed the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence>","However, before Yuan could even process what was happening, his entire body was suddenly engulfed in flames—invisible flames that couldn’t be seen with the naked eye.","This invisible flame was so fierce and potent that it tore straight through his fire resistance, flooding his body with an indescribable pain.","The pain was nearly unbearable for Yuan, so intense that he found himself howling in agony during those first few moments.","<Your fire resistance has improved drastically>","<Your fire resistance has improved drastically>","<Your fire resistance has improved drastically>","\"H-Hang in there, Yuan!\" Lan Yingying cheered him from within his Dantian, but Yuan was in too much pain to even hear her voice.","Yet, the strength and heat of the invisible flames only grew with each passing moment. The space around Yuan warped under the searing force, the distortion spreading wider as the heat intensified.","His body was constantly being burned and torn apart, yet his regeneration kept pace so perfectly that it seemed as if no damage was being done at all.","Soon, the flames began to burn not only his body, but his very soul as well, and the only thing keeping his existence from being burned away was Heaven’s Undying Soul."]},{"number":2065,"title":"Chapter 2065: Refining the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence","paragraphs":["After absorbing the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence, time seemed to slow to a standstill for Yuan as he was consumed by endless, indescribable pain.","Minutes turned into hours, and hours into days, yet the invisible flames continued to burn Yuan relentlessly, showing no sign of fading anytime soon.","Even worse, the pain from the invisible flames only grew more intense with each passing moment.","Two weeks later, the invisible flames had spread across the entire world, engulfing it completely and causing the very fabric of space to warp and ripple without end. Yet, the trees appeared completely fine, as if the flames didn’t even exist.","As for Yuan, he had stopped screaming, but that didn’t mean the pain had vanished. Even as his tolerance grew, the strength of the invisible flames always outpaced it by just enough to keep him in constant, unrelenting agony.","Suddenly—","Ding!","<Your Fire Immunity has evolved into True Fire Immunity>","Though it may seem like Yuan had achieved Fire Harmony, that was not the case, and he was only able to absorb flames and turn them into his power because of his physique. This meant that his fire resistance still had considerable room to grow.","After attaining True Fire Immunity, Yuan managed to endure the invisible flames with slightly more ease, though only for a moment. Almost as if it were sentient and realized it was no longer as effective as before, the flames suddenly surged in power.","Though it was painful, Yuan actually preferred it this way since it meant his fire immunity wouldn’t slow down its progress.","Then, after another month, Yuan achieved Fire Harmony.","<Your True Fire Immunity has evolved into Fire Harmony>","<Completed Harmonious Heaven Refining Immortal Physique has activated>","<Completed Harmonious Heaven Refining Immortal Physique has begun to evolve>","<Progress: 55%>","Then, after another three months, his fire immunity improved again.","<Your Fire Harmony has evolved into Perfect Fire Harmony>","Upon attaining Perfect Fire Harmony, the invisible flames lost their power over Yuan. They could no longer inflict pain on him, finally bringing an end to his relentless torment.","However, this didn’t mean he was finished absorbing the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence. In truth, he was only just beginning—the ordeal so far had merely been a test to determine if he was worthy.","<Immortal Monarch’s Bloodline is reacting to the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence>","Unlike when he consumed the Dragon God’s Blood Essence, Yuan was strong enough to refine the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence without any assistance. However, it would take some time.","After an entire year of relentless refinement, Yuan finally succeeded in fully absorbing the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence.","<Immortal Monarch’s Bloodline evolution has progressed slightly>","<Progress: 22%>","<You have acquired the power of a Primordial Phoenix through its Blood Essence>","<You have learned ’True Phoenix Awakening’>","<You have learned ’True Primordial Fire’>","[True Primordial Fire]","[Rank: ???]","[Mastery Level: 1]","[A unique flame possessed only by the Primordial Phoenix—completely invisible to the eye, yet so destructive it can burn through reality itself.]","<Your Completed Harmonious Heaven Refining Immortal Physique has evolved into True Harmonious Heaven Refining Immortal Physique>","The instant his physique evolved, Yuan’s cultivation—which had been bottlenecked at the peak of Bronze Immortal—immediately surged to the next level, elevating him to Silver Immortal. But it didn’t stop there, and his cultivation continued to soar until it reached the peak of Silver Immortal in one go.","Shortly after finishing the refinement of the blood essence, Yuan activated True Phoenix Awakening to test its power.","Instantly, his long black hair turned a brilliant crimson and ignited with flickering flames, while his eyes gleamed a radiant gold. His appearance now bore an uncanny resemblance to Feng Yuxiang’s when she uses her phoenix powers.","It wasn’t just his appearance—his aura, and even his scent, became indistinguishable from that of a true phoenix, as if he had truly transformed into one.","Yuan raised his arm and activated the True Primordial Fire. Instantly, invisible flames surged forth like a tidal wave, engulfing everything in front of him.","\"Not bad,\" he murmured, clearly satisfied with the results. Now, he could easily pass himself off as a true phoenix.","He retrieved the Ancient Phoenix Robe a moment later and wore it without any issues. Even if it didn’t recognize him as a phoenix, its curse wouldn’t have any effect on his Perfect Fire Harmony.","Sometime later, Yuan emerged from the Immortal Cave to reunite with Feng Yuxiang, who had been standing watch outside the entire time.","\"Y-Young Master...?\" Feng Yuxiang’s eyes widened, her mouth slightly agape as she stared at Yuan, still clad in his phoenix form.","Unbeknownst to her, a soft flush of red had already spread across her cheeks.","\"What do you think?\" Yuan asked, a calm smile on his face.","\"...\"","But Feng Yuxiang couldn’t respond, as she was utterly speechless. She had always believed Yuan was perfect, yet seeing him in his phoenix form and wearing the Ancient Phoenix Robe felt like witnessing an entirely new, breathtaking side of him.","A sudden tingling sensation ran through her body, sending an involuntary shiver down her spine. The last time she had felt something like this was when she had used her hands to assist Yuan, but now, just his scent alone was enough to arouse her.","However, Feng Yuxiang quickly snapped herself out of her daze by forcefully slapping her own cheeks, just as one might do to jolt oneself awake.","\"C-Congratulations, Young Master. If I were seeing you for the first time, I wouldn’t have been able to tell you’re actually human and not a true phoenix,\" she said.","\"If even you can’t tell the difference, then fooling everyone else should be easy,\" Yuan said with a faint smile. \"Anyway, thank you for the blood essence, Feng Feng. If there’s anything you need, I’ll do my best to make it happen.\"","Still feeling a bit dazed, Feng Yuxiang silently nodded.","Sometime later, Feng Yuxiang and Yuan departed from the volcano and set out on their journey toward the Rising Phoenix Clan."]},{"number":2066,"title":"Chapter 2066: Arriving at the Rising Phoenix Clan","paragraphs":["\"So, how should we approach the Rising Phoenix Clan?\" Yuan asked Feng Yuxiang as they traveled on the flying treasure.","\"...\"","When Feng Yuxiang didn’t respond, Yuan opened his eyes and turned to her, only to find her staring at him with a dazed expression, completely mesmerized by his new appearance.","\"Feng Feng?\" he called out to her again.","This time, she snapped out of it and stammered in a panic, \"H-Huh? What did you just say? Sorry, I was thinking about something...\"","\"I asked if you have any suggestions on how we should approach the Rising Phoenix Clan,\" he repeated calmly.","\"I’ve thought about it for the past year, but I still can’t come up with anything. After all, I severed our ties when I left—so it would be strange to just return as if nothing ever happened,\" she sighed.","\"Why don’t you just do what you did with the dragon clans?\" she suddenly said.","\"You mean pretend to be a Phoenix Emperor? Does such a title even exist among the phoenix clans?\" Yuan asked, raising an eyebrow.","\"Of course. It would be weird if we didn’t.\"","Yuan pondered for a moment before speaking, \"While that might have worked in the lower heavens, I doubt the Rising Phoenix Clan, one of the Royal Phoenix Clans, would fall for such a trick.\"","\"That’s true...\"","She added after a brief pause, \"Additionally, even if you show up as a Phoenix Emperor, I cannot imagine how you’ll convince them to hand over something as precious as the Ancient Seal.\"","Yuan closed his eyes to ponder again.","A few days later, he asked, \"Dragons deeply respect—sometimes even revere—those with a stronger bloodline. Is it the same with phoenixes?\"","Feng Yuxiang nodded, \"Not just phoenixes. It’s basically like that for every single beast race out there.\"","\"In that case...\" He paused for a moment before continuing, \"This might be a long shot, but if pretending to be a Phoenix Emperor won’t work, why not appear as a Primordial Phoenix instead? Your bloodline is essentially the ancestor of phoenixes, right?\"","\"That’s correct. The Primordial Phoenix is the most ancient and powerful phoenix bloodline.\"","Suddenly, Feng Yuxiang’s expression shifted, as if a thought had struck her.","\"If you’re going to do that, why not try to recruit the Rising Phoenix Clan?\" she suggested. \"As far as I know, they’ve been trying to improve their bloodline for a long time. With your Immortal Monarch’s Bloodline, you could easily win them over. Of course, you won’t be going there as the Immortal Monarch but as a Primordial Phoenix.\"","\"Now that I think about it, the position of Phoenix Emperor is too lowly for someone like you, Young Master,\" she added.","Yuan nodded, \"That does sound like a good idea. Not only would it benefit me to have one of the Royal Phoenix Clans on my side, but they might be more willing to hand over the Ancient Seal if I present myself as a Primordial Phoenix.\"","\"Then let’s go over our plans.\"","Time passed, and in the blink of an eye, three months had already gone by since Yuan consumed the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence.","The Rising Phoenix Clan was a small yet powerful clan situated in the Nirvana Crest—a mountain range where, according to legend, those who perish within its bounds could be reborn as a phoenix.","Just like the dragon clans, due to the rarity of pure and authentic phoenix bloodlines, the phoenix clans were primarily composed of beasts related to phoenixes but not true phoenixes themselves. Only the core members of the clan were true phoenixes.","To expand their power and influence, the Royal Phoenix Clan continuously recruits new beasts into their ranks. Because of this, the Nirvana Crest is always bustling with a steady flow of immortal beasts coming and going.","Much like a sect, the Rising Phoenix Clan puts every recruit through rigorous trials and tests the quality of their bloodline. In the world of beasts, the strength of one’s bloodline determined one’s potential, making it the most vital measure of worth.","As thousands of powerful beasts lined up, forming a long queue at the Nirvana Crest, they suddenly sensed a formidable presence steadily approaching their way.","\"Which idiot is showing off before the Rising Phoenix Clan? Who are they trying to impress?\"","Though the presence was formidable, it was nothing they hadn’t felt before. After all, there was always someone trying to show off now and then, hoping to attract the attention of the Rising Phoenix Clan.","However, when the phoenixes within the Rising Phoenix Clan sensed this presence, they were shocked to find their own bloodlines reacting to it—something that only happened in the presence of a bloodline vastly superior to their own.","Very quickly, members of the Rising Phoenix Clan began to gather outside their residence, standing in quiet anticipation as the powerful presence drew steadily closer.","Soon, they realized it wasn’t just a single presence approaching but two, and one of them felt oddly familiar, yet strangely unfamiliar at the same time.","Eventually, the figures came into view, and the phoenixes’ eyes widened in shock when they recognized one of them.","\"That woman... isn’t that Feng Yuxiang?\"","\"What?\"","\"...You’re right! That’s Feng Yuxiang!\"","\"What’s she doing here? It’s been thousands of years since I last heard from her.\"","\"Do you think she’s trying to return to the clan?\"","\"So soon? Didn’t she just leave?\"","The phoenixes immediately began to speculate upon seeing Feng Yuxiang. Although it had been thousands of years since she had left them, such a span of time was nothing to them, and in their eyes, it felt as if she had only just departed.","\"Is it just me, or is there something very different about her? Though her appearance is the same, her aura is very different, not to mention her presence.\"","\"Who’s that next to her?\"","\"Wait a second... Isn’t that the Ancient Phoenix Robe he’s wearing?\"","Soon, Yuan and Feng Yuxiang arrived at the Rising Phoenix Clan, coming to a halt directly in front of their grand residence."]},{"number":2067,"title":"Chapter 2067: Rising Phoenix Clan","paragraphs":["Shortly after their arrival, one of the phoenixes from the Rising Phoenix Clan approached them in the air.","\"It’s been a while, Junior Sister Yuxiang.\" The phoenix, a middle-aged woman, greeted her.","\"It’s only been a few thousand years, Senior Sister Zhenyan,\" said Feng Yuixang.","It was pretty common for phoenixes from different clans to share the surname ’Feng’, much like how many dragon clans have the surname ’Long’ despite coming from different backgrounds.","\"Where have you been all these years? We haven’t heard a word from you since you left us.\"","\"I went on a little adventure in the lower heavens...\" Feng Yuxiang replied, purposefully avoiding any mention of the curse.","\"The lower heavens...? There’s nothing to see down there.\" Feng Zhenyan shook her head.","\"That’s not true. There are a lot of things to do there, and my life has changed a lot because of it.\"","\"If you say so. Anyway, why have you come here? Have you decided to return to us? And who is that handsome phoenix beside you?\" Feng Zhenyan’s gaze suddenly shifted to Yuan, and her face flushed slightly at Yuan’s handsome appearance and distinct scent.","\"This is my Young Master, whom I met in the lower heavens,\" Feng Yuxiang said, a warm smile on her face.","\"Young Master...?\" Feng Zhenyan’s eyes widened at how she addressed him.","Everyone in the Rising Phoenix Clan knew of Feng Yuxiang’s proud and haughty nature, so to hear her call someone ’Young Master’ was simply unimaginable.","’No, maybe I misheard or am misunderstanding it. His actual name must be Young Master...’ Feng Zhenyan thought to herself.","Almost as if she could read Feng Zhenyan’s thoughts, Feng Yuxiang added, \"That’s right. I’m serving him now, so he is my Young Master.\"","Feng Zhenyan was left speechless. She had already been curious about Yuan’s identity, but now, realizing that he had managed to subdue someone as difficult as Feng Yuxiang, she felt a flicker of nervousness. What kind of heaven-defying background did he possess?","\"Anyway, we came here because the Young Master has some business with the Rising Phoenix Clan. Is the Matriarch available right now?\" Feng Yuxiang asked a moment later.","Feng Zhenyan shook her head and replied, \"No... the Matriarch had some business and left a few months ago. That said, we received news that she would be back soon.\"","Feng Yuxiang looked at Yuan and asked, \"What do you think, Young Master? Should we leave for now and return later?\"","\"What a hassle.\" Yuan sighed.","Hearing this, Feng Zhenyan quickly said, \"If you’re willing, you’re welcome to stay with us until the Matriarch returns.\"","\"I’m a bit pressed for time,\" Yuan replied calmly. \"Why don’t I just speak with whoever holds the highest authority available right now?\"","\"Right now...? That would be the Grand Elder, Feng Lingtian,\" Feng Zhenyan replied after pondering for a brief moment.","\"I’ll speak to him, but he’ll want to know what he’s dealing with...\"","Yuan then said calmly, \"My name isn’t important. Just tell him that a Primordial Phoenix is here.\"","\"P-P-Primordial Phoenix?!\" Feng Zhenyan gasped, her voice trembling with shock and disbelief.","\"Primordial Phoenix? What are they talking about?\"","Those who had been watching from a distance were startled by Feng Zhenyan’s sudden outburst, their curiosity instantly ignited.","Shortly after her outburst, Feng Zhenyan turned to look at Feng Yuxiang for confirmation.","In response, Feng Yuxiang nodded her head and calmly confirmed, \"My Young Master carries with him the most ancient and noble phoenix bloodline in existence—the Primordial Phoenix Bloodline.\"","Hearing this, Feng Zhenyan instantly lowered her head and bowed toward Yuan, \"P-Please excuse my lack of respect, Senior Primordial Phoenix!\"","\"I don’t really care about such things, but if you want to repent, just notify your Grand Elder of my presence.\"","\"As you wish! In fact, please come with me. I’ll bring you to him.\"","Yuan nodded and followed Feng Zhenyan into the depths of the Rising Phoenix Clan’s territory.","They stopped before a specific mountain some time later, and Feng Zhenyan said, \"Please wait here for a moment. Only members of the Rising Phoenix Clan or those permitted are allowed past this point.\"","Feng Zhenyan flew away and disappeared behind the mountain shortly later.","Upon reaching her destination, Feng Zhenyan called out, \"Grand Elder, we have an emergency.\"","Moments later, a short old man with white and red hair appeared before her like a ghost.","\"What happened?\" he asked her in a stern tone.","\"A guest claiming to be a Primordial Phoenix has appeared at our Rising Phoenix Clan, and he wishes to speak with you.\"","The Grand Elder’s half-closed eyes snapped open in surprise at the mention of ’Primordial Phoenix.’","\"Are you certain you heard that correctly? A Primordial Phoenix hasn’t appeared in this world for millions of years,\" he said, his voice tinged with disbelief.","\"I am certain. In fact, Feng Yuxiang is here with him, and she even addresses him as ’Young Master’.\"","\"Feng Yuxiang? That young phoenix who recently left?\"","\"That’s correct.\"","\"Do you know what they want?\" The Grand Elder then asked.","\"No, but they initially wanted to speak with the Matriarch. Unfortunately, she’s not here right now, so they want to speak with you instead.\"","\"Very well. Bring them here. I shall see for myself whether we’re dealing with a true Primordial Phoenix or just some fraud.\"","Without another word, Feng Zhenyan left to return to Yuan and Feng Yuxiang.","\"The Grand Elder has agreed to meet with you. Please, follow me.\" Feng Zhenyan said to them the moment she returned.","Sometime later, Yuan and Feng Yuxiang followed her to the Grand Elder, who was waiting at a sprawling flower garden nestled behind a secluded mountain.","When the Grand Elder laid eyes on Yuan and sensed his presence fully, he suddenly felt a warmth stir within him, as if his very blood was responding to Yuan’s existence.","’This feeling... Could it be? Could he truly be a Primordial Phoenix?’ The Grand Elder swallowed hard, a flicker of nervousness passing through him."]},{"number":2068,"title":"Chapter 2068: True Primordial Fire","paragraphs":["\"Welcome to the Rising Phoenix Clan, esteemed guest. My name is Feng Lingtian, the Grand Elder of this clan.\"","The short old man introduced himself to Yuan shortly after their arrival.","But before Yuan could do the same, he continued, \"I heard that you have the Primordial Phoenix’s Bloodline, but before we can even begin our conversation, I must verify something first. We haven’t seen this bloodline for millions of years—since the Immortal Monarch’s Era, so I apologize for being skeptical, nor am I trying to offend you.\"","Yuan shook his head calmly and spoke, \"No, I fully understand your skepticism. I just need to prove my identity, correct?\"","Naturally, Yuan had predicted this would happen and was prepared for it.","\"Then, allow me to apologize in advance.\" Yuan suddenly said.","\"Huh?\" The Grand Elder couldn’t understand his words at first, but quickly realized why he was apologizing.","\"Kneel.\"","Yuan activated Immortal Monarch’s Dominion, commanding the Grand Elder to kneel on the ground.","The Grand Elder was at the 5th level of the God Ascension Realm, but Yuan had not only improved his cultivation but also his Immortal Monarch’s Bloodline after consuming the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence. This allowed him to command God Ascension Realm beasts with much more ease and for far longer than before.","\"G-Grand Elder!\" Feng Zhenyan gasped in shock when she saw him kneel to the ground—something he wouldn’t do even for the Matriarch of the Rising Phoenix Clan.","Although Yuan had withdrawn the Immortal Monarch’s Dominion almost immediately, the Grand Elder’s knees remained firmly rooted on the ground. His head was bowed, but if one could see his face, they would find his eyes wide with shock and his mouth agape, as if he had just witnessed a miracle.","Just as dragons could wield Dragon Authority to command those of weaker bloodlines, phoenixes could invoke Phoenix Authority to command phoenixes with lesser bloodlines.","Though the Grand Elder’s bloodline wasn’t the absolute strongest, it was among the very best, strong enough to elevate him to the position of Grand Elder within the Rising Phoenix Clan, one of the Royal Phoenix Clans.","However, while impressive, it wasn’t enough to prove Yuan’s identity as a Primordial Phoenix.","Aware of this, Yuan said calmly, \"That was just an introduction. Now, here’s the real proof.\"","He lifted his hand and, with a smooth motion, flipped his palm over—summoning the Primordial Flames into existence.","Feng Zhenyan’s eyes widened as she silently stared at the invisible flames dancing above Yuan’s palm. The Grand Elder, who had begun to lift his head at Yuan’s words, suddenly sprang to his feet and instinctively backed away—every fiber of his being warning him of the flames’ danger, despite his nature as a phoenix.","\"This is...\" The Grand Elder swallowed hard, his voice trembling.","Though he had never seen them with his own eyes, he had read of them in ancient records—flames invisible to the eye, capable of burning even a phoenix with fire immunity. A power wielded only by the most ancient and exalted bloodline, the True Primordial Fire.","\"Would you like to experience the flames yourself, to be certain it’s no trick?\" Yuan asked suddenly.","The Grand Elder trembled at the mere thought of subjecting himself to the strongest fire in the universe.","As phoenixes, it was in their very nature to immerse themselves in the strongest fires they could find, both to temper their bodies and as a mark of pride worth boasting about, almost like moths drawn to flames.","Therefore, when the Grand Elder was offered a chance to experience the strongest fire known to exist—something long thought extinct—there was no way he could pass up such an opportunity, even if it might cost him his life.","The Grand Elder nodded his head with a stern expression on his face, agreeing to Yuan’s offer.","\"Very well.\"","Yuan looked at Feng Zhenyan and said, \"You should stand back a little.\"","However, Feng Zhenyan shook her head and responded in a resolute but somewhat nervous voice, \"No, please allow me to experience the True Primordial Fire as well.\"","After all, she was also a phoenix.","\"If you say so.\"","Without hesitation, Yuan released the True Primordial Fire, instantly engulfing their bodies in its invisible, all-consuming blaze.","Feng Zhenyan immediately let out a scream of pain, while the Grand Elder clenched his fists and gritted his jaw in silence, veins bulging across his body as he endured the searing agony.","Yet, despite their obvious agony, both Feng Zhenyan and the Grand Elder wore almost sadistic smiles on their faces, clearly relishing the pain.","\"Yes! This is it! This is the pinnacle of fire! I’ve survived all these years just for this moment!\" the Grand Elder shouted, spreading his arms wide and crying out to the heavens.","Moments later, Feng Zhenyan suddenly collapsed to the ground. Seeing this, Yuan withdrew the flames from her, leaving her body steaming with wisps of smoke, almost like a roasted bird.","At a glance, the Grand Elder seemed fine, but Yuan could sense that his body was sustaining damage. Since he had no intention of harming them, there was no reason to continue, so he withdrew the flames from the Grand Elder as well.","However, the very next moment, the Grand Elder suddenly let out a scream, but unlike Feng Zhenyan’s, his cry wasn’t just from physical pain. It carried the raw edge of emotional anguish, as if he’d just lost something precious or endured a deep, mental wound.","\"No! The light is gone! Ahhhh!\" he cried out in despair, even dropping to the ground and rolling around like he was on fire.","Yuan could only watch in stunned silence, his eyes wide, speechless at such an unexpected reaction. He couldn’t help but wonder if the True Primordial Fire had some side effects that caused hallucinations.","\"Don’t worry about him. This is quite normal,\" Feng Yuxiang said to Yuan.","\"If you say so...\"","A moment later, the Grand Elder crawled toward Yuan and pleaded in a desperate voice, \"Please... use the True Primordial Fire on me again... I’m so cold...\""]},{"number":2069,"title":"Chapter 2069: Immortal Monarch’s Blessing","paragraphs":["\"Please! I beg of you! Burn me with the True Primordial Fire!\" The Grand Elder continued to beg when Yuan didn’t respond the first time.","\"...\"","\"If I do that, you could die—your physical body, that is,\" Yuan shook his head.","\"I don’t care! I am willing to take that risk!\" The Grand Elder immediately responded without any pause.","Yuan turned to look at Feng Zhenyan, who was still lying on the ground, her body twitching slightly. If not for the euphoric expression on her face, Yuan might have been genuinely concerned for her well-being.","\"Please! The fire! I am freezing to death here!\"The Grand Elder continued to beg.","After a brief moment of silence, Yuan decided to grant the Grand Elder’s wish. After all, it would only work in his favor, helping him bring the Rising Phoenix Clan to his side.","Without uttering a word, Yuan used True Primordial Fire on the Grand Elder for a second time.","\"YES! THE LIGHT! IT’S BACK!\" the Grand Elder exclaimed joyfully, his voice filled with delight as he reveled in the embrace of the invisible flames.","Moments later, the Grand Elder suddenly sat down cross-legged on the ground and closed his eyes, slipping into cultivation.","Feng Zhenyan snapped out of her daze a few hours after the Grand Elder entered cultivation and said, \"It seems the Grand Elder has gained enlightenment. I apologize for any inconvenience this may cause. We’ll definitely compensate you for it.\"","Yuan calmly shook his head and said, \"It’s fine.\"","\"Would you like to wait at our residence? We’ll prepare our finest guest house for you,\" Feng Zhenyan offered quickly.","Yuan glanced at the Grand Elder and shook his head. \"We’ll return at a later date.\"","\"That’s...\" Feng Zhenyan began, not wanting to let them leave so easily, but she couldn’t think of any way to keep them there.","\"There’s no need.\"","The Grand Elder suddenly opened his eyes.","\"You’re done already?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","He stood up and bowed to Yuan, \"Thank you, Esteemed Guest, for granting me a moment of enlightenment. As brief as it may be, I have gained a lot of insight. Now, let’s talk about your reason for coming to the Rising Phoenix Clan, shall we?\"","Yuan nodded and said, \"Then I will get straight to the point. I am here to recruit the Rising Phoenix Clan.\"","\"Recruit... us?\" The Grand Elder lifted his head, surprise written all over his face.","Given their status as one of the Royal Phoenix Clans, Yuan’s offer could have easily been seen as brazen and arrogant—an outright claim that he stood above the Rising Phoenix Clan itself. But as a Primordial Phoenix, Yuan had every right to make such an offer.","Yuan continued calmly, \"If you agree to serve me, I will elevate your bloodline and your standing within the Royal Phoenix Clan to a far greater height.\"","The Grand Elder trembled at the thought of their bloodline being strengthened. Knowing Yuan was a Primordial Phoenix, he had no doubt about his capability. After all, the Primordial Phoenix wasn’t just the most ancient bloodline—it also possessed the power to elevate the bloodlines of other phoenixes.","\"If you doubt my capabilities or sincerity, I’m willing to give you a demonstration,\" Yuan said, shocking them all. \"Bring me one of your phoenixes, and I will strengthen their bloodline.\"","\"Are you really willing to do that for us?!\" The Grand Elder asked.","Yuan silently nodded.","The Grand Elder immediately turned to look at Feng Zhenyan and commanded, \"Bring Feng Haoyu here immediately!\"","\"Yes!\"","Some time later, Feng Zhenyan returned with another figure at her side—a handsome young man with long red hair and striking crimson eyes. He carried himself with a certain quiet charm and a scholar-like demeanor.","Feng Yuxiang immediately recognized the handsome young man—he was the eldest and most talented genius of the Rising Phoenix Clan, the very one they had once tried to pair her with.","Once they arrived, the Grand Elder introduced, \"This is Feng Haoyu, the pride of our Rising Phoenix Clan.\"","\"This junior greets Senior Primordial Phoenix,\" Feng Haoyu said, bowing deeply. Having been briefed by Feng Zhenyan, he knew what was about to take place and showed Yuan the utmost respect.","He then bowed to Feng Yuxiang and said, \"It’s good to see you again, Junior Sister.\"","Naturally, he didn’t forget Feng Yuxiang.","\"Do you know why you were summoned?\" Yuan asked him.","\"I had been briefed.\"","\"Then I will proceed to strengthen your bloodline now.\"","\"W-Wait. What about the preparations?\" the Grand Elder suddenly interjected.","He had expected some elaborate ritual—after all, enhancing a bloodline was no simple feat and was usually an extremely complex and time-consuming process.","\"Don’t treat him like an ordinary phoenix,\" Feng Yuxiang said with a faint smile. \"My Young Master isn’t bound by common sense.\"","\"Well, are you ready?\" Yuan asked Feng Haoyu.","Feng Haoyu knelt on one knee and said firmly, \"I am prepared.\"","Yuan gave a silent nod, then raised a finger and, a moment later, lightly touched it to Haoyu’s forehead.","<Immortal Monarch’s Blessing has activated>","<Target ’Feng Haoyu’ has received your blessing for one year>","After consuming the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence, Yuan had gained a new technique through his Immortal Monarch’s Bloodline—one that allowed him to bestow power and strengthen the bloodlines of beasts.","Feng Haoyu suddenly felt a surge of power flow from Yuan’s fingertips into him, flooding his body with strength unlike anything he had ever felt before.","The change was so profound that even the Grand Elder could immediately sense that something was different about Feng Haoyu.","\"How do you feel?\" Yuan asked, withdrawing his finger.","Feng Haoyu rose to his feet and clenched his fists, a look of awe on his face. \"I’ve never felt better. This overwhelming energy coursing through my body... I was only expecting a slight improvement, so this has far surpassed my expectations.\"","Yuan turned to look at the Grand Elder and continued, \"You’re more than welcome to test his bloodline.\""]},{"number":2070,"title":"Chapter 2070: Heavenly White Valley","paragraphs":["Shortly after Yuan used the Immortal Monarch’s Blessing on Feng Haoyu, the Grand Elder retrieved a crimson needle shaped like a feather and used it to test his blood.","With a quick prick, he collected a single drop of Feng Haoyu’s blood.","Moments later, the Grand Elder excitedly exclaimed, \"It worked! Your bloodline has improved by nearly five percent—not just in strength, but in purity as well!\"","Although five percent might not sound like much, it was actually an extraordinary improvement, given how quickly it had been achieved. In fact, even among the other Royal Phoenix Clans, a one or two-percent increase in bloodline purity could take decades to attain.","\"F-Five percent?!\" Feng Haoyu almost couldn’t believe what he was hearing and nearly collapsed from shock.","However, Yuan quickly added, \"I should remind you that this improvement isn’t permanent. After a year, your bloodline will return to its original state. But if the Rising Phoenix Clan agrees to serve me, I won’t just make it permanent—I’ll raise it far beyond five percent.\"","The Grand Elder trembled at the thought of the entire clan’s bloodline being elevated by more than five percent. It was an offer no phoenix could resist. However, there was one issue.","\"As much as I’d like to decide on the spot, I don’t have the authority to do so. In fact, not even the Matriarch could make such a decision alone. Once she returns, we’ll convene a meeting with all the elders to reach a conclusion. That said, given the circumstances, I believe the outcome will be favorable.\"","\"In that case, I will take my leave now and return exactly one year from today,\" Yuan said, already planning to visit the Heavenly White Tiger Clan in the meantime.","Hearing this, the Grand Elder felt a flicker of worry, fearful that Yuan might leave and never return. Unfortunately, there was truly nothing he could do to prevent it.","Suddenly, Feng Haoyu stepped forward, dropped to his knees, and said firmly, \"Even if the Rising Phoenix Clan does not agree, I am personally willing to serve you.\"","\"What?!\"","Both the Grand Elder and Feng Zhenyan exclaimed in shock.","\"Are you doing this just to impress me?\" Feng Yuxiang asked, narrowing her eyes at him suspiciously. \"Unfortunately for you, my heart, body, and soul already belong to the Young Master.\"","Feng Haoyu chuckled at her assumption and calmly shook his head. \"I don’t mean to sound rude, but I have no interest in you. That idea was my mother’s doing from the start.\"","\"Then what’s your reason for wanting to serve me?\" Yuan asked.","With a serious expression, Feng Haoyu responded without hesitation, \"My instincts.\"","\"You have good instincts.\" Yuan smiled. \"Very well. If you wish to serve me, I won’t disagree.\"","\"Thank you, Young Master.\"","\"Then I will return in a year. Until then.\" Yuan left with Feng Yuxiang shortly later.","Once Yuan had left, Feng Haoyu turned to the Grand Elder and said, \"I’m sorry if my decision makes things more difficult for the clan, but I truly believe in this. The moment I first saw him, I could tell there was something extraordinary about him, and his abilities only confirmed it.\"","The Grand Elder shook his head and said, \"There’s no need to apologize. If I have to be honest, I also wanted to do the same, but I didn’t have the courage.\"","After leaving the Rising Phoenix Clan’s territory, Yuan said, \"They weren’t bad. I was expecting much worse.\"","\"You just haven’t been with them long enough to see their flaws. While they’re not bad people, they’re a hassle to deal with,\" said Feng Yuxiang.","\"Who isn’t a hassle nowadays? I bet you were also a handful before going to the lower heavens,\" Yuan chuckled.","Feng Yuxiang could only lower her head in silence.","\"Anyway, let’s head to the Heavenly White Tiger Clan now,\" he said. \"Hopefully, it won’t take longer than a year.\"","\"Fortunately, there is a teleportation device near their territory, so it won’t take long to arrive at their territory,\" said Feng Yuxiang.","Once they arrived at the nearest city with a teleportation device, Yuan said to the operator, \"Heavenly White Valley.\"","Some time later, Yuan and Feng Yuxiang arrived at the Heavenly White Valley—a vast expanse blanketed in a thin veil of white mist, almost like they were standing on clouds.","The spiritual energy in this area was incredibly dense, much more than even the Rising Phoenix Clan’s territory.","\"So, how are you going to approach them?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","\"Since their ancestor was one of the Nine Divine Supreme, there’s only one way to approach them,\" he said.","\"You’re really going as the Immortal Monarch? Won’t that cause a huge commotion once it’s revealed?\" Feng Yuxiang asked, raising an eyebrow.","\"Who said anything about revealing it to everyone?\" Yuan replied calmly. \"I’ll only show it to a select few. And even if word does get out, it was bound to happen sooner or later anyway.\"","\"I only hope the Heavenly White Tiger Clan still respects the Immortal Monarch. It has been countless years, after all.\"","\"Should I hide in your Dantian?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","Yuan pondered for a moment before shaking his head.","\"No need.\"","He smiled and continued, \"We still have some business with Bai Xutao, after all.\"","Although the Heavenly White Tiger Clan ruled over the entire Heavenly White Valley, their main residence lay deep within a massive valley nestled between two towering, snow-covered mountains.","The Heavenly White Valley teemed with magical beasts, many of which soared through the skies. So even while flying, they still had to contend with these creatures.","Most of the magical beasts were around the Immortal Ascension level, posing no real threat to Yuan, only a mild inconvenience. However, as they drew closer to the Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s residence, the number of magical beasts diminished significantly.","Suddenly, Yuan spotted a shadowy figure moving swiftly in the distance—its movements sharp and fluid, as if locked in combat. Because the white mist had grown so thick, he could only make out the vague outline of the figure. From what he could see, it appeared quite small—almost the size of a child.","After pondering for a moment, he decided to approach this figure."]},{"number":2071,"title":"Chapter 2071: Bai Sulan","paragraphs":["Chapter 2071: Bai Sulan","As Yuan drew closer, he realized there were actually two figures—one a small, human-like silhouette and the other resembling a massive bull.","Once he was close enough to see clearly, Yuan spotted a little girl with short black-and-white hair wielding a metal rod, locked in a fierce battle with a red bull radiating the aura of a peak Immortal Ascension beast. Yet, on closer inspection, it was clear the girl was merely toying with the bull, despite her cultivation being only at the fifth level of Immortal Ascension.","Her metal rod was also cloaked in weapon aura, and each swing sent visible ripples coursing through the air.","The little girl, who had been gleefully toying with the bull, suddenly paused when she sensed Yuan’s presence. Then, as if she’d discovered a new plaything, she turned her attention back to the bull and ended the fight with a single, decisive strike to its head, killing it instantly.","“Are you lost, handsome brother?” The little girl faced Yuan and asked, her face wearing a playful smile.","“Something like that. I’m looking for the Heavenly White Tiger Clan. Do you know the way?” Yuan asked.","“Of course. That’s my home, after all,” nodded the little girl. “But what business do you have there? Ah! Are you looking for a mate? Unless you’re really strong, you won’t be able to attract my Senior Sisters even if you’re handsome.”","Yuan raised an eyebrow at her unusual words, but then he recalled the Heavenly White Tiger’s lustful nature.","“Actually, I have some business with Bai Ning. Do you know her?”","The little girl’s eyes widened at the unexpected name, and she repeated in a surprised voice, “You’re looking for Senior Sister Ning?”","He nodded.","The little girl shook her head and sighed, “Don’t even bother, handsome brother. Senior Sister Ning is way out of your league. And even if you’re the most talented individual in the Nine Heavens, she only has eyes for someone you can never replace.”","“Oh? And who might that be?” Yuan asked, deciding to play along since he found it amusing.","“That would be the Immortal Monarch, of course!” the little girl declared. “Everyone knows Senior Sister Ning is obsessed with him. Even though he’s long gone, she still only has him in her eyes.”","“And why is she so fascinated with the Immortal Monarch? It’s not like they’ve ever met,” Yuan asked.","The little girl shrugged, “How would I know? I am not her.”","She continued, “Anyway, if you’re looking for Senior Sister Ning, you’re only wasting your time.”","“In that case, is Bai Xutao home?” Yuan then asked.","The little girl looked at him with a horrified expression and slowly backed away. “Handsome brother... You actually swing that way?”","Yuan sighed, “I’m not here to mate. I just have some unfinished business with them.”","“Oh... why didn’t you say so then? Senior Brother Xutao is currently at home, but you probably won’t be able to see him.”","“Why not?”","“Because he’s been in closed cultivation for the last several years. Something happened when he went to the lower heavens, and he’s been training like crazy since then.”","“That sounds terrible. What did he experience?”","“No clue. He refuses to tell us, so it’s most likely something embarrassing. According to Senior Sister Ning, he would’ve died if she hadn’t shown up in time.”","“Poor guy. He must’ve had a hard time,” said Yuan.","“Well, he’s a known troublemaker, so don’t feel too sorry for him. He probably deserved whatever happened to him.”","Yuan smiled and said, “I’m Tian Yang. What should I call you?”","The little girl smiled back and introduced herself, “I’m Bai Sulan.”","“Then, can you bring me to the Heavenly White Tiger Clan? I’ll be in your debt.”","Though they knew the Heavenly White Tiger Clan was located in the Heavenly White Valley, they didn’t know the exact location, and Yuan didn’t want to waste time wandering around.","Bai Sulan didn’t immediately respond and pondered in silence.","“I don’t mind, but you’ll have to wait until I am finished with my trial,” she said. “I cannot return home until I am finished, after all.”","It was common practice for powerful families to send their inexperienced members out on trials to help them gain real-world experience, and Bai Sulan was currently in the middle of this trial.","“How long will that take? I’m short on time,” Yuan said.","“It won’t be too long. I am almost finished. I just need to slay one more magical beast to finish the trial,” she said.","“Alright, I’ll follow along. Let me speak with my companion real quick.”","“Okay.”","Yuan returned to Feng Yuxiang, who was waiting at a distance, and explained the situation to her.","“I guess a small detour is fine. It’ll be much easier for us to approach the Heavenly White Tiger Clan if we have one of them with us, too,” she said.","Yuan returned to Bai Sulan shortly later with Feng Yuxiang.","“Your companion... is a phoenix?” Bai Sulan’s eyes widened in surprise as she recognized Feng Yuxiang’s identity from her unique scent alone.","Though she tried to maintain a brave front, her body betrayed her true feelings, trembling slightly with fear.","“Why are you looking at me like I’m about to eat you?” Feng Yuxiang asked, raising an eyebrow.","“I-It’s just... this is my first time meeting a phoenix...” Bai Sulan replied timidly.","“Don’t worry, she won’t do anything to you.”","Bai Sulan nodded with stiff movements.","“So, where are we going to go for your trial?” Yuan then asked.","“The Phantasm Serpent’s Nest,” she answered.","“Ah, I almost forgot...”","Bai Sulan suddenly turned to the corpse of the bull she had defeated moments ago and casually tossed its head into her spatial ring.","“I need evidence, or it won’t count,” she subconsciously explained her actions to Yuan.","A few moments later, Bai Sulan transformed into a massive white tiger and said, “Try not to fall behind.”","Then, she shot forward, her speed so great that it left a trail of afterimages in her wake.","Join Privilege for 50 Adv Chapters! Only Available in the App!"]},{"number":2072,"title":"Chapter 2072: Bai Sulan(2)","paragraphs":["When Bai Sulan sped off, Yuan and Feng Yuxiang immediately chased after her.","\"Hey, how old are you?\" Yuan asked her as they traveled the misty mountain valley.","\"I’m almost eight hundred this year,\" she calmly responded.","Yuan was caught off guard by her answer and said, \"Eight hundred years? You’re even older than me.\"","\"Really?\" Bai Sulan looked at him with intrigue, almost as if she was seeing someone younger than her for the first time.","He nodded.","\"But why do you have the appearance of a little kid?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","\"Because I am still a child. In our clan, we don’t become adults until we reach 2,000 years old,\" Bai Sulan explained.","\"Two thousand years, huh? That’s quite low compared to some of the other bloodlines out there,\" Feng Yuxiang remarked.","Some bloodlines required tens of thousands—if not hundreds of thousands—of years of experience before one could even be considered an adult.","\"Can you tell me more about this trial of yours?\" Yuan then asked.","Bai Sulan nodded and explained, \"In the Heavenly White Tiger Clan, we’re all required to go out and hunt specific magical beasts as part of our trials. We have to complete one trial every hundred years until we reach adulthood.\"","\"Each trial increases in difficulty, and I am currently on my eighth trial,\" she added.","\"What happens if you fail a trial?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","\"Then we’re deemed defects and executed for staining the bloodline,\" Bai Sulan replied calmly, as if it were the most ordinary thing in the world.","\"Executed for failing a trial...? That’s not right,\" Yuan said while shaking his head.","Yet, Feng Yuxiang didn’t seem surprised in the slightest.","\"The Heavenly White Tiger Clan has no use for the weak,\" said Bai Sulan. \"If we don’t want to be disposed of, we’ll need to succeed.\"","Due to how fast the Heavenly White Tiger Clan increases its population, they believed it would be for the best to cull those unworthy of carrying their prestigious bloodline. In fact, many were disposed of even before their first trial for having an insufficient bloodline.","However, this harsh reality wasn’t unique to the Heavenly White Tiger Clan, and similar ruthless practices existed among many other powerful bloodlines as well. After all, this would save them a lot of time and resources, allowing them to invest in those truly worthy.","\"Young Master, you grew up among humans, so you wouldn’t know, but this kind of practice is very common in the world of beasts,\" Feng Yuxiang explained. \"Especially among the stronger clans, as this is how they preserve resources and ensure they produce only the best of the best.\"","\"To many, our bloodline is everything, and having an inferior bloodline is akin to having no talents for humans.\"","\"I understand the reasoning behind it, but I don’t have to accept it or like it.\"","Feng Yuxiang sighed, \"Unfortunately, there’s not much you can do about it... Unless you repeat what the Immortal Monarch did during his era.\"","\"You mean bringing most of the beast clans under my control?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","She silently nodded.","\"I’ll think about it,\" he said, seriously contemplating it.","Feng Yuxiang smiled, but she didn’t say anything else.","A few days later, Bai Sulan came to a halt as they finally arrived at the Phantasm Serpent’s Nest—a large cave hidden beneath one of the countless mountains scattered throughout the Heavenly White Valley.","Bai Sulan returned to her human form and retrieved her metal rod.","\"I’ll be right back. You can wait here for me. It shouldn’t take too long,\" she said to them.","\"Are you sure you want to go inside alone?\" Yuan asked.","\"Yes. Don’t worry about me.\"","Bai Sulan calmly strolled into the cave a moment later, her small figure soon vanishing into the thick mist that drifted out from within.","\"I have a bad feeling about this...\" Yuan muttered.","\"I’m sure she’ll be fine.\" Feng Yuxiang said.","However, Yuan wanted to be certain, so he swept the entire cave with his divine sense. He immediately detected several large snakes with pearlescent scales scattered throughout the cavern, most of them between the seventh and ninth levels of Immortal Ascension.","’Since she could toy with a beast at the peak of Immortal Ascension, she should be fine...’ Yuan thought to himself and stopped thinking about it.","He sat down and closed his eyes, waiting patiently for Bai Sulan’s return.","Two days later, his eyes snapped open as the ground began to shake beneath him. Turning around, he saw the entire mountain quivering, and a moment later, a powerful pressure filled the air.","\"This pressure belongs to a being at the True Immortal realm!\" Feng Yuxiang exclaimed.","BOOM!","Before they could even react, the entire mountain suddenly erupted, shattering outward as if a massive bomb had detonated within it.","Then, a massive serpent figure emerged within the swirling mist, its size nearly rivaling that of the mountain itself.","\"Where the hell did that thing come from?\" Yuan muttered in surprise. He had already scanned the entire mountain with his divine sense, and there was simply no way he could have overlooked such a massive and powerful entity.","However, he didn’t have time to dwell on it, as there was something far more important demanding his attention.","\"Bai Sulan! Are you okay?!\" He shouted, his voice echoing in every direction.","\"...\"","Silence. There was no response.","\"Young Master! Over there!\" Feng Yuxiang suddenly shouted, pointing toward the serpent’s head. The mist had parted just enough for them to see a bloodied white tiger trapped between its massive jaws.","Yuan clicked his tongue in annoyance, then immediately summoned Number One Under Heaven. Without a moment’s hesitation, he launched an attack on the serpent.","With his Silver Immortal cultivation, a mere True Immortal was no match for him. It took only a few seconds for Yuan to completely defeat the serpent.","After slicing the serpent’s body into countless pieces, Yuan retrieved Bai Sulan, who was unconscious but still alive."]},{"number":2073,"title":"Chapter 2073: Familiar Inscriptions","paragraphs":["After saving Bai Sulan, Yuan placed her on the ground and quickly fed her some medicine.","Then he realized that he didn’t have any on him since he mainly relied on his regenerative abilities and didn’t need them. Fortunately, Feng Yuxiang was there, and she had plenty on her.","\"What happened to me...? Am I dead?\" Bai Sulan mumbled as she slowly opened her eyes.","\"You’re still alive,\" Yuan responded.","Her eyes snapped open, and she quickly sat up.","\"T-The Phantasm Serpent! What happened to it?!\" she asked him.","\"I took care of it. Are you going to complain and say that you could’ve defeated it yourself?\"","Bai Sulan shook her head and said, \"No, why would I say that? That thing was beyond my league.\"","After a moment of silence, she looked at him and said, \"Thank you, handsome little brother. You saved my life.\"","\"Little brother, huh?\" Yuan smiled.","\"Well, you are younger than I.\"","A moment later, Yuan turned to look at where the mountain had once been, and he noticed a massive hole in the ground.","\"So that’s where it came from...\" he muttered.","Bai Sulan nodded and explained, \"I was hunting the Phantasm Serpents when the ground suddenly started shaking. Before I knew it, that thing came out of the ground with its mouth wide open. That’s the last thing I remember before waking up and seeing you.\"","Yuan looked at the tunnel again and used divine sense to scan it.","After a brief moment of silence, he smiled and said, \"I’ll be right back.\"","Then he turned and walked toward the gaping hole in the ground. Without hesitation, he leapt in, leaving Bai Sulan staring after him in stunned disbelief.","\"What’s he doing?\" Bai Sulan asked Feng Yuxiang.","\"I don’t know, but he’ll be fine.\"","After jumping into the tunnel, Yuan followed the winding path, retracing the serpent’s movements step by step.","Eventually, he reached the end of the tunnel, which opened into a vast underground cavern that appeared to be the serpent’s lair.","The air was thick with a pungent scent, and piles of bones from all kinds of magical beasts were scattered throughout the cavern.","However, what truly caught Yuan’s attention was the intricate carving on the wall at the far end of the cavern. Upon closer inspection, he realized it wasn’t just a wall—it was actually a massive sealed gate, and there was a powerful formation protecting it.","Yuan approached the sealed gate and spoke out loud, \"Yu Ning, can you take a look at the formation?\"","She responded a few moments later, \"There are several defensive formations protecting this gate. All of them are between level eight and nine. Whatever is behind it... it must be extremely valuable, perhaps even priceless.\"","\"What are the chances of you cracking the formations?\" Yuan then asked.","\"None. This is way beyond me, even during my peak days,\" she sighed.","\"So I will have to force it open, huh?\"","Without hesitation, Yuan drew Number One Under Heaven and struck the gate with all his strength, making the entire cavern quake from the force. Hell, even Feng Yuxiang and Bai Sulan felt the tremor even though they were thousands of miles away.","\"T-That was extremely reckless, Young Master!\" Yu Ning exclaimed afterward. \"What if the defensive formations had retaliated?!\"","Fortunately, there was no response from the formations, but the gates remained sealed.","Yuan smiled and said, \"I struck it because I couldn’t feel anything from it—not even a hint of danger.\"","\"Still, you should warn me before you do something like that next time. It’s bad for the heart—soul,\" she sighed.","\"Alright.\"","Yuan turned his focus back to the gate, studying its intricate inscriptions.","\"These markings... they look familiar,\" he muttered to himself.","Then, his eyes widened in realization, and he exclaimed, \"That’s it! Han Zexian’s Cavern!\"","Though it wasn’t the exact same, the inscriptions around this gate resembled the ones found in Han Zexian’s Cavern—the method to contact an Outer God.","’Whatever is behind this gate is likely connected to the Outer Gods... I need to get inside—but if brute force won’t work...’","Yuan narrowed his eyes. For now, the only option was to hone his skills as an Array Master and unlock it properly.","Suddenly, the entire cavern began to shake violently as an ominous presence flooded the space, thick and oppressive.","Yuan immediately put distance between himself and the sealed gate, which was now leaking an ominous aura.","BANG! BANG! BANG!","The gate shuddered under three thunderous strikes from the other side, each impact shaking the entire cavern even more violently.","BANG! BANG! BANG!","Whatever was pounding on the gate didn’t stop, as if it were desperately trying to break free—or to announce its presence to the world outside.","\"How creepy...\" Yuan muttered, shaking his head as he lowered his guard when it was clear whatever was inside wouldn’t be breaking out anytime soon.","He stopped paying attention to the gate and began looking around the cavern with more scrutiny.","Once he was unable to find anything of interest, he decided to leave.","However, just as he turned to leave, Yuan found himself unable to move, almost as if something unseen was holding him in place.","Then, as if sensing Yuan’s attempt to leave, the entity behind the gate began pounding even harder, each impact echoing with greater force. It was to the point that Yuan worried the entire cavern might collapse.","Yuan sighed before shouting at it, \"What the hell do you want me to do?! Unless you have a method to help me open the seal, stop causing such a ruckus!\"","Surprisingly, the banging stopped.","’It understood my words?’ Yuan swallowed nervously.","\"Knock once if you understand me,\" Yuan spoke to it again.","Bang!","\"Knock twice if you’re a human.\"","\"...\"","\"Knock once if you’re an Outer God.\"","BANG!","Yuan’s eyes widened with surprise at this response.","\"There’s an Outer God behind this door...? What in heaven’s name is this place?\" he mumbled in a dazed voice."]},{"number":2074,"title":"Chapter 2074: Sealed Outer God","paragraphs":["After a brief silence, Yuan spoke again, his voice calm yet tinged with amusement. \"Well, Outer God or not, there’s nothing I can do about this situation. And if you really are an Outer God, you wouldn’t be trapped behind this door by a few formations. Aren’t you lot supposed to be all-powerful?\"","BANG!","In response, the Outer God slammed against the gate, and in the very next instant, every formation protecting it shattered like fragile glass.","Yuan was jumpscared and immediately distanced himself from the gate.","However, nothing happened even after many moments, almost as if the formations had no effect on the gates in the first place.","\"It appears that the formations weren’t holding it back in the first place, but something else,\" Yu Ning muttered.","\"The hell? Then what was the point of that?\" Yuan remarked.","\"It was probably made as an assurance, but who really knows...\"","\"If it’s not the formations keeping it inside, then what is...?\" Yuan mumbled as he stared at the sealed gate.","Suddenly, Yuan noticed a trail of red smoke seeping through the narrow gap between the gates. His body instinctively shifted into a battle-ready stance, preparing for whatever was about to emerge.","The smoke began to twist and swirl, slowly forming words until an entire wall of text hovered in the air before Yuan. However, the words weren’t written in any human language and they closely resembled the strange inscriptions carved into the gate itself.","Since Tian Yang had deciphered the inscriptions in Han Zexian’s Cavern, he could somewhat understand the words before him.","\"This is... a technique,\" Yuan muttered with raised eyebrows.","\"A technique?\" Yu Ning repeated.","\"I’m not certain, but I think so.\"","Yuan sat down and closed his eyes after memorizing the entire.","A few hours later, he opened his eyes and spoke, \"It’s definitely a technique, but I don’t understand their language enough to decipher it right now. It will take some time.\"","Yuan stood back up and spoke out loud, \"Why can’t you just use my language? You clearly understand me, so why can’t you use it?\"","\"...\"","After a brief moment of silence, the red smoke began to shift once more.","Then, two massive words formed before him.","\"OPEN SEAL\"","This time, Yuan could read the words.","\"Are you telling me that the technique just now would open the seal to this gate?\"","Bang!","The Outer God acknowledged with a loud bang.","\"So the gate can only be opened from the outside, huh? Anyway, why should I help you escape? You’re an Outer God, and as far as I am aware, you’re nothing but bad news. It would benefit me and the entire world if you remained in there for an eternity.\"","The red smoke changed again, this time forming into a single word.","\"FATE\"","\"...\"","Yuan silently frowned at this word. Despite its vagueness, Yuan knew what the Outer God was trying to say—that they were connected in some way and that fate would lead him to opening the gate eventually.","Although Yuan did not like the idea of unsealing this unknown Outer God, he knew that not all Outer Gods were evil, as he’d recieved help from Shura.","’If it’s true that we’re connected by fate, I will definitely remove the seal and release this Outer God eventually...’ Yuan sighed inwardly.","’Who knows? Maybe I have another Outer God as an ally and just don’t remember. Whatever. I’ll worry about it once I actually decypher the technique.’","\"Can you not tell me the technique using my language?\"","\"...\"","No response.","’If he cannot translate the technique, then it’s likely because the technique would not make sense in our language. A technique used by Outer Gods, huh? How intriguing...’","Then, he spoke a moment later, \"In that case, I can only return here later once I decipher the technique and learn it, so wait a little longer.\"","Bang!","The Outer God acknowledged.","\"Then I’ll leave now.\"","Yuan turned around and left. This time, the Outer God did not try to stop him.","Once Yuan left the cavern, Yu Ning asked him, \"Are you really going to release whatever is inside? I mean, it was probably sealed for a reason, right?\"","\"I doubt it was humans who sealed it. If it’s truly an Outer God, then it was likely sealed by another Outer God. I’m also not sure what I should do. I guess I’ll figure it out as I try to decypher the technique.\"","\"By the way, what’s an Outer God?\" Yu Ning suddenly asked.","Though she’d listened to his conversation with it just now, she didn’t understand its existence.","Yuan shook his head and said, \"I would tell you, but it might destroy your soul.\"","\"So they’re an existence beyond my understanding, huh?\" Yu Ning remarked.","\"You’re quite perceptive.\" Yuan smiled.","\"Probably because I’ve already experience this before.\"","\"You what?\" Yuan suddenly stopped moving.","Yu Ning explained, \"During the Primordial Era, shortly after cultivators gained the ability to traverse the Starry Sky, some claimed to have seen things out there—entities so incomprehensible that those without sufficient soul strength would perish just from hearing about it. Some even began to revere them as gods. I believe they were also called True Rulers of the Universe.\"","\"True Rulers of the Universe...\" Yuan mumbled.","\"What else do you know about them?\"","\"Not much. Since no one could prove their existence—and those who claimed to witness them couldn’t truly share what they’d seen—they eventually faded into myth. Some even consider it nothing more than a hoax,\" she said.","\"Then, once the war with the Celestial Emperor begun, it became irrelevant to most people.\"","\"I see... Well, in that case, there’s a good chance these True Rulers of the Universe are Outer Gods,\" said Yuan.","\"They’re basically beings that exist exclusively within the Starry Sky, so I can’t fathom why one would be sealed here in the Nine Heavens—or what it must have done to be sealed away. They’re also unimaginably powerful. Even a Cultivation God would be like an ant in their eyes.\"","\"A Cultivation God... akin to an ant...?\" Yu Ning whispered, swallowing nervously at his words."]},{"number":2075,"title":"Chapter 2075: Heavenly White Tiger Clan","paragraphs":["After nearly an entire day, Yuan returned to Bai Sulan and Feng Yuxiang’s side.","\"Where did you go?\" Bai Sulan asked, her eyes filled with curiosity.","\"To the serpent’s lair.\"","Bai Sulan continued asking, \"Then did you find any treasures?\"","In her eyes, there was only one reason why Yuan went out of his way to go there, and that reason was to find treasures.","\"No, there was no treasure.\"","\"Then why are you covering up the tunnel?\" Bai Sulan raised her eyebrows in a doubtful manner, as Yuan was currently closing up the hole to the tunnel, clearly trying to hide something.","\"What’s wrong with fixing a massive hole in the ground? I don’t want anyone accidentally falling into it.\"","Bai Sulan’s jaw dropped at his terrible excuse and said a moment later, \"You do realize that we’re deep into the Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s territory, right? Only magical beasts roam this area, and even they’re not stupid enough to fall into such a massive hole.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"If you don’t believe me, you’re free to check it out yourself. There’s really no treasure there.\"","\"...\"","Bai Sulan looked at the hole with intrigue, but she ultimately shook her head and said, \"No, it’s fine. I don’t really care.\"","Yuan then spoke, \"Anyway, what about your trial?\"","Bai Sulan retrieved a Phantasm Serpent corpse from her spatial ring and said, \"Fortunately, I defeated one before that massive serpent ambushed me, so I didn’t fail my trial.\"","\"So you’re ready to return to the Heavenly White Tiger Clan?\" Yuan asked.","She nodded, \"Yes, I can return now.\"","Once Yuan completely filled the hole, he followed Bai Sulan to the Heavenly White Tiger Clan, which took nearly a week of journey.","\"We will arrive at my home soon,\" said Bai Sulan, who was traveling in her beast form.","A few hours later, Yuan and Feng Yuxiang spotted a cluster of white buildings appearing in the distance. As they drew closer, Yuan could sense numerous powerful presences emanating from the area.","\"We’re here!\" Bai Sulan declared.","When they reached the massive gates, the guard there approached Bai Sulan and asked, \"Who are these two with you?\"","\"They’re my friends and savior,\" she said. \"They are also here for Senior Brother Xutao and Senior Sister Ning.\"","\"Your savior...?\" The guard looked at her with raised eyebrows.","\"Yes, they saved me from an accident,\" she said, purposefully not giving too many details as she didn’t want to appear weak.","\"Alright.\"","The guard gave her a quick nod before opening the gates for them.","\"Let’s go, handsome little brother.\" Bai Sulan walked over to Yuan and suddenly held his hand, pulling him toward the entrance.","When she noticed Feng Yuxiang staring at her with a sharp gaze, she chuckled and explained, \"I am doing this so the others won’t bother him. This may sound weird, but handsome little brother here has an attractive scent to him. I fear he might become overwhelmed by the females in our clan if they see him.\"","\"An attractive scent?\" Feng Yuxiang tilted her head closer to Yuan and leaned in, giving him a deep, deliberate sniff.","\"He does smell very good, but I don’t get it—not to say my Young Master isn’t attractive. Or maybe I am just used to it by now,\" she remarked.","\"It’s very subtle, but we Heavenly White Tigers have a strong sense of smell,\" said Bai Sulan.","Once they were inside, Bai Sulan said, \"I’ll bring you to our guest room for now. As for meeting with Senior Sister Ning or Senior Brother Xutao, you’ll have to speak with their servants.\"","\"Sure.\"","As Bai Sulan led them to the guest room, Yuan and Feng Yuxiang could sense numerous presences gathering around them, though none revealed themselves directly.","\"I knew you’d attract the others, but I didn’t expect this many to show up this quickly,\" Bai Sulan remarked when she also noticed their presence.","\"Should I be worried?\" Yuan asked calmly.","\"No... at least not yet,\" Bai Sulan replied. \"We’re still in the outer area, where most of the lower-ranking members live. As long as I’m with you, they won’t dare come too close.\"","\"Lower-ranking?\" Yuan asked.","\"It’s similar to how sects work,\" Bai Sulan explained. \"We’re divided by the quality of our bloodline.\"","\"I’m from the main family, so my status is automatically at the top. Also, while everyone is required to complete trials, those of us in the main family face far harsher requirements, and for us, failure simply isn’t an option, as we are killed for it.\"","\"Meanwhile, the others train as soldiers or servants. If their bloodline meets the standards, they might earn a chance to move up in rank. Oh—and it’s strictly forbidden for those with high-quality bloodlines to breed with lower-quality ones, so only those of the same rank are allowed to mate.\"","To preserve and strengthen their bloodline, it was common for beasts to engage in selective breeding practices like this. Of course, humans weren’t much better, and they simply used talent as their measure instead. That’s why geniuses often look down on those with inferior talent and arranged marriages between two powerful families are incredibly common.","\"What’s the population like in your clan?\" Feng Yuxiang suddenly asked.","Bai Sulan pondered for a moment before responding, \"Around 3,000,000, I guess.\"","\"That’s quite the population...\" Yuan mumbled with a surprised look on his face.","\"That’s because we Heavenly White Tigers often give birth to more than one child at a time. In fact, anything beyond four children is considered abnormal,\" said Bai Sulan.","\"So not only are you guys perverted, but you also have ridiculous reproductive capabilities?\" Feng Yuxiang remarked.","\"P-Perverted...?\" Bai Sulan could only shake her head in silence at Feng Yuxiang’s remark since she wasn’t entirely wrong.","Eventually, they reached the next area, where the middle-ranking members lived.","\"I only have enough authority to bring you this far into our territory. Wait here while I contact Senior Sister Ning and Senior Brother Xutao’s servants for you,\" Bai Sulan said once they arrived at the guest house."]},{"number":2076,"title":"Chapter 2076: Heavenly White Tiger Clan(2)","paragraphs":["Once Yuan and Feng Yuxiang entered the guest house, Bai Sulan retrieved a silver medallion and placed it on the doorstep before leaving to find the servants.","Shortly after Bai Sulan left, the presences that had been shadowing them from a distance finally revealed themselves and began approaching the guest house. However, when they saw Bai Sulan’s medallion resting on the doorstep like a ward for ghosts, these Heavenly White Tigers hesitated to approach the door.","Just as they were preparing to leave, the door swung open and Yuan stepped out to meet the tigers head-on.","At a glance, there were around two hundred of them, all sharing similar traits—white and black hair that marked their lineage. As for the gender ratio, about 90 percent of them were females.","\"How can I help you guys?\" Yuan asked.","The female tigers exchanged glances with each other before one of them spoke, \"Um...Sorry, we didn’t know you were Lady Sulan’s partner.\"","Yuan raised his eyebrows at this remark and said, \"What are you talking about?\"","The tiger pointed at the medallion by his feet and explained, \"That is Lady Sulan’s medallion. It’s a declaration that you belong to her...\"","Yuan looked at the medallion and picked it up.","\"What were you going to do if I weren’t her partner?\" Yuan then asked.","The female tigers exchanged glances again.","\"We wanted to see if you wanted to have some fun...\" one of them eventually responded.","Yuan cleared his throat and said, \"Ah, then I’ll respectfully decline.\"","The female tigers lowered their heads in a dejected manner. As for the men, one of them said, \"We’re here for the lady with you.\"","\"Get lost!\" Feng Yuxiang’s irritated voice rang out from inside the house.","The tigers immediately scattered, scrambling away in a panic.","Yuan then placed Bai Sulan’s medallion back down on the doorstep and returned inside the house.","A few hours later, three figures approached the house.","\"Handsome little brother, I am back.\" Bai Sulan spoke as she knocked on the door.","Yuan opened the door.","\"Welcome back.\"","Bai Sulan and the two servants entered the house shortly after.","\"They are Senior Brother Xutao and Senior Sister Ning’s servants,\" Bai Sulan gestured toward the two female tigers.","The one on the left, who had short hair, bowed and said, \"I am Young Master Xutao’s servant.\"","The one on the right, whose long hair reached all the way to her lower back, followed suit. \"I am Lady Ning’s servant.\"","\"I’d like to meet with your masters,\" said Yuan, going straight to the point.","The short-haired servant responded first, \"I apologize, but Young Master Xutao is currently in closed cultivation and won’t be able to meet you.\"","The long-haired servant then spoke, \"Lady Ning is also in closed cultivation right now.\"","\"Any idea when they’ll come out?\" Yuan asked.","\"No.\" They both shook their heads.","Yuan pondered for a moment before retrieving a jade slip from his spatial ring. He offered it to the long-haired servant and said, \"I’d like to return this to your master.\"","\"This...?\" The servant raised her eyebrows in a puzzled manner.","\"This is—!\"","When she glimpsed inside the jade slip and saw what was inside, her eyes widened with shock and disbelief. She was so shocked that she almost dropped the jade slip.","\"What’s that?\" Bai Sulan asked, her eyes flickering with curiosity.","\"T-This is Lady Ning’s personal logbook...\"","\"A logbook? On what?\"","\"The Immortal Monarch...\"","\"WHAT?!\" Bai Sulan exclaimed, her face filled with bewilderment.","Everyone in the Heavenly White Tiger Clan knew of Bai Ning’s obsession with the Immortal Monarch. It had reached the point where even the Clan Leader had given up trying to convince her to find a suitable partner.","\"Senior Sister Ning actually handed you something so precious? She wouldn’t even let father touch it, let alone borrow it... Unless... you actually stole it from her?\" Bai Sulan looked at Yuan with worry.","Yuan chuckled, \"Of course not. She allowed me to borrow it. If you don’t believe me, you’ll know once you return it to her.\"","The long-haired servant nodded and said, \"I’ll return it to her immediately. Is there anything else you need me for?\"","\"No, you can go.\"","\"I understand.\"","The long-haired servant left shortly after.","\"What about me?\" asked the short-haired servant.","Yuan paused for a moment before asking, \"I’d like to learn more about your master, Bai Xutao. Is that possible?\"","The servant hesitated—sharing such information could easily be seen as betrayal, a crime punishable by death. Yet Yuan was clearly someone important to Bai Ning, and refusing him outright didn’t seem wise.","Noticing this, Bai Sulan spoke, \"She might get in trouble with Bai Xutao if she reveals information about him. I don’t know as much as his personal servant, but I’ll tell you everything I know about him.\"","Yuan nodded, \"Sure.\"","While Bai Sulan revealed everything she knew about Bai Xutao to Yuan, the long-haired servant headed straight to Bai Ning.","Somewhere deep within the Heavenly White Valley, Bai Ning was honing her techniques—each strike demolishing entire mountains with ease. Ever since her humiliating defeat to Yuan, she had been training in this place without rest.","\"Lady Ning, I apologize for interrupting your training, but this is an emergency.\"","The servant dropped to her knees the moment she appeared before her.","\"I don’t care,\" Bai Ning immediately dismissed her.","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, the servant retrieved the jade slip and placed it on the ground.","\"Then I’ll leave this here for when you have time.\"","Bai Ning subconsciously glanced at the jade slip, her eyes narrowing slightly as she caught a familiar scent lingering on it.","The moment she recognized the object, her eyes widened with shock.","Just as the servant stood and turned to leave, Bai Ning suddenly roared, \"STOP RIGHT THERE!\"","The servant was so startled by her voice that she tripped over her own feet and fell face-first to the ground.","As the servant scrambled back to her feet and turned around, she saw Bai Ning charging toward her with a terrifying expression, scaring the living soul out of her."]},{"number":2077,"title":"Chapter 2077: Heavenly White Tiger Clan(3)","paragraphs":["\"L-Lady Ning! I am sorry! I swear I will never disturb you during your training again! Please, spare my humble life!\" The servant immediately went on her knees and began begging for her life, thinking that Bai Ning was going to kill her, judging by her angry expression.","However, Bai Ning stopped in front of the jade slip and picked it up. Once she confirmed the contents inside, she looked at the servant and spoke, \"Why would I kill you? Stand up.\"","\"Yes!\"","The servant immediately stood back up, but her head remained lowered.","\"Tell me, where did you acquire this?\" Bai Ning asked while holding up the jade slip.","\"F-From a guest brought by Young Lady Sulan...\" she quickly replied.","Bai Ning immediately recalled her interaction with Yuan at the Pavilion of Knowledge. Hell, she still had the Immortal Monarch’s blood that was given to her by him.","\"Is he still there?!\" Bai Ning asked.","\"Umm... I think so?\"","\"Bring me to him right now!\" Bai Ning commanded urgently, as if it were a life-or-death matter.","\"Right away!\"","The servant said as she began leading Bai Ning to where she had met Yuan.","Meanwhile, back at the guest house, Bai Sulan had finished telling Yuan everything she knew about Bai Xutao, though most of what she shared painted him as a perpetual troublemaker.","Yuan had hoped to hear something redeeming about Bai Xutao, something that might give him a reason to show leniency, but instead, it only made him dislike Bai Xutao even more.","According to Bai Sulan, Bai Xutao was an infamous predator—and not the kind found in nature. He was a vile scumbag known for harassing females, often relying on force and his privileged background to bend them into submission.","He was so vile that he even terrorized his own people within the Heavenly White Tiger Clan. The only reason he hadn’t faced serious punishment was because he carried a trace amount of their ancestor’s bloodline and was considered the hope of the clan.","While that trace of bloodline was far too weak to have any real effect, the Heavenly White Tiger Clan still hoped to strengthen it through future generations.","\"Why am I not shocked that he’s a true scumbag?\" Feng Yuxiang shook her head with a look of disdain on her face.","Yuan looked at his servant and spoke, \"You must have it hard being his servant.\"","The servant trembled at Yuan’s words, and tears began flowing from her eyes uncontrollably.","\"Huh?\" Yuan did not expect her to cry and didn’t know how to respond.","\"Senior Brother Xutao often changes his servants because he often breaks them,\" Bai Sulan explained. \"Being his servant is basically a death sentence. That said, she holds the current record for staying alive the longest.\"","\"Young Master, you should do everyone a favor and just kill that son of a bitch,\" Feng Yuxiang suddenly cursed out loud.","\"Eh?\" Bai Sulan stared at them with wide eyes, having assumed they were on friendly terms with Bai Xutao.","But before she could ask any questions, someone suddenly pounded on the door—so hard that cracks splintered across its surface.","Bai Sulan immediately went to open the door, and to her surprise, Bai Ning was standing at the doorstep with a serious expression on her face.","\"S-Senior Sister Ning? What are you—\"","\"Where is he?!\" Bai Ning shouted as she stepped inside the house.","\"I am right here,\" Yuan calmly responded as he approached her.","Bai Ning’s eyes widened at Yuan’s handsome appearance.","\"It’s been a while. We last spoke at the Pavilion of Knowledge. Do you remember?\" Yuan asked.","\"Of course, I remember! You think I could forget an event like that after what you gave me?!\" she exclaimed.","\"Since you’re here to find me, does this mean you’re finally going to let me meet the Immortal Monarch?\" she asked, her body trembling uncontrollably with excitement at just the thought of it.","\"I don’t mind letting you meet him, but you’ll have to do something for me first,\" he said.","\"Anything!\" she replied without any hesitation.","\"Bai Xutao. I mentioned that I wanted to speak with him, right? Bring him to me and I’ll let you meet the Immortal Monarch.\"","\"Bai Xuatao...?\" Bai Ning quickly recalled having this conversation with him before.","\"Alright. I’ll bring him to you,\" she immediately agreed.","Before leaving, she turned to glance at Feng Yuxiang, who stood boldly at Yuan’s side.","’Why does she look so familiar? Where have I seen her before?’","It wasn’t just Feng Yuxiang’s appearance that stirred her memory—her scent, too, was strikingly familiar. Yet Bai Ning couldn’t quite put her finger on it. Their past encounter had been brief, and right now, her mind was consumed by something far more important.","Thus, after just a quick glance, Bai Ning stopped paying attention to Feng Yuxiang and left the house.","\"Stay here until I return,\" Bai Ning commanded her servant before leaving.","Once Bai Ning left to fetch Bai Xutao, Feng Yuxiang mumbled, \"She didn’t recognize me...\"","Yuan looked at her and said, \"Well, you’ve changed a lot since then.\"","Yuan returned to his seat shortly after to wait for Bai Ning’s return.","Meanwhile, after leaving, Bai Ning traveled straight to Bai Xutao’s training area, which existed underground beneath a mountain.","Upon arriving before a specific mountain, Bai Ning approached the sealed entrance at the bottom and said to the guard standing before it, \"Tell Bai Xutao to get his ass out here.\"","The guard was baffled by Bai Ning’s sudden appearance and demand.","\"Lady Ning... The Young Lord has ordered that no one is to disturb him unless it’s the Clan Leader. If I disobey, I’ll definitely face a gruesome death,\" the guard said nervously.","Bai Ning fell silent for a moment.","\"I understand,\" she said softly.","But just as the guard let out a sigh of relief, Bai Ning suddenly shot forward, slammed her foot into the sealed entrance, and kicked the door down with a deafening bang."]},{"number":2078,"title":"Chapter 2078: Meeting Bai Xutao Again","paragraphs":["\"L-Lady Ning! What are you doing?!\" The guard exclaimed with a shocked expression on his face after she kicked down the door to Bai Xutao’s training area.","\"You didn’t disobey Xutao’s order since I will be forcing my way to him,\" she said to him.","\"That’s not the issue here...\" the guard wore a look of disbelief.","Bai Ning narrowed her eyes at him and spoke in a threatening voice, \"What? Should I tear one of your limbs to make it more convincing?\"","The guard trembled in fear, and he immediately took several steps back.","\"That won’t be necessary, Lady Ning!\"","Then, without hesitation, the guard punched himself in the face with so much force that he knocked himself out cold.","\"...\"","Bai Ning stared at the guard’s unconscious body for a brief moment before turning around and walking into the cave.","Inside was a long descending staircase that continued for several minutes.","Eventually, Bai Ning arrived before another closed door.","Bai Ning glanced at the metal door for a moment before lifting her slender leg and also kicking it down with a loud bang.","Bai Ning stepped through the shattered entrance into a massive training hall. The space was filled with a wide array of amenities—racks of weapons lined the walls, several cauldrons brimmed with medicinal pills, and further in, a luxurious bathtub sat quietly.","In the middle of this training hall was none other than Bai Xutao, who appeared to be in a vicious battle against a ghost as he constantly swung at the empty air before him.","Bai Ning approached him, but before she could even call out to him, Bai Xutao suddenly lunged in her direction with immense killing intent.","Judging by Bai Xutao’s blank expression, he was likely too absorbed in his training and instinctively attacked Bai Ning.","\"You dare bare your claws at me? You must have forgotten how to behave in just a few short years!\" Bai Ning sneered without an ounce of concern within her.","Then, she raised her hand and gave a powerful slap to Bai Xutao in the face once he was close enough.","Pap!","Bai Xutao was sent flying instantly, his body slamming into the metal wall moments later.","\"Which fucking bitch dares to disturb my training?!\" Bai Xutao cursed out loud the moment he snapped out of his daze.","However, when his eyes snapped to Bai Ning, they immediately widened with horror.","\"S-Senior Sister Ning? What are you doing here...?\" He asked her in a timid voice, even appearing as harmless as possible before her presence.","\"Come with me,\" she said, not even bothering to offer an explanation.","\"What is this about? I don’t have that much time to spare. Once I finish my training, I am immediately going to return to the lower heaven to find that bastard who humiliated me,\" he said.","\"Are you questioning me?\" Bai Ning narrowed her eyes at him.","\"I-I am just asking for clarification... I have received Father’s approval, too.\"","\"You can get your revenge later. This matter is much more important, and it probably won’t take long. If you dare dillydally any longer, I’ll forcefully drag you out of here.\"","\"Ok, ok! I will come with you! Just give me a minute to clean up...\"","Sometime later, Bai Xutao followed Bai Ning outside. The first thing he noticed was the guard who was still lying unconscious by the entrance.","\"What a useless bastard...\" he mumbled under his breath.","As they traveled to Yuan, Bai Ning said, \"Listen here, you troublemaker. We’re about to meet someone incredibly important. I don’t know why he wants to meet you, but you will treat him like you treat our father. If I dare sense any disrespect from you, I’ll make you beg me to kill you.\"","Bai Xutao wore a look of disbelief on his face as he realized the reason for Bai Ning’s appearance.","\"I have never seen you treat someone with such importance. Who the hell is this guy, and what does he want with me?\" Bai Xutao frowned.","Bai Ning suddenly stopped moving and turned around to slap Bai Xutao in the face.","\"That will be my first and last warning to you. Don’t you dare use that disrespectful tone before him. Also, I already said I don’t know why he wants to meet you, but from the sound of it, you seem to know each other.\"","Bai Xutao rubbed his face with a defeated face, looking like he had been wronged.","’Who the hell is this bastard? I don’t recall knowing anyone so important to her... It’s not like we’re meeting the Immortal Monarch, so why is she acting like this?’ Bai Xutao sighed inwardly, no longer daring to speak out loud.","Eventually, they arrived at their destination.","\"I have returned with Bai Xutao.\" Bai Ning knocked on the door this time to announce their presence.","Bai Xutao swallowed nervously as they waited for the door to open.","The door opened a few moments later, and it was Bai Xutao’s servant who greeted them.","\"The esteemed guest is waiting inside...\"","Bai Ning entered the house without a hint of hesitation, her steps firm and confident.","Meanwhile, Bai Xutao stood motionless at the threshold, a strange expression twisting his face, as though he’d forgotten how to move.","’What is this feeling...?’ he wondered, staring at the open doorway.","His instincts screamed at him—warning him not to step inside.","\"Bai Xutao! What are you doing? Hurry up and come inside!\" Bai Ning’s voice snapped him out of his daze, and before he realized, Bai Xutao had entered the house.","The sense of dread became undeniable and was almost suffocating, but Bai Xutao ignored it and subconsciously followed Bai Ning’s presence.","Once he entered the living room with Bai Ning, Bai Xutao could see three other individuals there. He instantly recognized Bai Sulan, but he didn’t instantly recognize Feng Yuxiang or Yuan.","’Who the hell is this guy? I definitely don’t know him!’ Bai Xutao exclaimed inwardly after seeing Yuan’s handsome face."]},{"number":2079,"title":"Chapter 2079: Meeting Bai Xutao Again(2)","paragraphs":["When Bai Xutao saw Yuan, his eyebrows immediately raised in a puzzled manner. Bai Ning made it sound like they knew each other, but he was certain that he’d never seen Yuan before in his life.","His gaze slowly shifted to Feng Yuxiang, whose beauty caught his attention. However, he didn’t immediately recognize her, as Feng Yuxiang’s aura and scent had changed drastically since she awakened her bloodline and got rid of the curse.","Noticing Bai Xutao’s lustful gaze on her body, Feng Yuxiang had the urge to strangle him to death, but controlled herself.","\"What are you doing? Greet the esteemed guest,\" Bai Ning suddenly spoke.","\"Uh... I greet... um... who are you?\" Bai Xutao couldn’t help himself and asked.","Bai Ning snapped her head to glare at him with a threatening gaze, even clenching her fists in anger. After all, she’d given Yuan’s name to him before they arrived.","However, Yuan spoke before she could act, \"It’s only been a few years and you’ve already forgotten about me, old friend?\"","\"A few years?\" Bai Xutao became even more confused, as he’d spent the last few years training inside the Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s territory and hadn’t met any new individuals.","Yuan calmly nodded before leaving his seat to approach Bai Xutao.","Then, using voice transmission, Yuan spoke to Bai Xutao, \"Have you already forgotten about our time together in the Third Heaven? How you were utterly humiliated by me?\"","Bai Xutao’s face twisted in horror, his eyes wide with shock and disbelief. Without a moment’s hesitation, he instinctively unleashed his cultivation and launched an attack at Yuan.","\"Y-You?!\" Bai Ning gasped, her voice laced with fear. She was so stunned by his action that her body refused to move.","Yuan calmly raised his hand, intercepting Bai Xutao’s strike with a single motion. His fingers closed around the fist, halting the attack effortlessly.","\"W-What?!\" Bai Xutao’s eyes widened in disbelief.","He tried to pull away, but no matter how much strength he used, his hand wouldn’t budge from Yuan’s grasp. It was like being caught in an unbreakable vice.","\"What is the meaning of this, Bai Xutao, you little bastard?!\"","Bai Ning finally snapped out of her daze. In a flash, she appeared beside Bai Xutao, seizing him by the neck and yanking him away. Yuan released his grip without resistance, allowing her to drag him away.","\"If you don’t have a good explanation, I’ll snap your neck where I stand!\" she roared.","\"W-Wait! Why are you helping him?! He’s the one who attacked me in the lower heavens!\" Bai Xutao exclaimed.","\"Bullshit!\" Bai Ning didn’t believe him even for a second. \"That masked individual had the scent of a dragon! Tian Yang here is clearly a human! Also, he was only a Spirit King a few years ago!\"","Bai Xutao’s gaze suddenly landed on Feng Yuxiang, and his eyes widened with realization. He then pointed at her and shouted, \"T-That’s the phoenix who offended me in the lower heavens! I’m sure you met her, too!\"","Bai Ning turned to look at Feng Yuxiang and frowned. However, she couldn’t believe it.","\"Nonsense! That phoenix was nowhere near the realm of True Immortal! Her scent is also different!\"","\"Young Master, may I?\" Feng Yuxiang suddenly stepped forward and asked.","Yuan calmly nodded, \"Go ahead. He’s all yours.\"","\"What?\" Bai Ning raised her eyebrows in confusion. However, before she could even ask, Feng Yuxiang shot forward like a bolt of lightning, seizing Bai Xutao by the face. With a single, fluid motion, she tore him from Bai Ning’s grasp and slammed his body into the wall with bone-rattling force.","Bai Xutao coughed up a mouthful of blood, though his injuries weren’t anything serious.","However, Feng Yuxiang didn’t stop there. She yanked him away from the wall, only to slam his face into it again—relentlessly, over and over—until the entire wall crumbled beneath the repeated blows.","\"So you enjoy bullying the weak and preying on women, huh?!\" Feng Yuxiang snarled. \"Today, I’ll return the favor—for me and for Xi Meili—and turn you into a roasted tiger!\"","With a burst of fiery laughter, she hurled Bai Xutao’s body into the next wall, shaking the entire house.","\"Senior Tian Yang...\" Bai Ning turned to look at Yuan for answers.","\"What’s wrong?\" Yuan asked with a nonchalant expression on his face.","\"I understand that you’re upset he attacked you, but can you tell her to calm down? I’ll make sure he recieves the proper punishment,\" she said. \"It won’t be a good look on our clan if we let outsiders harm our members... whether they deserve it or not.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan sighed, \"That is what’s wrong with the current Heavenly White Tiger Clan. You guys have fallen too much.\"","\"What are you...?\"","\"Bai Xutao has harmed so many people, causing irreparable damage to your clan’s image and reputation. Yet, you continue to protect him like he’s some priceless treasure. Why? Because he has a miniscule amount of your ancestor’s blood in him? How pathetic.\"","Yuan stared at Bai Ning’s dumbfounded face with a calm expression as he continued, \"I’m sure you know what happened to your ancestor because of his unruly behavior. If your ancestor can be punished, then what about Bai Xutao? Are you trying to say that he’s even more important than your ancestor?\"","\"I...\" Bai Ning gritted her teeth and clenched her fists in frustration.","\"Even if I want to punish him, I do not have that authority. Only our Clan Head can make such a decision.\"","One of the reasons Bai Ning treated Bai Xutao so harshly was because it was all she could do. Any further, and their father would undoubtedly punish her. Although she was the clan’s top genius and held more status than Bai Xutao at the moment, her bloodline was still inferior to his, and that was what truly mattered.","\"That’s just an excuse. A poor one, at that.\" Yuan shook his head.","Meanwhile, Feng Yuxiang’s relentless beating of Bai Xutao had grown so intense that the entire guest house collapsed under the pressure."]},{"number":2080,"title":"Chapter 2080: Chaos Within the Heavenly White Tiger Clan","paragraphs":["After beating Bai Xutao until he was almost unconscious, Feng Yuxiang released him and said, \"Go ahead and heal yourself. I don’t want to end this too quickly.\"","Hearing this, Bai Xutao immediately distanced himself from her and consumed a recovery pill. However, he was only a Golden Immortal while Feng Yuxiang was a True Immortal. The difference between their cultivation was simply too great for him to do anything to her.","Meanwhile, their commotion attracted the attention of those around them, but nobody dared to approach them after realizing Bai Xutao and Bai Ning were there and only watched from afar.","After healing himself, Bai Xutao immediately transformed into his beast form, and despite the difference in their cultivation, he attempted to fight back.","\"Good! If you’d given up too quickly, my revenge wouldn’t feel as satisfying!\" Feng Yuxiang laughed out loud as she resumed his beating.","Her phoenix flames scattered everywhere like fireworks, engulfing the entire area with flames. However, she wasn’t using True Primordial Fire, so these flames didn’t do too much damage.","Bai Xutao was relentlessly scorched by her flames. With each blow, his body charred black, only for him to hastily consume a recovery pill and repeat the cycle, just as he’d done during his battle with Yuan.","Eventually, Feng Yuxiang summoned the True Primordial Fire. The moment it touched Bai Xutao, his screams pierced the heavens. These flames were relentless, clinging to him like a curse, burning not just his body but reaching deep into the core of his soul.","\"Senior Sister! Please! Help me!\" Bai Xutao pleaded for her help.","Bai Ning gritted her teeth and urged Yuan, \"That is enough! You’re really going to kill him at this rate!\"","Yuan’s face remained nonchalant as he responded in a calm tone, \"What if we want to kill him? What are you going to do about it?\"","Bai Ning roared, \"Why are you doing this?! Are you really related to the Immortal Monarch?!\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes and replied, \"My precious companion nearly lost her life because of him. Not only that, but he’d harmed many innocent lives when he attacked them, not to mention the countless other lives he’d ruined.\"","\"SISTER! PLEASE!!!\" Bai Xutao continued to scream for help.","Bai Ning could no longer afford to remain still. Regardless of her hatred toward Bai Xutao, allowing his death would seal her own fate as well.","However, Yuan blocked her path and said, \"If you want to save him, you’ll have to get past me.\"","\"Are you trying to start a war with the entire Heavenly White Tiger Clan?!\" she roared.","However, Yuan didn’t say anything and retrieved Number One Under Heaven.","Bai Ning’s eyes widened with shock after seeing his weapon.","\"Y-You are—!\" She almost couldn’t believe her eyes.","\"That’s right. This will be our third time fighting each other, and it will also be your third time losing.\"","\"YOU BASTARD!!!\" Bai Ning roared, her True Immortal cultivation erupting like a dam bursting under pressure.","\"How dare you trick me using the Immortal Monarch’s name?! I’ll skin you alive!\"","In the next moment, Bai Ning and Yuan clashed, their exchanges unleashing violent ripples that tore through the Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s territory. Buildings crumbled under the pressure, and the clan’s members fled in panic like frightened cats.","’This bastard’s cultivation went from Spirit Emperor to Silver Immortal in just a few years?! What the hell has he been doing since our last encounter?!’ Bai Ning was shocked by Yuan’s cultivation progress, not to mention his overwhelming prowess.","Despite many years of relentless training, Bai Ning found herself utterly overwhelmed by Yuan. Forced entirely on the defensive, she couldn’t even catch a glimpse of an opening to counterattack.","Yet, Yuan wasn’t even fighting with all of his strength and was merely toying with her like he’d done before. Of course, Bai Ning realized this, but there was nothing she could do.","\"What’s happening...? How did things end up like this...?\" Bai Sulan muttered, her voice dazed as she stood amidst the rubble of the guest house.","Everything happened so quickly that she failed to comprehend the situation.","\"Young Lady, we must leave this place immediately!\" Bai Ning’s servant cried as she grabbed her and swiftly carried her away.","Meanwhile, Bai Xutao’s servant rushed toward the battered figure of her master. She knew all too well that if she didn’t at least try to save him, she would face severe punishment... likely a death sentence.","\"Why are you even helping him after everything he’s done to you?! Get lost if you don’t want to die a pointless death!\" Feng Yuxiang warned her.","\"I’ll still die if I don’t try!\"","Despite only being in the Immortal Ascension realm, the servant rushed to help Bai Xutao.","However, Feng Yuxiang knocked her out before she could even reach him. Then, she sent the servant’s unconscious body far away with a flick of her sleeves.","\"There. You tried.\" Feng Yuxiang mumbled before returning her focus to Bai Xutao, who was attempting to run away while his body was still engulfed in flames.","\"And where do you think you’re going?!\" Feng Yuxiang immediately chased after him.","The commotion from their battle shook the entire Heavenly White Tiger Clan, its intensity so great that it reached even the inner sanctum. Alarmed by the chaos, the elders immediately assumed they were under attack and moved into action. However, they were quite far away and would need several minutes to reach the scene.","Meanwhile, Feng Yuxiang continued to torture Bai Xutao, who had returned to his human form in an attempt to get rid of the fire.","\"Even if I can’t kill you today, I’ll make sure you’ll never harm another woman again!\" Feng Yuxiang snarled, her finger suddenly pointing toward the area between Bai Xutao’s legs.","\"Burn that vile thing away!\" she commanded, and her flames surged forth with murderous intent.","In the next moment, a surge of True Primordial Fire exploded at Bai Xutao’s crotch, incinerating his manhood in an instant and erasing any trace of his identity as a man.","\"!@*#)!@&#(*!@&$\" Bai Xutao let out a bloodcurdling scream, shrill and pitiful like a butchered pig, before collapsing into unconsciousness from the agony."]},{"number":2081,"title":"Chapter 2081: Chaos Within the Heavenly White Tiger Clan(2)","paragraphs":["\"Bai Xutao!\" Bai Ning exclaimed in a terrified voice after seeing his body fall from the sky.","\"Do you even have time to worry about others?\" Yuan blocked her from attempting to approach Bai Xutao again.","\"You! Do you have any idea what you have done?!\" She shouted at him. \"To attack us in the middle of the Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s territory, you’re extremely foolish! Once our elders arrive, you’ll regret attacking us!\"","\"I’ll deal with that when the time comes.\" Yuan smiled before continuing his attack.","Meanwhile, Feng Yuxiang went to catch Bai Xutao’s falling body. She caught him by the leg and dangled him like a butchered chicken.","\"Wake up.\"","\"...\"","Feng Yuxiang used her True Primordial Fire to wake him up when shaking him didn’t work.","\"Ahhh!\" Bai Xutao immediately woke up screaming.","\"Welcome back. Are you ready to continue?\" Feng Yuxiang asked with a sadistic smile on her face.","\"N-No! Please! I’m sorry for what happened before! I swear I won’t ever approach you again!\" Bai Xutao begged.","\"You think I’m doing this just for myself? I’m also acting for those who never had the strength to seek justice!\" Feng Yuxiang laughed coldly. \"We’re just getting started, so don’t you dare die on me too soon!\"","Bai Xutao’s agonized screams returned, echoing like a curse in the ears of all who heard them.","Eventually, the elders and true powerhouses of the Heavenly White Tiger Clan arrived at the scene, only to be struck with shock and terror at the sight that awaited them.","Bai Ning, their number one genius of the younger generation, was being tossed around like a rag doll by a mere human Silver Immortal.","As for Bai Xutao, they failed to recognize him at first. Feng Yuxiang’s flames had reduced him to a scorched husk: naked, hairless, and with every inch of his skin charred black.","\"What in heaven’s name is going on here?!\" one of the elders snapped, his 2nd-level God Ascension cultivation erupting forth. The surge of power flooded the area with immense pressure, instantly bringing Yuan and Feng Yuxiang to a halt.","\"E-Eleventh Elder! We’re being attacked! These are the bastards that nearly killed Bai Xutao when he went to the lower heavens!\" Bai Ning revealed to them.","\"What!? Surround them!\"","Thousands of Immortals surrounded Yuan and Feng Yuxiang at the elder’s command. Yet, neither of them appeared worried in the slightest, almost as if they had the situation under control.","Yuan then spoke, speaking directly to Bai Ning, \"I guess you don’t have what it takes to defeat me, after all.\"","\"Shut up!\" The Eleventh Elder roared.","He moved toward Yuan and demanded, \"Who the hell are you? Why are you attacking the Heavenly White Tiger Clan? Do you even realize who you’re dealing with?\"","Yuan replied calmly, \"Of course I do. Your ancestor was one of the Nine Divine Supremes who once served the Immortal Monarch. But so what? That was long ago. You hold no ties to him or his legacy now, so stop waving around a title that no longer means anything.\"","\"Blasphemy!\" Bai Ning roared.","\"Then let me ask you this... Do you know who I am?\"","\"You’re a nobody who tried to claim to have ties with the Immortal Monarch! I was foolish to have believed you!\"","Yuan looked at her and smiled, \"Do you still have what I gave you at the Pavilion of Knowledge?\"","Bai Ning’s body trembled the moment she was reminded of the vial of blood. Retrieving it with shaky hands, she exclaimed, \"Whose blood is this?! It’s definitely not the Immortal Monarch’s!\"","She had revered this vial of blood ever since she acquired it, but now, realizing it was a fake all along, she was shaken to the core.","\"If you think it’s fake, why don’t you hand it back to me?\" Yuan extended his hand toward her.","Bai Ning instinctively drew her hand back as if to throw the vial away, but her motion froze halfway, hesitation clearly written in her eyes.","\"Immortal Monarch? What nonsense is this?\" the Eleventh Elder sneered.","He motioned toward Bai Ning and barked, \"Hand me that vial!\"","Bai Ning hesitated once more, a flicker of doubt in her eyes, but eventually released her grip and passed the vial to him.","Once the vial of blood was in his grasp, the Eleventh Elder didn’t even bother to check it and immediately crushed it, destroying the vial and the blood within it.","Bai Ning felt a gripping pain in her heart after seeing this, even though she knew it was fake.","\"What a waste...\" Feng Yuxiang shook her head with an exaggerated sigh. \"Do you have any idea how many beasts would kill for that blood?\"","\"Silence!\" the Eleventh Elder roared, his voice thundering across the valley.","After a heavy pause, he continued coldly, \"For the crimes of attacking the Heavenly White Tiger Clan and attempting to deceive us with the Immortal Monarch’s name—I hereby sentence both of you to death!\"","\"How scary.\" Feng Yuxiang chuckled, still treating their situation like it was a joke.","\"Young Master, what should we do now?\" she then asked him.","Yuan turned to the Eleventh Elder and asked calmly, \"Where is your Clan Leader?\"","The Eleventh Elder sneered with disdain. \"You really think the Clan Leader would appear for two insignificant nobodies?\"","Yuan swept his gaze across the tens of thousands of Immortals encircling him, then said coolly, \"Then, until your Clan Leader shows up, let’s keep playing.\"","After saying these words, Yuan activated True Dragon Awakening, causing his aura to skyrocket.","The moment they sensed Yuan’s overwhelming aura, the surrounding Immortals instinctively backed away, their faces pale with fear and bodies drenched in cold sweat.","Bai Ning’s eyes widened, and in that moment, she finally realized just how vastly superior Yuan had been all along.","\"So it’s finally time to get serious, huh?\" Feng Yuxiang muttered as a sphere of flames appeared around her, rapidly expanding and engulfing her figure in a blazing aura.","When the flames subsided, Feng Yuxiang was no longer in human form. In her place stood a majestic phoenix wreathed in golden fire, radiating immense heat and awe-inspiring presence."]},{"number":2082,"title":"Chapter 2082: Chaos Within the Heavenly White Tiger Clan(3)","paragraphs":["Following her transformation, Feng Yuxiang unleashed a vast sea of flames that surged outward, engulfing those nearby. Though the fire scorched their skin and singed their hair, it carried no killing intent, as she had no desire to take their lives.","As for Yuan, he stowed his sword away and began beating the Heavenly White Tigers with his bare fists.","\"A human dares challenge us in physique? Laughable!\" a Golden Immortal scoffed as he stepped forward to confront Yuan.","But the moment their fists collided, his laughter died. His eyes widened in shock as his entire arm shattered like brittle glass under Yuan’s strike.","\"Can’t you sense his aura? He’s no human! He’s a dragon!\" Someone exclaimed.","Despite being surrounded by Immortals, neither Yuan nor Feng Yuxiang could be stopped by the Heavenly White Tiger Clan.","The Eleventh Elder and the other elders quickly realized that they needed to personally act if they wanted to subdue them. However, they didn’t immediately act, so the others could wear them down first.","Eventually, after several hours of trying to subdue Yuan and Feng Yuxiang, the Eleventh Elder shouted, \"All of you, get back! We’ll handle this ourselves!\"","There were twenty elders in total, each one at the first or second level of the God Ascension Realm. Naturally, they didn’t all attack at once, as such a move would’ve been excessive. Instead, two elders moved to confront Yuan, while only one turned their focus to Feng Yuxiang. Despite his lower cultivation, they saw Yuan as the greater threat.","Since they were still within the Nine Heavens, Yuan wasn’t too worried about facing a God Ascension cultivator. As for Feng Yuxiang, her True Primordial Fire still affected them.","\"Since you decided to struggle, we won’t delay your death sentence and will directly kill you right here and now,\" said one of Yuan’s opponents.","Yuan smiled and calmly responded, \"Do you even have that ability?\"","The elders couldn’t understand where Yuan’s confidence came from, but they dismissed it without concern and launched their attack.","As the battle erupted, the surrounding Immortals quickly retreated to clear the field, while the remaining elders lingered at the edges, ready to intervene if needed.","Despite only being a True Immortal, Feng Yuxiang held her ground against her opponent, a first-level God Ascension expert, and was even forcing him back. The elder had no way to counter her True Primordial Fire, which burned with relentless ferocity.","\"Damn it! What kind of flames are these? Even Celestial Qi can’t snuff them out!\" the elder cursed, struggling to contain the blaze. \"I’ve never seen or even heard of anything like this!\"","The other elders were equally stunned. None of them possessed the slightest knowledge of Primordial Phoenixes.","However, what shocked them the most was Yuan, who was overwhelming two God Ascension cultivators at once with nothing but his raw prowess.","\"Such overwhelming innate strength... Does he belong to the Ten Royal Dragon Clans?\" one of the elders suddenly thought of this possibility.","\"What about the phoenix? I have seen several phoenixes from the Ten Royal Phoenix Clans, but none of them could even compare to her fire. Where the hell did these two monsters come from?\"","The elders were worried that they might have to answer to both Royal Clans if they killed Yuan and Feng Yuxiang.","However, the Eleventh Elder remained calm and reassured them, \"They’re not with the Royal Clans. There’s no way the two clans would work together, much less attack our Heavenly White Tiger Clan in such a manner.\"","What the Eleventh Elder said made a lot of sense to the others, and they quickly stopped worrying about it.","\"W-We cannot defeat him with just the two of us! We need more help!\" One of the elders fighting Yuan suddenly said to the others.","\"I’ll go help.\"","Soon, another God Ascension cultivator entered the fray, turning the fight into a three-on-one assault.","\"I also need some help!\" said the elder fighting Feng Yuxiang.","Thus, her battle became one-on-two the very next moment.","Yet, the new addition did not seem to help, and Yuan still dominated the battlefield. However, Feng Yuxiang was slowly being pushed back because she was still not used to using her True Primordial Fire.","Despite that, she still didn’t seem to be worried in the slightest.","\"Young Master, I’ll start using ’that’ power, okay?\" Feng Yuxiang suddenly asked.","\"Go ahead, but try not to kill them.\" Yuan nodded.","\"Understood!\"","In the very next moment, Feng Yuxiang’s aura suddenly skyrocketed toward the heavens, shocking the elders.","\"What?! Where is this power coming from?!\"","Unbeknownst to the elders, Feng Yuxiang had just activated one of the Immortal Monarch’s powers through her Supreme Seal.","<Immortal Monarch’s True Blessing has activated>","[Immortal Monarch’s True Blessing]","[Rank: Celestial]","[Mastery Level: 1]","[Description: Grants those bearing the Immortal Monarch’s Supreme Seal overwhelming prowess, increasing their overall strength by 10,000%. This skill will remain active until deactivated by the Seal Bearer or the Creator and will constantly drain the Creator’s soul strength.]","The Immortal Monarch’s True Blessing was a direct upgrade of Immortal Monarch’s Blessing, which granted temporary strength to those who did not have the Immortal Monarch’s Supreme Seal.","Meanwhile, Yuan could feel his soul strength being drained at a rapid rate. However, since only Feng Yuxiang was using it, he could easily replenish it with his soul cultivation technique, essentially allowing him to keep it active forever if he wanted.","With the aid of the Immortal Monarch’s True Blessing, Feng Yuxiang instantly seized the upper hand once more, becoming the dominant force on the battlefield.","\"Hahaha! I haven’t felt this alive in ages!\" Feng Yuxiang laughed as she soared higher into the heavens. With a mighty beat of her majestic wings, she ignited a massive fireball in the sky—a blazing explosion that bloomed like fireworks.","\"S-Stop her!\"","Two more elders suddenly joined the battle, turning it into a four-against-one siege against Feng Yuxiang.","Meanwhile, another pair moved to support the three elders fighting Yuan, escalating the clash into a five-on-one confrontation."]},{"number":2083,"title":"Chapter 2083: The Clan Leader’s Appearance","paragraphs":["\"Good heavens, he’s fighting five of our elders all by himself! What a freaking monster!\" The Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s members were bewildered by what they were witnessing. A few even believed they were currently dreaming.","\"What should we do?\" One of the elders on standby asked the others.","\"Maybe we should just attack them at once and get this over with,\" one of them suggested.","\"You want twenty God Ascension cultivators to gang up on two Immortals? That would look terrible for our clan if news of it spreads!\" another rejected the idea.","\"And how do you think it currently looks now?! How will it look if he defeats even one of our elders?!\" another elder snapped back.","The Eleventh Elder closed his eyes and sighed.","\"Let’s just get this over with. As long as word doesn’t spread, it’ll be fine,\" he said a moment later.","He turned to look at one of the elders there with a suggestive gaze.","The elder gave a firm nod before swiftly weaving array symbols through the air. Once completed, a colossal formation rose around the Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s territory, shrouding it from the outside world, like a massive black curtain descending to conceal the chaos within.","\"It’s ready,\" he said a moment later.","\"Then let’s go.\" The Eleventh Elder took charge and joined the battle against Yuan.","Seeing this, the others followed.","In the blink of an eye, all twenty elders had joined the fray. Now, both Yuan and Feng Yuxiang had to deal with ten God Ascension cultivators at the same time.","\"Young Master, I cannot deal with so many of them at once!\" Feng Yuxiang said to him through voice transmission.","\"You’ve done enough. Come back to me. I’ll deal with them,\" he said.","Feng Yuxiang nodded and immediately backed away from her fight.","\"She’s running away!\"","\"Stop her!\"","Although the elders tried to stop her, Feng Yuxiang’s speed was simply too fast for them, not to mention her True Primordial Fire that constantly blocked their path.","Upon reaching Yuan, she immediately dove into his body, entering his Dantian.","\"What the—?\"","The elders watching were stunned. A dragon allowing a phoenix into his Dantian? It defied everything they knew, as such trust between two ancient, opposing bloodlines was beyond comprehension.","\"Yu Ning, I’ll have to rely on you again,\" Yuan suddenly said to her.","\"Huh? Don’t tell me you want to do ’that’ again?\"","\"Don’t worry, I am no longer a mortal, and my understanding of Celestial Qi has improved significantly since we last did it.\"","\"If you say so...\"","Yu Ning began gathering Celestial Qi for Yuan, shocking the elders.","\"H-He’s using Celestial Qi?! As a Silver Immortal?!\"","None of them dared to believe their eyes.","\"How do you feel?\" Yu Ning asked Yuan a moment later.","\"It’s still a little painful, but it’s manageable.\"","He looked at the twenty elders and said, \"The real fun begins now.\"","The elders exchanged uneasy glances. Then, after a brief, heavy silence, they all turned toward Yuan—striking in unison without a word.","A battle involving twenty God Ascension cultivators was nothing short of cataclysmic, unleashing devastation beyond imagination. Within mere minutes, the entire residential area of the Heavenly White Tiger Clan had been reduced to nothingness.","\"Is your Clan Leader still not going to show himself?\" Yuan asked. \"Or is he planning to wait until the entire Heavenly White Valley is reduced to rubble?\"","Despite being outnumbered twenty to one, Yuan showed no signs of faltering. The elders couldn’t so much as scratch his unrivaled physique, and not a single one could contend with the overwhelming force of his soul strength.","It felt as though they were battling someone far beyond their cultivation, yet in reality, they were up against a mere Silver Immortal. Thankfully, the formation had shielded their struggle from the outside world. Had it not, they would have likely perished from the weight of their own shame.","\"You are not worthy to meet the Clan Leader!\" One of the elders roared as he transformed into his beast form, becoming a massive white tiger that was almost as large as a mountain.","The other elders did the same, and very soon, twenty massive white tigers surrounded Yuan.","\"How scary.\" Yuan chuckled.","\"Since your Clan Leader won’t show up, it looks like I will have no choice but to kill some of you.\"","Yuan suddenly closed his eyes and took a deep breath, allowing his dragon transformation to fade.","But moments later, a new aura surged forth, and when his eyes reopened, they glowed with a majestic, silver brilliance.","Yuan’s presence shifted dramatically, now radiating an unfathomable aura that sent a primal fear surging through the surrounding beasts, forcing them to bow to his very existence.","\"What?!\"","The elders were stunned to find themselves subconsciously kneeling before Yuan, their bodies betraying a reverence their minds had yet to accept.","\"You wish to know my identity? Then allow me to tell you...\"","Yuan’s voice rumbled like thunder, its resonance sending a chill through their entire being.","Just as the tension reached its peak, another formidable presence suddenly emerged. Though it was initially distant, it closed the gap in the blink of an eye, arriving with astonishing speed.","Yuan turned to face the newcomer—an imposing middle-aged man with long, flowing white and black hair, his expression naturally stern and commanding. He wore a robe split in half, black on one side and white on the other, with a white tiger emblem emblazoned on the black side.","This individual’s cultivation far surpassed that of the elders, standing at the 7th level of God Ascension.","\"Clan Leader!\" the elders exclaimed in disbelief, astonished that he had appeared so suddenly.","\"There’s no need for you to act, Clan Leader! We can handle this ourselves!\" The Eleventh Elder said.","However, the Clan Leader paid no heed to the elders, his gaze fixed solely on Yuan’s glowing silver eyes.","\"So you have finally decided to show yourself, huh?\" Yuan said, staring back at him."]},{"number":2084,"title":"Chapter 2084: Immortal Monarch’s Supremacy","paragraphs":["The Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s Leader swept the scene with a cold, calculating gaze, his eyes briefly lingering on Bai Ning before moving to Bai Xutao, who lay buried beneath a mountain of rubble and dust. Although Bai Xutao appeared to be a burned corpse, he was still alive.","Eventually, the Clan Leader returned to Yuan and spoke in an emotionless tone, \"What are you trying to achieve here?\"","Yuan braced for the Clan Leader to erupt in fury, certain he would attack in a blind rage over the devastation to his clan. But to his surprise, the Clan Leader remained unnervingly calm.","\"I have two objectives here,\" Yuan said calmly. \"First, to deal with Bai Xutao, who harmed my companion. And second, to acquire your Ancient Seal.\"","At the mention of the Ancient Seal, the Clan Leader’s eyes narrowed, his expression betraying nothing. However, the elders couldn’t hold back, their voices erupting in shock. \"How does he know about the Ancient Seal?!\"","The Clan Leader whipped his gaze toward the elder who had spoken, his eyes brimming with deadly intent.","\"Shit!\" The elder cursed under his breath, immediately clamping his hand over his mouth as he realized his grave mistake.","\"There’s no use trying to hide it. I know you have it,\" Yuan said.","\"Let’s assume we do have it, for the sake of this conversation,\" the Clan Leader said, his tone laced with mockery. \"Do you really expect us to simply hand it over to you, after everything you’ve done here?\"","Yuan paused for a moment, then casually gestured toward Bai Xutao. In an instant, Bai Xutao’s body was yanked from the rubble, soaring toward Yuan as though an invisible force were pulling him.","Seeing this, the Clan Leader raised his hand, instantly halting Yuan’s attempt to seize Bai Xutao with an unseen force.","\"You’re quite foolish if you think you can act with impunity in my presence,\" the Clan Leader said coldly.","Yuan smiled, his tone unruffled. \"It was worth a try. That said, I could kill him at any moment, and there’s nothing you can do to stop it unless you hand over the Ancient Seal.\"","\"An empty threat.\" The Clan Leader did not believe Yuan for a moment.","\"I don’t usually resort to threats,\" Yuan said with a sigh, \"but your Heavenly White Tiger Clan has fallen so low that I simply don’t care anymore. If the Immortal Monarch were here, he’d be furious at how you’ve been running things.\"","\"Killing your own children simply because their bloodline doesn’t meet your standards or they fail a trial? Even barbarians wouldn’t stoop so low.\"","The Clan Leader sneered. \"Who are you to judge how our family operates? Unless you’re our ancestor, you have no right to speak on it.\"","\"I may not be your ancestor, but I do have a connection with him.\"","\"Hahaha!\" The Clan Leader suddenly laughed out loud, his tone filled with mockery.","\"Alright, enough of this farce. I don’t know who you are or why you’re truly here, but don’t think you’ll get out of here alive today.\"","The Clan Leader glanced at the elders, his voice cold and commanding. \"Get lost. I’ll clean up your mess, but be prepared for punishment later.\"","The elders trembled under his gaze, too fearful to protest. They silently bowed and quickly withdrew, leaving Yuan and the Clan Leader alone.","The Eleventh Elder didn’t forget to carry Bai Xutao away as he departed.","Yuan watched them leave, his voice cold as he mumbled, \"I’ll let you live a little longer.\"","Once they were alone, the Clan Leader unleashed his cultivation and, without a word, began his attack on Yuan.","Though the Clan Leader was at the seventh level of God Ascension, the Nine Heavens’ limitation kept him from being vastly stronger than the elders. Of course, he was also holding back, unwilling to completely destroy his own territory, and not seeing Yuan as a threat that warranted full effort.","As expected, Yuan was being pushed back by the Clan Leader’s overwhelming power. Yet, Yuan remained unfazed, his confidence unwavering as he continued to exude an aura of calm certainty.","Suddenly—","<Immortal Monarch’s Supremacy activated>","Yuan’s silver eyes suddenly blazed with intensity, glowing as if they had transformed into a silver sun.","[Immortal Monarch’s Supremacy]","[Rank: ???]","[Mastery Level: 1]","[Description: A mysterious power bestowed by the Immortal Monarch’s Bloodline. When activated during a battle against a beast, your overall prowess will increase by 50,000%]","The Immortal Monarch’s Supremacy functioned similarly to Heaven’s Supremacy, but it only activated when battling beasts. This unique skill had been awakened within Yuan after he consumed the Primal Monarch’s Blood Essence and unlocked his bloodline. However, until now, he had never been able to fully utilize it, as his cultivation wasn’t strong enough to activate its true power, and his bloodline before consuming the Primordial Phoenix’s Blood Essence was also lacking.","Yet, despite its overwhelming power, Yuan could sense that he was only scratching the surface of its true potential.","The instant Yuan activated Immortal Monarch’s Supremacy, his previous disadvantage vanished, and he stood on equal footing with the Clan Leader, their battle now burning with renewed intensity.","Though the Clan Leader’s expression remained barely altered, he was inwardly shocked by Yuan’s sudden increase in prowess.","Realizing that he was beginning to fall behind, the Clan Leader’s expression darkened, and he began to unleash more of his power, determined to reclaim control of the fight.","Meanwhile, the Eleventh Elder hurriedly transported Bai Xutao to the innermost, most restricted area of the clan’s territory—accessible only to those of the highest authority. There, they immediately began working to heal the grievous injuries he had sustained from Feng Yuxiang’s flames.","However, they soon realized that even with their most precious and valuable treasures, healing Bai Xutao would not be an easy task. Despite their personal disdain for his character, they knew they had no choice but to spare no expense in saving him, as the future of their clan relied on his bloodline."]},{"number":2085,"title":"Chapter 2085: Heavenly White Tiger’s Ancestral Altar","paragraphs":["It took several hours and an unfathomable amount of treasure—enough to send even the wealthiest merchant into a panic—but the elders managed to restore Bai Xutao’s burned appearance and heal all but one of his injuries.","When Bai Xutao woke up, the first thing he did was reach for the area between his legs.","\"I-It’s not there! Where’s my thing?!\" he exclaimed in a terrified voice.","\"I’m sorry, Young Master, but we could not heal it...\" one of the elders said in a defeated voice.","\"N-NO! YOU MUST FIND A WAY! IT MUST BE HEALED!\" he roared, even grabbing the elder by his collar.","The Eleventh Elder slapped his hand and shouted back, \"So what if it’s gone?! You don’t need it to conceive!\"","\"If I don’t have it, how am I going to satisfy myself?! What am I going to do about my natural lust?!\"","\"We’ll find a way, but for the time being, you’ll have to live without it,\" said the Eleventh Elder as he shook his head.","Bai Xutao lowered his head and fell silent.","\"Unforgivable...\" he muttered in a cold voice.","\"UNFORGIVABLE!\"","Bai Xutao suddenly leapt from the bed, roaring with fury as his entire cultivation base erupted in a violent surge of power.","Then, without another word, he rushed out of the building.","\"Young Master, where are you going?!\" the elders shouted, hurrying after him, a growing sense of dread twisting in their guts as Bai Xutao stormed off.","\"I will get my revenge! I don’t care how!\" he roared.","\"How will you do that when even we cannot defeat them?!\"","Bai Xutao didn’t respond and continued speeding ahead.","It didn’t take long for the elders to realize something was off—Bai Xutao wasn’t heading toward the battlefield, but in the opposite direction.","\"Where is he going?\"","\"Maybe he’s still in a daze...\"","Eventually, they realized where they were heading.","\"Wait a second... Aren’t we heading toward the Heavenly White Tiger’s Ancestral Altar?\"","\"But why would he—\"","A sudden realization struck the elders again, and when it did, their hearts lurched with terror.","\"He can’t be!\"","\"Is he trying to consume the Ancestor’s Blood Essence?!\"","Before its death, the Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s ancestor left behind a single drop of its Blood Essence—a sacred remnant the clan had safeguarded ever since.","The Blood Essence was kept at the Heavenly White Tiger’s Ancestral Altar, a sacred area where the Clan Leader spends most of his time.","\"Calm down. Even if he’s trying to acquire it, he won’t be able to get past the barrier without the Clan Leader’s approval,\" said the Eleventh Elder.","Hearing this, the elders quickly calmed down.","However, when they arrived at the Heavenly White Tiger’s Ancestral Altar, they were met with another shock. The barrier that was meant to protect the sacred site had vanished without a trace.","\"What?! Where’s the barrier?! There’s no way the Clan Leader would’ve left this place without ensuring it’s protected!\"","The Eleventh Elder exclaimed in disbelief.","The Ancestral Altar was arguably the most important area in their territory. It was simply unthinkable for the Clan Leader to leave it unprotected.","\"We don’t have the time to think about that! The Young Master has already entered the site! We need to stop him before he does something terrible!\"","The elders wasted no time and rushed into the Ancestral Altar with growing panic in their hearts.","When they arrived at the end, they could see Bai Xutao standing right before the altar with a glass vial containing a drop of blood in his grasp.","\"Young Master! Put that back immediately!\" The Eleventh Elder screamed after seeing the object in Bai Xutao’s grasp. \"The Clan Leader will kill you if you do any more!\"","However, Bai Xutao merely laughed, \"Kill me? Do you know who I am?! I was born with our ancestor’s bloodline in me! If anybody should touch his Blood Essence, it would be me!\"","\"Who knows?! Maybe my bloodline will fully awaken after I consume his Blood Essence!\"","\"Your body will not be able to handle the Ancestor’s Blood Essence! You’ll die a violent death if you consume it without preparation! Are you trying to waste the Ancestor’s Blood Essence and suicide right afterward?! That’s double the waste!\"","\"Die? I won’t die until I kill those two bastards who humiliated me, especially that damn phoenix who burned my manhood! I’ll make sure that bitch suffers the most!\"","The very next moment, Bai Xutao opened the seal on the glass vial.","\"STOP HIM!!!\" the Eleventh Elder bellowed, and in an instant, everyone charged at Bai Xutao, desperate to halt his reckless action.","Unfortunately, they were a split second too late. By the time they reached him, Bai Xutao had already consumed the Blood Essence.","\"No way...\"","The elders fell to their knees, despair etched on their faces. None of them could have ever imagined such a thing was possible. They had always known Bai Xutao to be reckless, but it seemed they had never truly grasped the depth of his recklessness until today.","\"S-Spit it out! Immediately!\" the Eleventh Elder pleaded, his voice trembling.","But Bai Xutao remained silent, his body trembling before unleashing a deafening howl so powerful it nearly shattered the elders’ eardrums. In the next instant, his form began to swell, his body morphing into his beastly shape.","\"It hurts! It hurts! IT HURRRTS!\" Bai Xutao screamed out in pain, but there was nothing that could be done.","In mere moments, Bai Xutao’s body swelled to an unimaginable size, far surpassing his usual limits. He grew so colossal that he tore through the walls of the Ancestral Altar, the entire structure collapsing in the wake of his transformation.","When the transformation finally ceased, Bai Xutao let out another earth-shattering howl, his aura rippling across the entire Heavenly White Valley. In an instant, his cultivation, once at Golden Immortal, surged explosively to the first level of God Ascension, and it continued to rise toward the next level with every passing moment."]},{"number":2086,"title":"Chapter 2086: Gone Berserk","paragraphs":["\"Heavens! He’s actually managed to consume the ancestor’s Blood Essence without dying!\" The elders were shocked by the results.","However, the Eleventh Elder’s expression shifted with concern. \"No, something feels wrong.\"","Though Bai Xutao was still alive, his energy was a turbulent storm, chaotic and wild, as if he had lost all control over his own body.","A moment later, one of the elders stepped forward to confront Bai Xutao.","\"Young Master! How are you feeling?\" he asked, his voice filled with concern.","But instead of answering, Bai Xutao turned to face him and, without warning, launched a brutal attack.","The elder was instantly sent flying, crashing into a nearby mountain.","\"Be careful! The Young Master has gone berserk!\" The Eleventh Elder warned everyone before distancing himself from Bai Xutao.","The others quickly followed.","Meanwhile, after hours of fierce combat, both Yuan and the Clan Leader abruptly paused as they sensed a powerful presence appearing out of thin air.","Yuan recognized the presence as strangely familiar, but couldn’t place its origin. The Clan Leader felt the same unease, his brow furrowing in confusion.","Though the presence wasn’t stronger than the Clan Leader’s, it carried a far more menacing and threatening aura, making it feel far more dangerous.","It was at this moment that one of the elders at the scene notified the Clan Leader of the situation through his communication jade slip.","\"That bastard did what?!\" The Clan Leader didn’t believe the news at first.","\"The Young Master entered the Ancestral Altar and consumed the Ancestor’s Blood Essence!\" The Eleventh Elder repeated.","\"That’s impossible! How did he enter the Ancestral Altar?! The barrier should’ve kept him out!\" the Clan Leader exclaimed in disbelief.","\"The barrier was gone when we arrived!\" The Eleventh Elder hurriedly responded. \"I don’t know if the Young Master tampered with it or if something else caused its disappearance, but it wasn’t there when we arrived!\"","Noticing the Clan Leader’s distraught expression, Yuan couldn’t help but ask, \"Ancestral Altar? What are you talking about?\"","Since the Eleventh Elder was conversing through the communication jade slip, he had no idea about the situation.","Yet, the Clan Leader ignored him and focused on Bai Xutao’s situation.","\"What happened to Bai Xutao?!\"","The Eleventh Elder quickly explained Bai Xutao’s situation.","\"He’s alive, but he’s gone berserk and is destroying everything in sight! He doesn’t even recognize his own people!\"","\"That useless bastard! Keep him restrained until I get there! There must be a way to extract the Blood Essence he consumed!\"","After putting away the communication jade slip, the Clan Leader looked at Yuan with a serious expression on his face.","\"I don’t have time to waste on you any longer,\" the Clan Leader snarled. \"I’ll grant you a painless death—be grateful.\"","Before Yuan could respond, the Clan Leader unleashed the full force of his cultivation, striking with his most powerful martial technique.","\"Heavenly Tiger’s White Flash!\"","The Clan Leader swung his claw-like hand toward Yuan, unleashing a blinding flash of light, as bright as a flashbang. In an instant, Yuan’s world turned pure white, and before he could react, a forceful, unstoppable blow struck his body, tearing him apart in the blink of an eye.","After delivering the crushing blow and being certain it had struck Yuan, the Clan Leader wasted no time in flying away, not even bothering to check if Yuan was still alive. He was absolutely certain that no Immortal could survive such an attack.","Moments after the Clan Leader flew off, Yuan emerged from the mountain of rubble, completely unharmed, his expression as calm as ever.","\"He must be in quite the hurry to leave so quickly, not even bothering to check if I’m still alive,\" Yuan murmured, his gaze following the direction the Clan Leader had disappeared to.","\"Are you going to chase after him, or are we going to leave now?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","\"Leave?\" Yuan shook his head and continued, \"Why would I leave when we still have plenty of time before we return to the Rising Phoenix Clan? Not to mention the Ancient Seal isn’t in our possession yet.\"","\"Then...\"","\"Let’s see what’s got him so worried,\" Yuan muttered, before soaring off in the direction the Clan Leader had vanished.","Sometime later, the Clan Leader arrived at the scene, his eyes widening as he saw the elders still struggling to subdue Bai Xutao, whose cultivation had now surged to the 3rd level of God Ascension.","\"You’re here, Clan Leader!\" The Eleventh Elder hurried toward him upon noticing his arrival.","\"What is this? Why is it taking you so long to subdue him?\" The Clan Leader demanded, his frown deepening with frustration.","\"That’s... He’s growing stronger with each passing moment,\" the Eleventh Elder said hesitantly, \"but his cultivation isn’t the real problem we’re facing.\"","Before the Eleventh Elder could continue, the Clan Leader’s attention snapped to Bai Xutao, who unleashed a powerful roar that resonated with profound energy. The sound reverberated through the air, causing the Clan Leader’s bloodline to tremble in response.","\"This feeling is—!\" The Clan Leader’s eyes widened with disbelief after realizing something.","Seeing the Clan Leader’s reaction, the Eleventh Elder let out a deep sigh. \"We believe the Young Master’s bloodline has awakened after consuming the Ancestor’s Blood Essence, and his ’Bloodline Authority’ is now above ours, making him nearly impossible to handle. We can’t even land a proper attack on him because our instincts force us not to harm him.\"","\"What a fucking pain in the ass,\" the Clan Leader snapped, his face reddening and veins bulging with rage. \"How many times do I have to clean up your mess today?!\"","\"I’m sorry for being useless...\" The Eleventh Elder murmured, lowering his head in shame.","\"I’ll deal with you all later. Right now, I need to subdue him before his bloodline becomes too powerful for me to control,\" the Clan Leader growled, his tone full of annoyance.","With that, he went to confront Bai Xutao, intending to subdue him without taking his life.","Meanwhile, Yuan watched from a distance while hiding his presence with Shadow Veil."]},{"number":2087,"title":"Chapter 2087: I am the Immortal Monarch","paragraphs":["\"Good lord, what happened to that pervert?\" Feng Yuxiang commented after seeing Bai Xutao’s new appearance.","Not only was Bai Xutao much bigger than before, but the patterns on his body had also changed.","\"The Clan Leader mentioned Blood Essence, so that was most likely what he consumed,\" said Yuan.","\"Blood Essence... What are the chances that he consumed the Heavenly White Tiger—one of the Nine Divine Supreme’s Blood Essence?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","\"Judging by the Clan Leader’s reaction, it’s likely.\"","\"Isn’t that really bad? I mean, it was likely prepared for you.\"","Yuan fell silent for a moment before responding, \"Don’t worry, I have a way to extract the Blood Essence even if he consumed it. However, it’s going to be very painful for him, and he’s certainly going to die afterward.\"","\"How are you going to do that?\" Feng Yuxiang asked, unaware of Yuan’s abilities as the Immortal Monarch.","\"You’ll see in a bit.\" Yuan said with a mysterious smile on his face.","Meanwhile, the Clan Leader struggled to subdue Bai Xutao, facing increasing difficulty. In the world of beasts, superior cultivation alone wasn’t the key to dominance—it was the bloodline. Those with a more powerful bloodline could command those of lesser heritage, regardless of cultivation.","Though Bai Xutao’s bloodline was only slightly stronger than the Clan Leader’s, it had been amplified by their ancestor’s blood essence. Moreover, the Clan Leader had to act in a way that wouldn’t kill Bai Xutao, making the process incredibly tricky.","The other members of the Heavenly White Tiger Clan watched from afar, their eyes wide with shock and disbelief.","None of them realized that Bai Xutao had consumed their ancestor’s blood essence and figured his rampage was caused by another factor.","Several hours had passed since Bai Xutao consumed the blood essence and lost control, yet the Clan Leader still hadn’t been able to subdue him. Meanwhile, Bai Xutao’s cultivation had soared to the fourth level of God Ascension, his power growing exponentially.","The Clan Leader eventually had to accept a harsh truth—that he alone was incapable of subduing Bai Xutao without killing him. However, doing so would not only squander Bai Xutao’s bloodline potential but also waste the precious blood essence he had consumed.","’Fuck! What should I do with him?!’","Killing Bai Xutao was out of the question for the Clan Leader. If he couldn’t handle the situation on his own, he would rather allow Bai Xutao to continue rampaging until a solution presented itself—regardless of whether it meant the destruction of the entire Heavenly White Valley.","\"Looks like you’re having trouble. Need some help?\"","A familiar voice suddenly echoed, pulling the Clan Leader out of his stunned daze.","\"W-What’s he doing here?!\"","The elders gasped in shock as Yuan materialized out of thin air. They had believed that the Clan Leader had already taken care of him.","When the Clan Leader saw Yuan, his face went pale, his expression filled with disbelief as if he had just seen a ghost. Startled, he jumped back, instinctively distancing himself from the unexpected appearance.","\"Y-You! How the hell are you still alive?!\" he exclaimed.","\"Why wouldn’t I be alive? You never killed me.\" Yuan calmly shrugged.","\"Bullshit! I know my attack landed on you!\"","\"It did. But that doesn’t mean I’ll die from it.\"","The Clan Leader was speechless.","\"So, do you need help?\" Yuan asked again, his voice snapping the Clan Leader out of his daze.","\"Do you really think you can pretend you didn’t attack our clan?\" the Clan Leader shot back, his voice hardening. \"Even if we accept your help, it won’t save you from your death sentence.\"","\"Sounds like you want my help,\" said Yuan.","\"Get lost!\" The Clan Leader roared, launching the same devastating technique he had used before.","\"Heavenly Tiger’s White Flash!\"","The attack tore through Yuan’s body, but this time, the Clan Leader watched in astonishment as Yuan’s injuries healed almost instantly, his form regenerating with a fluid, liquid-like motion.","\"What the fuck are you...?\" The Clan Leader asked, his voice laced with nervousness.","\"I’m a human,\" Yuan replied calmly, his tone unwavering.","He then turned toward Bai Xutao, still rampaging, and added, \"Even if you don’t want my help, I’m going to do something about him, as he consumed what belongs to me.\"","\"What? Do you even know what he consumed?\"","\"One of the Nine Divine Supreme’s blood essence, correct? The Heavenly White Tiger—your ancestor’s blood essence.\"","\"If you already know, then why would you claim it to be yours—\" The Clan Leader suddenly halted his words when Yuan turned around to face Bai Xutao.","Before the Clan Leader could continue, Yuan flew at Bai Xutao.","\"What are you planning to do to him?!\" The Clan Leader hastily chased after him.","\"What I was trying to do from the very beginning—kill him.\"","\"Bastard! If I wanted to kill him, do you really think I would need your help?! I will not allow you to kill him!\"","\"And how are you going to stop me when you can’t even kill me?\"","\"You bastard!!!\"","The Clan Leader erupted with fury, unleashing his most powerful martial techniques upon Yuan in rapid succession. The sheer force of his attacks obliterated the surrounding area, as if a nuclear blast had detonated at the heart of the valley.","The attack didn’t manage to kill Yuan, but it did attract Bai Xutao’s attention, who immediately pounced at them with surging killing intent.","\"Stay away!\" The Clan Leader roared before attempting to throw Bai Xutao as far as possible with his spiritual energy.","Though he couldn’t pinpoint it, there was something about Yuan that made him fearful for Bai Xutao’s life.","However, Bai Xutao forcefully stopped himself from being blown away and immediately pounced at them again.","\"This stubborn fool!\" The Clan Leader roared.","A moment later, Bai Xutao reached Yuan and opened his mouth in an attempt to consume him.","Yuan’s eyes suddenly flickered with immense killing intent, and an indescribable aura exuded from his entire being, halting Bai Xutao’s movements.","Although he had no control over his body, his primal instincts screamed at him to run away before it was too late.","Then, he turned around and started running away, dumbfounding the Clan Leader and the others watching.","Yuan narrowed his eyes and coldly sneered, \"Do you really think I will let you escape a third time?\"","He raised his hand and made a grasping motion toward Bai Xutao’s escaping figure, instantly halting him.","\"I don’t know what you’re planning on doing, but it will not happen on my watch!\"","The Clan Leader quickly moved to stand between them before extending his claw-like hands at Yuan’s neck.","Yuan’s silver eyes flickered, and he spoke in a commanding tone, \"Stand down.\"","In an instant, the Clan Leader’s movements halted.","\"W-What is this?!\" The Clan Leader exclaimed in shock and confusion.","Yuan didn’t answer him and made another command, \"Move aside.\"","The Clan Leader tried to resist his command this time, but alas, it was a futile attempt.","\"Who the hell are you?!\" The Clan Leader roared as his body forcefully listened to Yuan’s command.","Yuan stared at him dead in the eyes and calmly revealed, \"Who am I? I am the Immortal Monarch.\"","\"What...?\" The Clan Leader’s eyes widened with shock and disbelief.","From a distance, Bai Ning watched in bewilderment, her jaw dropping to the ground."]},{"number":2088,"title":"Chapter 2088: Forbidden Blood Extraction","paragraphs":["\"You... are the Immortal Monarch?\" The Clan Leader muttered after snapping out of his daze.","\"Do you really expect me to believe such nonsense?\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"You don’t have to believe me immediately, as I’ll show you evidence in just a moment.\"","\"A-Are you really going to kill Bai Xutao?\" The Clan Leader asked with a deep frown on his face.","\"If you had raised him properly, he wouldn’t be in this situation.\"","In the next moment, Yuan activated Forbidden Blood Extraction on Bai Xutao.","Instantly, the entire sky darkened, as though the heavens themselves were displeased, casting an ominous shadow over the valley.","Nothing had happened when Yuan used the Forbidden Blood Extraction in the Primal Expanse, for there was no ’heaven’ there to respond.","But now, back in the Nine Heavens, the technique invoked Heaven’s wrath, as it was a heaven-defying power that the heavens did not want to exist.","The dark clouds rumbled ominously, as if the heavens themselves were warning Yuan to stop.","But Yuan paid no heed, his focus unwavering as he continued to activate the Forbidden Blood Extraction, unshaken by the growing threat above him.","\"He’s invoked Heaven’s Judgment! And it doesn’t seem to be a small one!\" the elders exclaimed in shock, their eyes drawn to the dark clouds swirling above their territory.","\"What the hell is he trying to do?!\"","As everyone watched in stunned silence, Bai Xutao, still frozen in midair, suddenly screamed in agony. Blood began pouring from his eyes, nose, and ears, staining the air around him.","Seeing that Yuan ignored the warning, the heavens unleashed its judgment upon him, striking with a massive bolt of lightning far more powerful than what Yuan had faced at the Frozen Cloud Ethereal Sect.","BANG!","The bolt was so thick and colossal that it engulfed both Yuan and the Clan Leader entirely, swallowing them in a blinding flash of raw power.","\"Clan Leader!!!\" The elders cried out in terror, their eyes wide with fear as they saw him struck by Heaven’s Judgment.","But their panic quickly shifted to relief when the dust cleared, revealing the Clan Leader, who was only slightly injured.","However, their eyes widened in disbelief when they saw Yuan emerge from the chaos, completely unharmed by the devastating attack.","Yuan gazed up at the dark clouds with a mocking smile. \"Didn’t you learn anything from the last time? You won’t get rid of me with that pathetic power!\"","The dark clouds above him responded instantly, expanding massively, its ominous presence now covering the entire Heavenly White Valley, stretching across hundreds of thousands of miles.","\"Heavens!\"","Seeing the overwhelming power above, the elders and everyone else scrambled for their lives, including the Clan Leader, who had finally regained control of his body after the lightning strike.","Yet Yuan remained rooted in place, unfazed, as he continued extracting the blood essence from Bai Xutao.","When the process was complete, the heavens responded with its second Heaven’s Judgment—a strike so powerful and devastating that it sent a tremor through the entire Eighth Heaven for a brief moment, startling experts throughout the realm.","As the attack subsided and the dust settled, a massive crater was revealed.","Despite the catastrophic force of the attack, Yuan remained completely unharmed, his Flawless Heavenly Physique rendering Heaven’s Judgment utterly useless against him.","\"If this is all you’ve got, I guess you don’t really mind me using this technique.\"","Yuan continued the Forbidden Blood Extraction on Bai Xutao, but due to the complexity of Bai Xutao’s cultivation and the volatile nature of his situation, the process was taking far longer than Yuan had anticipated.","Realizing its efforts were futile against Yuan, the Heavens withdrew, and the dark clouds slowly dissipated, leaving behind a clear sky once more.","Seeing this, everyone returned to spectating Yuan’s actions.","\"What is he doing to the Young Master?\"","\"That bastard is forcefully extracting his blood essence!\"","\"What?! Such a technique exists?!\"","\"What a fearsome technique!\"","The members of the Heavenly White Tiger Clan were stunned and terrified by Yuan’s mythical technique, their minds slowly grasping the reason behind his invocation of Heaven’s Judgment.","\"That technique... It’s definitely Forbidden Blood Extraction...\" The Eleventh Elder suddenly muttered, his body trembling in fear and awe.","\"You know about it?\" The others turned to look at him for answers.","\"You would know as well if you’d spend some time in our family’s archive,\" said the Eleventh Elder. \"According to our Ancestor, the Forbidden Blood Extraction is one of the Immortal Monarch’s techniques, used to extract a beast’s blood essence forcefully.\"","\"Are you saying that he’s the real deal? That the Immortal Monarch has returned?\"","The Eleventh Elder nodded nervously, his mind racing as he suddenly recalled the vial of blood he had destroyed.","’Fuck... Did I actually destroy the Immortal Monarch’s blood...?’ The thought struck him like a bolt of lightning, and he desperately hoped it wasn’t true. The guilt would be unbearable if it were.","\"Forbidden Blood Extraction...\" The Clan Leader stood at a distance, his gaze vacant. Like the Eleventh Elder, he recognized the technique. Yet, even with the undeniable evidence before him, he struggled to accept the truth—that Yuan was the Immortal Monarch. No, he refused to believe it.","If Yuan was truly the Immortal Monarch, then there was no saving his son, Bai Xutao.","Meanwhile, Bai Ning collapsed to her knees, her expression twisted with an emotion that seemed to mirror the anguish of the worst breakup imaginable. As the Immortal Monarch’s most ardent admirer, there was no mistaking his technique.","Yet, much like the Clan Leader, she refused to believe it. For if she did, it would mean that she had fought the Immortal Monarch and sought to end his life on more than one occasion. It was a reality that she didn’t want to accept.","Unfortunately for her, there was simply too much evidence that supported Yuan being the Immortal Monarch.","\"What have I done...?\" Bai Ning muttered in a low voice as she came to accept reality."]},{"number":2089,"title":"Chapter 2089: Leaving the Heavenly White Valley","paragraphs":["After many minutes of using Forbidden Blood Extraction on Bai Xutao, Yuan was finally able to extract his blood essence—or more specifically, the blood essence he’d consumed and hadn’t fully refined yet.","Once his blood essence was fully extracted, Bai Xutao, wracked with indescribable pain throughout the ordeal, reverted to his human form and plummeted from the sky, disappearing into the gaping crater below.","Yuan stowed the blood essence away before turning to face the Clan Leader, who was still staring at him with a perplexed face.","\"Was that not enough evidence to prove my identity? Should I give you some more evidence?\" Yuan asked, making a grasping gesture at him.","The Clan Leader trembled, and after a brief, heavy silence, he suddenly dropped to his knees and bowed deeply before Yuan, kowtowing in the air.","\"This humble one greets the Immortal Monarch!\" he proclaimed.","As the Clan Leader demonstrated his reverence, the others quickly followed suit, soaring into the air before bowing in unison to greet Yuan.","\"The Heavenly White Tiger Clan greets the Immortal Monarch!\"","Yuan calmly faced them and spoke, \"You’re all probably wondering why I have returned or where I have been since my disappearance. To tell you the truth, I died back then and have been reincarnated.\"","\"Although I have returned, I do not have any intention of getting involved with your Heavenly White Tiger Clan, especially after learning about how you’ve been using my name and how you’re protecting a filth like Bai Xutao because of his bloodline.\"","\"However, since your Ancestor was one of my closest companions, I will give you all a chance to change your ways and stop smearing your Ancestor’s legacy. If you can prove to me that you’re not irredeemable, I will personally elevate your bloodline beyond your imagination.\"","Everyone there trembled uncontrollably after hearing this, especially the Clan Leader, who was beginning to lose hope.","\"Are you willing?\" Yuan asked.","\"WE ARE WILLING!\"","The entire clan responded in unison, their voice loud and clear.","\"Good. From this moment onward, I forbid your clan from using my name for your own benefit. Cease the senseless slaughter of your own kin for possessing an inferior bloodline. Moreover, you will take full responsibility and correct every wrong Bai Xutao has brought upon the Nine Heavens. Do I have any objections?\"","\"WE HAVE NO OBJECTIONS!\"","\"Clan Leader,\" Yuan’s voice rang out, sharp and commanding.","\"I am at your command!\" The Clan Leader replied without hesitation.","Yuan extended his arm, making a subtle beckoning gesture.","\"Do you remember the two reasons I came here?\" he asked, his tone carrying an air of authority. \"Now that I have dealt with one...\"","The Clan Leader immediately realized what Yuan wanted and shouted, \"Eleventh Elder! Present the Ancient Seal to the Immortal Monarch!\"","The Eleventh Elder reacted swiftly, kneeling before Yuan and retrieving the Ancient Seal with reverence.","\"Here is the Ancient Seal, Your Excellence.\"","Yuan accepted the Ancient Seal and tossed it inside his spatial ring.","The Eleventh Elder hesitated before speaking, his voice trembling, \"Your Excellency, if I may...\"","\"What is it?\" Yuan asked, his tone unwavering.","\"Please, forgive my earlier actions. In my ignorance, I destroyed your precious blood... If you wish to take my life as punishment, I accept it without hesitation.\"","Yuan then spoke, \"I already gave that blood to Bai Ning, so if you’re looking for forgiveness, you’re asking the wrong person.\"","\"I understand. Forgive me for troubling you, Your Excellency.\" The Eleventh Elder quickly withdrew, lowering his head in shame, too embarrassed to lift his gaze.","\"Bai Ning.\" Yuan suddenly called out to her.","\"Y-Yes!\"","She instinctively stood up.","\"If I recall correctly, you wished to serve me. Has that changed since you last spoke of it?\" Yuan asked.","\"No, it has not!\" she immediately responded.","\"I see. Unfortunately, I cannot accept you in your current state. However, I am willing to give you a chance to become someone worthy of serving me.\"","\"I am willing to do anything! What must I do to prove myself?!\"","\"That is for you to figure out.\"","\"For myself to figure out...?\" Bai Ning was dumbfounded.","\"In the meantime, I will give you a small blessing.\"","Yuan bestowed the Immortal Monarch’s Blessing upon her, and in an instant, her bloodline and prowess surged to new heights.","Witnessing this miraculous transformation, those who had still harbored doubts about Yuan’s identity cast aside all suspicion, finally accepting him as the true Immortal Monarch.","\"Bai Sulan!\" Yuan called out suddenly.","\"H-Huh? Me?\" Bai Sulan, positioned at the back of the crowd, looked up in surprise, her face filled with astonishment.","Yuan retrieved a glass vial containing his blood and tossed it toward her.","\"Catch!\"","Bai Sulan fumbled as she hastily caught the vial, almost dropping it in the process.","\"That’s my blood,\" Yuan explained. \"It’ll improve your bloodline and make you stronger. Consider it a token of gratitude for guiding me here.\"","All eyes turned to Bai Sulan, their gazes filled with envy, yet none dared to harbor any malicious intent in the presence of Yuan.","\"T-Thank you!\" she stammered, bowing deeply in gratitude.","\"Now that I have accomplished my goals here, I will be taking my leave,\" Yuan declared, his voice firm. \"If anyone asks, I was never here.\"","\"W-When will you return to us?!\" Bai Ning hurriedly asked, her voice tinged with worry.","\"Who knows?\" Yuan replied with a faint smile. \"But the Heavenly White Tiger Clan better have changed their ways by the next time I visit, or... You don’t want to know what I’ll do.\"","\"We won’t disappoint you, Immortal Monarch!\" the Clan Leader vowed, his voice filled with determination.","Yuan gave a brief nod, then, in the blink of an eye, he departed from the Heavenly White Valley, swiftly disappearing into the horizon.","Shortly after Yuan’s departure, the Clan Leader called for an emergency meeting with the entire clan. With everyone already present, it was the perfect time to discuss the situation at hand and plan for the clan’s future."]},{"number":2090,"title":"Chapter 2090: Refining the Heavenly White Tiger’s Blood Essence","paragraphs":["\"Is it really okay for you to leave them just like that?\" Feng Yuxiang questioned after they left. \"You should’ve punished the Clan Leader and the elders, even if it’s just a little, since they enabled Bai Xutao’s behavior.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"Who said I’m leaving?\"","\"What?\" Feng Yuxiang muttered, confusion evident in her voice.","Yuan paused in his tracks and said, \"I still have plenty of time before I must return to the Rising Phoenix Clan. I intend to revisit the Heavenly White Tiger Clan before then.\"","\"What are you going to do in the meantime?\"","Yuan retrieved the Heavenly White Tiger’s Blood Essence and said, \"I’m going to refine this blood essence.\"","\"So we’re going to return to my Immortal Cave right now?\"","Yuan shook his head and said, \"I have another place in mind, and it’s much closer.\"","Some time later, they returned to where the Phantasm Serpent’s Nest once existed.","\"Isn’t this...\"","\"I’m going to refine the blood essence in that serpent’s lair,\" he said.","\"In that case, I’ll guard the entrance,\" said Feng Yuxiang as she emerged from his Dantian to stand guard.","\"Thanks.\"","Yuan dug a small hole and disappeared into the ground.","Once he returned to the underground area with the sealed gate, Yuan spoke to the Outer God on the other side, \"I’m going to cultivate here for a bit, so don’t disturb me, or I’ll leave you in there forever.\"","\"...\"","No response.","Yuan sat down in the center of the cave and retrieved the Heavenly White Tiger’s Blood Essence a moment later. Once he prepared himself, he removed the seal and poured the blood essence into his mouth.","<You have consumed the Heavenly White Tiger’s Blood Essence>","<Completed Harmonious Heaven Refining Immortal Physique has activated>","<Completed Harmonious Heaven Refining Immortal Physique has begun to refine the Heavenly White Tiger’s Blood Essence>","Upon consuming the blood essence, Yuan unleashed a deafening roar, one that reverberated through the air like the mighty roar of a tiger.","An immense torrent of spiritual energy suddenly surged forth, so powerful that even Yuan struggled to absorb it. The overwhelming flow threatened to tear his body apart, pushing his Dantian to the brink of destruction.","To prevent his body from being overwhelmed, Yuan had no choice but to expend the spiritual energy within him constantly. Fortunately, there was an indestructible gate near him, allowing him to unleash as much spiritual energy as he wanted.","Though the process was agonizing, it was far more manageable than when he had to refine the Primordial Phoenix’s Bloodline.","Time seemed to fly, and before Yuan realized it, half a year had passed since he began refining the Heavenly White Tiger’s Blood Essence.","<Immortal Monarch’s Bloodline evolution has progressed slightly>","<Progress: 33%>","<Your Immortal Monarch’s techniques have improved>","<You have acquired the power of a Heavenly White Tiger through its Blood Essence>","<You have learned ’Heavenly White Tiger Transformation’>","<Your Dantian has been strengthened, evolving into a Heavenly Dantian>","<Due to your Heavenly Dantian, your cultivation speed has increased by 500,000%>","<You have met the requirements for a breakthrough>","<Your cultivation has reached Golden Immortal>","Yuan opened his eyes, and a faint golden glow radiated from within.","<Heavenly White Tiger Transformation activated>","Yuan’s aura instantly shifted, becoming primal and overwhelmingly domineering, like a predator reigning unchallenged at the pinnacle of the food chain.","Half of his jet-black hair turned stark white, manifesting the signature trait of the Heavenly White Tiger.","Beyond the changes in his appearance, his Heavenly Dantian also strengthened, allowing him to absorb spiritual energy twice as fast.","At his current state, it was essentially impossible for Yuan to run out of spiritual energy if he didn’t exhaust all of it in a single attack. Even if he did, it would replenish in the blink of an eye.","Yuan left the underground cave shortly after refining the blood essence and returned to Feng Yuxiang.","\"It only took you half a year this time, huh?\" she remarked after seeing him in his Heavenly White Tiger transformation.","\"Yes. That said, the Heavenly White Tiger’s blood essence wasn’t as strong as the Primordial Phoenix’s.\"","\"Congratulations on your breakthrough. Now, you’re only one level away from reaching True Immortal and catching up to me,\" said Feng Yuxiang.","\"Have you fully recovered your cultivation?\" Yuan asked her since her cultivation had remained at the True Immortal level for some time now.","She nodded, \"Yes, this was my peak cultivation before I got cursed, but I can feel myself inching toward God Ascension.\"","\"I see...\"","\"So, are we going to return to the Heavenly White Tiger Clan now?\" she then asked.","Yuan nodded.","\"Yes, let’s see how much they’ve changed in half a year.\"","Once Feng Yuxiang entered his Dantian, Yuan made his way back to the Heavenly White Tiger Clan.","\"Wow, what happened to your Dantian? It feels so different now,\" Feng Yuxiang remarked.","\"It evolved after I refined the blood essence. It’s a Heavenly Dantian now, whatever that is.\"","\"I’ve also never heard of such a thing,\" she said.","However, Yu Ning spoke up, \"A Heavenly Dantian was a legend during the Primordial Era. It’s said to be a superior Dantian, a concept that has only ever existed in theory. You know how Body Refiners temper their physiques? Some believed they could temper their Dantian, but it was considered incredibly dangerous, as even the slightest mistake could cripple one’s cultivation.\"","\"A legend, huh? Well, it’s no longer just a theory since we’re living in one right now,\" Feng Yuxiang chuckled.","Some time later, Yuan returned to the Heavenly White Tiger Clan. The place was nearly unrecognizable, having undergone drastic restoration since the devastation he left behind half a year ago.","Yuan activated Shadow Veil, his form fading into the shadows as he silently infiltrated their territory. Once inside, Yuan deactivated Shadow Veil and began wandering the territory in the guise of a Heavenly White Tiger.","Though he had disguised his appearance, he couldn’t change his overwhelming, domineering aura, which immediately drew the attention of everyone nearby, especially the women, who gazed at him with passionate looks on their faces."]},{"number":2091,"title":"Chapter 2091: Returning to the Heavenly White Tiger Clan","paragraphs":["\"Hey, handsome. Where did you come from? I haven’t seen you around here before,\" one of the female tigers said, her movements teasing and suggestive as she approached Yuan.","Yuan calmly faced her and replied, \"That’s probably because I haven’t returned to this place in a few hundred years. What happened here? It’s completely different from before.\"","\"That’s... We decided to renovate the place,\" answered the female.","The female decided not to mention the Immortal Monarch even though Yuan was a Heavenly White Tiger at this moment, as it was essentially forbidden to mention the Immortal Monarch to keep his return a secret.","\"Are you sure? I feel like you’re not telling me everything.\" Yuan said, sounding somewhat aggressive, to increase the pressure.","The woman then said, \"If you give me a good time, I’ll consider telling you about it.\"","Yuan let out a quiet sigh. Without another word, he activated Shadow Veil and vanished like a ghost, disappearing before the stunned onlookers could react.","After leaving, he went deeper into the Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s territory. Although everything appeared normal at a glance, Yuan could tell that something was off about the atmosphere, as it felt unnaturally heavy.","’Everyone seems nervous. They’re probably still having a difficult time accepting the fact that the Immortal Monarch has returned,’ Feng Yuxiang remarked after seeing the situation.","’Or, there could be another reason why they’re so nervous,’ said Yuan.","As Yuan wandered the streets, he continued to draw attention despite his efforts to suppress his aura.","As for those who were bold enough to approach him, he would question them about the state of their clan and if anything weird had happened recently. Of course, none of them would reveal anything about the Immortal Monarch, only mentioning that the clan had decided to change.","\"What? The clan decided to change? Where did this come from? It’s hard to believe.\"","\"It’s true. If you want to know more, you should speak with the elders,\" said the woman Yuan was speaking to.","Since he wasn’t having any luck with the ordinary members of the Heavenly White Tiger Clan, Yuan decided to approach those of higher status. He made his way to the center of their residential area, where the most talented individuals and those with the purest bloodlines resided.","Once a strictly forbidden zone for anyone unqualified, Yuan was pleasantly surprised to find that no one even attempted to stop him. In fact, the area now resembled a tourist attraction, with people freely coming and going, many of whom had never been allowed to set foot there before.","The heavy, oppressive atmosphere that lingered in the outer areas was absent here. Instead, the people seemed more at ease, relaxed and carefree, as if untouched by the concerns weighing down the rest of the clan.","Of course, just like the outer areas, Yuan immediately attracted the people there with his presence.","When one of them approached him, Yuan made some small talk before asking about the situation.","\"I haven’t been to the clan for hundreds of years, and I couldn’t help but notice how different this place has become. What happened while I was away?\"","\"The Clan Leader and the Elders received enlightenment and realized they had been managing the clan improperly, so they decided to change things for the better.\"","\"What enlightened them? I doubt they woke up one day and decided to change the clan so drastically,\" Yuan continued to ask.","\"Since you’re part of the clan, you’ll eventually learn the truth, but it’s forbidden for us ordinary members to reveal it.\"","\"Then, do you know why the atmosphere in the outer areas is so heavy?\"","\"They’re probably struggling to trust the Clan Leader, especially after so many generations of being treated poorly. I don’t blame them. I was like that too for the first two months. The change was simply too sudden.\"","\"Still struggling to adapt, huh? What about the Clan Leader? What’s he doing these days?\"","\"Who knows? Ever since that incident half a year ago, he hasn’t shown himself. But that’s nothing new—he was rarely seen even before everything changed.\"","The residents in this area were far more willing to speak, yet not a single one mentioned the return of the Immortal Monarch.","’They’re really keeping a tight lip about your appearance, huh?’ Feng Yuxiang chuckled.","Once he was satisfied, Yuan left to find Bai Sulan, but since he didn’t know where she lived, he had to ask for directions.","\"Young Lady Sulan? She’s currently living within the main household with the Clan Leader and the elders, so you won’t be able to meet her without their permission.\"","\"Why did she move there, you ask? Well... let’s just say her bloodline has awakened, and now she’s the clan’s top priority.\"","Yuan casually dropped a name to gauge their response. \"Really? That’s amazing. Bai Xutao must be pretty upset about that.\"","As expected, the moment the name left his lips, the people around him exchanged uneasy glances, their expressions turning awkward and tense.","\"What’s wrong?\" Yuan asked after seeing their reaction.","\"The Young Master—No, that troublemaker is no longer with us. Apparently, he died in an accident,\" one of them said.","\"He’s dead?\" Yuan’s eyes widened, pretending to be shocked by this news. \"How did he die?\"","They shook their heads and shrugged their shoulders.","\"I see. What about Bai Ning?\"","\"She’s also at the main household. I heard she went into closed cultivation.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Since there were no other places he could go to investigate, Yuan decided to head to the main household to find the Clan Leader and the Elders.","However, unlike entering the center of their residential area, it was still prohibited for ordinary members to approach the main household without permission.","\"Stop right there. Who are you, and what are you doing here?\" The guard, a Bronze Immortal, questioned Yuan.","Yuan looked at the guard and spoke a single word in a commanding tone, \"Sit.\"","Instantly, the guard sat down on the ground with a dazed look on his face.","\"You... you can’t be...\" he swallowed hard, his eyes as wide as saucers."]},{"number":2092,"title":"Chapter 2092: Returning to the Heavenly White Tiger Clan(2)","paragraphs":["Still in his Heavenly White Tiger form, Yuan offered the guard a calm smile. \"I am who you think I am. Do me a favor and keep it quiet, will you? I don’t want to cause a panic.\"","The guard gave a silent nod, his face pale with disbelief.","\"Thanks,\" Yuan said before turning to approach the massive residence before him.","Even after Yuan had disappeared from his sight, the guard remained seated on the ground, motionless, as if he had forgotten how to stand.","Before entering the residence, Yuan activated Shadow Veil and completely erased his presence.","Then, once inside, he began wandering the place.","After wandering for several minutes, Yuan noticed several powerful presences gathered in one room, so he approached the room and eavesdropped from outside.","\"It’s been half a year since the Immortal Monarch left. Do you think he’ll return any time soon?\"","Yuan knew the people gathered inside the room were the elders even before they spoke based on their aura.","\"Who knows? He could be coming here right now for all we know,\" one of them casually remarked, unaware that he’d hit the nail on the head.","\"I just hope that he’s satisfied with the changes. It wasn’t easy to suddenly change rules that had been in place for many generations.\"","\"If not, we’re probably screwed. The Immortal Monarch could kill all of us with just his words alone.\"","\"There’s no way he’d do something like that, right? According to historical records, the Immortal Monarch worked to protect the beast race from humans and from each other. He’s essentially the reason beasts and humans can co-exist in this day and age,\" said another.","\"He’s saved some and completely eradicated others, especially those who defied him. Some even considered him a tyrant,\" the Eleventh Elder revealed, his voice carrying a clear tremor of fear.","\"In that case, aren’t we defying him right now? After all, we—\"","\"Enough.\" The Clan Leader’s voice suddenly interrupted. \"Nobody is to mention this subject again, especially not before the Immortal Monarch.\"","\"But if he finds out...\"","\"I said enough! I will figure things out myself!\" the Clan Leader snapped.","Yuan narrowed his eyes slightly after hearing this.","\"What do you think they’re trying to hide from you?\" Feng Yuxiang asked, her voice full of curiosity.","\"Who knows? But I will figure it out.\"","Yuan stopped listening to them shortly after when their conversation drifted off topic, and he continued to wander the residence.","Sometime later, Yuan stopped before another room when he sensed a familiar presence within, and it was none other than Bai Sulan.","Yuan knocked on the door after realizing it was her.","\"W-Who’s there?!\" Bai Sulan’s terrified voice rang out a moment later, as if she’d just seen a ghost.","With Yuan’s Shadow Veil still active, she couldn’t sense anyone outside her door, despite the unmistakable sound of knocking. In her panic, she assumed it could only be a ghost.","\"It’s me,\" Yuan calmly replied.","It took a moment, but Bai Sulan recognized his voice. Although she couldn’t believe it, she still had to confirm it.","Once she opened the door and saw Yuan standing outside, her eyes widened with shock and confusion.","\"Who are you?\" she asked, not recognizing his new appearance.","Yuan deactivated his Heavenly White Tiger and returned to his original appearance.","\"Handsome lit—\" Bai Sulan quickly covered her mouth after recalling his true identity.","Yuan smiled and said, \"Just call me whatever you feel comfortable.\"","\"B-But you’re the Immortal Monarch... You’re our Ancestor’s Master...\" she spoke nervously.","\"So what?\"","\"I might get punished for not respecting you.\"","\"I gave you permission, so who would dare to punish you?\"","\"If you say so, handsome big brother...\" Bai Sulan said.","\"Can I come inside? I came here secretly, and I don’t want the others to find out yet.\"","She nodded and gestured for him to enter her room.","\"How come I cannot sense your presence even though I am staring right at you?\" she asked once he closed the door.","\"I am using a technique to hide my presence.\"","\"I see... Then why are you hiding from the others?\"","\"I want to see if the Heavenly White Tiger Clan—the Clan Leader and the elders actually acted on their promise and changed the way they managed the clan.\"","\"In that case, you don’t have to worry,\" Bai Sulan said reassuringly. \"Things have definitely changed for the better. While a hierarchy still exists within the clan, it’s no longer as rigid, and we’re no longer executed for failing our trials.\"","\"That’s good to hear. What about you? Did anyone try to steal the blood I gave you?\" Yuan asked.","Bai Sulan let out a soft chuckle. \"No one’s dared to take it by force, but plenty have tried to convince me to share it, offering treasures and all sorts of things. Naturally, I refused.\"","\"By the way, is this really your blood?\" Bai Sulan asked, retrieving an empty glass vial. \"Why does it taste so good? I meant to try just a drop, but before I knew it, I’d finished the whole thing.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"Want to confirm it?\"","She nodded eagerly.","Yuan retrieved a drop of his own blood before her eyes and flicked it into her mouth.","\"Wow! This tastes even better than before!\" she exclaimed.","Since Yuan’s bloodline had advanced after refining the Heavenly White Tiger’s Blood Essence, it was only natural that the quality of his blood had improved as well. Of course, Bai Sulan wasn’t aware of this fact.","\"How does this work? Why does it taste so good?\" Bai Sulan then asked.","\"I don’t know, but it likely has something to do with my bloodline.\"","\"Do you do something special to give it this taste? Can you give out as much blood as you want? Is there a limit?\" She then bombarded him with several questions.","Yuan raised an eyebrow and pondered silently for a moment before responding, \"That’s a good question, but I’ve never considered it, nor have I ever reached a limit.\""]},{"number":2093,"title":"Chapter 2093: The Clan Leader’s Secret","paragraphs":["\"You’ve never reached a limit? So you basically have an unlimited supply of blood?\" Bai Sulan muttered, a strange flicker in her eyes. Unbeknownst to her, she was licking her lips, looking like a child staring longingly at a jar of candy.","Yuan smiled at her reaction and said calmly, \"No, it just means I rarely give out my blood. Even if it were unlimited, giving away too much wouldn’t be wise, considering the powerful effects it carries.\"","The Immortal Monarch’s blood was precious for a reason. If Yuan were to give it freely to anyone who asked, it could lead to unimaginable consequences, disrupting the balance of power across the Nine Heavens.","\"My bloodline awakened and became the most powerful within the clan after consuming that little amount you gave me. I cannot imagine what could happen if it were accessible to everyone...\" Bai Sulan mumbled.","She looked at him thoughtfully and asked, \"Since your blood is so powerful and precious, I imagine you’ve had more than a few troublemakers trying to get their hands on it, haven’t you?\"","To beasts, Yuan’s blood was the most coveted treasure, and their greed was no different from that of humans. Some would go to any lengths to claim it for themselves.","Yuan let out a calm chuckle and said, \"That’s right. Back in the Immortal Monarch’s Era, I was constantly dealing with beasts trying to steal my blood. They’d ambush me without warning, hoping to claim even a single drop.\"","\"Because of that, I had to learn how to control my blood, ensuring it would only be effective when I allowed it to. It took some time, but I eventually managed to do it. Of course, that didn’t stop the troublemakers from trying anyway.\"","This meant that even if Yuan were injured and bled in a battle, the blood he shed wouldn’t carry the Immortal Monarch’s power.","After chatting for a little longer, Yuan asked, \"Do you know where I can find Bai Ning?\"","\"Senior Sister Ning? She left the clan a month ago,\" she replied.","Before Yuan could ask, Bai Sulan continued, \"She had a falling out with the Eleventh Elder, who destroyed your blood. Of course, that wasn’t her only reason for leaving. She said something about exploring the Nine Heavens to seek enlightenment.\"","\"I see...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan asked, \"On my way here, I overheard your elders and the Clan Leader’s meeting. Apparently, they’re hiding something from me. Do you know what they’re hiding?\"","Bai Sulan raised her eyebrows and looked genuinely puzzled.","\"No,\" she eventually shook her head.","\"Is that so...\"","\"Do you want me to find out what they’re hiding?\" Bai Sulan suddenly asked.","Yuan quickly responded, \"No, there’s no need for you to do that. I’ll figure it out myself.\"","\"Okay.\"","\"Anyway, I guess it’s about time I check up with them.\"","Yuan suddenly deactivated Shadow Veil, allowing his presence to spread throughout the residence.","Not far away, the Clan Leader and the elders instantly froze when they sensed his appearance out of thin air like a ghost.","\"T-This presence! It can’t be!\"","\"The Immortal Monarch has returned!\"","They hastily rushed out of the room, even breaking down the door in the process, and followed the presence to Bai Sulan’s room.","When they arrived, Yuan was calmly standing inside.","\"We greet the Immortal Monarch!\"","They all lowered their bodies and bowed to him.","\"It’s been half a year.\" Yuan faced them with a calm expression on his face.","\"Did you just arrive?\" the Clan Leader asked.","\"No,\" Yuan replied calmly. \"I’ve been here for some time. I chose not to announce my return since I wanted to observe the current state of the Heavenly White Tiger Clan first.\"","The elders trembled at these words.","\"We’ve implemented many changes already, but some require more time to take full effect. If there’s anything you find lacking, please let us know and we’ll address it immediately,\" said the Clan Leader.","Yuan looked at him and spoke calmly, \"I’m not asking you to change the entire clan or force yourselves to live a completely different life. But understand this—no matter how much you refine the surface, if the core remains rotten, it’s all meaningless.\"","At that moment, Yuan activated Immortal Monarch’s Supremacy. His eyes turned silver, and his presence flooded the entire space with an overwhelming pressure. Then, in a firm and commanding voice, he said, \"If you think you can hide anything from me, just know that I need only speak a few words, and you’ll reveal everything on your own. I’ll give you a chance to speak willingly now. Is there anything you want to tell me?\"","The elders trembled with fear, instantly turning their eyes to the Clan Leader, awaiting his response. It was clear that Yuan had somehow learned of their secret.","Realizing that silence would be futile—and that one of the elders would surely speak up if he didn’t—he let out a deep sigh and said, \"There is one thing I need to tell you. But... it’ll be easier if I show you instead.\"","\"Please, follow me,\" the Clan Leader said before turning and walking away.","Yuan and the elders followed in silence, their expressions solemn. Driven by curiosity, Bai Sulan quietly trailed behind them.","A few minutes later, they stopped before another room. However, this room had several formations on the sealed door, preventing anyone from looking inside.","’Whatever they’re trying to hide from you, it must be quite serious.’ Yu Ning remarked after seeing the formations.","After taking a moment to undo the formations, the Clan Leader spoke cautiously, \"Immortal Monarch, please understand that this wasn’t done to defy you...\"","\"Spare the excuses for later,\" Yuan interrupted, striding forward and pushing the door open without hesitation.","As Yuan stepped into the room and took in the sight before him, his eyes widened in surprise, a look of genuine amazement spreading across his face.","Lying peacefully on the bed was none other than Bai Xutao. Though unconscious, he was still breathing. His appearance had also changed drastically, now looking like a shriveled old man on his deathbed, a far cry from the healthy young figure he once was."]},{"number":2094,"title":"Chapter 2094: Bai Xutao’s Persistence","paragraphs":["\"That’s... Bai Xutao?\"","At first glance, Yuan didn’t recognize Bai Xutao due to the drastic change in his appearance, but even in its weakened state, his aura was unmistakable. It was undeniably Bai Xutao.","\"No way... he actually survived? Maybe he’s not a Heavenly White Tiger after all, and his true bloodline might just be that of a cockroach,\" Feng Yuxiang remarked, sounding utterly dumbfounded by his persistence that rivaled cockroaches.","’I only extracted his ancestor’s blood essence, so that must be what kept him alive. Still, even then, it’s nothing short of a miracle,’ Yuan explained to her.","Yuan turned to look at the Clan Leader and the elders, who were still standing outside the room with guilty expressions on their faces.","\"Explain yourselves,\" Yuan said.","The Clan Leader spoke immediately, his tone heavy with reluctance. \"We all believed he had perished. But during the restoration of our territory, we found Bai Xutao barely clinging to life. We thought about letting him die, but... my fatherly instincts compelled me to save him. Though he’s still breathing, he hasn’t woken up since we found him.\"","\"Your fatherly instincts?\" Yuan sneered coldly, his gaze turning to the Clan Leader with disdain. \"That’s rich, coming from someone who’s killed countless of their own children simply because their bloodlines didn’t meet your standards.\"","\"T-That’s...\" The Clan Leader fell silent, unable to refute Yuan’s sharp rebuke.","\"What’s so special about Bai Xutao that you decided to save him, despite everything that’s happened?\" Yuan pressed, his voice cold. \"Looking at him now, his injuries are likely permanent. He’ll be crippled for the rest of his life. Is he really worth the risk?\"","Before the Clan Leader could respond, Yuan approached him and continued, \"What if I were to say that I will eradicate the entire Heavenly White Tiger Clan over this? Have you thought of this possibility? I doubt you didn’t. Yet, you still decided to take the risk.\"","\"I have no excuses...\" The Clan Leader sighed, his voice heavy with defeat.","Yuan turned his gaze to the elders, his tone sharp. \"You’re no better for allowing him to act so selfishly. You’re supposed to be the elders of this clan. Where is your authority? Are you only capable of flaunting it when trying to suppress others?\"","\"We have no excuses.\"","The elders lowered their heads in shame.","\"I’m deeply disappointed in you all,\" Yuan said, his voice cold. \"And don’t misunderstand. This isn’t about the fact that you allowed Bai Xutao to live. I’m actually impressed by how quickly you’ve changed, at least on the surface. But inside, you’re still selfish, and when the time comes, you wouldn’t hesitate to sacrifice your own people.\"","Yuan began walking toward the door, his voice steady and firm. \"Until your Heavenly White Tiger Clan shows real change, I won’t be able to accept you. And don’t think you can win my favor by killing Bai Xutao now.\"","\"In fact, it’s mostly the leadership that’s the problem. I could kill all of you and replace you with more competent individuals, but I won’t do that.\"","The Clan Leader and the elders trembled at Yuan’s words, but what truly caused their hearts to sink wasn’t the threat itself—it was the crushing realization that they had lost the chance to receive the Immortal Monarch’s aid.","\"As for Bai Xutao...\" Yuan continued. \"Since he’s managed to survive time and time again, I’m sure fate hasn’t finished with him yet. So, I won’t kill him—provided he remains in this territory for the rest of his life.\"","As Yuan walked out of the room, Bai Sulan suddenly grabbed his robes and asked with a saddened face, \"Will I ever see you again?\"","\"If fate allows it,\" Yuan replied as he rubbed her head.","\"Okay...\" Bai Sulan nodded her head as she released his robes.","Yuan turned to look at the others and warned them in a cold voice, \"I hope you won’t be foolish enough to reveal my identity for revenge.\"","\"W-We wouldn’t dare!\" They quickly shook their heads.","Then, Yuan activated Shadow Veil and disappeared from their sight like a ghost.","Although the Clan Leader and the elders were desperate to stop him, they hesitated, unwilling to risk angering him further, fearing that it might prompt him to change his mind and wipe them all out.","\"Are we really leaving this time?\" Feng Yuxiang asked Yuan after they left the Heavenly White Tiger Clan for a second time.","He nodded, \"Yes, we’re going to return to the Rising Phoenix Clan now.\"","\"Alright. Although you didn’t kill the Clan Leader or the elders, I feel like this is a more fitting punishment for them since they will have to live the rest of their lives with regret. Hopefully nothing will happen to Bai Sulan, though.\"","Yuan then reassured her, \"Nothing will happen to her. With Bai Xutao in that condition and Bai Ning leaving the clan, she’s their only hope now.\"","\"I see. That makes sense. There’s also that little surprise you left behind for her.\" Feng Yuxiang chuckled.","Shortly after Yuan left, Bai Sulan quietly returned to her room while the Clan Leader and the elders started another meeting to discuss their future.","When she returned to her room, Bai Sulan was surprised to see a wooden box placed on her bed, something she wasn’t familiar with and hadn’t existed before.","When she opened the box, her eyes widened with shock and disbelief. Inside, there were several glass vials containing blood.","Although no note was left behind and they were sealed, Bai Sulan instantly recognized whose blood it was.","She held it close to her chest and mumbled with a sweet smile on her face, \"Once I become a capable adult, I will definitely come find you, handsome big brother.\"","Then, she stowed the glass vials away and left her room to train.","After several days of intense discussion, the Clan Leader and the elders decided to adapt to the new rules and continue working towards improving their clan, hoping that, one day, Yuan might return and give them another chance."]},{"number":2095,"title":"Chapter 2095: A Detour","paragraphs":["After departing from the Heavenly White Tiger Clan, Yuan began his journey back to the Rising Phoenix Clan, despite still having several months left before the one-year promise.","However, along the way, he was forced to halt when he spotted two groups of cultivators clashing in the middle of nowhere.","Typically, Yuan wouldn’t have paid such a scene any mind, as it had nothing to do with him. But this time, something caught his attention, as the attire of these cultivators looked familiar, compelling him to stay and observe.","\"Hm? Those robes... Aren’t they the Demon Sealing Clan’s robes?\" Feng Yuxiang commented after seeing them.","\"Yes, and the other one belongs to the Demon Sealing Grotto,\" Yuan confirmed.","The Demon Sealing Clan and the Demon Sealing Grotto members noticed Yuan shortly after he arrived, but immediately stopped paying attention to him once they realized that he wasn’t reinforcement from the other side and continued their fight.","These members were mostly Bronze Immortals, with a few still in the Divine Realm.","\"I have been getting really tired of you guys lately! Do you think you’re better than the Demon Sealing Clan because you’re slightly better at controlling Demon Sealing Aura?!\"","\"Hah! What Demon Sealing Clan? You guys are nothing but old news! There’s a reason why most of your original members have left and joined us at the Demon Sealing Grotto instead!\"","\"Right?! You’re just a bunch of envious bastards! That’s why you schemed against us during the Supreme Demon Sealer qualifications!\"","\"What scheme?! You’re just slandering us at this point!\"","The battle intensified with each passing moment.","\"Aren’t you going to stop them?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","Yuan replied calmly, \"They may be fighting, but I don’t sense any real killing intent. They’ll be fine—it’s more like watching a bunch of kids squabbling.\"","Suddenly, a powerful presence descended upon the place, instantly halting everyone’s movement.","\"What do you idiots think you’re doing?! Stop this immediately!\" A familiar voice resounded the very next moment, and a beautiful woman appeared before them.","It was none other than Yan Hara.","\"Senior Yan, they’re the ones who started this fight!\" said one of the Demon Sealing Clan members.","\"That’s right! They attacked us on sight! We were only defending ourselves!\"","Yan Hara turned to look at the Demon Sealing Grottos with a frown.","\"Explain yourselves,\" she demanded.","\"What is there to explain? Your Demon Sealing Clan started this.\"","\"...\"","Instead of being angry, Yan Hara merely said, \"Since nobody was seriously injured, I’ll let you leave. Get lost before I change my mind.\"","\"Hmph.\"","The Demon Sealing Grotto did not stay and quickly left the scene.","\"Senior Yan! Why did you let them go that easily?! They’ll think they can bully us and get away with it!\"","\"We need to fight back, or they’ll just keep doing it!\"","Yan Hara looked at them and sighed. \"Regardless of how you feel about each other, with the recent movements from the demon worshippers, we’ll need to stand together. Fighting among ourselves won’t just weaken us—it will endanger the rest of the world.\"","\"So are we just supposed to endure it?!\"","Yan Hara narrowed her eyes and said coldly, \"Do you really take me for a fool? What are you doing near the Demon Sealing Grotto’s headquarters? If you expect me to believe you came here unaware, I’ve got bad news for you.\"","The Demon Sealing Clan’s members instantly panicked, their composure unraveling under her piercing words. Though the Demon Sealing Grotto had attacked first, they had clearly provoked the conflict by deliberately trespassing into their territory.","In other words, they were asking for trouble.","\"B-But—\"","\"Enough with your excuses. Get out of here before I get angry for real,\" Yan Hara interrupted, raising her voice.","The Demon Sealing Clan members didn’t dare to linger any longer and swiftly fled the scene.","Once the others had left, Yan Hara finally turned her attention to the presence observing from afar.","At first, she didn’t recognize Yuan, as his aura had changed so drastically. But the moment she saw his familiar, handsome face, her eyes widened in shock and disbelief.","\"Y-Yuan?! What are you doing here?!\" Yan Hara exclaimed as he approached her.","Yuan greeted her with a calm smile, \"I could say the same to you. What are you doing out here in the middle of nowhere? I’m on my way to the Rising Phoenix Clan.\"","\"The Rising Phoenix Clan...? Well, I am on my way to visit the Demon Sealing Grotto for a meeting. Since Qian Chu is still away, I have to take his place.\"","Yuan raised his eyebrows and asked, \"Don’t they have the Grand Elders to take his spot?\"","\"Yes, but my position within the clan has reached the point where even the Grand Elders are wary of me. In fact, they’re the ones who told me to go in Qian Chu’s place. They’re probably hoping that I’d screw up or something.\"","Yuan pondered for a moment before responding, \"Do you think I can go with you?\"","\"Eh? I don’t mind, but don’t you have business with the Rising Phoenix Clan?\"","He nodded and explained, \"Yes, but I still have about half a year to spare.\"","\"If you say so.\"","Thus, Yuan made a detour to visit the Demon Sealing Grotto with Yan Hara.","\"When did you arrive at the Eighth Heaven?\" Yan Hara asked.","\"Very recently.\"","\"Then what have you been up to?\"","\"I was just at the Heavenly White Tiger Clan.\"","\"You have ties to both the Rising Phoenix Clan and the Heavenly White Tiger Clan? Those are incredibly exclusive places—neither of which usually welcome humans.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"I’ll tell you about it someday.\"","A few days later, they arrived at the Demon Sealing Grotto’s headquarters—a hidden stronghold that existed within its own separate dimension. The portal leading to it was tucked away in a remote city deep within the wilderness.","\"I’m Yan Hara of the Demon Sealing Clan, here on behalf of Qian Chu, who’s currently unavailable,\" she said, presenting her medallion to the guards as proof of her identity.","\"We have been expecting you, Master Demon Sealer Yan Hara, but who is that next to you?\"","The guard pointed at Yuan with his gaze."]},{"number":2096,"title":"Chapter 2096: Visiting the Demon Sealing Grotto","paragraphs":["When the guard questioned about Yuan, Yan Hara calmly responded, \"He’s an Elite Demon Sealer of the Demon Sealing Clan and my disciple. Is there any problem with him being present?\"","\"Well, the higher-ups will be there, so it might not be a good idea to bring him with you,\" said the guard. \"The pressure might be too much for him to handle.\"","\"You don’t have to worry about me. If I get overwhelmed, I won’t blame anyone,\" Yuan said with a calm smile on his face.","\"You heard him. I also won’t say anything,\" said Yan Hara.","\"In that case...\"","The guard silently stepped aside and activated the array behind him, revealing the portal to the Demon Sealing Grotto’s headquarters.","Yan Hara entered first, with Yuan following closely behind.","On the other side, they were greeted by the sight of a city—more refined and orderly than the one outside, and the entire place was suffused with a dense Demon Sealing Aura.","\"So this is the Demon Sealing Grotto, huh?\" Yuan muttered as he looked around.","Yan Hara looked at him and asked, \"This is your first time visiting this place, right?\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"This is where most of their demon sealers train,\" Yan Hara explained. \"Unlike our Demon Sealing Clan, whose members are scattered across the Nine Heavens, the Demon Sealing Grotto keeps most of its members here. They rarely leave—only venturing out when necessary to investigate or eliminate demon worshippers and demons.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"So, in other words, the Demon Sealing Grotto takes demon sealing far more seriously than the Demon Sealing Clan? Sounds like comparing a full-time professional to someone working part-time.\"","\"T-That’s...\" Yan Hara was momentarily speechless at his comparison, but upon reflection, she understood his point.","Compared to the Demon Sealing Grotto, the Demon Sealing Clan was indeed far more relaxed and casual. For many within the clan, being a Demon Sealer was a secondary pursuit—something they practiced alongside their main cultivation path. In contrast, those from the Demon Sealing Grotto treated it as their primary purpose, dedicating their lives wholly to the art of sealing demons.","This was also the reason why the Demon Sealing Clan had declined, no longer able to compare to the Demon Sealing Grotto in recent times.","Yuan wanted to explore the place for a bit, but shortly after their arrival, a member of the Demon Sealing Grotto appeared to escort them to their destination.","Some time later, they arrived before a grand white building that exuded a formal and solemn atmosphere, clearly a place reserved for important meetings and official gatherings.","\"The Elders are waiting inside,\" said the escort as he opened the door for them.","Yuan and Yan Hara stepped into a vast chamber lined with hundreds of seats, most of which were already occupied by members of the Demon Sealing Grotto.","Every Demon Sealer within the chamber was at least a Golden Immortal, their very presence radiating a dense Demon Sealing Aura that seemed to suppress the air itself.","\"Please, proceed to the front,\" the escort said, gesturing toward two distinct seats set apart from the rest—clearly positioned as the center of attention. However, one of the two seats was already occupied by an old man radiating a profound aura, leaving Yuan to stand beside Yan Hara as she took the remaining seat.","\"Welcome to our humble estate, Demon Sealer Yan Hara.\"","The old man seated beside her immediately started the conversation.","\"It’s been a while, Senior Zhou,\" Yan Hara respectfully greeted him.","\"This old man is the Demon Sealing Grotto’s leader, Zhou Yanfei,\" she revealed to Yuan using voice transmission.","The old man noticed that she was using voice transmission and turned to look at Yuan.","\"I wasn’t expecting a second guest today,\" he said.","Though the old man released no pressure, the atmosphere in the room grew oppressively heavy, and Yuan could distinctly feel the weight of hundreds of powerful gazes bearing down on him.","Yet, Yuan remained tranquil, looking completely unaffected by it.","\"He is my disciple and an Elite Demon Sealer,\" Yan Hara stated calmly. \"Since he’s never visited before, I brought him along.\"","\"Quite the bold decision, Demon Sealer Yan Hara,\" Zhou Yanfei responded coolly. \"If I were in your position, I wouldn’t risk bringing someone who might become a liability to a place like this.\"","Yan Hara smiled faintly and asked, \"Why not? Have I walked into a trap? Will you strike us down now that we are in your territory?\"","\"Unlike a certain someone, we are not so uncivilized,\" Zhou Yanfei shook his head, and he continued, \"And even if we were, we’re not foolish enough to start infighting while the threat of the demons looms over us all.\"","\"So, what is this all about? I’m only here to act in Qian Chu’s stead, since he’s unavailable,\" Yan Hara asked.","Zhou Yanfei’s expression darkened the moment Qian Chu’s name was mentioned.","\"The world teeters on the brink of chaos, and that scheming bastard has vanished without a trace for years now,\" he said coldly. \"I cannot fathom why the Demon Sealing Clan chose such a bastard as their leader.\"","Yan Hara shrugged and calmly responded, \"Beats me. I was just an ordinary member who recently joined when he was appointed as the leader.\"","Zhou Yanfei sneered coldly. \"You incompetent fools are dragging the Demon Sealing Clan into ruin.\"","He paused, his gaze sharp. \"Our original intention was to force Qian Chu to reveal why he’s targeting our Demon Sealing Grotto, but since he’s absent, our attention will shift elsewhere today.\"","\"Demon Sealer Yan Hara,\" Zhou Yanfei continued, his tone edged with curiosity. \"Your recent activities have greatly intrigued me. With how you’ve been quietly rallying members of the Demon Sealing Clan to your side and raising your position within the clan, are you aiming to challenge Qian Chu for his position?\"","\"Maybe I am. Maybe I’m not. What’s it to you?\" Yan Hara replied with a calm smile.","Zhou Yanfei’s eyes narrowed slightly before he declared, \"If you truly intend to bring down Qian Chu, the Demon Sealing Grotto is prepared to lend you our support.\""]},{"number":2097,"title":"Chapter 2097: Visiting the Demon Sealing Grotto(2)","paragraphs":["\"The Demon Sealing Grotto will support me?\" Yan Hara raised an eyebrow, genuine surprise flickering in her eyes. \"That’s quite the unexpected offer. However, I must ask—what if I am not trying to challenge Qian Chu for his position? What if I am just trying to increase my position for my own benefits?\"","Zhou Yanfei paused briefly before speaking, his gaze steady. \"That’s difficult to believe. I may not know everything about you, but I know enough to say you’re not the type to act so selfishly. And those you’ve been rallying—they’re all individuals who are not under Qian Chu’s influence.\"","\"If you’re not aiming to challenge Qian Chu, then whatever you’re planning must be something that will shake the very foundation of the Demon Sealing Clan.\"","\"You sound very confident in that statement.\"","\"That’s just the feeling I am getting from you.\"","\"Well, unfortunately, I have no intention of challenging Qian Chu,\" Yan Hara said, lying without the slightest hesitation.","She couldn’t afford to trust Zhou Yanfei so easily—not when there was no telling if his offer was sincere or if spies loyal to Qian Chu were lurking within the chamber.","Zhou Yanfei narrowed his eyes slightly, but he didn’t continue to dwell on the topic and said, \"Let’s talk about something else then. During the Supreme Demon Sealer Qualifications... What happened?\"","\"Why are you asking me that again? I already told you everything back then.\" Yan Hara raised her eyebrows in a puzzled manner.","\"My memories are getting a little hazy these days, so why don’t you remind me?\"","Yan Hara rubbed her eyes and let out a soft sigh. \"As I’ve said before, I was in the midst of battling the Demon Emperor when I was suddenly seized by the Demon Sealing Flag. At the time, I didn’t understand what had happened, but I later learned it was Qian Chu who had saved me.\"","She paused briefly before adding, \"That’s also why I have no intention of challenging him. I could never turn against the one who saved my life.\"","Naturally, she’d already realized that it was Yuan who saved her that day, but it was true that she initially thought it was Qian Chu who saved her life.","\"Ah, yes. I recall now,\" Zhou Yanfei said, his voice laced with curiosity. \"Though, I find it rather strange that Qian Chu saved you, yet allowed the others to perish. Why is that? Are you two perhaps... involved in that kind of relationship?\"","Yan Hara’s expression turned cold as she said with quiet fury, \"Even if you’re the Demon Sealing Grotto’s leader, I won’t allow such disrespect.\"","Zhou Yanfei quickly offered a courteous nod. \"My apologies if my speculation came off as offensive. But that only deepens the mystery—why did he save you? To my knowledge, Qian Chu has never intervened personally for anyone before.\"","\"You’ll have to ask Qian Chu since I have no idea what he’s thinking.\"","Zhou Yanfei let out a heavy sigh. \"That day, three of our most gifted Demon Sealers lost their lives, while the Demon Sealing Clan suffered not a single casualty. We will not rest until the truth is unveiled, and those responsible are held accountable.\"","\"...\"","Yan Hara fell silent. There was nothing she could say to defend that incident, as she understood how guilty the Demon Sealing Clan looked. She had been there, but held no control over what had transpired. And even if Qian Chu had truly tried to orchestrate their deaths as an accident, they had no proof.","\"I will ask you one last time. Do you know what happened on that day?\" Zhou Yanfei asked again a moment later.","\"No.\" Yan Hara instantly responded with an adamant face.","\"In that case, there’s nothing more to discuss. Should you choose to challenge Qian Chu or want to switch sides, you may contact us again. And before you leave, we’d like you to pass a message to the rest of the Demon Sealing Clan.\"","Zhou Yanfei paused briefly, his expression turning cold and his gaze radiating killing intent.","\"We, the Demon Sealing Grotto, hereby declare war on the Demon Sealing Clan. From this moment forth, any member of your clan who dares approach us will be killed without mercy.\"","Yan Hara’s eyes widened with disbelief. \"What happened to not turning on each other because of the looming threat?! You called it foolish just minutes ago!\"","Zhou Yanfei responded with a cold sneer.","\"I was talking about you, Yan Hara. It would be foolish to eliminate a Demon Sealer of your caliber. But the rest of the Demon Sealing Clan?\" He scoffed.","\"They’re nothing but dead weight—fodder in the face of war against the demons. Purging them would be a mercy, not a loss.\"","\"Th-That’s—!\"","\"Why are you so shocked?\" Zhou Yanfei said. \"You of all people should’ve seen this coming. Our factions have been at each other’s throats for decades, and it was only a matter of time. This war didn’t begin with us. Your Demon Sealing Clan lit the fire. We only sought to hone our Demon Sealing Aura and hunt demons, but your people forced our hand.\"","Although Yan Hara couldn’t refute Zhou Yanfei’s words, she still sought a path to reconciliation. A war between them now, with the looming threat of demons, would be nothing short of catastrophic.","Just as Yan Hara struggled to find a solution, Yuan finally broke his silence and calmly said, \"If you don’t mind, there are a few things I would like to say.\"","\"Huh?\" Zhou Yanfei’s gaze snapped to Yuan, his eyes sharp with disdain. \"This conversation is far beyond your station, boy. Do yourself and your master a favor: keep quiet and walk away before you make this any worse.\"","Despite the threat, a tranquil expression remained on Yuan’s face as he spoke, \"I understand your fury over the loss of your Demon Sealers. However, both factions bear some responsibility for what transpired—and if blame must be assigned, Qian Chu bears the greatest burden. To condemn the entire Demon Sealing Clan for the actions of one man would be both unreasonable and shortsighted.\""]},{"number":2098,"title":"Chapter 2098: Visiting the Demon Sealing Grotto(3)","paragraphs":["\"What...?\" Zhou Yanfei’s eyes widened in shock at Yuan’s response.","The other Demon Sealers in the room exchanged uneasy glances, clearly taken aback.","\"Do you even know what you’re saying?! Why should we bear any responsibility when it was Qian Chu who clearly plotted against us?!\" someone in the room exclaimed out loud, his voice full of anger.","Yuan turned to look at the man who had just spoken and calmly explained, \"The fact that both sides agreed to release a Demon Emperor means that both are responsible. You’re naive if you think you have the strength to deal with a Demon Emperor. Who do you think you are? The Divine Paragon?\"","The man opened his mouth, but no words came out.","Yuan’s tone remained unwavering as he continued, \"I’ve heard that for the last Supreme Demon Sealer Qualifications, you only used a Demon General. So why the sudden shift to a Demon Emperor? I was present during that incident, and I can say with certainty that none of you had the power to kill the Demon Emperor—not even Qian Chu, who claimed to have captured it. If it had truly wished to, it could’ve slaughtered everyone that day. Fortunately, it chose to leave.\"","The room fell silent, as nobody knew how to respond.","\"What do you know? You’re just a mere Elite Demon Sealer!\" Someone there eventually snapped.","\"That’s right! What gives you the qualifications to make such claims when you’ve probably never even killed a demon before?!\"","Hearing her idol being slandered, Yan Hara could not remain silent and subconsciously defended Yuan, \"What the hell do you know?! He’s killed more demons than anyone in this room combined!\"","The room fell silent again, but moments later, it erupted with laughter. Even Zhou Yanfei couldn’t help but burst out laughing.","\"He’s killed more demons than anyone in this room combined?\" Zhou Yanfei repeated in a mocking tone. \"Not even Qian Chu would dare make such a claim! Yet, you’re saying that a mere Elite Demon Sealer has killed more demons than him?! If that is true, then why the hell is he still your disciple?! With such an amazing achievement, he should be leading the Demon Sealing Clan instead! Hell, I’d even let him lead the Demon Sealing Grotto! Ahaha!\"","Yan Hara looked at Yuan with an apologetic gaze.","\"I’m sorry, I couldn’t keep my mouth shut...\" she said to him using voice transmission.","Yuan shook his head with a calm smile and said out loud, \"It’s true, though.\"","\"What? You can’t be serious.\"","Zhou Yanfei and the others immediately stopped laughing, their expressions hardening with anger. They looked as though they were being mocked.","\"Do you really take us for fools?\" Zhou Yanfei narrowed his eyes, his voice dripping with disdain.","Yuan didn’t respond right away. Instead, he turned to Yan Hara and asked calmly, \"May I?\"","Understanding his intent, Yan Hara nodded and stood up, silently giving him her seat. The others watched in surprise, for her actions clearly indicated that Yuan held more status than she did.","Once Yuan sat down, he unleashed a massive wave of Demon Sealing Aura that not only filled the room but also began to petrify those around him, which was only possible if his Demon Sealing Aura vastly surpassed theirs. Yet, everyone in the room was a top-ranking member of the Demon Sealing Grotto and an established Demon Sealer.","\"T-This is—!\"","Zhou Yanfei’s eyes widened in shock and disbelief. While his body didn’t appear petrified under Yuan’s overwhelming Demon Sealing Aura, it became so stiff that even lifting a finger felt like an impossible task.","\"Who the hell are you?!\" he muttered with much difficulty.","The sheer volume of Demon Sealing Aura Yuan exuded was unlike anything they had ever felt before. Not even Qian Chu—hailed as the most talented Demon Sealer since the Divine Paragon—could compare to the overwhelming force Yuan was unleashing.","Although Yuan wasn’t hiding his face with a mask, he’d consumed an appearance-altering pill before visiting the Demon Sealing Grotto. After all, if he’d gone in his original appearance, there was a good chance they would recognize him, which could complicate things.","However, even though he’d revealed some of his Demon Sealing Aura, he didn’t plan on revealing himself as the Divine Paragon so soon.","\"I am just a mere Elite Demon Sealer from the Demon Sealing Clan,\" Yuan nonchalantly responded to Zhou Yanfei’s inquiry.","\"There’s no way you’re just a mere Elite Demon Sealer with that level of Demon Sealing Aura! Hell, I doubt you’re even Yan Hara’s disciple!\"","\"Does it really matter if I am her disciple or an Elite Demon Sealer? You only need to know that I am not only Qian Chu’s side and that I am not the Demon Sealing Grotto’s enemy... at least for now.\"","\"For now...?\" Zhou Yanfei quickly realized that Yuan was trying to say he could be their ally or enemy, depending on how they handled the situation.","\"Naturally, I don’t want to be your enemy. In fact, I am very impressed by how the Demon Sealing Grotto has managed its members compared to the Demon Sealing Clan. If you ask me, I dare say you are this era’s true Demon Sealing Clan.\"","\"...\"","Zhou Yanfei was slightly taken aback when Yuan suddenly began praising them.","\"You guys didn’t like how the Demon Sealing Clan had fallen, so you created your own place, passing down the Demon Sealing Clan’s true legacy. If the Divine Paragon were here, he’d definitely say the same thing.\"","Yan Hara could only listen in silence. Even though she agreed with Yuan, it still pained her to hear the Divine Paragon and founder of the Demon Sealing Clan discrediting them in such a manner.","\"Where are you trying to go with this?\" Zhou Yanfei asked with a suspicious look on his face.","Yuan smiled and said, \"It’s quite simple. I want—\"","Right as Yuan opened his mouth to respond, a shift occurred in the room when nearly every Demon Sealer there suddenly retrieved their communication jade slip, including Zhou Yanfei.","This unusual event halted Yuan, and he watched as the Demon Sealers’ faces twisted with surprise.","\"D-Demon Worshippers have appeared and are attacking the outside city!\" one of them exclaimed, revealing the situation to Yuan."]},{"number":2099,"title":"Chapter 2099: Demon Worshippers’ Invasion","paragraphs":["\"What in heaven’s name?! We’re being attacked by Demon Worshippers?!\" Zhou Yanfei was in disbelief after hearing this information from his communication jade slip.","He couldn’t fathom what the Demon Worshippers were thinking since they typically avoided Demon Sealers like the plague and would never willingly approach them. Yet, they were attacking the Demon Sealing Grotto’s headquarters out of the blue.","\"If they’re attacking the Demon Sealing Grotto, what about the Demon Sealing Clan?!\" Yan Hara asked out loud amidst the confusion.","\"How would we know? You should ask them yourself. Our meeting here is done. We have some business to take care of.\" Zhou Yanfei stood up and looked at the other Demon Sealers in the room before continuing, \"These Demon Worshippers have gotten brazen! Make sure you kill each and every last one of them for pulling this stunt!\"","As everyone swiftly left the room, Yan Hara retrieved a communication jade slip to contact someone from the Demon Sealing Clan.","\"Are you at the Demon Sealing Clan’s headquarters?! Is everything okay there?!\" she asked whoever was on the other end.","\"Huh? Why wouldn’t we be okay?\" a calm voice responded.","\"I am at the Demon Sealing Grotto, and they’re being attacked by Demon Worshippers.\" Yan Hara revealed.","\"What? Demon Worshippers attacking the Demon Sealing Grotto? Are you sure? That’s unheard of.\"","\"I’m serious.\"","\"That’s crazy... but no, we’re fine at the Demon Sealing Clan. However, I will notify the others just in case they do attack later.\"","After ending the conversation, Yan Hara looked at Yuan and asked, \"What should we do now?\"","\"There’s only one thing to do,\" Yuan said as he stood up.","Yan Hara nodded and followed Yuan. As they walked outside the building, they could see tens of thousands of Demon Sealers rushing to the portal to go outside to deal with the invasion.","\"Demon Worshippers have invaded our territory! Kill them all!\"","Yuan and Yan Hara followed them outside, and the moment they stepped out of the portal, their ears were assaulted by deafening explosions. As their eyes adjusted, they saw the city engulfed in chaos—surrounded on all sides by countless figures clad in black robes, each wearing a demon-faced mask that radiated malevolence.","The Demon Sealing Grotto fought desperately to defend the city, but the sheer number of Demon Worshippers proved overwhelming. To make matters worse, some of the cultists self-destructed upon confrontation, turning their bodies into deadly bombs and plunging the battlefield into further chaos.","\"Watch out! These bastards are sacrificing themselves!\"","\"I need more people in the west!\"","\"The north also needs more reinforcements!\"","\"What the hell are they trying to achieve with this stunt?\" Yan Hara questioned out loud after witnessing the scene.","Yuan narrowed his eyes slightly and said, \"Looks like they’re trying to cause as much chaos as possible, but their objective is still unclear. Let’s just take care of them for now.\"","\"Alright. I’ll go help out in the west,\" said Yan Hara as she flew away to help.","Yuan joined the battle shortly after, lending his strength to the northern front. Though his opponents were humans, he deliberately wielded Demon Sealing Aura, both to conceal his true identity and because the Demon Worshippers bore traces of demonic energy, making them especially vulnerable to such power.","The Demon Sealing Grotto’s forces were caught off guard by the unexpected assistance from the Demon Sealing Clan. While Yan Hara’s reputation preceded her, drawing little surprise, it was Yuan—whose identity was unknown—who left the most significant impression. The sheer potency of his Demon Sealing Aura stunned even the most seasoned Demon Sealers present, as it was even stronger than what he revealed during the meeting.","\"Heavens! Who the hell is that?! He’s sealing the Demon Worshippers by just being near them!\"","\"I heard that he’s Yan Hara’s disciple.\"","\"No way! His Demon Sealing Aura is clearly even stronger than hers!\"","The Demon Worshippers quickly recognized Yuan as a threat to their plans and wasted no time marking him as their top priority.","\"Kill him!\"","A black-masked leader roared, thrusting his finger toward Yuan with murderous intent.","In the next instant, hundreds of red-masked Demon Worshippers surged toward Yuan like a tide. Yet, strangely, not a single one of them made a move to attack. Instead, they hurled themselves at him like lifeless ragdolls.","Seeing the incoming wave, Yuan’s eyes narrowed as he warned, his voice calm yet commanding,","\"Leave now if you don’t want to die.\"","The Demon Sealers around him didn’t hesitate. Sensing the abnormality and realizing what the worshippers intended, they immediately scattered in all directions, retreating from the impending blast zone.","A split second later, just as the red-masked worshippers reached the very edge of Yuan’s Demon Sealing Aura, they all simultaneously crushed their Dantians.","Their bodies pulsed violently before erupting into a chain of catastrophic explosions—each one infused with destructive spiritual energy, turning them into living bombs aimed solely at annihilating Yuan.","The force of the explosions depended heavily on the cultivation of each individual. However, with most of the red-masked worshippers barely at the Spirit Realm, their self-destruction amounted to little more than sparks against Yuan, not even enough to harm a single strand of his hair.","\"If you want to take me down, you’ll need to sacrifice Immortals at the very least,\" Yuan said to the Demon Worshippers after coming out of the explosion unscathed.","Once again, the black-masked individual commanded, \"Kill him!\"","Without hesitation, three Bronze Immortal and one Silver Immortal charged at Yuan and detonated their Dantian right outside of Yuan’s Demon Sealing Aura.","Boom!","Suddenly, a far greater explosion erupted—one so immense that it engulfed half the city in a blinding inferno.","\"Surely, he must be dead...\"","The Demon Worshippers muttered as they watched from afar.","Moments later, as the blinding light of the explosion faded, the Demon Worshippers stood frozen in disbelief, their eyes widening with horror upon seeing Yuan emerge completely unscathed.","\"Looks like mere Immortals won’t cut it,\" Yuan said with a calm smile, his gaze settling on the black-masked figure at the second level of God Ascension. \"Why don’t you give it a try?\""]},{"number":2100,"title":"Chapter 2100: Divine Paragon’s Demon Sealing Arts","paragraphs":["\"How dare a mere Immortal...\" the black-masked figure muttered coldly, his voice laced with disdain.","Yet, despite Yuan’s provocation, he remained composed. Unlike the expendable pawns that littered the battlefield, he was no mindless fanatic and wouldn’t risk himself so easily.","Though he could theoretically overpower Yuan with sheer cultivation alone, he dared not act recklessly. The threat of Yuan’s Demon Sealing Aura loomed like a blade at his throat. Having accepted a demon’s power, he was now inherently vulnerable to its natural counter—Demon Sealing Aura. In such confrontations, cultivation alone meant little.","However, despite Yuan single-handedly holding the northern front, the other regions struggled to contain the relentless advance of the Demon Worshippers.","\"Damn it! Why the hell are there so many Demon Worshippers?!\"","\"This is unprecedented!\"","\"Look over there! More are coming!\"","Suddenly, the Demon Sealers spotted fresh waves of Demon Worshippers approaching from the horizon, an overwhelming black tide surging toward them like a living storm.","\"Something isn’t right! There can’t be this many Demon Worshippers!\" Zhou Yanfei had a deep frown on his face as he contemplated the situation.","Then, a look of realization—and disgust—washed over his face.","\"It can’t be...!\"","Not only were there too many Demon Worshippers, but most of these individuals were within the Spirit Realm and Divine Realm.","\"They must be controlling these people like puppets! They’re not true Demon Worshippers—just sacrificial pawns!\" Zhou Yanfei exclaimed, shocking everyone present.","\"Then how the hell should we deal with them?!\" Someone there asked.","If these people were truly innocent people being controlled by the real Demon Worshippers, they’d feel guilty killing them. However, if they didn’t stop them, these people would turn into suicidal bombs, inflicting immeasurable damage to the Demon Sealing Grotto.","\"Those wearing the black demon masks must be the ones controlling them! Take them down first—the control should end once they’re dead!\" Zhou Yanfei commanded with urgency.","The Demon Sealers immediately shifted their focus to the black-masked figures.","However, reaching them was easier said than done. The pawns swarmed around their masters like a living shield, and any attempt to approach was met with detonations from the red-masked ones, turning themselves into deadly explosives.","Since there was no definitive proof that the red-masked individuals were merely innocent people under control, the Demon Sealers made no effort to minimize their casualties. Even if they were innocent, the fall of the Demon Sealing Grotto would bring about far greater destruction.","If the Demon Sealing Grotto were to collapse, the demons would no longer need to hide in the shadows in fear.","Although cultivators today far surpass those from the Demonic Era and might ultimately repel another demon invasion, the demons would still wreak catastrophic havoc across the Nine Heavens, claiming countless innocent lives in the process.","Realizing how desperate the situation was, Yan Hara spoke to Yuan using voice transmission, \"Yuan, can I use your techniques to stop these people from destroying their Dantian?\"","Yuan responded, \"If your Demon Sealing Aura is strong enough, it’s possible.\"","\"But if I do that, it’ll reveal to the world that I have received the Divine Paragon’s legacy.\"","Since Yan Hara had yet to reveal any of the techniques bestowed upon her by Yuan, only a select few were aware that she now wielded the Divine Paragon’s Demon Sealing Arts.","\"It has to happen eventually anyway,\" said Yuan.","\"I understand.\"","With Yuan’s approval, Yan Hara tossed aside all hesitation and unleashed the Divine Paragon’s techniques.","A torrent of Demon Sealing Aura erupted from her, sweeping across the battlefield like a divine tempest. Both Demon Worshippers and Demon Sealers alike were shaken by its sheer magnitude.","\"Demon Sealing Zone!\"","In an instant, a massive barrier was erected, covering the entire battlefield.","\"Th-This technique is—!\" Zhou Yanfei’s eyes widened as he quickly recognized the technique being deployed and was shocked endlessly.","\"The Divine Paragon’s Demon Sealing Art—Demon Sealing Zone!!! Why the hell do you have this technique?!\" he shouted at her in a cracked voice.","However, Yan Hara ignored him and focused on the technique.","Sensing the imminent threat, the Demon Worshippers immediately turned to flee.","\"SEAL!\"","Yan Hara’s voice thundered across the battlefield as her Demon Sealing Aura surged forth, enveloping the red-masked individuals and sealing them all within the confines of the Demon Sealing Zone.","In the blink of an eye, nearly all of the Demon Worshippers were sealed. However, since the black-masked individuals had a much higher cultivation, they were able to escape the Demon Sealing Zone and avoid being sealed.","The Demon Worshipper reinforcements froze in their tracks upon witnessing the scene, and they even began retreating in fear.","With a single technique, Yan Hara had single-handedly halted the Demon Worshippers’ invasion. However, the feat had drained nearly all of her energy, and if they were to strike again, she wouldn’t have the strength to stop them a second time.","\"Well done,\" Yuan praised her through voice transmission.","\"Thank you... I’ve been training in secret ever since you entrusted me with the technique,\" she replied, her heart uplifted by the praise of its creator.","\"Yan Hara! Answer me! Why the hell do you have the Divine Paragon’s Demon Sealing Art?!\" Zhou Yanfei approached her afterward, demanding an answer.","\"What? That was the Divine Paragon’s technique? I thought it disappeared with the Divine Paragon...\" The Demon Sealers were shocked to learn this.","Yan Hara met Zhou Yanfei’s gaze with a composed expression and said clearly, \"It’s simple. I’ve inherited the Divine Paragon’s legacy.\"","\"You what?!\" Zhou Yanfei burst out in disbelief.","\"The Divine Paragon’s legacy?!\" Even the black-masked Demon Worshippers froze in shock. None of them had foreseen such a staggering revelation emerging amidst their invasion.","\"What should we do?! Our plans will—\"","\"Calm down.\"","A cold, commanding voice cut through the rising panic.","In the next instant, a suffocating pressure swept across the battlefield—sinister and oppressive—drenching the land in a malicious aura that made even the bravest tremble.","\"This presence... a demon has appeared!\"","The Demon Sealers instantly recognized the presence of a demon and prepared for their appearance."]}]);
